        "Washing windows wasn't as glamorous as they made it out to be. There was no big hoist, crane or even a fancy scaffolding. All he had was a rope, a plank with some guardrails to sit on and a bucket. For a seven-story building like this one, it was enough. He usually did the top four floors quite quickly. All it took was a quick squeegee wipe on the outside and wiping off the dirt. However, the cleaner the windows became, the pinker the light shone. Three hours later, Bobby had a splitting headache. He had just three floors left on the west side, but the pain was moving in behind his eyes. He didn't want to try the chew, but he had no choice. If he wanted a bonus from Yichen, he needed to finish. The doctor assured him they would do the job.",
