        "Her battered Hyundai pulled into the parking lot. If he raised an eyebrow at her dress, he knew enough not to say one word about it or risk losing one of his testicles.",
        "\"What the hell is going on, Lifante?\" She glanced up at the hanging plank and broken window covered in plastic.",
        "Dean said nothing but motioned for Ming to follow him toward the service elevator, then climbed to the fourth floor. When Dean ushered her into the room, forensics was there taking samples. The sheets were bloodied, soaked through to the mattress. Even the carpet had puddles of coagulating red. One would think the body might have lost every pint of it. The room was cold. Someone had turned on the air conditioner to prevent the scene from spoiling.",
        "\"Female, twenty-two, I.D. says she's a Computer Science student from UNLV. We're running the name now, but my gut says it's a fake. We think she might be a highly paid escort. The maid who entered the room found the body badly mangled and the window blown out from the inside. But here's the thing: when we showed up, the body was gone.\"",
        "\"What do you mean, gone?\"",
        "\"Faded into thin air. One of the local cops, Jeremy, was here. He said he saw it just dematerialize.\"",
        "\"You mean it got up and walked away, or like Star Trek beam-me-up-Scotty gone?\"",
        "\"More like the latter.\" Dean popped a candy into his mouth.",
        "\"That's ridiculous. Is your guy stressed out? High on something?\" She pointed to the window. \"Someone pay him to throw the body out the window and give this crazy story?\"",
        "\"They're questioning him right now, back at the precinct,\" Dean said. \"I arrived no more than fifteen minutes after the call. When I got here, Jeremy was white as a sheet. Even if someone had the mind to steal the corpse, there wouldn't have been time.\"",
        "\"What's with the equipment outside?\" she asked.",
        "\"We're running that down now,\" Dean said, flipping out his notebook. \"From what we could tell, the owner had a private contractor come here and clean the windows once a month. We're having trouble getting the name, though. Probably some illegal off-the-books thing. As far as we can tell, the bosun chair was outside the room when the window exploded. Witnesses saw a man fall from it and run away. They're pulling the traffic cams, but it'll take some time.\"",
        "\"You gonna let me take pictures?\" Ming asked, pulling out her phone.",
        "\"I'm not permitting you. You're doing that all on your own,\" Dean said, looking away.",
        "\"Right.\"",
        "Dean stepped into the room and watched Ming dictating notes as she went around the bed. One of the Shujing's smaller rooms, in the standard hotel style, if you ignored the blood-stained bed. Dean hated hotel rooms, even if they were better than his place.",
        "Ming went to the plastic and pushed it aside. She bent down to check the glass. A huge chunk was missing from the middle of the window, but the rest had spiderwebbed and remained intact. They'd found the piece of glass in the parking lot.",
        "Dean saw her bleary eyes. Combined with the dress, she must have been somewhere with her parents. They were the only ones who could get her into something that flashy.",
        "He'd never admit it, but he was envious of her. She said they were very traditional, with her mother going for glam over substance. Ming didn't have much to say about her father. Dean remembered their name from when he lived in their apartment building, but other than a vague recollection of them, nothing stood out. He didn't know what happened to his own parents. They split when immigration came sniffing around, shoving him into foster care when he was twelve.",
        "\"Wanna go for some coffee?\"",
        "\"I gotta get out of this dress, Dean.\"",
        "He swallowed the candy and pounded his chest as the image flashed across his mind. He filed it away and locked it behind a strong door. There was no way he was going there, even for her. But he kept the key. \"I suppose it can wait until the morning.\"",
        "\"Oh, bullshit. You and I both know we won't get any sleep over this. I'm already deep into the mysteries of this place, and this just adds one more.\" She stifled a yawn with her fist. \"How about I meet you at Darah's Diner down the street? Give me half an hour to shower. I'll need a clear head for this.\"",
        "Dean scowled and let her finish her filming. She switched off the phone and put it back into her purse.",
        "\"Later, Detective Lifante.\" She gave him a two-finger salute and flowed out the door.",
        "He couldn't tear his eyes away from her retreating figure, especially in that dress, and watched her swish out the door*.*",
        "*She would probably break me in two for considering it*. *Must have been some party she was at.*",
        "Ming did not favour fancy fashion. She lived in jeans and t-shirts or hoodies. But God, did she smell good. Dean sighed. This murder was a serious matter, and he needed to keep his focus on the crime and the mysterious disappearance of the victim, not Ming's leg every time she bent to take a picture or peer into something on the floor.",
        "Dean pinched his leg and refocused on the case. It was going to be a long night, and distractions only brought back feelings he'd tried hard to suppress.",
        "\"Detective. We've finished here,\" the CSI said. \"We need to clean up.\"",
        "Dean nodded, keeping his scowl in place. He loved how good they were, but could never trust the evidence completely. There was always some angle behind it, and it could be planted. He'd had enough experience with that to last three lifetimes.",
        "\"Good. Let's get out of here. I have a meeting to get to,\" Dean grumbled.",
        "\"Let me through!\"",
        "A disturbance in the hallway intruded on his thoughts. Dean grunted and stomped to the door. \"What's happening here?\" He stepped outside the room. \"This is an active crime scene.\" A short Chinese man was wrestling with two uniforms. \"What do you want?\"",
        "\"I'm the owner of this place.\" He shrugged his shoulders out of the grip of the two uniforms and thrust his head up at Dean. \"This is my hotel. I need to know what's happening in these rooms. I heard the body disappeared! What kind of funny business are you pulling here? I'm a legitimate businessman.\" He tapped his finger on Dean's chest. \"I refuse to be shaken down.\"",
        "\"Lee Chen? Or is it Yichen? Hold on a moment, sir. You'll find out what we know when we're finished here,\" Dean dismissed him and turned to the other uniforms. \"Seal this room. I don't want anybody going in or talking to the press until we've finished canvassing the hotel.\"",
        "\"Yes, sir.\" The two men saluted Dean. Turning back to the older man, he placed his hands on his shoulders. \"Don't worry, sir. Nobody will be getting into this room until I'm finished.\" He pointed to one of the uniforms. \"Go with him, and he'll take your statement.\" Brushing past the owner, Dean left the floor. He had a date to get to.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Yichen",
        "Yichen stalked down the hallway, followed by three guards and Wu, his secretary. She held out her iPad and swiped through the pages, flipping past image after image. At one, she stopped and tapped Yichen on the shoulder, showing him the tablet. Grimacing, he gestured to one of his guards and had him bend down. Whispering in his ear, he gave the man an order. The burly man stood up and nodded. He turned around and headed in the other direction. Yichen continued down the hallway, pulling out his phone."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "title": "Chapter 3",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "7:30 PM",
        "Bobby pounded on the door to Dr. Slazney's office. It said Stanley on the sign. When Bobby had asked about it, the doctor laughed and said he'd bought the building from another doctor and didn't want to change the name. It was close enough, and he wanted to keep the same clients.",
        "That should have been the first red flag.",
        "It was well outside office hours, and the small office was locked. According to Kat, Dr. Stanley mostly catered to the oddball and cosplay crowds, but he was discreet and located on the way home. He would take any commission, no questions asked. Bobby came here last week to get the chew. Several people had been waiting in the small office located just behind the strip mall. Whenever he stopped at McDonald's, even late at night, people went in and out. \"I should've known better.\"",
        "\"Ya looking for the doctor?\" A woman in a blue smock said, walking by with a take-out bag, puffing on a smoke. \"He left here this morning. Pushed everyone out and locked the door. I was fricken pissed. I needed to get my prescription filled so I could go back on comp,\" she hacked her way through the smoke.",
        "Bobby narrowed his eyes and took a step back from her.",
        "\"Don't mind me. Just ate some bad chilli. No plague or nothing, sheesh!\" She took another drag and pointed her fingers at him. \"If you see him, tell him Jillian's looking for him.\"",
        "He nodded and went back to his truck. Getting behind the wheel, Bobby punched the steering wheel and let out a sigh.",
        "\"Dammit. What's going on here? I just picked up the chew this morning. I knew the Shujing would call soon and wanted to be ready.\" Picking up his phone, he dialled Ryan. It was time to get out of here.",
        "He held the phone to his ear and listened to the dial tone. No answer. He hung up and tried again. Still nothing, not even a voicemail. \"Fuck, Ryan. You told me to call if anything happened. This qualifies.\" He threw his phone on the seat next to him and put his hands over the steering wheel.",
        "His mind raced back to where he first saw that code. It was a year before his brother died. Gregory sent him to break that sketchy business and take care of the owner. That was the easy part. Then he'd found that crazy bootleg Crue single and the code hidden underneath, which he swore was written in his own style. It had been eye-opening, magic even, able to pull things through time and space, but it ruined his life. It had forced him to come to America, costing him everything.",
        "\"Fucking-hell. What do I do now, Vlad?\" Bobby lay his head on his hands and looked at his missing pinky. When he first got to America, he wanted to get revenge on Ivan and Gregory, but as the memory blocks settled in, he'd forgotten about that. Now all he had to do was make it through the day. Not make waves. Maybe hit the odd Crue concert.",
        "Bobby jerked up. \"I remembered blocking my memory, fuck me. If that code is back, maybe I could use it? Last time it stole my life as payment, but now, I've got nothing.\" He could still feel it tickling around his memory blocks, but when he tried to focus on it directly, it was like grabbing onto what was left of Vince Niel's talent. You know it's in there and can feel nuggets of gold, but when you focus on it, only the dross comes pouring out. \"If I work on it, maybe...\"",
        "\"No, that code is what killed Vlad.\" Bobby started his truck. \"It can't be controlled. The cost is too high.\"",
        "His computer had a better net connection. Maybe he could reach Ryan that way, and he could listen to some Crue videos while looking into Slazney.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "8:30 PM",
        "Ming doodled on the napkin. She wrote Slazney's name in cursive and underlined it. Flipping the pencil across her knuckles, she brought it back around and started drawing circles under his name. \"Fricken bastard! Where the hell are you?\" she murmured.",
        "She was back in her hoodie and jeans. Dean's eyes were ready to pop out when she turned up in the glitzy dress, but that wasn't her. Maybe she could find time to wear it again. It was fun to tease him, but she wasn't sure where their relationship was headed. He was still trust-shy after the thing with his wife, but warming up to her, though. No matter what, she was willing to take her time. She'd been waiting ever since they were kids.",
        "She'd arrived at Dhara's Diner a few minutes ago. The hefty owner brought her a coffee and scoffed when Ming Na waved her away without ordering anything more. This place was an exposé away from getting shut down, the way Dhara ran it. She'd do it too if the Red Dragon wasn't such a juicer target. When Yichen bought it from the triad and changed the name to The Shujing, it didn't fool anybody. It was still the same thing, laundering money for its secret backer. Every lead she'd found on the man had led nowhere. He was a ghost.",
        "*What is his connection to my family?*",
        "Sipping her black gold, she watched the door open, and Dean walked in.",
        "Colin Farrell came to mind when she imagined who'd play him in a movie if the man were a shade darker. They shared the same aura before the penguin thing. Ming imagined him sweeping her off her feet, just like when they first met. She wished he'd wear a better brand name than K-Mart, but a cop's salary, even a detective's, didn't leave much to spend on anything. Besides, after the scandal with his wife, he refused to put on airs. Said it wasn't necessary.",
        "\"Gotta break through his ice shell,\" she mumbled.",
        "\"What was that?\" he said, sitting across from her. He pulled out a menu. \"You say something?\"",
        "\"Just wondering what the specials are?\" She covered her mouth with a cup of coffee. \"You're late, Lifante. I've been here for ten minutes.\"",
        "\"Sorry. I had to deal with your angry uncle, and some interesting things came up when we checked the security feeds.\" He waved the server over and ordered a plate of hash browns and a coffee.",
        "Ming placed her coffee down and got out her notebook. This was not the time for fantasies. \"What did you find?\" she asked, her pencil twitching. \"The body?\"",
        "\"I wish,\" he said, putting his elbows on the table and steepling his fingers in front of his face. \"If it weren't for the blood and the security camera, we wouldn't even have a lead. So far, nothing has come back on the name. I don't believe it's her real one, but we'll go through the motions. We're looking into her connections to the Shujing. I know your investigation is in the works on your uncle, but I don't think the victim's connected.\"",
        "Ming Na wrote in her notebook. All her colleagues recorded their notes on their phones, but she liked the tactile feel. Besides, nothing could hack into paper. \"I see,\" she clicked her tongue in frustration. One day, she'd find something on Yichen. \"Do you have a name for me?\"",
        "\"Barbie,\" Dean said, through a mouthful of hash browns. \"Based on the pink clothes we found in the room, she embraced the name.\" He washed everything down with a gulp of coffee, spilling some on his tie.",
        "She sighed and held her hand to her eyes.",
        "\"What?\"",
        "\"I like you, Lifante. You're the best detective I've ever met, even if you rely on your instinct too much, but I know exactly why women hate you.\" She lowered her hand, and he'd already inhaled the potatoes. \"You eat like a pig.\"",
        "He wrinkled his nose at her. \"Hardy, Har, Har. Just for that, I won't tell you the other thing we found.\"",
        "Ming put on an innocent face and put her fingers into her cheeks. \"Please, Mr. Lifante. I didn't mean to insult your manliness.\" She couldn't stop her eyes from rolling when she said that and watched him chuckle. She knew exactly what buttons to push with this man, and as long as she always told him the truth, they'd be okay.",
        "\"Fine. The security cameras corroborated what the witnesses said. There was someone outside the room cleaning the windows when they blew. We don't know who it was yet, but we recorded him trying to break into the room. There's no way to tell if he saw the murder or if he was trying to give himself an alibi. Records from the hotel say their contracted window cleaning company is outside the strip. A place called Squeegee R' Us.\"",
        "\"Where do they come up with these names?\" Ming snorted and took a sip of her coffee. \"That's not the important news, is it?\"",
        "Dean told her.",
        "\"Say that name again,\" she said, grabbing her pencil and leaning forward. \"It can't be.\"",
        "Dean pursed his lips and repeated himself. \"When we ran the cleaning business, we found it was tied to a shell company. It took some favours, but I discovered the owner is someone named Slazney. Weren't you looking for him?\"",
        "Ming snapped the pencil in her hand. Finally, after all these years. This was the backer. He was now tied to two businesses. She was getting close. \"You've given me the perfect present. I'm going to kiss you for this, Lifante. I need to talk to the Squeegee Place owner. Now!\"",
        "\"I thought you might.\" Dean handed her a note with the information on it. \"Be quiet about this. If word got out that I was handing information in an active investigation to a reporter, Zacoski would have me back on traffic duty.\"",
        "\"You don't have to worry. This is just between you and me.\" She stood up and planted a kiss on his cheek. \"Paid in full,\" she said, leaving so he wouldn't see her red face. She didn't turn back until she was at the door to the diner. When she glanced at him, Dean hadn't moved, but he'd placed a hand on his cheek.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "8:00 PM",
        "Closing the door to his truck, Bobby tried Ryan again. The number rang and rang, but this time it went to voicemail. \"Dammit. If you're out on a date, I'm going to kill you,\" he grumbled. \"You're supposed to be available twenty-four seven.\" Turning, he walked to his trailer. Located outside Vegas on the edge of the desert. It got too hot during the day, but the land was useless for anything else. The hotels didn't want it, and the tourists stayed away. It usually took him an hour to get to work, but Bobby didn't mind. With the window cleaning business paying in cash and not asking questions, he could hide from Gregory. Other than Chip, it was perfect.",
        "He wouldn't miss leaving Miss Grafinks, his neighbour, though. The curtain twitched in the trailer next door. That old bat was probably waiting for him to show up. He waved at the closed window, and the curtain twitched again. She needed a better hobby.",
        "Getting out his keys, Bobby halted. Today, there was a package on his doorstep. It was about the size of a small pillow, wrapped in plastic. A chill ran through him, and it wasn't from the desert breeze.",
        "He narrowed his eyes. \"What the hell is this?\" Picking up a stick from the brush next to his trailer, he poked the package. \"Someone's idea of a joke?\" When it didn't go off, he looked at the address on the top. It was addressed to him from Dr. Slazney.",
        "\"Slazney. That quack,\" he growled and picked it up. Probably his idea of a joke. Picking up the thing, he opened the door to his trailer and went inside. Tossing it on the table, he went to his fridge and pulled out a beer. He popped the top and chugged the whole thing. Today had been the worst day he'd had since coming to this country. He still didn't know who the dead girl was, and after pushing his guilt down, he didn't want to. He had gotten his fill of dead bodies in Russia. The further he stayed away from this, the better.",
        "He turned back to the package; all the tension left his body, and he sagged. \"Fuck!\" He had to know what was inside it. Grabbing a cutter from his drawer, he slit the plastic and opened it up. There was another tin of the chew, half the size of the first one, with the name Slazney across the top and a note.",
        "\"Thank you for coming to my store today, Bobby. Kat always spoke very highly of you. I hope you enjoyed the product. Here is a free sample to pass out to your friends. I forgot to give it to you this morning when you arrived.\" It was signed 'Slazney'.",
        "Bobby looked at the tin and tensed up again. If this were a free sample, he was a Metallica fan. He blinked and shook his head to relieve his fatigue.",
        "\"I can't believe someone could just weave a code into a window.\" He took another sip of the beer. \"Those windows have been there for years. There was no way that was the same code as before,\" he said out loud. \"It just didn't make sense. That code doesn't just exist in a vacuum. Besides, I haven't met anybody here who even knew how to write in proper Cyrillic. They'd screw up any attempt to code properly.\" Bobby ran his hand through his hair. The code had faded somewhat and was no longer poking at his memory blocks. He yawned. \"I'm going to regret this, aren't I?\"",
        "\"Whatever letters I saw must have just been my mind filling in the blanks at seeing another dead body. A flashback to when Vlad was killed.\" He smacked his fist into his palm. He'd erased everything about how to use the code and set up strong blocks to prevent any relapse. \"There's no way I saw that thing. My blocks were too good,\" he snorted.",
        "Convinced, he opened up the tin and winced. \"What is it about Americans and medicine that makes them want it to taste like the inside of a toilet?\" He set the tin on the counter and covered it with a towel. Maybe he'd get Ryan to mail it to Kat after he got out of this place.",
        "His stomach started growling. Grabbing a bowl from the sink, he filled it with some Captain's cereal and milk. He turned on the TV and sat down on his bed. He had maybe a day or two before the police got here if he was lucky. They'd have to contact Chip first, and that yutz hated working off the clock. Reminded me so much of Vlad at times. Maybe tomorrow morning at the earliest. He could get some sleep and deal with this crap then.",
        "\"Tonight's Top Story!\" the TV blared.",
        "\"Police have closed down the Shujing Hotel, located in the downtown area, while they search for a missing body,\" the reporter standing in front of the hotel said. \"Sources have confirmed that the police have lost the body of a young woman found in the fourth-floor room and are combing the hotel at the moment.\"",
        "Bobby continued to eat his cereal, drooling milk. After this, he'd do a quick run around the neighbourhood, shower, and exercise before sleep. He never missed the news, though. The reporter was a cute one, and he always liked watching her move.",
        "\"Detective Dean Lifante is in charge of the investigation. While no suspect has been named, the police have released a picture of a person of interest. They are looking for him now. We have obtained a copy of the picture from a trusted source and will show it to you here. First.\" She waved to the man off-screen.",
        "The spoonful of Captain's dropped from Bobby's hand, and he spilled milk and cereal all over his bed. He grabbed his phone and tried Ryan again. There was no way he could stay here now, not with his picture all over the TV. They didn't have his new name yet, but it was only a matter of time before Gregory showed up. What the fuck was Chip doing? \"Must have been thinking with his little 'ip',\" he mumbled.",
        "\"Hello, Ryan speaking.\"",
        "\"Finally! Where have you been? I need...\" the message continued, cutting him off.",
        "\"I'm sorry, but my machine is down. I will be unavailable for the next few days. If it's urgent, please contact Mr. Wilson at 555-6767. Thank you.\"",
        "Bobby let go of his phone and put his hands over his head. \"Fuck!!!\"",
        "***POV_HEADER***Barbie",
        "8:30 PM",
        "Barbie stuck her head through the bathroom wall. The plebs had finally left, taking all the blood evidence with them. She needed that back if she wanted to regain her corporeal form. For the moment being in this ghost form was saving energy, but it was limited to only keeping her together.",
        "She'd expelled most of the remaining nanites to create that counter code. Even if they were offline, the Maker could bring them back. They only have a twenty-four-hour window outside a living host; after that, they start to break down and become completely inert after forty-eight hours.",
        "Squealing in glee, she pumped her fists in the air and rotated around in a circle, drifting towards the open window. It had worked. She'd confirmed it before going ghost. The virus wasn't in the Maker now. Her program had supplanted it and suppressed Bobby's cortisol levels. All he had to do was go to sleep, and then it would activate. When he woke up, he'd complete the code in his sleep, and it would lead him to her and force him to recreate her body.",
        "Then he'd have no choice but to come back with her.",
        "Soul transfer was much easier. She reached up and touched the scar on her neck and grimaced. It was good she found that knife. If only she hadn't had to slice her neck, but blood was always the most powerful, and lifeblood would ensure the connection had been severed.",
        "\"Why'd you have to medicate yourself, Maker?\" she said, stomping her foot and puffing out her cheeks. \"You were fighting the download so well, too. Headaches are just a small price to pay for your safety.\"",
        "Concentrating on her feet, she forced her remaining nanites to retain cohesion. Being a ghost was draining them quicker than she expected. Floating was fun, but it made it difficult to get anywhere. Stepping on the floor, Barbie walked through the door. Until the Maker finished recreating the code, she had no way to find him before the damage to her body became irreversible. Records of Vegas in this time were spotty, at best, and he lived on a grid.",
        "She'd seen the owner stalking away from the lead detective. \"Maybe if I stick around the old man, he'll lead me closer to the Maker,\" she mused. \"I can also haunt you in the meantime. Pay you back for feeling up my tushy.\"",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ivan",
        "8:00 PM",
        "LA",
        "Gregory wiped the remains of the remote control from his lap and looked up at Ivan, knocking a folder to the floor. A picture of Petor slid out. The scar down Gregory's cheek pulsed with his anger. Two men approached a third man with a smoking hole in his chest, the size of a dinner plate, but shaped like a hand.",
        "\"We were in Vegas a few months ago on a business trip. Why didn't we know Petor was there?\" Gregory asked.",
        "Ivan didn't move. His shadow swallowed Gregory.",
        "\"Who is this Slazney? Why'd he send this information?\"",
        "Ivan pointed to the man being dragged out.",
        "Gregory sighed. \"Drive to Vegas. All night if you have to. Find Petor. You have my permission to use your talents, but don't kill him. I don't want a repeat of this incident, and I want that code.\"",
        "Ivan nodded."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "title": "Chapter 4",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Yichen",
        "8:30 PM",
        "Yichen waved his phone in the air as he yelled at the wall. \"You promised me there wouldn't be any trouble here, Slazney. That you could handle it!\" Leaning back on his chair, he waved his hands in the air. \"A woman was offed in my hotel room! Then her body disappeared. I had to give the police the window washer footage to get them out of here before they found something else to harass me about.\" He spun around and pounded his hands on the desk, standing up.",
        "\"What! You never said he was important! Why didn't you say something before you told me to hire his company?\" Yichen smiled as he glanced at his secretary. She held up five fingers.",
        "Five minutes till his man arrived at Bobby's place.",
        "\"Slazney, I won't have you screw my family over on this. Tell me what you're up to!\" The phone went dark, and Yichen ripped the earbuds from his head and threw them across the room. They bounced off his secretary's chest. She picked them up, wiped the wax off them and put them in the charger.",
        "\"Wu! Let me know when they get the Washer. I want him by my side or in the ground.\" He shivered. \"Why is it so cold here? Turn up the heat!\" He left the room mumbling to himself",
        "Wu nodded and wrote on her tablet. Her face never moved.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "8:30 PM",
        "There was no way Bobby could sleep now. He wasn't worried about the police. They were usually inept in any country. Gregory was another matter. That prick would be sending Ivan for him now. Bobby threw a change of clothes, a laptop with a Motley Crue decal, and some Crue CDs into a duffel bag. It was only a matter of time before he was dead.",
        "\"Screw you, Ryan,\" he mumbled. The FBI handler was the worst thing about his stay in America. Always cracking jokes and trying to be funny. If Ryan was going to take a vacation, he should have told him.",
        "Bobby ran out of the trailer and jumped into his truck, suppressing a yawn. He needed a coffee and some cash. Popping a CD into his truck, he turned up the volume, full blast and headed back to the McDonald's in the strip mall. He could use their Wi-Fi to access the internet and hack into the bank. He'd promised Ryan he wouldn't do that anymore, but there was no choice now.",
        "He swerved to avoid the Jaguar coming into the lot and continued to the strip mall. \"Drive vetter, you fool!\" he said. \"Vis is no time to get into vaccident.\" Whenever he started speaking in Vlad's accent, things were getting bad.",
        "11:30 PM",
        "He backed into the parking space at the Moonbeam Strip Mall and poured some sugar from the little packets into his coffee. The cheap brew stung his nose and would burn going down, but it was effective. Usually, one pack of sugar was enough, but today he needed the extra energy. He'd already played his collection of Crue CDs, and the world they showed him wasn't working anymore. He held up the Baby Metal one Kat had given him as a joke, but wasn't ready to go there just yet.",
        "He'd been driving for the last three hours, trying to kill time. It was closing in on midnight. \"Whoever set up the bug with the day change must have learned programming from a monkey.\"",
        "Cracking his knuckles, he opened his computer and started hacking into the local Wells Fargo next door. The security system there was a joke. Not only did they keep tons of cash on hand, but they also refused to pay their employees enough to secure the firewalls.",
        "Typing, he almost fell on the keys. \"This is dangerous. Even a joke can trip you up. Just five minutes,\" he mumbled and closed his eyes.",
        "His eyes closed, math chipped away at the block in his mind, bringing back memories of a woman. He knew her. He was afraid of her, but happy to see her at the same time. \"Who are you?\" he mumbled. \"Why pink?\"",
        "Seconds later, a headlight from an approaching car jolted him awake. Shaking his head, Bobby took a sip of coffee and turned back to the computer. His eye twitched. On the screen was the same code he had seen in the Shujing windows. It was staring back at him, only more complete.",
        "\"When did I write this?\" He stared at the numbers and commands. \"No, it's different.\" The beauty of the code, its simplicity beckoned, called to him in music and poem. So, unlike the clunky Python or even the outdated C++. \"I can see the genius of Nikki Sixx mixed in here. The Shujing code had none of this.\"",
        "Hitting the backspace button, he erased everything.",
        "\"Where did that piece of der'mo come from? I remember parts of it, but I thought I'd destroyed it,\" Bobby said, panting. A chill went down his spine. \"What did that code do to me?\" He remembered that the code could rewrite reality and change the natural order of things. \"Is it writing itself? Did it plant a Trojan? I blocked it, didn't I?\"",
        "He rubbed his eyes, trying to massage out the sleep. He checked his watch. It read 12:03. \"Just five minutes.\" He closed his computer, leaned his seat back and drifted off.",
        "Again, numbers flowed across his vision. He remembered some things from Russia. Pulling the lost Spanish version of Glitter from somewhere.",
        "\"WEOWEOWEO!\"",
        "The police sirens pierced the night. Bobby shot up, knocking his computer off his lap and stared out the window. It was still nighttime, but fires covered everything. The McDonald's was a hollow shell, and the parking lot had been blasted with craters. There was a stack of skulls under what was left of the arches, and a Mad Max wannabe stalking his truck.",
        "\"What the Fuck?\" He checked the dashboard clock, and it showed that only three minutes had passed. He rubbed his eyes and stared out the window again. Everything was normal. Two teenagers were heading out of the restaurant with some take-out. The boy still looked like Mad Max but was stuffing his face with a French fry. The usual American diet. He scanned the parking lot, and there were three other cars there. No craters. No fires in the background and no stack of skulls.",
        "However, the dead woman's face filled his mind. She was calling to him, beckoning. He couldn't close his eyes without seeing her.",
        "\"The hell?\" He picked up his computer and reconnected to the Wi-Fi. Checking the local news for anything to explain away what happened, he found a breaking story about his trailer park. The news panned in for a closer look. Miss Garfinks' house always had the same ugly dwarf outside her door. He hated that thing, but it was distinctive.",
        "And broken. The news reporters were showing his house in the center of a crater. He turned up the volume on the news.",
        "\"Reports are coming in about an explosion in the Paradise Trailer Park. Information is scarce, but we see Dean Lifante on the scene. This may have a connection to the missing body case at the Shujing. We will keep you updated as events unfold.\"",
        "A few firefighters were there, but it didn't look like there was a fire. Bobby put his hand on his head.",
        "\"That wasn't a bomb. What the fuck do I do now? I wasn't expecting Ivan to get here this quickly.\"",
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "12:30 AM",
        "\"This place is a complete mess. Are you sure this is the right address?\" Dean asked the uniform. She was new to the force and hadn't had time to hear all the rumours about him yet. That meant she was still willing to talk. \"What's that smell?\" He wrinkled his nose at the mix of gas and an overpowering scent of musk invading everything.",
        "\"Yes, sir. According to the manager of Squeegee R' Us, this is the address on file for Bobby Miladev. A Russian immigrant. Arrived here a year and a half ago.\" She looked up. \"That's all we have.\" She closed her notebook and stood back. \"As for the smell, I don't know where it's coming from.\"",
        "\"Who the fuck leaked his name to the press?\" Dean stared at what was left of the trailer, trying to piece together the destruction, and rubbed the back of his head. He turned back to the rookie, \"What's your name?\"",
        "\"Cammy Ortiz, sir. I just started last week. I transferred from New York.\" She picked her way across the wreckage of the trailer.",
        "\"Well? Any idea where the press got his name, Ortiz?\" Dean liked the way she moved, but it was nothing compared to the gracefulness Ming would show. He turned his head and focused on the destruction. There was no reason to spark another investigation into his conduct.",
        "\"No, sir, but I'll call the news office.\"",
        "\"Do that.\" Dean stared at what was left of the trailer and frowned. There was something wrong here. He sniffed the air and sneezed. There was a musk smell, but he couldn't quite pin it down. It was unlike anything he'd smelt before.",
        "The trailer had been destroyed. Whatever happened here was quick and strange. Pieces of the wall were found embedded in the neighbouring trailer, but no other trailer had been touched. There was no fire either, which was good, but it didn't explain how a crater could appear without leaving any evidence. It was as if something set off a concussion blast like in that anime with the shiny star balls and caused the trailer to burst.",
        "\"Dammit,\" he mumbled. Turning to the CSI group, he held out his phone, the record button pressed. \"Give me something, Fisher.\" He wished Ming were here. She was much better at talking to the science types and could follow what they said without a translation program. \"Was this a bomb?\"",
        "The ranking CSI, Fisher, scowled. After Ming, he was the best there was, but hated being disturbed when he was looking over a crime scene. It went against his personality to speculate. Dean tried to stay out of his way when he was working, but every so often Fischer needed a little poke to remind him that he was part of a team. It was the least Dean could do after the mess he put him through three years ago.",
        "\"According to the neighbours, Bobby Miladev arrived back here around eight pm. He went inside, and then they heard his truck start up around eight-thirty. A few other people came by soon after, but didn't stick around. The explosion happened an hour ago, at about ten. There was no warning, just a boom. There were no bodies found in the aftermath,\" Fisher turned back to the scene. \"This was the center.\" He pointed to the clear patch. \"If there was a bomb, we've found no traces of any explosive device or residue.\"",
        "\"Can you give me anything?\" Dean asked, \"A trailer just doesn't explode like this.\"",
        "\"I'm not a wizard, Detective, and I don't make guesses. All I can tell you is whatever it was, it wasn't a bomb. Anything that survived is over there on the table,\" Fisher pointed outside the destruction.",
        "Dean sighed and let the man get back to his work. He may hate him, but Fisher knew what he was doing. By this time next week, he should know everything there was to know. Even so, his gut was digging into his spleen. Something was wrong with this place. He rubbed his arm across his nose to get rid of the smell.",
        "He stepped to the forensics table and peered at the material they had bagged. \"What did Fischer find?\" He asked the tech cataloguing everything. They pointed to the end of the table and went back to their clipboard. Dean frowned and picked up a half-burnt CD. A pair of ugly, thick coke bottle-like safety goggles with shattered lenses, and a tin of chewing tobacco. Turning the tin around, he whistled at the name of Slazney's clinic inscribed outside.",
        "\"Again? You're turning up everywhere today, aren't you, Doctor?\" He took a picture and sent it to Ming. Fischer was good, but there was no one better at hunting down secrets.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "12:30 AM",
        "Ming checked her phone and sent a kissy face emoji back to Dean. It had only been a few hours, and he was finding a fresh lead on the Shujing. After getting chewed out by her editor for missing the press conference, Ming needed something to shut him up. Her fingers twitched just thinking of his smug attitude, imagining them wrapped around his throat. It's not her fault that he rushed a story about what happened to print without checking all the facts first.",
        "\"Just because Daddy got you the job doesn't mean you'll keep it.\"",
        "Ming dialled the number for the cleaning company. A sleepy voice answered the phone.",
        "\"Yes?\" a yawn rolled out of the speaker in her car dashboard.",
        "\"Is this Chester Punk Jr., of Squeegee's R'Us?\" Ming asked",
        "\"Yeah. It's late. What do you want?\"",
        "She couldn't place the accent. \"I'm sorry to bother you at this late hour. My name is Ming Na Liu. Is this a good time to talk?\"",
        "\"No. Tomorrow, during business hours. I'm off now.\" Chester's voice was clipped, and the tone was rising.",
        "\"I understand, but I have some questions about the owner...\" She wasn't going to mention Slazney over the phone. The last time she'd done that, her source had disappeared.",
        "\"I'll ask my father. Anything else can wait till tomorrow.\" He hung up.",
        "Getting out of her car, she stood up straight, stretching the kinks out of her shoulders and turned off her recorder. Paper was so much better, but the last time she tried writing her thoughts down while driving, she'd almost hit a tree. \"Screw Chester and his nasal voice. I'll ask about borrowing a truck in the morning.\" She couldn't back down here if she wanted to get the story. \"I can feel Slazney nipping at my heels, but I need the proof.\"",
        "She stepped into the Shujing lobby, ignoring the slot machines and the old ladies playing them. Located outside the main Vegas strip, far enough away from the excitement to stay quiet, the Shujing catered to the older, conservative crowd even as Yichen tried to pivot to the convention circuit. Slots were a part of the background colour and were everywhere. One of the devices went off, sending some ear-splitting shrieks through the lobby and a shower of coins into the woman's lap. She was giggling and holding her purse open to catch all the silver. Ming wondered how much of her pension she'd already put into the machine.",
        "\"My name is Ming Na Liu, for the Las Vegas Sun. I'd like to speak to the owner. Please,\" she said to the two front desk staff as she placed her card on the counter. Her uncle was still the best chance she had at getting in touch with Slazney.",
        "\"I'm sorry, but he is unavailable at the moment.\" They ignored her card and started speaking in Cantonese to each other. She didn't have a suitcase, and it was past check-in time. Reporters weren't usually welcome here, either. They had no reason to help her.",
        "Sighing, she switched to Cantonese. \"*Can't ignore me now, boy. Get me, my Uncle. I know he's still awake*.\" Tapping her foot and frowning, she crossed her arms to hide the phone, recording everything.",
        "The front desk staff flinched, and a phone rang. He picked it up and nodded.",
        "Ming heard a loud voice behind it.",
        "Replacing the phone, the staff pushed a buzzer. \"You can go up, Miss Liu. The owner is waiting for you.\" He pointed to the side door.",
        "She nodded and went into the back. Unlike the lobby, the hallway showed how fake this place was. The paint was peeling, and the floor was cracked in several places. The hotel was built in the eighties by triad money, as a place to launder their casino winnings and as a refuge from the politics in the Strip itself.",
        "Since then, it'd changed hands several times. Through it all, the name Slazney had been behind it. She had spent years tracking him down since she found his name in her father's medical file after his accident. The shadowy Vegas power player, with his hands in everything. Including chewing tobacco, if Dean's mail was to be believed.",
        "Yichen's office was in the back. Opening the door, she was hit by the change between it and the hallway. Here, he'd decorated in blues and purples: A villain's lair. It was also cooler than the rest of the building. The red and pink motif was so strong in the rest of the hotel that this room was like a cancer just trying to dig its way into the light.",
        "\"Ming, how are your parents? I was hoping to stay longer at Don's birthday party earlier, but the story of a murder in my hotel was more pressing,\" Yichen said as Ming closed the door. His cologne hit her hard. It was a spicy cinnamon smell, but it did nothing to cover up his sweat. He was nervous. Stress made him look older. He was still wearing the same tailored Armani suit from earlier. It looked a little wrinkled. He hated appearing less than perfect.",
        "\"Please have a seat.\" He pointed to a chair with a drink in his hand.",
        "She nodded, scowling. She hated the man. He was her grandmother's brother, so a great-uncle. Uncle Don and Auntie Jinn loved to talk about their famous relative, and he'd often visit her parents when Ming was a child. He was always watching her. She liked the sweets he'd bring and called him Uncle, but as she got older, she started questioning the things he'd do. There was no way someone who smelled like him could be a good person, but she couldn't find the proof. Dean's way just didn't work for her.",
        "\"Your face tells me otherwise. For a reporter, you like to wear your heart on your sleeve.\" He took a sip of his drink and sat down behind his desk. \"What can I do for you?\" He smiled. \"Are you still looking to expose me and drive me out of business? I'm sure your mother would be very disappointed.\"",
        "\"Leave her out of this.\" She took out her notebook and flipped to a new page. \"I'm here for another reason.\" She paused. \"Bobby Miladev. I know he cleaned your windows. What can you tell me about him?\"",
        "\"Bobby.\" Yichen raised an eyebrow. \"He's a window washer and a good one. Why do you ask?\"",
        "\"He's a suspect in the murder, as I'm sure you already know. Don't try and play dumb with me, Uncle.\" She took a deep breath. There was no reason to drive him away; she needed him to answer her questions, and he was family. \"What can you tell me about the girl who was murdered in your hotel?\"",
        "\"What murder?\" He spread his hands out. \"There is no body, only blood, which your friend in the police took with him.\" He took another sip of his drink. \"As far as I'm concerned, it was a prank played by some bored high school kids to discredit my hotel.\"",
        "Ming expected this response and went to the next question. \"Who's Slazney?\" She watched his face closely. There was no reaction, but he paused, ever so slightly, then downed his whole drink.",
        "\"Sorry, I don't know anybody by that name. Is he someone I should know?\" He got up and poured another drink.",
        "It was time to play the next card. \"Detective Dean Lifante tracked down the window washer. His place had been destroyed. Pieces everywhere. Maybe you saw it on the news.\" She paused for effect. \"They found some evidence of Slazney there.\" She watched his back tense up, but there was less reaction than she expected.",
        "She wrote in her notebook, 'He knew,' and underlined it twice. When she was a child, she'd seen him get angry and whale on a stranger with his cane when they stepped in front of him in line. He was not one to hold his temper in check. Watching his bodyguards drag the man away was when she knew her uncle for what he truly was.",
        "\"What does that have to do with me?\" he asked, turning back to her. He was gripping the drink in his hand so hard that a crack spread up the glass.",
        "Ming narrowed her eyes and smiled. \"When I was researching this place, a man's name kept coming up, but I could never track him down. Slazney. I know you've heard it before. What can you tell me about him?\"",
        "He sat down in the chair and took another sip of his drink. \"This is the first time I've heard of him. What's he got to do with you?\"",
        "Ming flipped to the back page of her notebook. \"You remember the accident my father had a few years ago?\"",
        "Yichen nodded.",
        "\"I was going through some old finance records and found out that a Slazney paid the bill. I wanted to thank him, but I couldn't find him. I thought it might have been you, but there was no proof of a connection. Everywhere I looked, he seemed to be a ghost. The deeper I dug, the more I found that I didn't like.\" She didn't trust him, but he was still her best chance to find the man. \"Mom told me to let it go, but I couldn't. The mystery is too big.\"",
        "\"You always were a curious one.\" He picked up a phone. \"Tell you what, though, for old time's sake, I'll see what I can find: On one condition.\"",
        "She smiled. His help usually had a cost. However, she could play along for a little bit. \"What is the condition?\"",
        "\"You and your detective friend join me for dinner tomorrow. I've seen the way you look at him, and I wish to approve of anyone seeing my niece.\" He smiled and started dialling.",
        "\"We aren't dating,\" she blushed. Her dark complexion kept it from being more visible. Ming hated mixing business with her personal life. What she did with Dean was her own business. Still, if it got her closer to Slazney, she could do it. The hard part would be convincing Dean to come. He was still skittish about anything that appeared to be a date. \"And I'm not your niece. But we'll be here. What time?\"",
        "\"Give me some time to make some calls. I will text you tomorrow with a time, but please leave the early evening open over the next few days.\"",
        "\"Okay. But I would like to come here in the morning and clean the windows. Retrace Bobby's steps. Is that okay with you, Uncle?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"Be my guest. But be careful. I also won't be paying you any money.\"",
        "Ming nodded, stood up and closed her notebook. There was nothing else she'd get from him tonight. He was too guarded. However, if she watched his men scramble to put out the fire she had just set, maybe she'd find a tidbit of truth in all his lies. \"Until tomorrow.\"",
        "*I will find out what you're hiding, Uncle.*",
        "***POV_HEADER***Barbie",
        "12:30 AM",
        "Floating in the corner of the old man's office, Barbie waited until the Chinese woman left. The old man was making more phone calls now, but he'd been doing that for the last few hours. He was very angry when his man had missed the Maker. She remembered the tantrum he'd thrown, breaking the tablet in two on the desk.",
        "\"Get someone to the pigpen. I need a cleaning done,\" the old man said. Barbie just sighed. Twenty-first-century lingo was difficult to follow, but this guy was even harder than most.",
        "Barbie spent the last few hours waiting for something, anything, to lead her to the Maker. She had to absorb the heat in the air to maintain her nanobots. It was a temporary measure, but she had no choice. They worked better in the desert, not in this air-conditioned box.",
        "If she stayed with the old man, maybe he'd lead her to the Maker. She'd already spent several hours waiting for him in the hotel room, and nothing. He never came back. When she'd slit her throat, only the nanites in her body had kept her from the big sleep, and they could only keep her like this for another day, two if she conserved their energy. The Maker would have to show up then and read the bad virus.",
        "\"Stupid dork. Why won't you go to sleep?\" She didn't want to use her last resort and turn herself into this spirit, just them, even if it worked, maybe. Now if only he'd finish writing the code she'd planted in him, Barbie could regain her body and finish her mission.",
        "\"What do I do next, Maker?\"",
        "Yichen looked around the office for a second. \"What was that?\" He waited a few minutes, but Barbie didn't respond. He shrugged and returned to his phone calls.",
        "Barbie stuck her tongue out at the man and floated through the door. She'd made up her mind. The Asian woman had a better chance of finding the Maker, and the old man had already tried to kill him once. She needed him alive if she was going to regain her real body. Besides, Slazney seems like a bad man, and the old man was working with him."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "title": "Chapter 5",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "9:00 AM",
        "Bobby yawned and knuckled his eyes. He couldn't fall asleep here. He had moved to the Starbucks across the street when the sun rose to get out of his truck and use the toilet. The coffee was expensive, and they didn't offer free refills, but the Wi-Fi was better here. Besides, his bladder couldn't handle any more.",
        "Every time the caffeine wore off, and he closed his eyes for a few seconds, the same devastation he'd witnessed at MacDonald's came back. Each time, worse than the last. He couldn't head back home either. Ivan's message was very clear. Bobby rubbed the bridge of his nose. His head was pounding, and not in the fun, after an all-night bender, way.",
        "\"What the fuck is going on here?\"",
        "That code. It all kept coming back to that code. It could rewrite time and space in the wrong hands. He didn't know which was worse: the one in the window or the one that destroyed the window. Bobby played with the sugar packets and started tying the empty ones in a knot. Anything to keep his fingers busy.",
        "\"*The last time I worked on it was just before Gregory tried to kill me. It's what brought the American to me*.\" He stared at his missing pinky finger. \"*I wish I'd never discovered how to manipulate it. That Motley Crue demo at the end was so true*,\" he mumbled in Russian.",
        "\"It's what got Vlad killed,\" he whispered to the computer.",
        "He still thought about his twin brother and wondered what had happened to the body. He asked the American and Ryan after he'd escaped, and both of them said it had been handled, but it didn't feel right. One day, he would have to head back to Moscow and visit Vlad's grave. Maybe Ryan would tell him where it was if he wasn't too busy leaving him swinging in the wind.",
        "Wiping his face, Bobby stared at the computer screen. On it was something that looked like the code from the Shujing windows. He'd spent the last three hours recreating it from memory, and so far, it wasn't anything like before the memory block. He could tell that much. The block had degraded enough to tickle him with his trauma. Teasing memories that remained just out of reach. He'd tried to avoid the code and erase it, but every time he drifted off, some part of him wrote it again. Finally, he stopped fighting the memory, but now that he was awake and focused on writing it down, the numbers trickled onto the page. Like a writer stuck on a 'Dark stormy night.'",
        "*\"It's only been three years. I know I locked it down for my own safety, but why can't I remember everything?\"* he said to his computer*. \"It was flowing out of me when I wasn't even trying, but now.... What's stopping me?\"*",
        "A young man, about twenty-five, in a pink and yellow Speedo with a fancy pink cake, turned and glared at Bobby. \"Could you please be quiet? I'm live-streaming here! What language are you speaking anyway? German? This is America. Speak English,\" he scoffed.",
        "Bobby raised his hand in a karate chop gesture to say sorry, reversed it and gave the man the middle finger. \"It's Russian, you peacock. I'll shut up vhen you learn how to grow a decent beard. Vhat is that fluff on your chin? Your dog vomit?\"",
        "The man put his hand to his mouth and gasped. \"Well, screw you, man.\" He gathered his recording equipment and moved to the other side of the Starbucks.",
        "\"No, thank you. I don't sving that vay. Not enouff meat on you,\" Bobby laid on the Russian accent extra thick. The wannabe Tuber gave his middle finger to Bobby and sat down in a cloud of pink.",
        "Then it hit him. Pink.",
        "Colour was never important to the code, but it could be used to hide text, especially if it was in the light brown or blue spectrum. Every time he did the windows, he must have been reading the code, but the block must have been forcing him to ignore it. What did Kat say about the chew? Bobby racked his brains. 'It let the mind breathe.' That was it, he'd finally relaxed enough to unclench. He patted his pockets for the free sample Slazney'd sent.",
        "Nothing.",
        "\"Where did I put that...\" he slapped himself on the head. \"Fuck! It's at the trailer.\" Either the police had it, or it was lost when his house exploded.",
        "\"Damn you, Ivan! I hope you didn't go all out on my account,\" he scoffed and pulled up the video on a separate tab. Maybe he could check the scale of the destruction. \"Scram needs to get an iPhone if he's going to document the trailer park life. The Android he's got does nothing but destroy all sense of realism.\"",
        "\"Excuse me, sir, but could you keep it down?\"",
        "\"Sorry about that,\" Bobby apologized to the server and closed the video.",
        "He shut his laptop, shoved it into his bag, took the last swig of his coffee and tried his temporary handler again.",
        "Nothing.",
        "He used the toilet one last time to empty his screaming bladder. \"I'm never drinking this much coffee again,\" he muttered. Bobby got into his truck and headed back to his trailer. It was the last place he wanted to go, but the pressure in his head wasn't letting go. Something was drawing him back there. It was a long shot, but maybe he could find the tin. He didn't know what else to do. If he could get there without running into Ivan, he'd count that as a win.",
        "*\"What did that fucking window do to me?\"*",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "9:00 AM",
        "Kat pulled up to the Shujing in the Squeegees R'Us' Us's van. Ming jerked awake, pinched her leg and downed another gulp of coffee from her flask. It had been her third all-nighter in a row trying to dig up information on Slazney. There was nothing else tying him to the squeegee place. When she finally got to bed at three, the alarm woke her up at five. \"After this, I'm taking some of my vacation days,\" she mumbled. Her editor could go to hell. There was no way he was guilting her into cancelling again.",
        "When she'd asked Chip to let her borrow everything Bobby used to clean the hotel, with the addition of Kat, he said no and popped a caramel. Once she offered him some money and promised to do an article on him, it was quite easy. He was surprisingly passionate about cleaning.",
        "\"Thanks for getting me out of there today,\" Kat said. They were getting the gear out of the truck. \"Chip was on a tear with Bobby missing, said he stole a bunch of equipment. He wouldn't stop ranting about the sanctity of a promise.\" Kat shook their head.",
        "\"My pleasure,\" Ming said. \"I needed someone who knew how to use this equipment anyway.\" She continued to stack everything on the sidewalk. It was heavy. Having Dean here would have made this much easier.",
        "No! He was on her shit list right now. He'd refused to give her the tin. Said it was evidence in an investigation. It didn't help that he was right, but after the main suspect disappeared, retracing Bobby's steps seemed the only way to find out what he had been doing.",
        "\"So, what do you want me to do?\" Kat asked.",
        "\"I need you to set up the equipment on the roof and lower me down, doing the same thing Bobby would usually do. I'm trying to retrace his steps. It helps me get into his mind. According to the video, something happened here when he was cleaning, and I'm hoping to get some insight into him,\" Ming said.",
        "\"Sure. I love a mystery,\" Kat said. \"Besides, anything to help Bobby out. He was the only one who'd apologize when he got my pronouns wrong,\" they said.",
        "Ignoring the front desk, Ming and Kat went through the service entrance. Yichen had given his permission last night, but that didn't mean he'd told them what she was doing.",
        "Exiting to the roof, Ming took in the view. The sun reflected off the nearby hotels and buildings, promising more heat to come.",
        "\"I love this sight,\" Kat stuck out their arms and twirled around. The wind from the desert brought a hint of heat and dust in the air. It's what made it so difficult to keep the windows clean. \"When you can look over everything, all your problems seem so small.\"",
        "\"I guess I never really thought about it,\" Ming responded. She leaned forward to hide her awkwardness. It wasn't the pronouns; it was the lack of anything to say to a twenty-year-old human that left her tongue-tied. \"When did I get so old?\" she mumbled to herself.",
        "It didn't help that she was on edge all morning. When she woke up, her room was freezing, her mother had left a massive guilt trip on her voicemail, and her life-saving coffee machine broke. They were all small things, but combined with Chip's lack of help, they left her nervous. Dean would have consulted his instinct, checked the danger and taken it slow. She needed more than a vague stomach ache to give in to superstition. There was still too much she didn't know about this case, and that irked her. Her fingers twitched. She hated having a mystery she couldn't solve.",
        "Working on a problem like this usually helped her push those thoughts aside. Ming secured the lines to the roof's mounting pillar and stood up. \"What do we do here?\"",
        "\"Let me show you.\" Kat grabbed the line, swung it and tossed it over the edge. \"For bigger buildings, we had a crane and two-person scaffolding. For smaller ones, like the Shujing, we just used this bosun chair. Bobby would sit in it and lower himself to the ground. After, he'd climb back up the stairs and do it again for another set of windows. It's perfect for a one-man job. Safer with two, in case someone gets stuck, but the owner only wanted Bobby and would pay him a triple bonus in cash.\" They pulled the scaffolding back up and offered it to Ming. \"Ready?\"",
        "\"As I'll ever be,\" she said, putting one foot on the thing and securing herself to the chair. Part of her expected it to fall to the ground.",
        "\"I'll keep the line taunt so it doesn't swing out too fast.\" They grabbed another rope and handed it to Ming. \"Use this one to control your descent.",
        "\"Seems easy enough.\" Ming went to the edge of the building and looked over. Jerking her head back, she closed her eyes and thought of Colin Ferrell.",
        "\"I can do it!\" Keeping her eyes on Kat's smirk, she lowered herself to the first set of windows, mimed cleaning, and continued with the next floor. Afterward, she descended to the ground floor and sighed.",
        "\"I can feel a headache coming on. The pinkness is oppressive,\" she mumbled to herself. Rubbing the bridge of her nose, she climbed back up the stairs.",
        "Kat lowered Ming three more times for each set of windows on the first side. In the end, Ming was getting a headache. A small seed of pain was starting to dig in behind her eyes and exploding out from there. It was like staring at the computer screen for too long. The heat wasn't helping. She took out some aspirin and washed it down with cold coffee from her lunch, spitting out the dust.",
        "\"How did Bobby do all of the windows by himself?\" Ming asked Kat. \"Just lowering me takes about twenty minutes. And it's giving me a headache.\" She rubbed her shoulders, almost as if a presence had been staring over them all day. She shook her head. That was Dean's gut speaking, not her.",
        "\"Bobby was good at this job, and it usually only takes about four or five hours to do the whole building,\" Kat said, eating a sandwich. \"Bobby said the same thing about the pinkness, though. I like it. It's soothing.\" She reached into her pocket and pulled out a joint. \"Try this. I got it from my herbalist. It's great for headaches.\"",
        "Ming took the joint and twirled it around in her fingers. Shrugging, she had Kat light her up.",
        "\"This is the last side. Where the body was found,\" Ming said, rubbing the back of her head. She handed the joint back to Kat. \"I'm not going to hallucinate with that thing, am I?\"",
        "\"No, you should be fine. This stuff just gives you a nice buzz, like a cigarette, only safer.\" They took a hit, lighting up the paper. \"Oh, yeah. What happened to the body? The news said the police lost it,\" Kat set the scaffolding on the final side.",
        "\"They haven't found the body yet, but it'll turn up.\"",
        "\"Stupid,\" Kat scoffed. \"Why would anybody want to take a body?\"",
        "Ming got onto the scaffolding one last time and lowered herself to the window where Barbie was killed. \"This hole is in the exact center,\" she said, tracing the spiderwebs. They eventually reached the edge, radiating out from the middle in bigger and bigger circles. She stared at the pinkness, so much like the rest of the windows and leaned back. \"Nothing.\" She hit her palm with her fist. \"This was a fucking waste of time.\" Grumbling, she prepared to lower herself to the ground when the sunlight hit the window, reflecting off the pink. A small fleck of something peeked from the side, moving to the right. It was difficult to see, but Ming leaned forward. Nothing happened. She leaned back. Numbers and letters dug into her brain, sinking their claws and driving out all other thoughts. It changed her thoughts, bringing out new ideas and new worlds. Forcing herself away from the pink glass, she saw the destruction of the Strip. Buildings were gutted, and the road was in ruin. Craters filled the desert.",
        "Ming screamed, grabbed her head and slumped to the side.",
        "When she woke up, she was on the ground outside the Shujing. Kat was squatting over her, trying to get some water into her. \"You're awake. I was worried about you,\" they said. Kat was holding Ming's head, concern in their eyes.",
        "\"What happened?\"",
        "\"After you passed out, I had to lower you to the ground,\" they said, sticking their hand behind their head. \"I think the heat was getting to you. I was worried I'd have to call an ambulance, and I didn't know if you were insured.\"",
        "Two of Yichen's bodyguards stood next to them. Kat shrugged. \"They helped me get you out of the harness and brought everything down,\" they said, frowning. \"I don't think we can go back up there anymore.\"",
        "\"That's okay. I'm finished here,\" she said, holding her head and swaying to the right. \"It's probably the heat. Let's get back into the van. Chip's waiting for it, and I need to lie down.\" Ming got into the passenger's seat, turned on the air conditioner and closed her eyes while Kat loaded up the equipment. Between the refreshing coolness, the images of Vegas's destruction kept flashing behind her eyes. And the numbers. She could still see them, hovering there, just beyond her reach, but they were fading. She couldn't hold it in. She needed someone who understood computers to help her figure this out. If she saw whatever those numbers were in a broken piece of glass, what did Bobby see? She needed to find him. He might be able to explain what was going on."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "title": "Chapter 6",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "2:00 PM",
        "WHERE IS MY SHUJING STORY? I WANT IT BY 5 OR YOU'RE OUT OF A JOB.",
        "\"Useless piece of shit!\" Ming leaned forward and yelled at her computer screen. Her editor had just sent another all-caps message. She didn't have time for arrogant power trippers. Whatever happened to her at the hotel was still digging around in her mind, and she needed to take care of that first.",
        "After taking the window-washing truck back to Squeegees R Us and thanking Kat, Ming drove to Bobby's trailer park. Sitting in her car, she ran some time-travel, code-jumping scenarios through the AI programs. She needed to understand what she saw. Computer code doesn't just invade a person's mind. It stays on the screen and does ... computer stuff.",
        "\"Can you write a computer code that could cause bodies to disappear?\"",
        "-   Sorry, this function is unknown. ---",
        "Ming hit the side of her car seat. She didn't want to punch the computer. After the last time, her editor refused to supply a new laptop.",
        "\"Waste of space!\"",
        "\"Mother Fucker!\" she yelled at her phone and shoved it in her purse. \"What's up with you useless new AI programs?\" she asked the computer. \"Did somebody design you to screw up people's lives?\" She grumbled. \"I wouldn't put it past the FBI to piggyback on these things just to track down undesirables.\"",
        "Ming stared out the window. The Vegas sun was pounding down, and her AC was blasting her face. She tried again. \"Can you write a time travel program?\"",
        "-   Sorry, that is the realm of science fiction. Any program we write will be unable",
        "to perform such an act. If you have any other programming-related questions,",
        "please don't hesitate to ask. We are here to help. ---",
        "Ming pushed her computer away and closed her eyes. Numbers and letters were still flowing behind her eyes, but most of the understanding she had gained had faded. The destruction she saw was also gone. She couldn't grasp what any of it meant beyond the need to travel through time. Even then, she couldn't say why.",
        "She got out of her car and let the afternoon heat take her breath away. Coughing, she picked her way through the rubble of Bobby's home. Most of the big pieces had been hauled away, but there were still bits and pieces left to show her his life. A cracked Motley Crue commemorative plate, some CDs, mostly heavy metal, and one Best of Disney. She found a couple of computer programming books as well, but they had been badly burned and only covered the basics.",
        "She still had some numbers left, rattling around in her head, but she needed someone to connect the dots, and a basic programming language wasn't going to cut it. CSI had already bagged everything they could find, but that didn't mean they were perfect. They usually stick with the big stuff. She needed to dig into the small details.",
        "She waved her hand in front of her face to drive off the flies and get rid of a faint musk stinging her eyes. \"Damn bugs. Wish I'd brought some spray. Bobby must've had some kinky cologne,\" she mumbled, bending down to shift some of the dirt.",
        "After twenty minutes of shifting rocks, Ming stood up and stretched. \"Nothing. There's no way I'm too old for this yet. I'm not even breaking a sweat.\" Just shy of thirty-five, she was hitting her stride as a journalist, even if her private life wasn't going how she wanted it to. Her mother had been calling her 'over the hill' for the last ten years when she wasn't guilting her for being unmarried. When Ming reminded her that this was America and people didn't say they were useless after twenty-five, her mother just nodded and didn't stop. Her father continued to spend most of his time on business trips. She needed this win, even if only to show them she could do it.",
        "\"Hey! What are you doing in my house?\" a male voice said from her right.",
        "A man stood under the window of the next trailer. The ones around the destruction area had been emptied, and the residents were placed in a hotel until the exact cause of the destruction could be determined. However, he was glancing back and forth at the windows as if he was expecting someone to be there.",
        "He looked about forty, but his mullet made him seem older. He was still quite fit and handsome, in a cute, grungy kind of way. His Motley Crue T-shirt needed to be laundered, and he'd spilled coffee on his pants.",
        "\"Your house?\" The thought clicked instantly. \"That would make you Bobby Miladev then?\" Ming reached for her notebook in her back pocket.",
        "\"That's right,\" Bobby crossed his arms and glared at her. \"Now, what are the two of you doing in my house? Do you know how difficult it was to come back here? I had to make sure nobody was following me.\" He stopped and pointed to the right of Ming. \"Why are you acting like a superfan at a Crue signing?\"",
        "Ming raised an eyebrow and wrote a note in her book. \"Two? What are you talking about? I'm the only one here.\"",
        "Bobby pursed his lips and pointed to her right. \"I'm talking to the blonde in the pink clothes. I thought she died last night in the hotel room. Why are you even here? Do you know the trouble you caused me?\"",
        "\"There's nobody there,\" Ming said, pointing to her right. She waved her arm through the space he was pointing at, and his face turned white. \"The heat getting to you?\" It was about a hundred and four degrees (forty degrees Celsius) today, but still cool.",
        "\"Fuck!\" Bobby fell to his knees and pounded on the ground. \"I knew there was something fucked up going on in my head. I hate seeing ghosts! God damn you, Slazney! I was perfectly happy with the headaches!\"",
        "Slazney! That name. Ming perked up. *He knows his name*. \"You know a Mr. Slazney?\" she asked. She had to keep her voice steady, but there was a slight waver. Ming coughed and asked again, this time in a lower voice, her pencil twitching. \"Do you know Slazney?\"",
        "Bobby scoffed. \"Yeah. He gave me some chew that relaxed my brain a bit too much. The joke's on me, though. It's cost a lot more than the hundred bucks. When I went to his clinic last night to complain about the crap, it was closed. This morning as well.\"",
        "Ming clicked her tongue. \"A dead end,\" she hit her palm. But he'd met the man. Seen his face. She made a fist and did a fist pump. \"Yes!\"",
        "\"What?\"",
        "\"Nothing,\" she turned back to Bobby. \"You said you can see the woman who was killed at the Shujing, here?\"",
        "\"Yes. She's next to you, floating....\" Bobby closed his eyes and covered his face with his hands. Ming heard another' Fuck' come through his fingers. She wrote all of this down. He was drunk, maybe on something, hallucinating even, but this was still better than what she had before. There were no such things as ghosts.",
        "Rumours, on the other hand, could be just as powerful. She had a lot of experience with that when she exposed Dean's ex-wife. \"Why are you here?\"",
        "\"This was the last place I wanted to come, but I had no choice. I'm looking for the second tin of chew Slazney sent me. I gave the other stuff to Kat, and I don't want to get them involved.\"",
        "A cold chill went through Ming. \"Does she smoke it?\"",
        "Bobby nodded. \"They. I'm desperate and can't sleep. I'm hoping it could help me make sense of the code running through my brain.\"",
        "\"How so?\" Ming swallowed. Was he talking about the same code running through her brain as well?",
        "Bobby just ignored her and continued to search the ruins of his trailer.",
        "\"Why do you want it?\" This was Ming's chance. She had spent years trying to find out what Slazney wanted in Vegas. So far, she'd found only rumours and ghosts. Bobby was the first true lead she'd had.",
        "\"That's none of your business. The ghost agrees with me,\" he said, pointing to the space. \"What's her name anyway?\"",
        "\"Barbie,\" Ming answered, making some more notes. A loud \"Haw\" pierced the afternoon. He was holding his stomach, laughing. \"What's so funny?\"",
        "It took Bobby a few minutes to stop his hysterics. \"Nothing really,\" he said, wiping his eyes. \"I just thought she looked like one when I saw her outside the diner yesterday afternoon.\"",
        "\"You saw her before her death? Do you know what happened to her body?\"",
        "\"I don't know anything about a body,\" he said, waving his hands in the air. \"Have you seen the tin? Did it survive Ivan...\" Bobby trailed off",
        "Ming raised an eyebrow. \"The police have it.\" She pulled out her phone and showed him a picture.",
        "He took her phone and nodded. \"Dammit! I need it back. I can't focus. Every time I try, the block shuts me down, and I'm not going to sleep.\" He returned her phone and jerked back. \"Why are you angry?\"",
        "\"Who?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"Barbie.\" Bobby groaned. \"Who are you?\"",
        "She gave him her card, \"Ming Na Liu, Las Vegas Sun.\"",
        "\"A reporter,\" he grimaced and crushed her card. \"We're done here.\"",
        "\"Yes. But I can get you in touch with the detective in charge of the investigation.\" She let that news hang and watched as his face went from surprise to despair and back to indifference in the span of an eye-twitch.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ivan",
        "2:00",
        "Ivan watched the woman drive Petor away and pulled out his phone. He ran a search of her face and came up with a list of articles written by an up-and-coming Asian reporter. Scrolling through the list, he stopped on the oldest about a pharmacist and went back to a recent story about the detective seen on the news.",
        "Something about him being exonerated of spousal rape and murder. It had made the front page of the Tribune, and her name was on the byline. She wouldn't be after Petor for a small story. Ivan ran his finger across his flat nose and texted his boss. He started the car. He needed to wait another five hours or so before he could use his power again, but he could follow them.",
        "A newspaper with Petor's picture on it sat on the car seat of his rental. Ivan shook his head. A professional would have changed his face. It was getting harder to let him escape. The phone slid across it as a text blazed on the screen in Russian.",
        "\"Bring him to me!!\"",
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "4:00 PM",
        "Dean popped another piece of candy in his mouth and worked it between his teeth. He was trying to quit smoking and wasn't having much luck. Ming hated cigarettes. He was a little jittery without the nicotine, but the Japanese Hi-Chews helped. They tasted like real fruit, too. At first, he missed the chemical burn of Hubba Bubba, but now, who knew real sugar was better for you than that corn stuff?",
        "\"There's some Asian woman for you at reception,\" Starfield said. \"She's hot too. Are you moving on from us, Deanie-boy?\" The older officer joked. The two other officers with her joined in on the joke.",
        "\"Definitely, yes. There are so many more people politer than the trash in this room.\"",
        "She sneered and gave him the middle finger. He waved her away and shut his mouth before he said anything further. Why'd he always let his mouth lead? He should know better by now.",
        "His recorder wasn't on, and it needed to charge anyway. The last investigation had nearly destroyed him. Without Ming and Zacoski, he'd have been on the street. Risking his pension on another trumped-up charge, even with Lieutenant Zacoski here to back him up, wasn't worth it. The man's door was open, but he didn't know if he had heard anything. He was tired of having to walk on eggshells around people. His inner snark needed to come out from time to time.",
        "Ming was at the front desk. She looked good, even with a dirt smudge across her nose. It just added to her attraction. Coughing into his hand, he schooled his face to remain serious. He already gave her more than he should have. If she understood her effect on him, could he still trust her? His head was telling him it was already too late for that, but his gut was telling him to let go.",
        "\"What can I do for you, Miss Liu?\" he asked.",
        "\"Miss Liu, is it? I thought we were closer than family names, Lifante?\" She crossed her arms and pouted. \"Why so professional today?\"",
        "Dean bent forward and whispered. \"This is my workplace, and they are giving me a hard time. I don't want to provide them with any more ammunition.\"",
        "Nodding, she continued. \"Detective Lifante. I have someone who wants to talk to you.\"",
        "Leaning back, he pointed inside the precinct. \"Let's talk inside.\"",
        "She turned to the man beside her and nudged him forward. \"This is Bobby. The window washer you've been looking for. He's got something to tell you, and you need to listen.\"",
        "Dean looked at the man for the first time. Sizing him up, a feeling in his gut told him to be careful. Bobby was dangerous, but not deadly, though. Dean's instinct never gave him specifics, but he learned how to tell when someone wanted to point a gun at him.",
        "This Bobby was about thirty, maybe forty, in good shape under his ratty Motley Crue T-shirt. He needed a shave, but he had a rugged look many women fell for. Dean didn't trust him instantly, but he couldn't tell if it was a personal or an instinctual distrust. When Ming placed her hand on Bobby's arm and led him into the precinct, he realized it was jealousy. He forced the feelings down and put on his professional mask. This was not the time.",
        "*She probably smelled the story here. Ming would do almost anything to get the scoop.* His stomach was acting up. Going to his desk, he popped some antacids and shoved the bottle into his pocket.",
        "Closing the door to the conference room, Dean wished he'd chosen the interrogation room, but it was too late now. Glaring at Bobby, he sat down, pulled out a notebook and clicked a pen.",
        "He needed to calm down. Jealousy wasn't going to win him any points in Ming's eyes. According to the background check he'd done, she'd left her last boyfriend because he couldn't stand her job. Anything that interfered with her choices turned her off.",
        "The background check left a small kernel of guilt in his stomach, but he needed to know why she was willing to help him when she wrote the article about his case. Trust was still hard for him, but she had worked her way in. However, why hadn't she told him they had lived in the same building? He tried to remember if they had crossed paths, but he couldn't recall anything. The little secrets she still had pulled at him, but not as much as they would have a few years ago. She'd proven herself to him several times over. Without her, he'd be locked in prison, facing the next few years as someone's toy. He owed her.",
        "Dean faced Bobby and Ming across the table. He would trust her judgment. It had never steered him wrong.",
        "\"You are Bobby Miladev, the one cleaning the Shujing hotel last night?\" He put his pen on the paper and waited.",
        "\"Yes, but I had nothing to do with her death. She was dead when I got to her room window.\"",
        "\"Take it easy, Mr. Miladev. We don't suspect you of her death. We know you were outside the building the whole time. We have video proof of that. We just want to know what you saw.\" He paused. \"Do you mind if I record this interview?\" Dean asked, laying his phone and a charging cord on the table.",
        "\"Do you have to?\" Bobby fidgeted. He kept playing with his T-shirt. Dean glanced at Ming. She was writing in her notebook.",
        "\"It would make things easier.\"",
        "Bobby sighed and reached into his wallet. He pulled out a business card and put it face down on the table. He grabbed a pen and wrote a number on the back. \"Before we talk about anything, please call this number on the other side. He might still be on vacation; if so, try this number on the back. It should confirm some things about me.\"",
        "Dean picked up the card, raised an eyebrow and called the numbers. Both times, he got a voicemail box. Hanging up the phone, he asked Bobby, \"How do I know this is legit? I couldn't reach either of them.\"",
        "\"You don't. But I need you to stop searching for me and get my name off the TV news. The people after me already destroyed my home because of that story, and Ivan's probably tracking me now. Ryan will be able to fill in everything when he gets back. If he can't, I guess this Wilson should.\"",
        "\"Ivan?\" Dean asked, raising an eyebrow. Bobby was silent.",
        "Ming glared at Dean. She was clenching her jaw.",
        "\"How much have you told Miss Liu here?\" he asked Bobby.",
        "\"She knows someone is after me, and she saw what I did at the hotel,\" he said. Dean couldn't detect any Russian accent from him. \"According to what she said in the car ride over here, she's involved now. I can speak freely, as long as it's not recorded.\"",
        "Dean put his recorder back in his pocket, but he didn't turn it off. There should be enough power for a few minutes. He still didn't trust the man. \"I won't ask why you're in witness protection, Mr. Miladev, but I need to know what you saw.\" Dean peeked at Ming. Her eyes softened, and she jerked her head back to Bobby. \"I promise to keep your name and picture out of the news.\"",
        "A pencil snapped.",
        "\"Sorry. Was pushing too hard,\" Ming said as she got another one from her bag. She hated anybody who tried to silence the news.",
        "\"Yes. Get my picture out of the paper. I don't want anybody else to see it,\" Bobby said.",
        "\"Your best bet is to ask Ming. She has better connections than I, but I'll do what I can. No promises, though.\" Dean turned to a fresh page. \"Tell me everything.\"",
        "Bobby told them he went to Slazney's place, though he called it Stanley's, and got a tin of chew. \"I had hoped it would stop that. Instead, I've just created a bigger one.\" He took a sip of water. \"When I looked at the Shujin windows under the right sunlight, with an open mind, I saw something that shouldn't have been there. I panicked. Then, I noticed the woman sprawled on the bed, blood everywhere. I tried to break the glass and get to her, but the window was too strong. But that wasn't the biggest problem.\"",
        "\"What was it?\" Ming asked, placing her hand on his.",
        "A pen snapped.",
        "\"Sorry. Was holding it too tight.\" Dean grabbed a new pen and continued writing. \"Please continue.\"",
        "\"The biggest problem was the computer code embedded in the window. Like I said, when I looked at that pink thing, the sunlight must of triggered the program. I ran into the same code years ago, but I never would have expected to meet it here. I'd been fighting it for years, but it forced its way into my mind, like a songworm.\"",
        "Dean stopped writing. \"A computer code? Floating? What do you mean? How did it get into the window? Can you explain what you mean?\"",
        "Bobby wiped his face and started rubbing his eyes. \"I'm so tired. I can't tell you much about the code or how it got in there, except that it exists. It was too dangerous with the power to alter reality and make any dream you want real, so I blocked my ability to use it. When used, you have to pay a price, not just in energy. The cost is proportional to the thing you want. If you try and force it to do something unnatural, the rebound could take everything you love, shifting reality in the process. Most of the details are still vague, but it's becoming clearer by the hour. It's the reason Ivan killed my brother and why I'm in hiding in witness protection.\"",
        "\"This is a lot to take in, and your explanation is very confusing, Mr. Miladev.\"",
        "\"He's telling the truth, Dean. I went back to the Shujing and recreated Bobby's day. When I got to Barbie's room, the window was still broken, but something ran through my brain, I saw Vegas destroyed, and I passed out.\"",
        "\"Are you okay?\"",
        "\"Yes.\" Ming tucked a loose lock of hair behind her ears. \"The code didn't stay in my head, but I still have vague impressions of it. On the way here, Bobby asked me a few questions about it, and I couldn't answer. However, I have no coding experience whatsoever.\"",
        "Dean stood up, breathing out in relief. He couldn't believe a word this wannabe roadie was telling him, but his instincts were screaming to trust Ming. Dean turned to Bobby. \"Is that all, Mr. Miladev?\" He tried to keep the frustration out of his voice but could only disguise it with a cough. \"How did Ming see this code, if it's so dangerous?\"",
        "\"Anybody could do it if they met the right conditions. The constant headaches I felt were probably my subconscious working overtime, but it couldn't break through my blocks. I wouldn't be surprised if the code was in more windows, but needed a stacked effect to be activated. Pink also seems to be the key. To fix everything, I need to be able to work with the code already in my head, write it out.\" Bobby said, taking another sip of water. \"There's still a block in there stopping me from fully accessing the knowledge I need, and it's threatening to come out when I fall asleep. That scares the crap outta me.\"",
        "Bobby was swaying in the seat. He almost fell over twice but caught himself on the edge of the table. \"Stop getting angry at me!\" He shouted to the air next to Ming.",
        "\"It's evidence in the case,\" said Dean, crossing his arms.",
        "\"Please,\" Bobby begged. \"I can't find Slazney, and if I drag Kat into this, Ivan'll kill them just to find me. I need to know what's happening here and who this ghost is floating next to your head.\"",
        "\"Ghost?\" Dean mouthed.",
        "Ming shook her head.",
        "\"If I can work on the code, I can finish it, and then I can block it out again, get back to hiding and sleep.\"",
        "\"I'm not sure I can do that,\" Dean said.",
        "Ming narrowed her eyes and looked at Dean, \"I'm calling in that favour you owe me, Lifante.\"",
        "There was steel in her voice. She was serious if she was calling in that mark over this. All of his instincts were telling him to trust her while saying that this man wasn't to be trusted, \"All right. Wait here. I'll go get it.\" He ground his teeth again. If this kept up, he'd need a dentist soon."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "title": "Chapter 7",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "5:00 PM",
        "Bobby watched the detective leave the room and chortled. Could he be any clearer? \"*He wants to jump the reporter, doesn't he?\"*",
        "Barbie's ghost agreed; she'd been making kissy faces at the two of them since he sat down.",
        "*\"I know. Why doesn't he just ask her out?\"* he said to the ghost in Russian.",
        "She giggled. He wished he could hear her. *When did I find talking to ghosts to be normal?* He narrowed his eyes. \"*I've met you before, haven't I?*\"",
        "Barbie's eyes widened, and she nodded her head so fast she spun around in a circle.",
        "\"You're speaking Russian, right? Who are you talking to?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"Barbie,\" Bobby said. \"As I told you before, she's floating right next to you.\"",
        "\"Right,\" said Ming as she flipped a page in her notebook and wrote another note.",
        "*\"Can you show her?\"* Bobby asked.",
        "Barbie started tapping her lips and made a lightbulb over her head pose.",
        "With an exaggerated eyeroll, Bobby sighed, sat back and started rubbing his eyes. The light in this room was too dim, and the coffee was wearing off. He needed sleep. After drifting off a few minutes earlier, the room had turned into a zombie playground, complete with a pair of flesh-eating monsters.",
        "\"What the Hell?\" The temperature in the room dropped five degrees.",
        "Bobby opened his eyes just as Ming waved her hand in the air where Barbie was and smirked, \"Told you.\"",
        "Ming's eyes were the size of beef buns, and she was trembling. \"You've been seeing this for the last hour now? How did she do that? Why couldn't I see her before?\"",
        "\"Don't know. You saw the code in the window, but it was broken, right?\"",
        "Ming nodded.",
        "\"Probably only got a partial download. Saved your life, I would bet. However, she can manipulate her code, but I can't hear a word she says. She's pretty good at pantomime, though.\"",
        "\"Why didn't she show me when we first met?\"",
        "\"Beats the hell outta me. Besides, I've been seeing a lot of screwed-up things every time I fall asleep, and I figured Barbie was just another hallucination,\" replied Bobby as he shoved a fist in his mouth to stifle a yawn. \"A freaking scary one.\"",
        "Barbie stuck out her tongue at him. She looked so much like Vlad. She even did the same things as his twin brother. No. It was impossible. Vlad hated women. She might have been a double.",
        "\"What kind of visions?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"Death, destruction, you name it,\" Bobby replied with a bigger yawn. Hell, just a moment ago I was seeing you as a zombie wanting to suck out my brains.\" He yawned.",
        "\"Really. I saw something similar after seeing the numbers,\" Ming said. \"It's mostly gone now.\" She turned to where Barbie was. \"I don't think I'd believe in a ghost, though,\" she muttered.",
        "\"Really?\" Bobby scratched his head. \"Are you sure you have no coding experience?\" he asked Ming.",
        "She shook her head. \"The only thing I've ever used is the AI program on my computer, but that's the extent of my computer skills.",
        "Bobby clicked his tongue. \"I wish I had never seen it. The sooner I get the code finished, the sooner I can figure out what's wrong and get it out. It's like a songworm that just gets lodged up in there and won't let go.\"",
        "\"What's this about worms?\" Dean asked, opening the door. A scowl disappeared from his face, but not quickly enough. Bobby noticed the hint remaining.",
        "\"Bobby was just telling me about the visions he's been seeing,\" Ming started. \"I also saw the woman who died and disappeared, so to speak.\"",
        "\"If he knows, why hasn't he told me?\" asked the detective, turning to Bobby, his voice moving to the \"I'm getting ready to shoot you\" tone.",
        "\"Stow the jealousy, Detective. I like my women with a bit more meat to them. Reporter's too skinny for me,\" Bobby interjected.",
        "Ignoring the sharp intake of breath from the reporter, Bobby turned to Barbie. \"Can you show him too?\"",
        "Barbie tapped her nose and puffed out her cheeks. The temperature dropped another ten degrees, and Bobby started rubbing his arms.",
        "Dean scowled, but looked around the room. \"Am I supposed to see something?\"",
        "\"I can. You were supposed to see Barbie,\" Ming said. \"I guess it doesn't work that way for everybody.\" She rubbed her eyes. \"I haven't slept well in three days. That could explain it.\"",
        "\"This is a trick, isn't it?\"",
        "\"I wish. Did you bring the tin?\" Bobby asked. Reaching down, he pulled out his laptop from his bag and plugged it in. Opening it to a program running the computer code. Bobby wrinkled his nose at the trash.",
        "\"This is shit,\" he muttered.",
        "The reporter leaned over Bobby's shoulder. \"I recognize some of this. The numbers and letters, but this. What is this?\" She pointed to an empty section of code on the screen.",
        "\"That's where the lyrics from the Crue are inserted,\" Bobby said, running his hands through his hair and wiping them on his pants. \"I think. I'm not sure. Music is necessary for my code. You can create magic without Heavy Metal, but you need the right vibe to make most magic work. Without the correct sound and syntax that works for the user in the operation, all you get is gibberish.\"",
        "\"You know this, how?\" Ming asked. \"What does this code do?\"",
        "\"I learned it in Russia, by accident. I kinda stumbled on it. Anybody can use magic, and most people touch the edges of it all the time,\" said Bobby.",
        "Ming raised an eyebrow and pursed her lips. \"Magic?\"",
        "Bobby sighed. \"Think of it like this: when you have a flash of insight or a hunch of inspiration, you're brushing up against the boundaries of magic. That connects you to the natural power that governs this world. Experts in all fields can access the tiny sliver of the barest part available to them, naturally. Some call it a gift or an innate talent.\"",
        "\"Kind of like Dean's gut feelings,\" Ming said, writing in her notebook.",
        "Dean snorted.",
        "\"I guess so.\" Bobby shrugged. \"As for what my code does, well, while I'm not a hundred percent sure, I believe it allows me to bypass nature and hack the system. Theoretically, it should allow me to control time and space, travel through time, warp reality, give the pretty boy a third nipple. Pretty much anything I want, if I'm willing to pay the price. That varies, and it may not be me who pays. One thing you have to understand is that nature is vindictive and will as soon crush your balls as give you a hug.\"",
        "Ming was silent for a moment. \"Time travel?\" She scoffed.",
        "Bobby nodded.",
        "\"A third nipple?\" Dean scoffed and handed Bobby the evidence bag with the tin of chew.",
        "Bobby opened it up and raised an eyebrow. \"It isn't damaged? How? Ivan totalled everything else.\"",
        "\"That's why we bagged it,\" Dean said as he crossed his arms and narrowed his eyes. \"What do you mean by Ivan?\"",
        "Bobby ignored the question. That was a conversation best avoided.",
        "\"Why is tobacco chew necessary?\" Dean asked. \"We've tested it, by the way. It's standard tobacco.\"",
        "\"It's not. I've been trying to recreate the code all day, but I've got a mental block stopping me from remembering how. I've got to lower my defences, and this chew helped me do that earlier.\"",
        "\"What do you mean, code?\" Dean raised an eyebrow.",
        "\"Before I saw the dead woman, a special code in the window tried to take over my mind and body,\" Bobby said, trying to keep his voice light. The Detective already thought he was Loony Tunes on crack. \"Before whatever was in the window could infect me further, the pink piece of shit blew itself out and dumped me off the bosun chair.\" He scratched his chin, \"That saved me, maybe?\"",
        "Barbie was wagging her finger at him. She kept miming sleep, but there was no way Bobby was giving in to that. One zombie dream was enough.",
        "Wincing at the smell, he took a small wad of the chew and placed it in his cheek. Ming giggled, and he could swear the detective stifled a cough, \"I know it smells like a donkey's asshole. Give me a moment.\" The stress from the last few hours didn't move. It stayed in a ball right behind his right eye, but he could sense his eyes opening. As he focused and took a deep breath, the code imposed itself on the screen. He sighed in relief. It had been a long shot.",
        "The code was fluid. When he tried to force the Crue into the structure he wrote earlier, it fell flat. The part of him still behind the block knew he needed more than just music, but he couldn't focus on why. If he had more written down, maybe. \"I knew it. The code was there, I just forgot how to write it... Bloody hell, it will work.\"",
        "\"That's great,\" Ming said. \"You sounded unsure.\"",
        "\"My initial attempt was messy and crude. There were so many bugs in it that I could easily imagine my old computer teacher punting my testicles across the room after caressing them with his steel-toed hiking boots.\"",
        "\"Watch the language, Rocker-Boy,\" Dean grumbled.",
        "\"When I got home, I realized I was seeing the same code I had created years ago, but never perfected. It had slowly been eroding my blocks...\" he trailed off. Something was missing from that statement --- something dangerous. He couldn't put it into words, but he was sure the original code had been finished; he'd just removed his ability to write it. Not only did he remember using it, but he also remembered deleting it after the American had rescued him from Gregory. Why had he never tried to recreate the code? For the first time in three years, he regrated putting the blocks in. The code was speaking to him, like a junkie looking for a fix.",
        "Bobby drifted off as the coding took over. His fingers flew across the keyboard, pulling numbers and applications from the depths of his memory. This was fun. He could do without the crap in his cheek, but he hadn't created code like this since coming to America. He'd missed this. His everyday life was okay, even if his job sucked a donkey's ass in a vacuum cleaner. Now his life was all about not sticking out and getting sucked dry, and doing the job assigned to him. Keeping his head down, well and truly out of Gregory's sight. Why did he never use this code to rewrite that relationship?",
        "Why did that very idea fill him with dread?",
        "No matter. It was relaxing to create again.",
        "\"I'm putting this into the drive.\" He held up a CD from his computer bag. \"If you don't like it, go away.\" He put the CD in and hit play. \"Gimme Chocolate!!\" filled the room, pounding the speakers and drawing stares from the passersby. Both Dean and Ming covered their ears.",
        "\"Wrong CD,\" he mumbled, popping it out and grabbing another one from his bag. Crue's \"Home Sweet Home\" soon replaced it. \"*I'm going to listen to that one later*,\" he said in Russian. \"*It had a good beat*.\"",
        "The music drowned out the clack of Bobby's fingers typing on the keyboard. The melody filled the room, bringing an energy missing from his earlier efforts. The other two disappeared. Barbie waved and faded out. His tiredness vanished, like the effect of a dozen cups of coffee fighting against the dim light.",
        "The computer screen filled his whole consciousness. He continued to work, filling line after line. Unlike before, the uniqueness spoke to him. It wasn't a Python script, though it had a basic similarity. There was a touch of SQL for the data aspect. He found himself falling into the code, the beauty of it washing over him.",
        "\"Bobby,\" he heard a voice through the fog. It sounded like a woman. He ignored it and continued diving, pushing everything out. The deeper he got, the more intricate it became. The blocks dissolved faster, and memories flooded back. The code itself was like combining Swift from the fruit company and Go from Google if those two didn't hate each other and allowed their code to work together. It was mixed with a raw primal language in the music that required an output of some kind. It was creating something new.",
        "He was creating nature. That was it. He was writing an algorithm for nature.",
        "\"Bobby!\" Was that Sasha's voice? It'd been so long. What had happened to her? Why did Barbie resemble her around the eyes? He misted up there and almost lost the code. The dim light from the room intruded, and he could smell Coke.",
        "He shook his head and continued coding, taking a sip of the cola someone had left. The chemical burn in the bubbles drove him forward, pushing him back into the code. He was getting to the end of the sequence. One or two more lines and he was done. He couldn't tell exactly what the code was going to do, but he needed to find out.",
        "\"Bobby!\" someone was shaking him, pulling him away from the computer.",
        "\"I was almost finished!\" He yelled at the detective. The sudden light shot deep into his eyes, blinding him. He winced and knuckled the burning sensation out.",
        "\"It's been three hours,\" Dean said. His hands were on his hips, showing his gun. \"Everybody's gone home.\"",
        "Bobby looked around. The reporter was curled up on the couch, drooling; the precinct was dark outside the room. 'Gimme Chocolate' was echoing from his speakers. \"When did I put Baby Metal in?\" he said, scratching his head.",
        "\"Sorry,\" Bobby said, messing up his hair and muting the CD. \"I got lost in the code. It'd been so long.\"",
        "\"Are you finished?\" Dean asked.",
        "\"Yes. Just one last piece to input.\" Bobby sat at the computer and started typing again. He rubbed his eyes and pushed the tin of chew away from the computer. Other than the small wad from earlier, it was still almost full. \"I'm done with that dross. You can have it back.\"",
        "\"Really? I thought it was important?\" Dean said.",
        "\"Only to force me to move past the block and get the code out of my brain.\"",
        "The Detective scratched his head.",
        "\"I had all of my memories locked away behind something, like a firewall,\" he trailed off again. He was missing a piece of information.",
        "Shaking his head, he continued. \"The block's mostly gone now. The chew helped bring out the hidden code embedded in me. Now that whatever was in the window is in the computer, I can see the connection.\"",
        "\"You know this, how?\" Dean asked.",
        "Bobby paused, opening and closing his mouth. \"I don't know, detective. I just do.\" He looked up at Dean. \"It's as if my instinct is telling me I'm right. I can't explain it.\"",
        "Dean grimaced but picked up the tin and plopped it back into the evidence bag. He went over to Ming and shook her shoulder to wake her up.",
        "Snorting, she opened her eyes and stretched. Dean turned away.",
        "\"Look at her, detective. If she were Russian, she'd want you to stare,\" Bobby said, typing the last bit of code. \"Although reporter, you might want to wipe your chin first.\"",
        "She used her sleeve and stood up. \"What's happening?\" She didn't look at Dean.",
        "\"Mr. Motley Crue here says he's finished the code,\" Dean said, not looking at her.",
        "\"You can get it on here. I don't mind watching,\" Bobby said, smiling. \"And done!\" he hit the last keystroke and typed 'execute'.",
        "Nothing happened.",
        "They waited. Ming looked around the room and shrugged.",
        "Bobby scrolled through the code. Ten minutes later, he looked up. \"Here it is. A period's in the wrong place.\" He hit 'execute' again.",
        "There was a slight power surge and a bright light, but still, nothing happened.",
        "\"Okay? Was this supposed to be more dramatic?\" Dean said.",
        "\"I don't get it?\" Bobby checked the code again. \"Maybe I mixed up a backslash with an apostrophe; they looked so similar, it's easy to screw them up. This could take me a few hours.\" He stuck out a tongue and started scrolling.",
        "The detective threw up his hands and went to the vending machine in the corner. The reporter checked her phone and winced.",
        "Suddenly, the door burst open. Dean spun and pulled his gun from his holster. A beautiful naked girl with long curly blond hair stumbled into the room, \"Thank you, Maker, for bringing me out of my ghost form. I knew planting my anti-virus in you would do the trick and override the block, but you should've just gone to sleep. It would've made this a whole lot easier if the anti-virus had rewritten your prefrontal cortex.\" She shrugged. \"Thank Goddess you had the Baby Metal CD as well. Their rhythm meshes well with Crue's and jives with my soul, and I prayed you'd recognize their sound.\"",
        "\"You? How the fuck aren't you dead?\" Bobby yelled, knocking over the chair. \"I saw your body. You were a bloody ghost!\"",
        "\"I just shifted myself out of sync, that is all,\" she said, shrugging. \"You're not done yet, Maker. The other virus, the bad one, is still inside you. You should just go to sleep. It would've rewritten everything.\"",
        "\"And bring out the zombies!\"",
        "\"Fine! If you won't sleep, I can show you what to do to overwrite it, so I don't have to kill you right away. Then you have to make a choice.\" She pouted.",
        "\"A choice?\"",
        "\"Well, we can either get it out of you and send me home, or you can come with me. I still might have to kill you.\"",
        "She smiled at Dean and bowed, \"Thank you for bringing my blood here, Mr. Detective, sir, but could you get me some clothes? Please? My nipples are standing up, and I don't have enough nanites left to recreate my clothes like last time.\"",
        "Ming elbowed Dean in the gut."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "title": "Chapter 8",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "8:00 PM",
        "Dean stared at the blonde woman. His murder victim was sitting in a blue LVPD sweatshirt and pants, drinking coffee with two hands. She called herself Barbie and matched the ID from the crime scene.",
        "\"Ahh! This is delicious.\" She smacked her lips. \"After the destruction of the coffee plant in twenty-three thirty-seven from the blight, all we had to drink was the fake version prepackaged in the New York factory slums.\" She opened her eyes wide and stuck her hand on her mouth. \"Oops. My Handler told me I shouldn't reveal too much about the future. Butterflies, you know. I wouldn't want anybody to become a dictator.\"",
        "\"I don't think you have to worry about that,\" Dean said, narrowing his eyes. \"Three hundred years is a long way away.\"",
        "\"That's right. Thank you, Detective. You're so helpful.\" Barbie giggled and looked at her fingers. \"You'd think I wouldn't be cold as a ghost, but I was. My nanites took in as much heat as possible to keep me in that state, but thanks to the Maker reenergizing my body, I have another twenty-four-hour window.\" She wrapped her fingers around the cup. \"This is perfect for warming them up.\"",
        "Dean just nodded. After the initial shock wore off, he just watched her. So did Ming. \"She looks like the woman they said they found in the Shujing,\" he whispered, \"but that's impossible. Her throat was slit. We have the knife.\"",
        "Bobby was passed out on the couch. Barbie had tried to wake him, but after doing something with his computer and muttering about it not rewriting his brain, he just mumbled that the Zombies could eat him later and flipped over.",
        "\"Why is the Maker like this? I know he's still recovering from the viral infection that this Slazney gave him, but I need him to finish the code so I can get home. I'd do it myself, but I promised my Handler I wouldn't touch the code unless I had to. Just setting the counter virus was risky enough. The last time I coded on my own, I set off a volcano.\" She looked sheepish.",
        "\"I see.\" Ming nodded. There was no way she would believe that. \"Where is this home?\" Ming said, opening her notebook to a new page.",
        "\"Ming Na Liu, is it?\" Barbie asked.",
        "Ming nodded.",
        "Dean moved to the corner and unplugged his recorder from the wall socket. The power was full, and he needed a better vantage point to continue recording. Whatever she was saying was crazy, and he needed to stay as far away as possible, but without a record of this, there was no way Zacoski would believe anything. Hell, he had a hard time believing it. He was taking a lot on faith here. If he didn't owe Ming his life, he'd have locked everybody up and gone home.",
        "\"Home is Greater Vegas. After the death of the Strip and the inundation of San Angelus, Greater Vegas became the capital of the Western States,\" Barbie said. \"Of course, that won't happen for another two hundred years or so.\" She took another sip of her coffee and sighed in pleasure.",
        "\"Of course,\" Dean said, rolling his eyes.",
        "Ming shushed him. \"And this code? Bobby said it controls time and space. Is that true?\" Ming asked.",
        "Dean chuckled and shook his head. There was no way she would believe that story, and the skepticism in her voice agreed with him. She was always the most rational of the two.",
        "Barbie smiled and closed her eyes. \"It's beauty in motion. With it, a person can control nature, travel anywhere, recreating reality to fit their desire, within limits, of course. The cost is quite high, but its perfection allowed man to colonize the stars, bypassing the inherent limits in nature. In the wrong hands, it could wipe out all of humanity, but you could say the same about the bombs in this era. That's why the code is strictly controlled. Only licensed users are allowed to manipulate it. If they tried to alter too much, the consequences would be a big pile of doo-doo.\"",
        "\"What are the consequences?\" Dean asked. \"You also said there was a cost.\"",
        "\"Well, it's hard to form new memories, but that's just a side effect. The highest cost was the ocean. We're still recovering from that one.\"",
        "\"The ocean?\"",
        "\"Un-huh. A missed subroutine in the code to clear San Angelous sent half the world's water to Mars and fried three dozen cloned coders. The Maker shut most of the independent factories down after that.\"",
        "Dean blinked and glanced at Ming.",
        "\"I remember seeing it in the window as well,\" Ming said. \"Do you have to kill me?\" she joked.",
        "\"No. You only got a small dose of the activated code. Besides, your brain doesn't work as well as the Maker's.\" Barbie took another sip of coffee and pursed her lips, \"He understands it on instinct. You'd need to train yourself for years to match his true level.\" She pointed at Bobby, \"This Maker here is still a novice, and he's made too many mistakes. Even now, he's still not fully open. If only he'd have let me remove the blocks. I still think I'll need to take him with me before real damage is done.\"",
        "\"Your story is very cute, but how do you expect us to believe a word you're saying?\" Dean asked, standing up and moving to the window. \"The time travel thing is a bit too science fiction.\" He turned around and narrowed his eyes at Ming, gesturing with his head to get away from the crazy girl.",
        "Ming glared at him, pointed her finger, and slowly brought it and her thumb together. Dean knew when to shut up if he wanted to keep his insides on the inside and not decorating the floor. Whenever she found a story, it was like an addict lost in front of a slot machine with a mountain of quarters. For Ming, he was willing to humour the strange blond.",
        "Barbie stared at him, cocking her head to the side.",
        "Dean stared back, meeting her eyes with his glare. She was beautiful, in a Hollywood AI dream kind of way, but like those dreams, Dean couldn't quite explain what was wrong with it.",
        "The problem was all of his instincts were telling him she was on the level, but that couldn't be possible. Time travel? Coming back from the dead? This was pulp fiction stuff.",
        "\"While we're waiting for the Maker to wake up, do you two want to have sex?\" Barbie asked Dean and Ming. \"I can join you? I've never had a threesome with a Macho Man and a MILF before.\" She tilted her head and smiled.",
        "Dean gulped his coffee, spilling some of it on his tie.",
        "A pencil snapped to his right.",
        "\"What's wrong?\" Barbie asked. \"Oh, is this some sort of taboo? Sorry. I studied up on all the twenty-first-century customs and learned all the lingo to blend in better if I had to, but I guess I missed some. I didn't mean to step in on your courtship. You want each other, don't you? Or am I misreading the signs? You've been gazing at each other all night, and when I watched you sleep for those few hours last night, you said his name, so I just assumed.\" Her face turned red. \"Psychology was never my strong suit.\"",
        "Dean coughed and got a towel to clean up the coffee and hide his red face. He was excited to hear that Ming was dreaming about him, but a relationship was something he wasn't ready for, yet. He snuck a glance at her, but she was being too professional and ignoring him for his instincts to get a good read on her. Dean narrowed his eyes. That usually meant a person was hiding something. How did Ming feel about him?",
        "\"You mentioned a Slazney,\" Ming said, changing the subject, \"Could you tell me more? How long have you known about him?\" Ming asked, writing notes in her book.",
        "Dean let out a sigh of relief mixed with a small pang of regret filling his gut.",
        "Barbie put her hands on her chin and made a pouty face. \"I'd say about three years, give or take several hundred. I didn't know his name, but based on what I heard the old Asian man say, he was probably the guy my people were looking for. He's been in this time for about thirty of your years, causing mischief. I think he arrived after some buggy guy started Vegas.\"",
        "\"You're talking about Bugsy Siegel. The mobster died in 1947. Has Slazney been here since then?\" Ming raised an eyebrow. Her pencil flew across the page.",
        "Dean shook his head and scoffed.",
        "\"I'm not sure. My Handler didn't tell me,\" Barbie said. \"Why are you so angry?\" she asked, but Ming didn't answer Barbie. Shrugging her shoulders, Barbie continued. \"Anyway. I believe Slazney was the thief of the Maker's will. We think he stole the computer code that would allow someone to reshape reality, along with travelling in time, but it fractured. We've recorded instances of him throughout the timeline of unstable jumps, and that really messes up nature. When that happens, nature gets all prissy.\"",
        "\"How so?\" Dean asked.",
        "\"Slazney uses it to inhabit recently deceased bodies. That's the only way time travel works for most people. We don't know exactly when or who he jumped into, but we have to stop him, or you might get an apocalypse. That's why I'm here. It's too early to activate the Maker, yet.\"",
        "\"You mean your body is dead?\" Dean asked, drawing back.",
        "\"Of course,\" Barbie said. \"Sort of. I'm special. My handler says I can reassemble any dead body from a small scrap, shaping it any which way I want.\" She pointed to herself. \"I picked it up a few days ago from a plot of land in the desert and repaired the necrotic tissue. She'd been chopped into pieces, and I had to reconstruct some of the bones. It should hold together for a few weeks or so.\" She held out her hand. \"Sorry, I don't know who killed her.\"",
        "Dean mumbled under his breath as he flipped through his notebook. \"That explains the UNLV connection.\"",
        "\"Why are you here?\" Ming asked. Her pencil was moving fast across the page.",
        "\"We're trying to save the world from the end of days. You saw it, didn't you?\" Barbie asked Ming.",
        "\"Why are you rolling your eyes, Miss Reporter? I'm speaking the truth.\" Barbie frowned and pursed her lips. \"The Maker's the only one who can do that, but he's not ready yet. Untrained, he'll destroy the world as easily as he would save it. Once he completes the formula to get me home, that is. I can't stay here, but maybe he'll come with me. This place has no TacoBucks, and he'd love it.\" She nocked her head back and drained the cup, holding it with both hands. \"Can I have another one?\"",
        "Dean put down his coffee and leaned on the table, while Ming poured Barbie another cup. He held up the UNLV student ID he'd downloaded, comparing it to Barbie's face to make sure and shook his head. \"The picture's grainy, and she's not a blond. I can see the resemblance, though. What do you think? Are you buying this story, 'cause I'm not.\"",
        "\"This is far out there. Are you sure this is the dead woman?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"Yes. She matches all the records we have on her. I'd have to ask Jeremy to confirm, but I think he's still in the psych ward.\" He turned to the woman. \"I'm sorry, but I don't believe you're a time traveller. I'm going to keep you here until you can get a mental evaluation.\"",
        "\"That's fine. I thought you'd mistrust me,\" she took another sip and sighed. \"I don't mean you any harm. I may need your help.\"",
        "\"Our help?\" Dean asked. \"What do you mean?\"",
        "\"I don't think you'll believe anything I say at this point. Maybe you'll believe him,\" Barbie said, pointing to the door. \"I saw him sneaking outside when I was getting my body back.\"",
        "Suddenly, the lights in the precinct shut off. \"There's no storm tonight,\" said Dean. \"Someone could be here.\"",
        "Ming and Dean exchanged a weary glance. Ming grabbed her phone and turned on the flashlight. Dean pulled out his gun and kicked the sofa where Bobby was sleeping. Dean was alone, and another presence could help.",
        "Bobby snorted and fell off, smacking his ass on the ground. \"What the hell was that for? The zombies were finally gone?\" he said, rubbing his eyes.",
        "The front door to the conference room opened, and Ming shone the flashlight on a tall man, built like a mountain. He dominated the doorway and glared into the light.",
        "\"Ivan!\" Bobby yelled as he shrank back and fell over, crab-walking on the floor.",
        "\"Freeze! Hands in the air!\" Dean shouted, raising his gun at the big man. \"This is the guy you were talking about?\" he asked Bobby, not taking his eyes off Ivan. He wasn't expecting someone so overpowering. He filled out every Russian stereotype imaginable.",
        "Ivan ignored Dean and went straight for Bobby. He ducked under the big man's hand and crawled under the table.",
        "\"Shoot him!\" Bobby yelled.",
        "\"I said don't move!\" Dean repeated.",
        "Ivan tossed a chair at Dean, knocking his gun across the room and under a cabinet. Dean grunted and picked himself up. Bobby was moving across the room. It sounded like a cockroach skittering under there.",
        "Ming scrambled over to Barbie and took her out of the room.",
        "\"Why won't you shoot him?\" Bobby yelled from under the table,",
        "Dean grabbed a chair leg, jumped on Ivan's back and started pummeling him with the piece of wood. It was like hitting a rock.",
        "Ivan reached behind and tossed Dean into the corner. He gasped for air as he struggled to his feet.",
        "Ivan grabbed Bobby by the throat, choking him. Bobby hit the giant's arm with his fist. Dean rushed in and gave a kidney shot, but Ivan didn't even grunt.",
        "\"Are you starting to hum?\" Dean shouted.",
        "Bobby's eyes went wide, and he began hitting Ivan harder, making shooting signs with his other hand.",
        "Dean reached for his second gun around his ankle, but Ivan put his slab of a hand over Dean's and yanked it away. Grabbing him by the back of the neck, Ivan hoisted the two men into the air.",
        "\"How in the fuck are you doing this?\" Dean shouted.",
        "Bobby's face turned purple.",
        "Holding the two of them in the air, Ivan spun around on one foot. Dean's legs swung out behind him as Ivan let go of Bobby first, then Dean.",
        "Bobby went flying through the office window and landed on a table. Dean followed him on top, collapsing the furniture. The tall mountain stepped through the window and landed next to the broken table.",
        "\"Why won't he say anything?\" Dean yelled as he stood up. Adrenaline pushing the pain away for later. \"It's unnerving. All he's doing is humming.\"",
        "\"He cut out his tongue years ago,\" Bobby yelled. \"We have to stop him from humming!\"",
        "\"What? Why?\"",
        "\"You can't let him finish his song,\" Bobby said, dodging Ivan's kick. \"He gets to the end, we're dead.\" He was bleeding all over his Crue shirt, and his eye was turning a dark purple.",
        "Barbie appeared in front of the giant man and put her hands on her hips. \"This shouldn't be happening now.\" She pointed her finger in Ivan's face, \"You leave the Maker alone!\" she said, stomping her foot on the ground. Ivan just continued his humming and slapped her in the face.",
        "\"No! I need her!\" Ming yelled and dropped her pencil.",
        "Making pouty lips, Barbie grabbed the big man's hand as it came back and flipped him in the air. He landed on another desk and shattered it. Splinters flew everywhere. \"I told you to stop it!\" She walked over to him and, using two hands, grabbed one arm, raised him high in the air and smashed him back into the concrete floor. Ivan let out a wordless grunt and collapsed. Letting go of his arm, she wiped her hands together and stood over Bobby. Steam rose from the big man, ramping up the temperature by ten degrees.",
        "\"Can you finish the rest of the code now, or are you going to continue to pretend to sleep, Maker?\" Barbie asked, tapping her foot on the ground.",
        "Dean stared at the young woman. \"How in the hell did you do that?\" He looked at Ivan. The big man was stunned, his eyes staring at nothing and beginning to gloss over. Dean turned to Barbie. She was tapping her foot and had her arms crossed.",
        "\"When did she get a pink sweatshirt?\" Dean closed his eyes and lay his head on the ground. Could this day get any weirder?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "title": "Chapter 9",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "12:00 AM",
        "Ming sat down at one of the desks. She had cleaned up most of the broken glass, but a gaping hole remained in the conference room window, and a spicy musky smell invaded the room. Dean had locked Ivan in the holding cell and was now sprawled out on the ground in front of Ming. His shirt had been torn, and he was bleeding. \"You sure he won't get up soon?\"",
        "\"Yes. Whatever freaky thing that girl is, she's strong. He won't be getting up for a while,\" Dean spoke through the cloth on his face.",
        "\"How did she pick him up?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"You're asking me? I have no idea where she came from. If Jeremy was right, she just vanished from the room,\" he said. \"Maybe she reappeared in the same way. Just like Star Trek. Saves me from having to investigate her murder.\"",
        "\"You don't believe her story, do you? Somebody did kill her, right?\" Ming needed to dig this out. Leaving a mystery like this alone was not in her nature. Part of her wanted to accept that Barbie believed what she was saying, but ghosts and nanites were a bit far-fetched, even if she had seen her.",
        "\"So, she said. But with no body to check and the victim walking around, I can file this under 'Unsolved' and let it go. Too bad we don't have 'Loony'. Or just plain freaky.\" Dean paused. \"I will probably get a uniform to check out the place where she said her body was dumped in the morning. Just to cover all the bases.\"",
        "Ming tapped her pencil on her notepad. \"You looked really good out there,\" she said, bending over him. \"I was impressed.\"",
        "\"Really?\" He pulled the towel off his face. \"I thought I was losing.\" He scowled at her. \"Next time, drop the smirk when you say that.\"",
        "\"Can't help it.\" Ming covered her mouth with her hand and suppressed the giggle. \"You set yourself up for it so well, and my lack of sleep has impaired my judgment.\" Turning serious, she leaned back over the detective. \"On the other hand, she knows who Slazney is and said the man had been in Vegas for over thirty years.\"",
        "\"Can you really trust her?\" Dean said, sitting up. \"You've been searching for this man for a while. Her story sounds unbelievable, impossible and just plain weird.\" He paused. \"But my instincts aren't telling me to stay away from her, so I don't think she's hiding anything.\" He shrugged. \"I wish my gut came with an instruction manual sometimes.\"",
        "A slight vanilla scent filled the room. For a second, Ming let her fantasies play out in her mind. She saw him, naked, muscles gleaming and grabbing her with his two strong arms.",
        "Then he farted, shattering the illusion into a million pieces.",
        "\"Sorry about that,\" he said. He didn't even have the decency to look embarrassed.",
        "\"Don't worry about it. It was exactly what I needed,\" she said, waving her hand in front of her nose. \"As for trusting her, I want to, but it's difficult. Believing everything she's saying about Greater Vegas, well, that won't happen soon.\" She ground her teeth just thinking about Barbie. \"Her story is too unbelievable.\"",
        "\"Let's go check on them.\" Dean stood and walked to the interrogation room. They passed by the holding cell. The big mute was sleeping. He was bigger than the cot, flowing over it. According to Bobby, the man was an enforcer for the Bratva in Russia. He was dangerous, but his employer, Gregory, was the real problem. That man had connections in everything from assassination to selling high-priced chocolate on the black market. Bobby still hadn't explained their connection to him or why he was so worried about the man's humming.",
        "\"Have you finished yet?\" Dean asked, slamming open the door to the room. \"I'm still not sure why I haven't arrested you.\"",
        "A slight odour of unwashed bodies mixed with coffee and something else assaulted Ming. For once, she was glad she had allergies and didn't have to smell it for long.",
        "Bobby looked up from the computer screen. His bloodshot eyes pierced the gloom of the room. \"Fuck off, Detective. You have nothing to arrest me for anyway.\"",
        "\"How about the destruction of the precinct? Impeding an investigation? Or just plain wasting my time.\"",
        "\"That wasn't me, and you know it.\" Bobby started mumbling, checking the code line by line. \"One small miss in a space or using an apostrophe for a backtick screws everything up. They both look so similar.\"",
        "Dean scoffed. \"Excuses.\"",
        "\"You leave the Maker alone,\" Barbie turned to Dean. She was drinking another cup of cheap police coffee. \"He's doing the best he can.\"",
        "Dean frowned and sat across the table from them. \"How many of those have you had?\" he asked her.",
        "\"I don't know. Is seven a lot?\"",
        "Ming watched the two of them banter. Dean must be feeling slighted because he couldn't touch Ivan, and the twig of a girl smashed him into the floor, breaking the tiles. She stared at the pink girl out of the corner of her eyes. Ming's eyes bugged. Hadn't they given her a blue sweater from the locker room?",
        "\"When did you get that *pink* sweater?\" she asked. It even said LVPD on it.",
        "\"Like it? Pink's my favourite.\" Barbie picked up the front of her sweater, showing it off. \"I can't stand wearing any other colour, so I changed it. My nanites have enough juice in them thanks to the Maker's jump start. He's coming with me.\" She clapped her hands.",
        "\"It's very nice,\" Ming said, getting out her notebook and hiding her eye roll. Her nerves were poking her. Dean would call it his gut, but she needed more evidence, \"How did you really do that?\"",
        "\"Nanites,\" she said slowly, sipping her coffee.",
        "Ming lowered her head and sighed. \"I thought we already covered that. Nanites are in the sci-fi realm. I've read a few reports on them, but nothing to the level you're saying.\"",
        "Barbie shrugged and continued drinking her coffee with two hands.",
        "\"Can we continue our discussion about Slazney?\"",
        "\"Maybe later. I want to watch the Maker work.\" Barbie stared into Bobby's face like she was absorbing every pore in his skin.",
        "Closing her book, Ming turned back to Dean. She needed assistance to get through to Barbie. His eye was turning purple, and there was a bruise spreading across his sculptured chest visible through his ripped shirt. The man had it all. He was handsome with a good job. Her mother would like him. Showing up with him at the next party would certainly get her to stop trying to fix her up. She licked her lips and stared at him.",
        "\"What are you looking at?\" he asked. His blue eyes were searching her face. Why hadn't she noticed how soft they were?",
        "\"Just wondering what you were doing tomorrow night? My Uncle wants to have dinner with us,\" she said. It was just the two of them now. Bobby's clicking in the background had faded away. She envied how Barbie could stare into the face of the man she loved.",
        "Ming jerked back at the thought of the word 'love' and noticed a strange smell in the room. It was vanilla, with lilacs and butter mixed with a cheesy tang that left an aftertaste on her tongue. It was the same as in the main hall. \"What's that smell? Why am I thinking crazy thoughts?\"",
        "\"Oh, sorry,\" Barbie said. \"I was releasing my lust scent. It's much better than that nasty chew the Maker was using. I had the nanites whip up some for me. It uses them up faster, but that's okay, we're going home soon. It usually helps people focus on the things they like the most and covers up the smell of blood quite nicely. I hate that smell. I'm surprised you noticed it.\"",
        "\"Your lust scent?\" Ming mouthed. A similar expression of disbelief was on his face. It was turning red. She wasn't the only one affected. Ming wondered what he was thinking. She went out to the break room, grabbed the jar of coffee from the corner, and inhaled. With her sense of smell back, she returned to the interrogation room and passed it to Dean. He copied her and said nothing.",
        "\"I'm almost finished,\" Bobby announced. \"I hate that goddamn backtick.\" He typed a few more keys and stopped. Turning to Barbie. \"Are you sure about this? I was surprised you knew so much about the code.\"",
        "\"Yes. My Handler forbade me from ever touching a computer again, but I can help. I need to get home. I want to take you with me, if you want to come. You're not safe here, especially with that man after you. Besides, my Handler said we could find a place for you, if we needed to.\"",
        "\"I don't know if that's a good idea, but something is making me trust you,\" Bobby said. \"I wish I knew why. The block is pretty weak now, but I know this code is not something anyone should play with. What if I got it wrong?\"",
        "\"You've just forgotten the beauty of this code,\" Barbie responded, grabbing his face and kissing him on both cheeks. \"If you've input it right, it can give you your heart's desire, bypassing most of the cost.\" She turned and hit enter.",
        "Nothing happened.",
        "\"Not again,\" Bobby groaned. \"Let me check it.\"",
        "\"No. Wait.\" Barbie went to the CD file and started up some Motley Crue. \"You just forgot the music. The music needs to exist with the math. They can't work alone.\" A drum solo blared over Bobby's speakers. She hit enter again.",
        "A hum filled the room. It started in the computer speakers and spread to the people sitting at the table. The sound grew louder, forcing Ming to cover her ears. Even then, it pierced between her fingers, shaking her fillings.",
        "\"What the hell is this? Turn it down!\" Dean yelled. \"My ears are going to burst!\" He stood up and went to the door, his hands covering his ears.",
        "\"It's working!\" Barbie giggled. She grabbed Bobby's hand. \"We're going home.\"",
        "\"What about us?\" Ming yelled over the racket. She reached down, pulled off her socks and stuffed them into her ears. They helped dampen the noise but didn't cut it out completely.",
        "\"You can come with us. Just type your names in the command prompt and hit enter again when we've gone. You'll love Greater Vegas.\" Barbie gushed.",
        "\"Fuck!\" Bobby squeezed his eyes shut as light poured out of his computer screen and engulfed everyone in the room. \"Not again.\"",
        "\"What did you do, Window Washer?\" Dean yelled, moving towards Bobby, hands outstretched into claws.",
        "Ming could no longer see anything. The light and sound invaded every crack, stabbing her eyes and blocking out Bobby's response. She could hear Barbie's squeal over the noise, but everything else went white.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ivan",
        "2:00 AM",
        "The sound woke Ivan up. He sat up and looked around the holding cell and sighed. Gregory was going to be angry. He wasn't nice when he was angry. Ivan tested the bars of the tiny cell and started a Gregorian chant. He did that whenever he was too stressed. The sound helped him relax. He could bend the bars, but Gregory didn't like that kind of attention. Ivan shivered and let the hum go. There was no way he was getting out of here before the morning, and there had been too much destruction already.",
        "A bright light filled the precinct, forcing Ivan to put his hand over his face. The white seeped through his fingers and stabbed the back of his eyes, but didn't go any further. He remembered this kind of thing happening before with Petor, and it never ended well. Then there was silence. Nothing moved. He winced and held his ribs. *That blond girl was strong. What had she been on?*",
        "The silence stretched for a few minutes before the sounds of someone walking echoed through the dead office. A door opened, and a computer clicked shut. The door closed, and the footsteps walked away.",
        "Petor was gone. Ivan closed his eyes and went back to sleep. He'd deal with this in the morning. Right now, this was the most comfortable bed he'd slept on in years, and he wanted to enjoy it. American prisons were so soft. It was almost worth it letting Petor go."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "title": "Chapter 10",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "4:00 AM",
        "Dean was lying on the hard ground near the door. The cement was digging into his back. He'd been this way for a couple of hours and was stiff. Groaning, he opened his eyes, but still couldn't see anything. He rubbed them with his fists. Whatever that light was, it wouldn't leave them. He could make out a blurry somebody, but not who.",
        "\"Who's here?\" he said and reached over. He touched a smaller shoulder and ran his fingers through the hair. It was long, coarse and thick. \"Ming, is that you?\" he asked and was rewarded with a groan.",
        "\"No. Stop playing with my hair,\" Barbie mumbled. \"My eyes hurt.\"",
        "\"Dammit. I'm worried that light fried my brain.\" He blinked. The light spots were fading. There were only two other people left in the room. The one to his left was Ming. The second blob was a smelly mass. Dean kicked the chair, \"Wake up, you rocker wannabe.\" Bobby jumped and slumped out of the chair, sprawling on the floor.",
        "\"Maker. Are you all right?\" Barbie pushed past Dean, rushed to Bobby and grabbed his head. She frowned and leaned forward. \"No! It can't be.\" She turned to Dean. \"Check on the woman.\"",
        "Dean went to Ming and shook her shoulder, but there was no response. He reached down and pulled up her eyelid. Still no response. A dread filled his voice. \"Ming. Wake up.\" He shook her shoulder a little harder. She felt cold and lifeless. He'd been around bodies before, and they were just like this. \"Ming, please wake up,\" he said, a wobble filling his throat. He grabbed her shoulders. \"Ming!\"",
        "\"You can stop now. She's gone. Along with the Maker.\" Barbie stood up with her hands on her hips and stomped her foot. \"I can't believe he'd betray me.\"",
        "\"What are you talking about?\" Dean yelled at Barbie. \"Ming can't be dead.\" Tears welling up, he wiped his arm across his face. He didn't want to deal with this freak right now. Ming was gone, and it was all his fault.",
        "\"Don't worry. It's only temporary. If they can return within twenty-four hours and nothing enters them in the meantime, they should be able to get back in.\" Barbie stuck her hands on her hips and started pouting.",
        "\"Huh?\" Dean stared at the woman, ready to throttle her, \"What the hell do you mean? People don't temporarily die!\"",
        "She rolled her eyes. \"When the Maker executed the program, it drew his and Ming's souls through time. There must have been a glitch somewhere. I don't know where they went, probably the past. It's easier to get there, especially by mistake.\" She picked Bobby up and put him over her shoulder with one hand. \"We should put their corpses somewhere safe until I can check the code. As I said, I promised my Handler I wouldn't touch the big stuff, but I know a few protection algorithms that should do the trick. And music should stop other people from getting in. Hopefully, the Maker set the timer, but I doubt it. He really needs to learn better techniques.\" She looked around the room. \"Where's his computer?\"",
        "Dean wiped his eyes. He was grasping at a freaky lifeline, but he wanted to believe she was telling the truth. He needed to believe it. His instincts and his heart told him to trust her even if she was as loopy as a fried chicken ice cream sandwich. However, if Ming could come back, then there was still a chance, and he was going to cling to it.",
        "He needed to cling to it.",
        "Barbie had already done it once, and now this twig was deadlifting an eighty-kilo man. \"How strong are you?\" he whispered, shaking his head.",
        "\"Very. I have good ears too, but that's not important.\" She pointed to the table and the open door. \"Someone was here. They took the Maker's computer. The code he created was designed to get me home and take him, too. If it did this ---\" she pointed to Bobby's body \"--- and didn't take me, there was a mistake with it. We need it back to save them.\"",
        "\"Dammit!\" Dean went to his desk and pulled up the camera logs. \"There's a blackout in the cameras. I can see a shadow before it happened, but that's it.\" Dean pounded his fist on the desk and flipped through the feed. He stopped on the holding cell.",
        "\"Can you speak Russian?\" he asked Barbie.",
        "\"Yes. Why? Everybody in Greater Vegas can speak at least three languages.\" She shook her head. \"I was surprised to learn that people in this time could usually only speak one.\"",
        "\"Follow me,\" he said, rolling his eyes and gesturing for her to put Bobby down. He led her into the back room where Ivan was being held. \"Be careful. The holding cells are designed to keep people in. It's hard to reach through, but I wouldn't put it past him.\"",
        "Ivan sat on the bed watching the two of them. Dean drew back, his instincts screaming at him to stay away. How long had he been sitting there? He was still covered in the dust from the broken desk. He'd wrapped his ribs with the blanket, but his expression remained the same.",
        "It was like watching a stone.",
        "Dean and Bobby had dragged him into the cell and locked the door. He had attacked a police officer and deserved to stay in there, but Dean put his hand on his gut. What was it trying to tell him? He wished his instincts came with a manual sometimes.",
        "\"Did you see what happened?\" he asked the giant.",
        "Ivan nodded.",
        "\"Are you going to tell me?\"",
        "He shook his head.",
        "Dean sighed and turned to Barbie. \"I know he understands me, but there's no way he can talk with no tongue. Can you try Russian?\" Dean asked. He patted down his pockets looking for some candy to take the edge off his nicotine craving.",
        "\"Fine,\" Barbie said from behind. She cracked her knuckles. \"I'll make him spill the beans on what happened to the Maker.\"",
        "\"Don't hurt him,\" Dean said and stepped out of the way. He watched the woman step up to the bars and speak in Russian. He had no idea what she was saying, but it sounded like she knew what she was doing. \"What will she do next?\" he mumbled. \"When did I start accepting this as normal?\"",
        "Grimacing, he pulled an old, unwrapped candy from his pocket. It had some fuzz on it, but that was easy to brush off. He was about to when something told him to stop. Ming wasn't here, but if he ate this piece, he'd be trading a reduced nicotine craving for a ball-crushing. He tossed the candy into the garbage and went back to his silent suffering.",
        "\"Thank you, Mr. Ivan. You were very insightful,\" Barbie said.",
        "Dean sighed. His candy was gone. He pointed to Ivan. \"What did he say?\"",
        "\"Nothing. He doesn't have a tongue,\" Barbie gave him a stupid face and stuck her tongue out at him. \"However, he did let me know that a man came in and grabbed the computer. He was wearing a suit and, based on his description, it looked like a white guy.\"",
        "Dean grunted. \"I need a bit more than that. A white guy doesn't narrow it down.\"",
        "Barbie shrugged.",
        "Dean started pacing back and forth. \"After the destruction of Bobby's trailer, I ran the plates of the cars going into the park. Most of them were locals, but there was a Jaguar registered to the Shujing.\"",
        "\"That short old man really wanted to find the Maker. He was angry when his man missed him and kept mentioning Slazney,\" Barbie said, jumping up and down.",
        "It was coming back to that man again. He had to find him and Bobby's computer. It was back to the Shujing.",
        "\"How did he say all that?\" Dean crossed his arms and gave Barbie an uneven smile. \"He doesn't have a tongue, remember.\"",
        "\"I know. But I'm fluent in sign language as well. Keep up, old man. I can't hold your hands forever. Now come-on. We have to put the Maker somewhere safe.\" She spun around and walked back to the squad room.",
        "Dean pulled out his recorder and turned it off. The battery was almost dead again, and she talked way too much. He was going to have to check it soon.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "6:00 AM",
        "Dean got into the driver's seat and buckled up. He connected the portable battery to his recorder and let it charge. \"You sure they'll be safe at my place?\" he asked Barbie. He stared back at his low-rent bungalow. Located near Bobby's trailer, it was the only safe place he had. \"Won't the neighbours complain about the noise and the smell?\"",
        "\"They should.\" Barbie shook her head and frowned at Dean. \"'Generation Swine' was the worst thing Motley Crue ever recorded. I'm not surprised the police lost and found had it. I can't believe whoever took the computer stole all of the Maker's CDs as well.\"",
        "Nodding, Dean rubbed his fingers in his eyes and let it go. He knew better than to argue with a crazy person. A few hours earlier, she was as innocent as apple pie. Now she was going all gung-ho.",
        "*That would include me as well. I'm going along with this farce.* He needed to hold on to the hope that Ming would come back. It was the only thing keeping him going.",
        "He could hear the music from the car. It was still early; the walls were too thin, and there was no insulation. Why the hell did she have to play that music on a loop? There would be a mountain of complaints tomorrow.",
        "Dean stared at Barbie. Most of what she was saying sounded like gibberish. He should drop her off at the mental hospital and forget about her. His gut was telling him to trust her, though, and that was all he had left. When he moved Ming's body, it was becoming stiff. Soon, complete rigour mortis would set in. According to Barbie, once that disappears in normal people, their souls can no longer return. He checked his watch. It had been about four hours since they had gone on their trip. He had twenty left, give or take.",
        "\"You're going to the Shujing, aren't you?\" Barbie said. \"To talk to that old man. I'm going with you.\"",
        "\"What makes you think I'm going there?\" Dean was. She was still a suspect. Hell, she was the victim. \"You still haven't told me what happened to you at the Shujing. Was your death a joke? I saw your body. How did you survive that?\" Dean asked.",
        "\"No, I was dead,\" Barbie smiled. \"I can't remember who killed me, though, but I can say it was important. I may even have done that myself, but I couldn't tell you why.\" She stuck her finger on her lips and looked up. \"The nanites in my system helped bring my body back, twice. However, I can't check their memory here. They're everywhere in the future, thanks to the Maker. With them, time travel is so much easier. The code usually deposits a batch with the traveller to repair any damage that might be in the body. \"",
        "\"I see,\" Dean said. \"Is that what happened to you?\" Why was he having this conversation?",
        "\"Yes, although I'm a bit different. I was born outside the time stream and absorbed the code directly into my soul. It even lets me shift my personality to match the situation. I'm usually in waif mode, but now I've added but-kicker. My Handler says I'm special and do things others can't.\" Barbie bit her lip. \"She doesn't want me to learn more, though. I think she's scared of me.\"",
        "He closed his eyes and let out a breath. \"I'd trust my ex-wife's lawyer if he could get Ming back,\" he said under his breath. Time travel was a scientific myth. Outside of a good story, it was just fiction.",
        "\"That's nice,\" Barbie said. \"Trust is good.\"",
        "Dean rolled his eyes. \"Fine. Let's go. Yichen is probably up by now.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "title": "Chapter 11",
      "paragraphs": [
        "3 years ago",
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "\"Fuck you,\" Petor spat out a tooth. He wiped the blood from the side of his face. \"I didn't betray you.\" Why was Gregory always going the hard route? Petor looked up at the boss from the pitted concrete floor and shook in fear. The factory Gregory had dragged him to stunk of mould and rotten meat. Most of the lights were broken, and they hadn't processed hogs here in five years, but there were still hooks in the ceiling they used to hang the pigs on and let the blood drain out of the carcasses. Gregory had washed it down, but bits of pig were left in the corner and stains from where the drains had overflowed.",
        "Petor struggled to stand. Ivan had smacked him hard earlier, back at the loft, and his ears were still ringing. Even after working out three hours a day, Petor was no match for the giant. He needed to get home and check on Vlad. When Ivan had burst into the room, Vlad had tried to tackle him, but the mute had smashed Vlad's head into a sink, shattering the porcelain. Vlad was an asshole, but he was his only family. Hopefully, the American had gotten him out of there. Petor reached for the transponder in his shoe and breathed a sigh of relief. The heel was still intact.",
        "If Gregory found out Petor had betrayed him, nothing was getting him out of there. He needed to stall for time.",
        "*\"What the hell is this? I don't remember this,\" Bobby thought, floating in darkness.*",
        "Gregory shook his head. He sat at a small table and tapped his nose. The scar running down his cheek flashed red in the dark light, then faded as the shadows covered his face. A badge of honour, it added to the charm of the handsome man and made him seem less like the first James Bond and more like the fourth. \"I wish I could believe you, Petor. God knows I've let you get away with less, but this time you need to be punished. You had to talk to someone outside our little family. I know you're hiding something. A little initiative is good, but you've pushed it too far.\" Gregory put a bullet into the chamber and spun it. He placed the loaded revolver on the table alongside a serrated knife on a towel. It was a standard loyalty test.",
        "\"What are you talking about?\" Petor shouted, trying to stand again. Ivan kicked his legs, sending him back to the cold concrete. Sweating, Petor stared up at Gregory. There was no way the American squealed. He wanted the code destroyed too badly. Gregory usually stayed hands-off, but if he got a hold of it, they'd be fucked. The American had been paid to provide the credentials, get Petor and Vlad out of Russia, and set them up somewhere in the US off the grid. Petor's plans were falling apart faster than Vlad's love life.",
        "\"We tracked you down to a hobby shop in St. Petersburg,\" Gregory sneered. \"What were you doing going into that comic book store that sells international goods anyway?\" He adjusted his brown Hermes jacket and crossed his legs. His glare never moved. The man could stare down a concrete gargoyle and still win.",
        "Petor let out a sigh of relief. They'd followed him to the VR idol Hatsune Miku store. He'd gone there to track down some rare singles of Motley Crue. They had the best bootlegs in the country. Crue had recorded some choice songs that never made it to their official releases. Rumour had it they could transport you to another reality. After finding the first one, he needed the rest, even with all the trouble they caused. Petor felt around with his tongue and spat out another tooth. They hadn't discovered the code yet. He still had a chance.",
        "*If only I'd never found that first single. I loved it, though.*",
        "\"You got it all wrong, Gregory,\" Petor said, easing himself up from the floor. \"They had some information on the target. I went there to meet a contact. He stood me up.\"",
        "\"I don't believe you, Petor,\" Gregory pointed to the table. \"You've been lying to me, playing with something far more interesting. It's partly my fault. I was too lenient. So, choose. The gun or the knife.\" He smiled.",
        "Petor hated Gregory's smile. It promised pain and the occasional ice pick to the brain.",
        "\"Shit!\" Petor sat down at the table and stared at the weapons. If he chose the gun, he'd have to point it at his head and squeeze four times. If a bullet were in the chamber, he'd be dead instantly. The knife was the better option. All he had to do was cut off the first digit of his pinky without uttering a sound. Gregory was a big believer in manliness and courage. Just his execution was twisted. He stared at the rafters above Gregory. What was taking the American so long?",
        "*I'm remembering this now. That fucking hurt. Is this a dream or my memories? I was in the police station, wasn't I? That light. I remember a light.*",
        "\"Well. What will it be?\" Gregory crossed his arms and glared. Petor stared back at the Russian boss. A cold wind brought the smell of rotting meat and old manure. Whenever he had to feed a mark to the hogs, the smell of the pigs stayed with him, no matter how many showers he took. He refused to see Sasha until he was clean, but she was gone now. He hated this job, but Gregory had taken him in. Gave him a home.",
        "*Sasha? I remember that name. Oh God my blocks are gone!*",
        "One choice. The gun or the knife, which would it be? Petor waved his hand over the two weapons. *Where is the American? I should never have trusted them.* He thought.",
        "Petor picked up the knife and placed it against the last part of the smallest finger on his right hand. He didn't want to do this and turned to Gregory, hoping he would show mercy. He just gave a small grunt, nodded and gestured to continue. Gregory never gave any quarter. Clenching his teeth, Petor thrust the knife down, severing his pinky in one swift move. Blood squirted from the exposed wound as the tip bounced onto the floor. He grabbed his hand and wrapped the towel around it.",
        "\"There. Was that so hard?\" Gregory asked, standing up. He was smiling and had his arms open to receive Petor's embrace. He'd proven his loyalty and his courage. In Gregory's eyes, that was enough. He didn't care about blood on his coat now. They were brothers again.",
        "\"Now, tell me all about this code of yours. How did you develop it?\" Gregory asked. Shadows fell across his face, drowning out all pretense at friendliness.",
        "Stiffening, a realization settled in that Petor was never going to escape this man.",
        "An explosion shook the room, throwing everyone to the floor. Ivan staggered back, bracing himself against a pillar. Gregory knocked over the table. Black smoke and white powder flooded in from a smoke grenade, covering everything. Coughing and covering his face with his arm, Petor took his chance and snatched the gun from the floor. He dropped the towel, turned, pushed off the side of the table, spun around in the air and kicked Ivan in the face, crushing his nose. Ivan fell and clenched his face. He opened his mouth, revealing the stub of a tongue. Ivan had cut it out years ago to cement his position as Gregory's bodyguard. He'd begged the man to run away, but Ivan wouldn't. Letting him do that was the worst mistake Petor ever made.",
        "\"Get him! I need him alive,\" Gregory shouted from where he crouched. His face was red in fury, his scar a deeper crimson. Petor raced to the door and freedom, pointing the gun behind him and clicking the trigger as he went.",
        "Bursting into the sunlight, he hacked the smoke out and rubbed his eyes. He turned left and sprinted toward a blue blur, just where the American promised it would be. He dripped blood over the handle and yanked the door open. Jumped in, he banged his knee on a toolbox.",
        "\"Fuck!\" He rubbed his knee. \"Move!\" Petor yelled.",
        "\"No, thank you for saving your ass?\" The fat American quipped from the driver's seat. He was wearing a Metallica T-shirt. Gaging, Petor almost dove back out. Metallica was the trash of the music world, and he didn't need their contamination. Ivan kicked through the steel door, bending it in half and sending it flying into the field beyond, where it landed with a thud.",
        "Petor grunted, survival overriding pride. \"Thanks for saving my pretty ass. All it cost me was my fucking pinky.\" He waved his hand at the American, spraying blood over everything. \"Now move!\" He fired the gun at Ivan, clicking the chamber two more times.",
        "*When did I start screaming?*",
        "Ivan wiped the blood from his nose and raced toward the van. Usually, he acted like a robot with as much emotion as a block of wood. Now, with blood streaming down his nose, Ivan looked like the reaper he pretended to be when they were children. Petor shied back and fired once more. The bullet hit Ivan in the shoulder, but didn't slow him down.",
        "He shut the door and flopped down in the back of the cargo van. \"Drive faster!\"",
        "\"The customer is always right,\" The American said, handing him a package, a new towel and his computer. \"It's all in there. You're now Bob Miladev, engineer. You've decided to move to America and start a new life after the death of your brother.\"",
        "*That's right. This was how I learned of his death.*",
        "\"Call me Bobby. I like that name better,\" Petor said, smiling. His head shot up. \"Wait. You said after the death of his brother. What happened to Vlad?\"",
        "The American was silent. \"Sorry, dude. When I went to your loft, Vlad was gone. There was nothing I could do.\"",
        "The now Bobby, formerly Petor, stared at the laptop, stunned. \"Vlad...\" He trailed off.",
        "\"Fuck!\" Bobby said. A tear slid down his face. He wiped his nose on his sleeve, wrapped his hand in the towel and pulled open his computer. Cradling his right hand under his arm, he popped in the Crue single. Music burst over the speakers as he pulled up the computer code. \"This is all your fault, Vlad,\" he said, typing. \"You had to fucking try and use it one last time, but it didn't work, did it? You couldn't just enjoy the music. You fucking deserved getting your head shoved through the sink. I just wish it had been the toilet bowl.\" Tears fell onto the keyboard.",
        "\"You finished destroying the code?\" the American asked, putting on some Metallica. Their screech filled the van.",
        "*I can believe I blocked the memory. The Metallica must have screwed up my coding.*",
        "\"Almost,\" Bobby said, gritting his teeth. \"I'm in hell,\" he mumbled. \"You'd better park. The next part's dangerous.\" Bobby finished typing the last line and hit enter. A light flashed from the screen, filling the back of the van. Bobby closed his eyes against the glare and rocked to the right as the van swerved.",
        "\"Careful there. I almost hit a pole,\" the American said.",
        "Rocking back, he kicked the computer. \"The code's gone from the hard drive, the cloud, everything. That was the easy part. Reality itself seemed to help me there. I've set it up to erase my ability to code as well. I don't want this getting out again, but I left a warning in case it comes back.\" He took a hammer to the computer and ripped open the circuit board, smashing the chips and CD inside to make sure no one could recreate anything. He leaned back and cushioned his injured hand. The pain radiated out from his finger stub as blood turned the towel a deep crimson.",
        "\"Good. We'll take care of everything else. When we get to the airport, I'll have a doctor do something for your hand. Sorry about that.\"",
        "Bobby just sighed and shook his head. He'd believe the American was sorry when Ivan cracked a smile.",
        "\"When you land, our agent will meet you.\"",
        "\"What's his name?\" Bobby asked.",
        "\"Ryan. He's got a good job for you lined up in Canada.\"",
        "Petor, now known as Bobby, closed his eyes and said a prayer to Vlad. \"I'll make those bastards pay someday. I promise.\"",
        "*Fuck. I had to leave Gregory, but not like this. I still wanted to save Ivan.*",
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "The Past.",
        "Bobby shot up with a jolt and winced at the pain in his neck. His throat twinged and spread down through his back. \"What the hell was that light? It knocked me out.\" He rubbed the back of his neck, memories flooding back to him. \"What Gregory did to me wasn't a dream, was it?\" He stared to the side. \"That was three years ago. When I left Russia.\" He rubbed his hand through his hair. \"Fuck! I was right! The blocks in my memory are gone.\"",
        "Blinking the spots out of his eyes, he realized the room light was softer than the precinct's. It smelled different, too. \"Where am I? Is this the future?\" He looked around. There was a bed and a dresser with a lamp on top. The design was retro. \"No, it's the past, maybe. Whose place is this? Reporter's? It looks too old and clean to be Detective's. It smells sweet, as well. She must love the classics. His place would smell like stale dog.\" Bobby looked down at the bed and looked at his right hand. It was thinner than before, and the pinky was back.",
        "\"How the hell?\" He stared at his hand. The fingers were long, clean, and the nails tapered to a point. He'd never really taken care of them beyond trimming them. This wasn't his hand. \"Fuck me! Not again!\" He swung his legs off the bed and ran towards the black toilet. Slapping the wall, he hunted around for the light switch. The old light bulb flickered on, clicking and spritzing. On the floor was a girl with long curly blond hair. He bent down and touched her shoulder. She groaned and turned over. Blood covered the front of her blouse, which had been ripped open, exposing her breasts. There was a slash wound in her shoulder, but it was closing up as he watched.",
        "\"This is nanite work,\" he said. It was a common add-on in the code. Pulled from the future, they only lasted about a day before they were flushed from the body.",
        "\"Are you okay?\" Ignoring the churning in his stomach, Bobby grabbed a towel from the sink counter and ran some water. The taps matched the bedroom. Old silver spoke types that squeaked when he turned them. Wetting the towel, he turned back to the girl and dabbed the blood, cleaning the wound.",
        "\"I think so. Barbie, is that you?\" the girl asked. \"Why can't I see anything?\"",
        "Bobby drew back. \"No. My name's Bobby. Who are you?\" He stared at the girl. She couldn't be older than seventeen. His stomach started rebelling against him.",
        "\"It's me, Ming Na Liu, Bobby.\" She groaned and rubbed her head. \"The last thing I remember is that light.\" She turned to face Bobby and squinted. \"Everything is still blurry, but why do you look like an older Barbie?\"",
        "Shaking, Bobby stood up and faced the mirror. In it was a woman's face. It looked like the younger one on the floor, but older, covered in heavy makeup that had smeared and run down his cheeks with poofy hair. There were wrinkles around the eyes and a handprint around the neck. It was fading slowly, disappearing back into the skin. Bobby sagged and collapsed. He stared at the ceiling, opened his mouth and swore.",
        "\"FUCK!\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "title": "Chapter 12",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Dean Lifante",
        "7:00 AM",
        "Barbie yanked open the doors to the Shujing Hotel and led Dean inside. It was seven in the morning, but the noise was still the same as two nights ago. Some people were playing the slots. Dean could have sworn a few of them were the same people he saw when he found Barbie's body.",
        "Ignoring them, they went to the front desk. The late-night clerk was still sitting there reading a book.",
        "In college, Dean had worked a night job at a different hotel. It had been a great way to make money and learn how to deal with the freaks that hung around.",
        "The clerk heard them coming, moved the bell away from the top of the desk, and returned to his book.",
        "\"Excuse me. We need to speak to the owner,\" Dean said.",
        "The clerk ignored him.",
        "Tapping his fingers on the countertop, Dean tried again. \"That's the new Jan Dark mystery, isn't it?\" He smiled. \"You wouldn't like me to spoil the ending now, would you?\"",
        "The clerk frowned, stuck his finger in the book to mark his place and stood up. \"How can I help you, sir?\"",
        "\"I need to speak to the owner,\" Dean said again. He crossed his arms and stared across the desk at the clerk.",
        "\"What is your name?\" the clerk asked.",
        "\"Dean Lifante.\"",
        "The clerk flipped through the notes at his desk. \"You were supposed to be here last night. He was very upset you didn't come. I have a note from the owner not to let you in if you come back.\" He shrugged his shoulders. \"I'm sorry, but you'll have to leave.\"",
        "Barbie pounded the countertop with her left fist, spiderwebbing the tiles there and grabbed the man with her right. \"You let that owner know we're coming up, or I will have to tell everyone here how he felt up my tushy.\" She dropped the man and stalked to the doors. Slamming them open, she went to the private elevator and pushed the up button. The doors opened, and Dean got inside behind her. Barbie pushed the button for the penthouse, and the doors closed.",
        "\"He touched your butt?\" Dean asked.",
        "Barbie stared out the window. \"Yes. Sorry, I used such harsh words there, but I was ready to break his neck. Then I remembered my Handler's instructions not to make waves and turned down my butt-kicking mode setting. It was making me crazy.\" She turned away and didn't look at him.",
        "\"No problem,\" Dean said. He turned away and started rubbing his eyes. This day was getting stranger and stranger.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "The doors to the penthouse opened. Dean and Barbie stepped out. They faced two bodyguards, each about the size of a mini-truck. Rumour had it that Yichen hired several former football players to act as his muscle. Dean wouldn't have been surprised to see one at Bobby's place before it exploded. Yichen had known where to find the window washer before Dean even went to the company.",
        "\"I'm here to see Yichen,\" Barbie said, crossing her arms and staring them down.",
        "\"We know Mr. Lifante. He's been expecting you. Your friend may join you,\" the one on the right said. The one on the left was silent and opened the door.",
        "The inside of the penthouse was a vast open plan and big enough to fit five of Dean's houses. There was one small set of walls in the back, probably to hide the toilet and bedroom. A series of smooth pillars held up the rest of the ceiling. Each pillar was circled by a shelf holding a series of pictures and knick-knacks. They gave the room a Grecian feel with a sense of the Forbidden City.",
        "Dean found his eyes searching for Ming in the pictures and thought he recognized her a few times. Along the walls were more pictures. A grand piano sat against the left side, taking up most of the open area. There was a small stage with guitars and a sax resting against the wall.",
        "\"Come in, come in.\" Yichen was sitting at the piano. He was in his silk robe, wearing fuzzy pink slippers.",
        "Yichen's Secretary was sitting on a chair in the corner. The suit looked the same as the one she was wearing yesterday.",
        "\"Don't you ever go home?\" he said to the woman. The secretary adjusted her half",
        "moon glasses and started typing on the pad in front of her.",
        "Dean shook his head and sat down in front of Yichen. Barbie approached the secretary, stuck her head directly in front of the secretary, and sniffed.",
        "\"Could the pink lady please leave Wu alone? It's not polite to sniff other people.\"",
        "\"Barbie, come here.\" Dean went over and led the woman to the couch. \"What were you doing? You can't just sniff people.\"",
        "\"I liked her smell. It was a mix of roses and candy, much subtler than mine. My Handler says I need to experiment. I was going to ask her where she got it. The Maker might like it.\"",
        "Yichen sat forward at Barbie's words and glanced at the men standing by the door. Dean watched one of them leave the room and close the door behind him. \"I know you, don't I?\" he asked Barbie.",
        "\"She's the woman who died in the hotel two days ago,\" Dean said, testing the water. \"She said you grabbed her ass.\"",
        "Yichen just nodded. \"You've done well, detective. Very quick. Where is Ming? I expected her to come with you and apologize for standing me up last night.\"",
        "\"She's busy at the moment,\" Dean said. Why hadn't he reacted? \"Barbie here tells me you know something about Slazney.\" He needed to keep him away from the subject of Ming. Besides, they didn't have any time to waste.",
        "Barbie stood behind him, glaring at the old man. He hoped she wouldn't cause a scene here. The longer it took to find Bobby's computer, the harder it would be to get Ming back into her body. \"This is the time to tell us everything.\" He got out a notebook and a pencil. \"Did you take Bobby's computer?\"",
        "\"What are you talking about?\" Yichen leaned back and sipped his drink.",
        "Dean flipped through his notes to give the impression he had a lot of information. \"Last night I talked with Bobby Miladev. He told me about the arrangement he had with you to clean the Shujing.\" He looked over his book to watch Yichen's next reaction. \"He said he had proof as to who killed the woman in the room, but there was an incident at the precinct, and his computer was stolen.\" He closed his book. \"Do you have it or did Slazney take it?\"",
        "\"Shit!\" Yichen stood up, walked to the bar and poured himself a whiskey. Breathing out through clenched teeth, he turned to Dean. \"Did Ming ever tell you why she's searching for Slazney?\"",
        "\"It started as a story. A mysterious person behind Vegas's best-known spots. I don't know much more than that. Knowing her, she got hold of a story and couldn't let it go.\"",
        "Dean watched Yichen's hands. Most people knew enough to stop their emotions from appearing on their faces, but forgot to control their hands. He'd cracked a few cases by watching what people do with them.",
        "Yichen took another drink. \"Yes, it is.\" He put his drink down. \"Slazney has made it his mission to control most of Vegas. If you weren't with him, he'd make sure you couldn't stay in the town.\" Yichen started pacing.",
        "\"Why?\" Dean asked. He wished Ming were here. This was what she had wanted to hear for so long. He checked that his recorder was working. It should have enough power for this.",
        "\"I don't know, but ...\" Yichen took another sip. \"Thirty years ago, I was with the crew when they were building this hotel. They didn't want to include the pink windows then. Slazney came here with some plans and suggestions. He even offered to provide the windows for free.\"",
        "\"I knew there was something. Those evil things couldn't just appear by accident.\" Barbie smacked her palm. \"When I see that piece of doo-doo, I'm going to rip his head off.\"",
        "Yichen raised an eyebrow. \"Anyway, the owners had him tossed into the garbage.\" Yichen continued to pace back and forth, ignoring Barbie and spilling his drink onto the carpet. \"The next day their men started dying.\"",
        "\"I remember that case,\" Dean said. \"I had just started junior high school, and it made all the news. Twenty men were found dead. They said it was a drive-by shooting from a rival gang.\"",
        "\"No shooting. They were all staked to the ground. Spelling out the word Pink Glass.\" He took another sip. \"There was a contract put out on the man after that.\"",
        "\"Are you confessing to hiring a murderer?\" Dean raised an eyebrow. \"In front of a Police Officer?\"",
        "\"Give me a break, Detective Lifante. I'm telling you what you want to know. The man came back the next day, returned the money and joined a monastery in Italy. He hasn't been seen since.\" Yichen sat down. \"Every other person sent after Slazney joined the first man. Soon, Slazney and the owners came to an agreement. They installed the pink windows at his cost.\"",
        "Dean wrote all of this down in his notebook, cursing when the pencil broke. \"Why did this Slazney do that?\"",
        "\"I don't know. When the Triad opened the Red Dragon, they had no more problems with the man, and they found that the windows were a hit. The tourists flocked to the hotel.\" He took a sip of his drink. \"However, the spectre of the deaths continued to haunt the place, and some people complained of headaches. Eventually, the Chinese members refused to come and started staying at the Jade Emperor across town. I bought the place and renamed it. The locals loved it, and the regular Chinese tourists didn't know about the murders.\"",
        "\"Is that it?\" Dean asked. There had to be a connection to Bobby. Something to explain why he could read the code Ming had found in the windows. \"Surely there's more?\"",
        "\"Almost two years ago, Slazney reached out to me. At first, I had forgotten the man, but when he reminded me about the pink windows, my bowels turned to water.\"",
        "Barbie scrunched her nose and waved her hand under it. \"Is this going anywhere? I want to find the Maker.\"",
        "Yichen put his empty glass down on the table. \"He called me up and had me hire a window washing company, specifically one man, Bobby. He never told me why.\" He got up and pushed a button. Three men came into the room from a side door. \"That's all I know. Now it's time for you to leave.\"",
        "\"Why did he have you hire Bobby?\" Dean asked, standing up. The bodyguards had their hands on their weapons and were moving toward them.",
        "\"When I find him. I'll ask him.\" He turned back to his bedroom. \"Goodnight.\"",
        "\"It's morning, silly,\" Barbie yelled out.",
        "Dean stared at the closed door and snapped the pencil in his hand. Yichen was lying about something. His gut was telling him the old man probably had the computer or knew where it was, but there was no proof. This wasn't over."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
      "title": "Chapter 13",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "The Past",
        "Ming backed up and hit the wall. \"Why did you scream like that?\" She rubbed her eyes to clear them and stared at her hand. She grabbed it with her left hand and started shaking it. \"Why is my hand white? What the hell is going on here?\"",
        "Bobby stayed hunched over on the floor, rocking back and forth. \"I knew it. I knew it. I knew it.\"",
        "\"What do you mean? What did you know?\" She grabbed Bobby's shoulders and shook them. She refused to listen and pulled herself tighter into a ball. \"Did we time-travel, Bobby? You're a woman now. What's happening?\" Ming's voice rose. \"I can't believe that.\" Her fingers twitched.",
        "She heard a door slam open and a man scream.",
        "\"Jessica? Where are you, Jessica?\"",
        "\"We're in here!\" Ming yelled. She didn't know who Jessica was. Maybe this older woman. It couldn't be Bobby, no matter what she said. She was going to start laughing in a moment.",
        "Ming looked down and saw the blood on the front of her blouse. \"Dammit.\" She didn't have time to change. Grabbing the two sides of the ripped cloth, she cringed at the wetness. Ming clenched them together to hide her chest and the blood. When she looked up, a strange man was standing in the doorway. He was taller than she was and had a runner's build.",
        "Bobby stared at the wall. He was rocking back and forth. Ming still didn't know why she looked like Barbie. \"What's going on here, Bobby?\" She reached for her shoulders when the man in the doorway tackled her.",
        "\"What the hell?\" Ming shouted.",
        "\"Jessica, I thought you were dead! I'm so glad you're okay,\" the man said, wrapping his arms around her. \"After what happened with your mother, I was sure you'd never forgive me.\"",
        "He was bawling. Ming patted the man on the back. She needed time to think before saying anything. She put her hands on the man's shoulders and pushed him back. He was holding her tight, the muscle cords bulging in his arms. \"What happened here? I can't remember anything.\" It was best to stick with the classics. Pretend ignorance and let the other person fill in the blanks.",
        "The man stood up and started pacing. He ran his hands through his hair and rambled. \"After you rejected me, I followed your mother, asking her for help, hoping she would be able to change your mind. She locked me out of your house and tried to call the police, but she forgot the kitchen. When I burst in, she hit me with the frying pan. I just wanted to talk to her, but she refused to listen. I had to do it. We were supposed to get married! When you walked in, I panicked and lashed out. I tried to stop the blood, but there was too much.\" He knelt and grabbed her hands. \"Can you forgive me?\"",
        "Ming only followed half of what he was saying. Looking down at her bloody blouse, his bloody fingers and the blood splatter on his clothes. \"*You killed my mother and then me. Is that correct*?\" Her eyes went wide, and she stared at the man. A fist took hold of her heart.",
        "\"What are you saying?\" he said. \"I didn't know you spoke another language. What is it anyway?\"",
        "Ming stopped. She'd spoken in Cantonese out of instinct. It was how she usually repeated scary information to herself. She turned back to the man. He was stronger than her, and his eyes were wide with fear. If she wasn't careful here, she was dead.",
        "Standing, she pointed to Bobby. None of this was making sense. Ming was on the edge of joining Bobby on the floor. \"Can you help my mother stand? She's feeling a little weak.\"",
        "\"Of course.\" He picked up Bobby and carried her to the bed.",
        "Ming turned and looked at herself in the mirror. She was taller than before, and dark freckles covered her small, pointed nose. Her hair was a mass of blond curls that spilled down to her shoulders and framed her face. Her eyes were wide and full of panic. \"Quantum Leap it is. Breathe. Focus on the story. Use that until you know what the hell is going on.\" She took a deep breath and let it out.",
        "\"Jessica?\" the male said from the bedroom.",
        "\"Coming. I'm just washing my face.\" Ming looked around the bathroom, but couldn't find anything to help defend herself. She clenched her blouse closed and stepped into the bedroom. Bobby was still staring at nothing. Ming grimaced. She needed her if they were going to get out of here. Two were always better than one.",
        "\"Can you get me something to drink? I'm feeling thirsty,\" she said to the man.",
        "\"Of course. Anything for you.\" He ran out of the room.",
        "Ming hurried to Bobby and shook her shoulder. \"Wake up, Bobby! I need you to tell me what's happening.\" She shook her harder. \"Bobby! Please! I'm going out of my mind here.\"",
        "Bobby sighed and blinked her eyes. \"We've travelled through time and taken over the bodies of two people who recently died. The same thing Barbie did, maybe. I have my doubts about her. My blocks are gone, though. Fuck.\" She started crying.",
        "Ming wrinkled her nose. \"What are you talking about?\" She couldn't hide the tension in her voice.",
        "Bobby looked around and sighed. \"Hold that thought.\" She got up, went to the door, stood to the side and stuck her leg out. The man tripped as he ran in, spilling the large glass of water all over Ming.",
        "\"What do you think you're doing, you bitch?\" the man said, pushing himself up. Bobby surged forward and kneed him in the face, stunning him and breaking his nose. Bobby then reached down and undid the man's belt and yanked it out of his pants. Drawing his leg back, Bobby kicked the man between the legs. The man screamed and clutched his crotch, doubling over. Bobby pulled the man's arms behind him and tied them together with his belt. She stood up and kicked the man in the head one last time, slamming it into the bedpost. The man was silent as blood dripped from the ruins of his face.",
        "Ming stared at the scene. Her mouth opened in shock. \"What did you do? How?\"",
        "Bobby shrugged her shoulders. \"I have no idea how strong he is, and the best defence is always surprise mixed with a healthy dose of violence. He's probably the one who killed us. I saw the blood on his hands and the crazed look in his eyes. Must've been his first time. He was in a frenzy at the guilt. When he saw we were alive, it sent him careening in the other direction. I was the same my first time, too.\"",
        "\"You've killed people before?\" Ming asked, stepping back. What was she getting into? Her fingers were twitching. The reporter in her was itching to write all this down. That feeling was the only thing keeping her sane.",
        "\"Sit down. You wanted to know what was happening.\" She patted the bed. \"He'll be out for a while, so we have time.\"",
        "Ming went to the opposite side of the bedroom and grabbed a chair from the vanity table. She wanted to sit as far away as possible from her. *When did I start thinking of Bobby as her?*"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 14,
      "title": "Chapter 14",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Barbie",
        "7:30 AM Present Day",
        "Barbie turned to Dean and stuck out her tongue at him. \"Why didn't you force that old man to tell the truth? I thought you'd go all John Wayne on him. My Handler said he was a real man. You aren't the help I thought you'd be. I'm going to find the Maker by myself.\" Huffing, she turned around and entered the waiting elevator, leaving Dean standing outside the old Chinese man's door.",
        "She hit the button for the first floor. Two of Yichen's bodyguards followed her in. One pushed the button for the sub-basement. The other one stared straight ahead. An arm appeared in the elevator doorway, bouncing it open. Dean stepped inside and glared at Barbie.",
        "\"You're not leaving me here,\" he said to Barbie, sticking his finger in her face. \"You're the only one who can read that code, and I don't trust you yet.\"",
        "She rolled her eyes and turned to the two bodyguards, \"You're crowding me in here. Can you give me some space? They stood back and looked at each other. The one on the right put a hand in his pocket and came out with a tube.",
        "\"What's that?\" Barbie pointed to the device.",
        "The man on the left grabbed her arms while the one on the right plunged it into her neck. Dean grabbed his hand before he could push the plunger down.",
        "\"Ow!\" She yanked her arm from the left's grip and punched the right one in the face. She heard his nose crack. He went down, taking Dean with him. The other one behind her depressed the plunger and grabbed her arms. \"What are you doing? I don't want to be touched like this! It's icky.\" The man didn't let go and stuck a cloth over her face, muffling her voice.",
        "\"Barbie!\" Dean yelled. He was fighting with the broken-nosed man on the ground and losing.",
        "\"What are you doing? You have to grab his hee-haw,\" Barbie said, stumbling against the wall. \"This isn't pos..ibule.\" The nanites should fight off anything in her blood, but they weren't working. Maybe they had been overworked repairing her body earlier. \"I'm not going to fo...rge..t th...is.\"",
        "She slumped to the ground.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "\"That wasn't nice!\" Barbie said. \"How'd you knock me out? There was something in that syringe, wasn't there?\"",
        "Her hands were tied behind her to a metal chair in a small, dirty room when she woke up. She puffed out her cheeks and rocked back and forth in the chair. It was solid metal and stuck to the ground.",
        "The detective sat across from her, still asleep, his head slumped forward. He was also tied to a chair, but he looked more comfortable. He had a black eye, and blood was dripping onto his pants. Maybe she was wrong about him. He wasn't very strong, but he did try to help.",
        "The two guards from the elevator with her were sitting across the room. One had a bandage over his nose, and his eyes were turning black.",
        "\"Why did you do that?\" she asked.",
        "They said nothing.",
        "\"Come on. Talk to me,\" Barbie whined. \"I need to go to the bathroom. I drank too much coffee.\"",
        "\"Has she been like this the entire time?\" The old Chinese man said as he walked into the room, leaning on a walking stick. He was dressed in a better suit than the pyjamas, and his hair had been combed. The nice-smelling secretary was following him.",
        "\"Hey, you're Ming's Uncle. You felt up my tushy,\" she said. \"Let me go so I can break your leg.\" She struggled against the chair.",
        "\"Please be quiet,\" he said. He directed one of the guards to put down a chair in front of Barbie. The secretary stood behind him. \"Tell me what you know about Slazney and how to find that code.\"",
        "Barbie was silent. She stared at the old man and the secretary.",
        "\"Say something! You wouldn't shut up a moment ago.\" Yichen smacked his walking stick against his palm.",
        "\"You told me to be quiet. You asked nicely, so I thought I'd comply.\" She shrugged.",
        "He just opened his mouth, raised his cane and smacked her on the head.",
        "\"That hurt. You are a big meanie,\" Barbie snarled. \"When I snap these things, I'm going to have to take her out first, before I return that,\" she said, looking at the secretary. \"Just from her sexy legs, I can tell her training is so much better than the guard's.\"",
        "Yichen smiled. \"What are you talking about? Those are the latest plastic cuffs. There's no way you can break them.\"",
        "Barbie struggled against the plastic, running her fingers over it, trying to locate a weak point. He was right. \"Maybe, I won't worry about them for now.\" She turned to the Chinese man. \"What do you want?\"",
        "\"Tell me where I can find Slazney and Bobby,\" he asked.",
        "\"I don't know,\" Barbie said. \"I want to find Slazney, too, but I've never met him. As for the Maker, he's gone on a trip. You won't find him soon.\"",
        "\"Is Ming with him?\"",
        "\"How'd you know?\" Barbie puffed out her cheeks. \"He was supposed to take me.\"",
        "Yichen stood up and waved to the two bodyguards. \"Do what you need to do to her. I don't care what happens as long as she can still answer questions. She's already listed as dead.\" He pointed to the detective. \"Be careful with him. Don't kill him and wait till he wakes up on his own. Ming likes him for some reason. I'll figure out what to do with him later.\" He left the room, followed by the secretary.",
        "\"Where did you get your scent?\" Barbie yelled after the secretary. \"I want to try it.\"",
        "Dean Lifante",
        "8:00 AM / 9:00 AM?",
        "Dean woke up from the darkness to the sounds of grunts and slaps. It was cold and dank, smelling like a rusty cellar. He could taste it. Keeping his eyes closed, he tried to understand where he was. His arms were tied to the side of a chair, and the bindings dug into his wrists. He felt them with his fingers; plastic. At least his feet were free. Why? He was in a closed place, probably the Shujing basement. A woman screamed out in pain, and he opened his eyes. \"Barbie! Are you okay?\"",
        "Across the room, the two big men from the elevator were in front of Barbie. One with a bandage across his nose was standing to her right side, his fist out, blood dripping down it. The other was rolling on the ground, clutching his crotch.",
        "\"Dean! You're okay! Great. I thought they had broken you. Give me a few minutes to take care of these two,\" Barbie spat out a tooth. Blood was dripping down her face, and her nose matched the man she punched. She was smiling and tied to a chair like Dean.",
        "\"Why won't you stop smiling?\" The big man to her right asked, on the verge of crying. His shoulders dropped, and he bent down to pick up the other man, dragging him out of the room in defeat.",
        "\"Did you scream?\" Dean asked Barbie.",
        "\"Me? No. That was the guy on the floor. He thought it would be okay to touch my chest. My knee told him that was a bad idea. My mother always told me to aim high.\"",
        "\"I see.\" Dean winced. He didn't wish that on any man, no matter how deserved. He looked around the room. It was a basement. Cold and covered in concrete. The pipes looked old. They were probably here when the place was built. The damp chill seeped into his bones, causing him to shiver. He sniffed and spat out a wad of blood. \"Sorry, I couldn't stop them in the elevator. They were too strong.\"",
        "\"It's okay. You did your best. Besides, not everybody is as strong,\" said Barbie as she worked on the restraints. \"Gee wiz, I spoke too soon. It looks like I can't break these things. I guess we're stuck here until that old man comes back.\"",
        "Dean couldn't wait until then. He'd already lost five or six hours looking for this computer. He couldn't lose any more. How long had he been out cold? He wasn't hungry, so maybe an hour? \"Damn!\" He strained his arms against the cuffs but stopped when they sliced into his wrists. That was a waste of time. He needed another way to get them off. Breaking the chair was out. It was made of metal, bolted to the floor and solid, not the folding type.",
        "\"What are you doing?\" he asked Barbie as she struggled to stand up with the chair. It was also bolted to the floor.",
        "\"If I can just pull this thing from the bolts, maybe I can get out of these cuffs,\" she said. Dean watched her strain against the floor and give up, panting. \"Why can't I do it?\" she said, her voice quivering. \"My nanites aren't working.\"",
        "\"Maybe you're human after all,\" he mumbled to himself. Dean strained back with his fingers to explore the cuffs. They were plastic and usually unbreakable, but easy to cut. He slipped off his shoes and socks.",
        "\"What are you doing?\" Barbie asked. \"This isn't time to strip down. The Maker needs us.\"",
        "Dean ignored her and rolled up his right pant leg with his left foot. Just inside the cuff was a small knife in a sheath, strapped to his ankle. He wore it just in case. Experiencing this kind of humiliation once was enough. Sliding it out with his toes, he gripped it and brought his foot to his hand, using the chair as support. They would regret not tying his feet.",
        "A leg was not meant to bend this way. He grunted at the pain, and the knife slipped. He needed to hurry. Sticking his tongue between his teeth, he strained against the cuffs, bending his body forward to give his leg more room to move. His fingers brushed against the blade, and he brought it into the palm of his hand. Breathing a sigh of relief, he flipped it around, slicing his hand. Wincing, he started cutting through the plastic strap.",
        "Barbie stared at him, her eyes bugging out. \"You can't see it, but I'm clapping my hands. Very John Wayne.\"",
        "The door slammed open, and Broken Nose Goon walked in with Yichen. They paused.",
        "Yichen asked, \"Why are your shoes and socks off?\"",
        "He shrugged and stopped cutting, palming the knife. \"I was hot, and I've found that rubbing your toes on the floor helps you to relax.\" Some blood seeped its way through his fingers and dripped to the floor.",
        "\"I see, play the wise guy. I'll let you have your little comedy routine, for Ming's sake.\" Yichen smiled. \"When Riley told me you were awake, I had to come see for myself.\"",
        "Riley placed a chair in front of Dean, and Yichen sat down. He placed his cane in front of him and leaned forward. \"Where's Bobby, Dean? I need him if I want to get to Slazney.\"",
        "Dean looked at the old Chinese man. His eyes were tired, and he looked like he hadn't slept. From what Ming said, he wanted to have dinner with her and Dean last night. Why was he so interested in their relationship when Dean wasn't even sure where it was going?",
        "Yichen was worried about Ming but didn't want to show it. He'd tied them to chairs and was torturing Barbie. Still, why was his gut telling him to trust the man? Usually, when he ignored his instincts, that meant more trouble, but the situation wasn't exactly conducive to trust. Barbie's face alone was enough evidence to put him away.",
        "\"Bobby's dead, Ming too, and they will stay that way unless I find his computer. Do you have it?\" Dean said, cringing. Just saying the words opened a pit within him.",
        "Yichen shook his head. \"Ming's not dead. I wouldn't allow it. As for the computer, if I did have it, I wouldn't tell you.\" He sighed and stood. \"I won't get anything from you without force, detective. You're lucky I'm not ready to go that route with you, not yet. Help me out of here, Riley. When you come back, take care of her. Don't touch him. A dead police officer brings too many questions.\" Yichen leaned on Riley as he hobbled to the door. He was looking ten years older than this morning. Something was happening with him, but Dean didn't have time to worry about that now,",
        "The door didn't lock when they left.",
        "Riley would be back soon. It had taken him about ten minutes the last time to bring Yichen. This time, he'd be faster. Dean continued cutting through the plastic zip tie. Fumbling with the blade, he almost dropped it, but managed to catch it by the edge before it dropped to the ground. \"Slow down, Lifante,\" he muttered. \"If you screw this up, it's over.\" He ignored Barbie's chants of 'You can do it.' They were distracting.",
        "Walking the knife back up with his fingers, he brought his arm around and cut through the second zip tie holding him to the chair. He then cut Barbie free.",
        "\"Thank you, detective. You're better at your job than I thought,\" she said, smiling. With a single motion, she straightened her nose and blew out the blood blocking it. \"That's better.\" The bruise around her eye looked like it was already fading.",
        "Dean shook his head, \"Let's get out of here.\" He put his shoes and socks on while Barbie grabbed her tooth and put it in her pocket. \"Why did you take that?\"",
        "\"Evidence I was here. Besides, I like having a full set of teeth, and they're a pain to grow back,\" she said, frowning. \"Especially when my nanites seem to be breaking down. I've been here too long.\"",
        "\"I should have guessed. It's never normal with you, is it?\" He rolled his eyes. \"It's about nine o'clock,\" he said, pointing to his watch. Checking his pockets, he closed his hand on his recorder. Keeping the surprise off his face, he pointed to the door. \"Yichen may have cameras around here. Try and get yourself on them, if you can. It'll make it easier to arrest him later.\" Dean needed to check out his recorder. There could be something useful on it.",
        "\"We should have about sixteen hours left to find Bobby's computer. Let's go and don't make a lot of noise now.\" He creaked open the door and peered out. The corridor was dark but empty. Only one light stood out by the elevator at the end of the hallway. There was a door to the side of it.",
        "\"Where to?\" she asked.",
        "Dean ignored the question. If Yichen didn't have the computer, that meant either Slazney or this Gregory, Bobby mentioned, did. They already tried Ivan, but maybe he could help them. Dean was running out of time, and he was no closer to finding this thing.",
        "The only other place he could think of was the doctors. He had the address Bobby had given him. It was either Stanley or head back home and wait for the bodies to rot."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 15,
      "title": "Chapter 15",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "19XX",
        "Ming watched Bobby tie up the man so he couldn't move. \"You've done this before?\" Ming admired the knots Bobby was using. They were beyond anything she could have done. She needed to focus on the small things. One step at a time.",
        "Bobby just nodded and picked him up by the shoulders. She directed Ming to grab his ankles.",
        "\"Are you sure we should be doing this?\" Ming asked Bobby as they lowered him into the bathtub and turned off the lights.",
        "\"Don't forget, he's probably the cock who killed us,\" Bobby said. \"In a tub that high, there is no way he'll crawl out easily. If he does, I've got the frypan ready for him.\"",
        "Sitting at the table, Ming watched Bobby turn off the gas, pick up the retro-looking metal kettle and pour some hot water into a mug of instant coffee. The smell embraced the two women. She needed something normal to take the edge off the freaky.",
        "\"I love the first smell of coffee. It makes everything seem easy,\" Bobby said, leaning back.",
        "\"You're taking all of this quite well, Bobby. I think I'm still in shock.\" Ming sipped her coffee, letting the aroma replace the metallic tang in the air and ignoring the blood stain on the checkered black and white tile. It would have to come out soon, or it would seep into the linoleum. She had found some clothes in one of the bedrooms and replaced the ripped blouse. \"Were they really dead? I can't believe it.\"",
        "\"Barbie told you before, but yeah.\" Bobby stared at her hand and the pinky finger, flexing them. \"This is the only way time travel works for most people. The spirit can only inhabit dead bodies. The recently dead are the easiest. The longer the person has been dead, though, the greater the causality fuck-up. It's how all those stories of ghosts and zombies spread throughout the centuries.\"",
        "\"I don't like the idea of using someone like this,\" Ming said, hugging herself. \"It feels like I'm violating her.\"",
        "\"If it makes you feel better, the longer you stay in the body, the greater the chance that Jessica will come back into it, once you leave.\"",
        "Ming raised her brows, surprised at this new revelation. \"Really?\" Hope filled her voice. \"Then she can live? How about you?\"",
        "Bobby took a sip and grimaced. \"I don't think so. Your wounds healed quickly, but mine took too long. My body's spirit was most likely gone. As long as the soul stays near the body, you can get a quicker effect from the nanites. It feeds them.\"",
        "\"Soul? Nanites?\" Ming asked, touching her chest. \"Small robots are floating around my blood? Barbie said something similar, but do you expect me to believe that?\" Panic welled up again, and she took a sip of coffee. The familiar action stabilized her, but it wasn't enough. She needed a piece of paper and a pencil.",
        "\"Maybe. The idea is as good as any. I'm not quite sure what was in the code I programmed, what with that piece of garbage in the window and the thing Barbie sent; everything got all mixed up. The last time I used this was to erase my memory of how to code, so I wasn't at my best at the police station. The piece of shit was probably buggy as hell. The block is gone, but that's not a good thing. I didn't want to ever do anything like this again.\"",
        "Bobby crossed her arms. \"I thought I could put everything back the way it was, but using the code is addictive, and it tends to write itself.\" She spat on the floor. \"I'd forgotten why I'd locked it away, but coming here freed all of those memories.\" She slammed her fist against the table, almost knocking over the coffee. Grabbing a towel, she wiped up the spill and the spit.",
        "Ming put some sugar in her coffee. \"Why'd you block your memory? I think it'd be cool to travel in time.\" She stirred the drink and put the spoon on the saucer. \"As long as I didn't have to share a dead body.\" She gave a nervous laugh and glanced around the kitchen for a pencil.",
        "\"That's because you don't know the cost.\" Bobby sipped her coffee. \"Every time you change something with the code, there is a price to pay. The code mitigates costs but doesn't eliminate them. The first few times I used it, the cost was so small, I had no idea. It wasn't until Vlad started using it to sneak around in history that I caught on.\"",
        "\"Please, tell me.\" Ming's fingers twitched. She was jonesing for a pencil to write everything down.",
        "Bobby looked out the window and took a deep breath. \"Well, this all started about five years ago when my name was Petor...\"",
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "5 years ago (201X)",
        "\"What do you think you're doing, Petor?\" Vlad said, wiping his revolver down with a rag. \"After you finish the job, you can't keep the gun. You have to toss it.\"",
        "Petor looked up from the computer at his twin. \"I will, brother, but this guy had some great videos.\" He flipped the laptop around and showed Vlad. \"Look! This must be an underground concert. I've never seen Crue looking so good.\" He turned the computer back and patted his pants. \"Fuck!\"",
        "\"What is it?\" Vlad dropped the rag he was using and picked up the gun again. \"Somebody here?\"",
        "\"No. I forgot to bring my memory stick. I can't download this video. There's some sort of computer code with it, too.\" Petor frowned. \"I wanted to look at the whole thing. The quality is excellent.\"",
        "Vlad scowled and picked up the rag again. \"Forget the computer. We have to destroy it anyway. You know what Gregory said. 'No evidence.' You don't want Ivan involved, do you?\"",
        "\"Don't worry. He'll never know.\" Petor closed the computer. He pulled out a plastic bag and a pair of branch clippers for a bonsai tree. Going to the body, he cut off the index finger and stuck it in the bag.",
        "Vlad scrunched his nose. \"Gregory just needed a picture. What are you doing?\"",
        "\"This is for the password lock. I can't use his eyes. Somebody shot him in the right one,\" he said, grimacing at Vlad.",
        "His brother just shook his head and continued wiping his gun. Petor put the plastic bag and the computer in his backpack and picked up his gun. He borrowed Vlad's rag and wiped his piece off. He was going to have a good time tonight.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "19XX",
        "\"What does a Motley Crue video have to do with time travel and me being stuck here?\" Ming asked. \"I know you like the music.\" She was cleaning the blood smear on the floor while wearing large yellow rubber gloves. The paper towel was already soaked through, but Ming didn't want to use a cloth that could be traced back to her. It felt wrong to manipulate evidence like this.",
        "\"I'm getting there. However, we should find out when we are,\" Bobby said, flipping through some newspaper in the pile by the door. \"As I was saying...\"",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "201X",
        "\"If you could take your eyes away from the computer and help me survey the target, I'm sure Gregory would be happy,\" Vlad's sarcasm pierced Petor's fog.",
        "\"Huh? What? Oh yeah. The target.\" Petor rubbed his eyes to get the sleep out of them. \"Give it up. He's in the middle of the American embassy. There's no way we can get in there.\" He turned back to the computer. Something about this code was calling to him the more he stared at it.",
        "\"Gregory won't accept that excuse, and you know how Ivan deals with failure. Why the hell did you bring that thing with you anyway?\" Vlad asked, pointing to the computer. \"It's not like you'll kill him with it, is it?\" He scoffed.",
        "\"Har. It's like you and jelly beans. I know about the secret bag in your socks. Keep the surveillance. Let me know when you want to switch off.\" Petor turned back to the computer and ignored Vlad's sigh. He was onto something here. Putting on a pair of headphones, he started his new favourite Crue single, a recording from an underground concert Sixx had given a few years ago. He'd heard about it on the web, but there was no official copy anywhere. After he found the first bootleg, he looked everywhere for the others, but it was useless. It wasn't until he tried entering what he wanted in the final prompt line of the code that everything changed. At the time, it was just a lark. He didn't expect anything of it. When he'd hit enter, a bright light flashed through his screen. He'd thought the machine was broken, but when it faded, nothing had changed.",
        "The next day, the target he was trailing wandered into a used CD and book store, Petor followed him and started browsing to blend in, and there the recording was. He couldn't believe it had worked. It was a gift from the gods. He'd bought it and rushed home, forgetting all about his job. It was probably a bust anyway. Nobody bought CDs anymore.",
        "Luckily, Vlad had been following from a different direction, but it was close. They almost lost the target. Vlad was pissed and threatened to snap the disk in two. Usually, he didn't care what Petor did on stakeouts, but if they had lost the man, Gregory would have taken their balls. Petor promised never to do it again and to give Vlad all the bonuses they'd receive this time and the next to get the single back.",
        "Ever since Petor had found the computer with that first special single on it, he had become obsessed. He couldn't remember who the target was, but that wasn't important. He'd started working on the new code, taking apart each section and testing how it worked. Scouring over the comments to find any secrets behind it. Each time he examined a line, the writer stared back at him. It was so familiar. Part of the time, it was as if he were the writer, but then something would jump out at him, and he was blown away. He could never create anything like this. It seemed to do the impossible. It could rewrite space and time, pulling things from the past into the future and reshaping reality, as long as the parameters were clearly defined. Whoever designed it was a genius and crazy. There was no mention of the cost either, but there had to be something.",
        "He'd tested it with the CD. Now it was time to try something bigger. With Niki Sixx's drum solo echoing in his head, Petor typed in the name of the American diplomat, added an accidental trip down the stairs and finished it off with a gunshot by the bodyguard assigned to protect him. He hit enter.",
        "Three hours later, Vlad was snoring, and the American embassy was silent. It had failed. Something was missing. Petor scratched his head and stared at the computer. The code was displaying an invalid message. Petor searched through the code but couldn't find what was wrong. Vlad snorted and turned over. \"Must be nice to sleep when I'm dying here,\" he mumbled. \"Why did the CD work and not this?\" Petor looked out at the American embassy and sighed. The building wasn't going to suddenly open up and let him in.",
        "\"Stupid American. Why'd you have to cheat Gregory?\" He drummed his fingers on the windowsill. \"He doesn't like to lose.\" Petor watched the guards pass notes to each other, and it clicked.",
        "\"Of course. The programming notes,\" he gasped. \"Not everyone does it, but there might be something here to explain what I did wrong.\" He went back through the comments in the previous notes and put in Sixx's drum solo again.",
        "\"Shut up over there,\" Vlad said, throwing a pillow. \"I'm trying to sleep.\"",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "19XX",
        "\"I set it up so that at the next dawn, a car would backfire outside. The noise would cause the security to check it out. This left the target exposed as he headed down to breakfast and vulnerable to a sniper, which Vlad took care of,\" Bobby said to Ming as he sat at the table. \"After the success with the CD and the hit, I realized I could shape reality somewhat, but I couldn't force it to do things reality didn't want to do.\"",
        "Ming stared at him, pulling back. \"Are you telling me a computer code helped you assassinate Jym Blyant four years ago? I heard about his death. There was no way anybody could have breached the security in London.\"",
        "\"Yes. Gregory was happy too. He gave us a month off and a bonus, which I gave to Vlad.\" Bobby took a sip of the coffee and opened the newspaper. \"It's February 16th, 1947. Looks like Bugsy Siegel will be reopening The Flamingo soon.\"",
        "Ming grabbed the paper. \"Bugsy Siegel? But he dies next month. We're in 1947? How?\" She stuck her finger in Bobby's face. \"You said you'd tell me how we travelled through time and space. Finish the story.\"",
        "Ming's eyes were starting to bug out. She'd found some paper, but it wasn't enough. She couldn't accept that this was happening.",
        "\"Take it easy. I'm getting there. But first, we have to deal with him?\" Bobby pointed his finger at the bedroom. The young man he'd knocked out had come to and was inching his way into the kitchen. Ming slapped her hand to her head, hyperventilating.",
        "\"Why didn't we hear anything?\" she asked.",
        "Bobby shrugged, \"How should I know?\" She picked up a frypan and stepped over to the young man.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "201X",
        "\"Why won't you use it again, Petor? Gregory is waiting for results,\" Vlad said, hands on his hips. He was standing over Petor's bed.",
        "Petor blinked his eyes and shoved the pillow over his head. He waved Vlad away. \"I thought you had enough of screwing up when we spent a week as kids in the Soviet era,\" he said through the muffled material. \"If you had just left it alone,\" he trailed off. \"You're lucky I found that LP recording, or we'd still be stuck there running from the baba yaga.\"",
        "\"Too many 'ifs', brother. I admit, getting stuck in 1960 Poland was not my idea, but I believe in you.\" Vlad leaned forward and shook Petor. \"What you did with the diplomat was inspired. Gregory wants more, and we can't disappoint him.\"",
        "\"I'll think about it. Now leave me alone. I have to get ready for my date with Sasha tonight.\" Petor burrowed himself into the covers of his bed. He heard Vlad leave the room and uncovered his head. He stared at the door and reached under the bed to pull out his computer, setting it on the bed.",
        "\"Vlad doesn't get it. He doesn't see the danger behind this thing,\" he mumbled as he scrawled through the code. The beauty of the design in the code had seduced him. How the numbers worked in each section and how they all flowed together into a beautiful whole was poetry. Reality caressed him with one hand and grabbed his nut sack with the other. One wrong move and it would twist.",
        "Things were perfect before he found the note hidden in a line of text. On the very last line, there was a prompt for a name. When he entered his name, a video message came up. He'd already watched it several times but had to see it again.",
        "\"If you're watching this, Petor, your life has gone to hell. Vlad is dead, and it's the code's fault. It finally extracted the cost.\" He stared at his older face. There was grey in his hair, and he was missing his pinky finger. Petor looked at his hand and flexed. It was still there. \"This is not the first time I've used this code. Each time I've found it, I erased my memory of how to use it. It's too dangerous, and the cost is too high. I wish you'd believe me, but you have to experience the pain for yourself. Too bad others keep trying to unlock it for you. I want to tell you, but this isn't the time. Enter 'Motley Crue Bobby Warning' to find out. After that, please enter the command 'Code Forget' in the final prompt field. It's already set up and will protect you for a little while.\" Older him scoffed. \"Although I know you won't do it until it's too late.\"",
        "With a final wave, the video shut off. From what Petor could see, he was in America. \"I can feel the danger, but what do you mean by the cost?\" Petor scratched his head. Other than electricity, what did it cost to use this code?",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "February 16, 1947",
        "\"Cost? You said that before. You mean us coming here costs something?\" Ming asked. \"What was it?\"",
        "Bobby looked away. He reached for the kettle, ignoring the question. \"Do you want more coffee?\"",
        "\"Bobby?\" Ming spoke in the same tone her mother used to use when she was a child. Bobby winced and slunk down in his chair, just like Ming did when her mother was on a tear.",
        "\"Aren't I supposed to be the mother? Shouldn't you speak to me with more respect?\" She turned back to Ming and frowned.",
        "\"When you deserve it. What was the cost?\" She stared at Bobby her eyes narrowing. This feeling she could get behind. This was who she was. One problem at a time. She tapped her foot.",
        "\"We died.\"",
        "\"What?!\" Ming shot up, knocking her chair over. \"You're lying. You have to be!\"",
        "\"Back in the present, our bodies are dead. Time flows differently for us here. If we can return within the week, I can find a computer to recreate the code, or Barbie can activate the return program; we should be fine. There, only about twenty-four hours will have passed.\"",
        "Ming started pacing back and forth in the kitchen. \"You're only now telling me this?\" She thrust her hands to her sides and started punching the sides of her leg. \"What happens if we are later than that?\"",
        "\"Then say hello to your new life as Jessica Something, or you'll vanish.\" He pointed to the bathroom. The water was running in the bathtub. \"Maybe he can tell us our family names.\"",
        "Ming rubbed her eyes with her fingers and let out a deep breath. This was not how she wanted to spend her week. Pushing her skepticism and doubt to the side, she focused on Bobby's tale. It was her lifeline. \"Finish your story, please.\" Picking up the pencil she found in the drawer, she continued to write everything Bobby was saying.",
        "\"I'm almost done. Anyway, I decided to ignore the warning I'd sent myself, as the me who recorded it knew I would, and used the code one last time...\"",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "201X",
        "\"Come on, Petor, finish up your work. I have some important news to tell you.\"",
        "Sasha said. They were video chatting while Petor was searching for a way to get to the target. Gregory was already upset at how long it was taking and was sending Ivan to join them in South Korea to 'encourage a better result'. As if the pungent smell of kimchi wasn't incentive enough.",
        "\"I'll be done soon. I just have to get through coding this program,\" Petor said. \"It's proving tricky. I think I've included an extra space somewhere and got to crawl through it line by line.\"",
        "Snort! \"Sorry. I wasn't listening,\" Sasha said. \"Whenever you talk about code, I tend to fall asleep.\"",
        "Petor smiled. \"I can always count on you to set me straight.\"",
        "\"That's what I'm here for.\" He heard a bell through the phone. \"Hold on. I'll be back soon.\" She left to get the door.",
        "\"No rush.\" Petor scratched his head, and it came to him. Someone had paid Gregory a shit-ton of money to eliminate the head of a South Korean conglomerate. The problem was the security. There had already been three attempts on the man's life in the last two years. So, the target was surrounded by a layer of armed guards at all times. He went to and from work in armoured cars and never took the same route two days in a row. Petor had been in Seoul for the last two weeks, but still couldn't figure out how to get to him. Vlad had scouted the office, but nothing was getting in.",
        "In the present.",
        "There was a funeral that the Korean CEO was scheduled to go to next week. It had been in the papers, and when Petor had hacked into the target's calendar before the firewall kicked him out. It was perfect. He could jump there, kill him and jump back. He just needed to create a loop. He'd never been to the future, but how difficult could it be?",
        "\"I'll talk to you later, Sasha,\" he said to his girlfriend and hung up. She'd call back after she finished cursing his name, but he needed to concentrate on this. Sweat dripped off his forehead as he planned out the movement. \"This is going to take time.\"",
        "Three days later, Petor looked up. Vlad was sleeping across the room, clutching a bag of jelly beans. He was leaning against the wall, snoring.",
        "\"Vlad! Wake up!\" he shouted.",
        "\"What?\" his brother snorted and rubbed his eyes.",
        "\"I'm ready to execute the plan.\" He handed his brother a timer. \"I'm going to set it for four hours. When I hit start, you do the same with the timer. When it hits zero, push the Enter button. You miss it, and I'll probably be dead. Got it?\"",
        "\"Perfect. Good luck, brother.\" Vlad gave Petor the thumbs up.",
        "Petor took a deep breath and hit Enter.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "February 16, 1947",
        "\"Is that it?\" Ming asked.",
        "The young man was thrashing in the bathroom, splashing water all over the floor. It was time to get out of this place. She shivered. When Bobby said Jessica's spirit was here, Ming couldn't stop imagining it was looking over her shoulder, demanding her body back. The guilt was going to kill her. She had to do something.",
        "\"No. I was able to go through time and take over the dead body at the funeral, but it had already been embalmed and was difficult to control.\" Bobby shrugged. \"Anyway, after the panic subsided, I was able to kill the target, and Vlad pushed the button in time before they chopped off my head. When I woke up, I was slumped over my computer. Vlad was pounding my back and smiling. Two days later, the man's death was all over the news.\" Bobby grimaced. \"The zombie wasn't.\"",
        "Bobby stood up and went to the stove. He grabbed the kettle and poured himself a new cup of coffee.",
        "\"That's your fourth cup.\" Ming took it away from her and led her back to the table. \"Please, what happened?\"",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "201X",
        "'Motley Crue Bobby Warning.' Petor entered it into the same place he'd entered his name. He wanted to know what it was.",
        "Nikki Sixx came on screen and plucked his guitar string. He faced the camera and tipped his hand to his forehead. \"You sure you want me to read this?\"",
        "There was a muffled yes off-screen.",
        "Nikki sighed and faced the camera again. \"Hey, Petor. You had to fucking use the code to travel in time again, didn't you? The future, right?\"",
        "Petor's eyes bugged out, and he grabbed the screen. \"How?\"",
        "\"Listen, you piece of shit. You tried to warn yourself, and it failed like you knew it would. Here's the thing. Every time you change reality, it doesn't like to change and fights back. Nature goes by many names, Gaia. Ishtar. Others lost to the mists. You can mess with the past a bit if you're careful not to make too many waves; the cost is usually borne by time. However, the future is a dangerous animal. It's like snorting chaos. You may have noticed things missing around you or other strange things you can't explain happening. Check on Vlad's favourite snack. That's reality resetting itself, and she doesn't play nice.\" He played a quick riff on his guitar. \"Also, check on your girlfriend when you get back to Russia.\" With a final riff, the video was gone.",
        "\"Sasha.\" Petor hadn't spoken to her since hanging up. He rang her from the apartment, but there was no answer.",
        "\"It's just a coincidence,\" he said and tried again.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "February 16, 1947",
        "\"That's what I kept telling myself, but I never saw her again. At first, I thought she was ghosting me, but her roommate said she'd just disappeared. One minute they were talking and the next... Poof!\" Bobby flung his fingers up in the air.",
        "\"I'm sorry, Bobby,\" Ming said, placing her hand on Bobby's shoulder.",
        "\"That wasn't the worst part.\" Bobby looked up, and tears glistened in her eyes. \"She was pregnant and had been trying to tell me that. After, I tracked down the Americans and gave myself to them. I used the code to find some of the things I caused, and it wasn't pretty. Maybe the U-2 incident. A few others, but I can't be sure. I didn't mind killing people,\" he shrugged. \"It was my job, and I was good at it. But I didn't want to hurt innocents. The cost was too much. I didn't want anything to do with the code, but as long as I stayed in Russia, Gregory would find some way to use me, especially if he found out about what I could do. He already had Ivan, but his abilities were too destructive.\"",
        "\"What do you mean?\" Ming asked. \"What can Ivan do?\"",
        "\"You saw it at my trailer and the station,\" Bobby said, shrugging. \"The Americans put me in the witness protection program, and I set the code to make me forget. I destroyed all my notes and computer and came to San Francisco.\"",
        "He raised his hands out and gestured to the 1940s kitchen. \"Now I'm here, in the body of a woman and have to find a way back home before the week is out or we'll be stuck here for the rest of our lives.\"",
        "\"You mentioned Vlad's snack. Why?\" Ming asked.",
        "Bobby went sheepish. \"A small thing, easy to miss. Vlad used to love jelly beans. He'd sneak them on every mission. One day, he started snorting caramels. When I called him on it, he said I was delusional. That was the final kicker.\"",
        "Ming stared into her coffee and listened to the young man struggling in the bathroom, knocking against the tub. On the radio was Prisoner of Love by Perry Como. This was not how she expected to spend her life.",
        "A crashing noise from the bathroom drew their attention. It sounded like the young murderer was breaking the shower. Bobby picked up the frying pan and went back into the bathroom. Ming sat at the table and gripped the sides to keep the room from spinning away. She stared at the paper, hoping for Al to suddenly appear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 16,
      "title": "Chapter 16",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "10:30 am",
        "It took them an hour to get to Dr. Slazney's pharmacy in the strip mall outside the city. Dean had a good feeling about this place. Its vanilla white image had to be hiding a secret. Something was going to turn up here, he could sense it. It was a small tingling, centred in his stomach and radiating out. He hated this feeling most of all. He felt just like this when he first met his ex-wife. It's what led him to his marriage and why he didn't see the cracks in it for so long when the feeling turned.",
        "Dean glanced at his watch and twisted his hands on the steering wheel. They had no time for this. They had wasted almost eleven hours and were still nowhere closer to finding the computer. Ming needed him to go faster. He couldn't lose her. He still hadn't figured out what she was to him.",
        "\"Before you get out, you might want to wipe your face,\" Dean said to Barbie, \"It's still covered in blood.\"",
        "\"Thank you. I'd forgotten about that.\" Barbie said, working the tooth back into her jaw. She spent the whole drive cleaning it off.",
        "Shaking his head and looking away from the absurdity, Dean got out of the car. \"She's nothing, but not consistent,\" he sighed. Approaching the darkened office, he pounded on the glass. It said 'Stanley's' on the sign. Bobby said it was the doctor's little joke. Dean couldn't get it. He peered inside, but couldn't see anybody moving, although there was a light in the back.",
        "\"The doc ain't been back in three days,\" a voice said from behind him. Dean turned around and met an older woman with long pink hair, smoking a cigarette. The scent of the smoke sent waves of nausea mixed with desire throughout Dean. He needed a smoke and was out of candy. She was wearing old jeans and a faded pink T-shirt. Dean couldn't tell if the hair was real or not, but based on the lines around her eyes and neck, she was probably pushing fifty. She started hacking at her hand. \"Sorry, got me a dust allergy.\"",
        "\"Do you know Dr. Slazney?\" Dean asked, rubbing his nose to clear the smoke. Barbie stepped up beside him.",
        "\"Know him?\" she scoffed. \"He's been my doctor for the last three years.\" She took a drag on her cigarette. \"' Course, he's been acting squirrely recently, driving away some of the regulars. Said his big retirement plans were about to pay off.\"",
        "\"I see. Thank you,\" Dean said, raising his hand.",
        "\"Jillian,\" the woman said, ignoring it. \"I don't trust strange hands.\" Her eyes narrowed. \"Who are you?\"",
        "\"Detective Lifante, LVPD.\" Dean pulled out his badge. \"I'm following up on a tip.\"",
        "\"Is he in some sorta trouble? I've been coming here for the last two days. I need him to fill in my prescription paperwork for my comp.\" She started hacking again.",
        "\"I don't know, ma'am. That's what we're here to find out.\" He turned back to the door and peered in.",
        "\"I checked around the back as well, to see if his door was locked, and it smelled really bad,\" Jillian said. \"I think he's got a sewer leak. Musta took off.\" She waved and headed into the MacDonalds.",
        "Dean nodded and went around to the side entrance. He put his hand on the wooden door, took a sniff and wrinkled his nose. It smelt of rotten meat and stale urine. \"A dead body,\" he muttered. \"Dammit!\" He tried the door, but it was locked.",
        "Pulling out his phone, he dialled the station. \"This is Dean Lifante, badge number 745253. I'm in front of a pharmacy in the Moonbeam strip mall named Stanley's. There is some suspicious activity happening here and a possible four-one-nine. The building is locked, but I'm attempting to gain entry by force. Will update after checking out the situation.\" He hung up.",
        "\"Suspicious activity?\" Barbie asked, coming up beside him. She sounded confused. \"Why the fib?\"",
        "\"I needed an excuse to get into the place, and the smell is indicative of a dead body,\" Dean said. \"I have a few minutes before dispatch responds to check it out.\"",
        "He stepped back and gestured to the doorknob.",
        "\"Yes. What?\" Barbie asked, crossing her arms.",
        "\"I need you to open the door, please.\"",
        "\"That's called breaking and entering. I don't think I should do that. My Handler would get upset,\" Barbie said, putting her hands on her hips.",
        "Dean rolled his eyes and put his hands together. \"Please, for Bobby?\"",
        "Barbie scrunched up her face, looked left, then right and lowered her shoulders, with an exaggerated sigh. \"Okay. For the Maker. Besides, you said please.\" She grabbed the door, took a deep breath, and yanked. The door resisted. Barbie frowned, braced her feet on either side of the door, grabbed the knob and twisted, forcing it open. \"That was harder than I thought.\" She stared at her hands.",
        "A stench of rotten meat and offal, with an undercurrent of peppermint in the back room, hit them like a tax man. You couldn't get away from it. He covered his nose with his sleeve. \"Dammit. Wait out here. This is police business now,\" he said to Barbie.",
        "He stuck his head in the open door and looked around. The back room was all clear. A few potpourri bags were hanging from the sides of the shelves, giving off a whiff of peppermint. They were doing nothing to hold back the foul order, though. Stepping through the door, he hugged the wall and moved to the office area, following the dead smell. In the first room in the back, he found the body on the floor, behind the desk. The deceased was a male, wearing a white jacket with an ID clip on the pocket. The eyes had already sunk into the head, and the skin had dried out. Flies were hovering around the body. He brushed them away and reached into the pocket. The clip said, Dr. Richard Stanley. Ming had better not look like that. Dean gritted his teeth.",
        "Moving away from the body, Dean went to the filing cabinet with three drawers next to the desk. It was locked. Searching the desk, he found the keys. He flipped through the records until he found Bobby's under 'M'. Pulling it out, he checked the details. It had his address, the prescription and payment information, but not much else. Putting it back, he flipped through the other files in the cabinet and found a few more names. He found Chester Punk from the squeegee place and Yichen from the Shujing. There were some names he'd never seen before, as well. Several had lines through them, but many didn't. In the second drawer, one name stood out.",
        "\"It can't be.\" He didn't want to look in the file. Zacoski wasn't a common name, but there were a few people who shared it. Dean's hand shook as it hovered over the file.",
        "\"Did you find anything?\" Barbie asked, coming through the door and pulling Dean away from his dilemma. \"Hey, who is the corpse?\" She held her nose and peered at the man.",
        "\"I thought I told you to wait outside?\"",
        "\"I couldn't just stand there. My nanites are breaking down. Opening that door took the last of my strength. Besides, I did break the door, so I thought I might as well go all Fujiko,\" Barbie said, rubbing her hands and scrunching her brows together. \"You know from that cinematic masterpiece of Japanese art, Lupan the Third?\"",
        "\"Yeah, of course.\" He grimaced. Where was she getting these things? \"Fine,\" said Dean, slamming the door shut and handing her the ID badge. She squinted.",
        "\"Do you need glasses?\" Dean asked.",
        "\"No. It's something strange. A smell...\" She trailed off and started sniffing the corpse. Dean narrowed his eyes and continued searching the desk. Anything to avoid the cabinet. Other than the files, he couldn't find anything about the connections between Slazney and this guy besides the similar name.",
        "\"I'm going to have to call in the investigators. I can't hide this,\" he said, biting his lip. \"Unless you've found something?\"",
        "\"Maybe. Give me a few minutes.\" Barbie continued to inspect the corpse, pushing at it and sniffing.",
        "Goosebumps travelled up his arms when she did that. She'd been right about everything up to now, so he let her poke and went over to the bookshelf. There were a few awards and several books on specialty medicines, which would explain how he could make Bobby's, but nothing to explain why somebody would kill him. He stepped out of the room and found a smaller staff room. Going inside, there was a small table in the middle with four chairs, a sink and a counter with a microwave on it. A mini-fridge and a bulletin board rounded out the room. Dean went up to it and pulled down an article.",
        "\"Local Doctor Survives Collision.\"",
        "\"By Ming Na Liu.\"",
        "Dean looked up. \"Shit, this was dated three years ago.\"",
        "\"Doctor Richard Stanley was driving to work today when a semi-trailer almost ended his life. He was thrown from his vehicle, through the front glass, but miraculously landed in a dune. Apart from a few cuts and scrapes, he survived virtually unhurt. Witnesses at the scene say they couldn't believe it and thought he was dead. As one witness said, 'God was with Dr. Stanley this day.'\"",
        "The article went on.",
        "\"I know what happened,\" Barbie said from the doorway. \"But I don't know if you'll believe me.\"",
        "\"Just tell me.\" Dean put the article back on the bulletin board.",
        "\"When Slazney jumped into Stanley's body, it left a smell like hot metal burning in acid on a summer day. It is difficult to catch if you're not familiar with it and soon disappears in the living, but remains in the dead.\"",
        "\"Huh?\" Dean's face fell. \"Explain with more words, please. I don't understand what you mean.\"",
        "Barbie grimaced. \"Fine. With the code in play, it's possible he jumped bodies. However, it's difficult to go into living ones. The soul, in living bodies, forces the extra soul out. With dead ones, it's like putting on a meat suit. In that case, the new soul heals the body with the nanites that follow the soul through time from the future. In most cases, it can bring a body back to life. That activity causes the smell.\"",
        "\"Nanites?\" He still had trouble wrapping his head around that and would think about tiny robots later. Pointing to the article, he asked, \"Then Slazney jumped into Stanley three years ago and took over his life?\"",
        "\"Looks that way, but it was incomplete. Something went wrong, and the smell should have disappeared by now. He must have been looking for a new body.\" Barbie stood back with a smug look on her face.",
        "\"So, if we look at recent accidents and deaths and compare them with the names in the filing cabinet, we might find a connection to Slazney,\" Dean said. He pulled out his phone and paused for a moment. \"However, this article is over three years old. Slazney could have been planning this for a long time.\"",
        "\"That's true; however, it's possible he was split into multiple bodies at the same time, but it would put a great strain on the planet,\" Barbie said. \"The smell from that one is wrong.\"",
        "\"What kind of strain?\"",
        "\"The Maker could never figure out the reason for global warming.\"",
        "\"I can't believe I'm even considering this.\" Dean scrunched his face. \"Dammit!\" He went back to the first room and yanked open the filing cabinet. He took out his phone and snapped a picture of each of the names in it, including Jillian.",
        "\"What are you doing?\" Barbie asked.",
        "\"I found his list of names. Some may be regular clients, but others could be the bodies he's using.\" He counted the names and closed the door. \"There are over fifty names here.\" Dean hit the top of the filing cabinet with his fist. \"There's no way we can get through all of them in twelve hours.\"",
        "Dean hovered his hand over the cabinet and closed his eyes. His instincts, when he let them, never failed him. When he ignored them, everything went to shit. He pulled out three files and laid them on the desk. Opening his eyes, he sighed.",
        "\"I thought so the first time,\" Dean said. \"I guess I just didn't want to believe it.\"",
        "\"Who are you talking to?\" Barbie grabbed the files and read the names off of them. \"Lee Chang, Chester Punk Sr., Bartholomew Zacoski.\" She opened them up and scrunched her nose. \"The only thing in here is some biographical information. There's nothing of substance. Who are they?\"",
        "Dean was silent for a moment and let out a sigh. \"The Shujing owner, Squeegees R' Us,\" he said, pointing to the first two files. He paused on the third one.",
        "\"Who is it?\" Barbie asked, impressed.",
        "\"My Lieutenant,\" Dean said. He closed his eyes. It couldn't be him. Bart was his best friend and the only one who believed in him, besides Ming. He couldn't be working with Slazney."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 17,
      "title": "Chapter 17",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "February 17, 1947",
        "Ming Na waved a fan in front of her face as she pushed her way through the crowd of people. She'd read on a history blog that Vegas was a quiet city before WWII and that it couldn't handle the sudden influx of people flocking to the glitz just beginning to show. There were scores of unfinished buildings and people living on the streets. She'd walked over five already just outside their small apartment near the edge of the desert. The Asian population was almost non-existent. Being a white girl was unnatural and icky. She wanted to go back to her own skin as soon as possible. At least she was no longer startled when she looked in the mirror. She wondered how Bobby felt, a man in a woman's body.",
        "Wiping her forehead, she stared up at the new hotel being renovated. Bugsy Siegel's Flamingo. It had been completed a few months before, but the grand reopening was coming soon. Another pink-themed hotel. She was tired of the colour, but if they were here, then maybe Slazney was here as well. Bobby had been evasive on that topic.",
        "If nothing else, maybe she could meet Bugsy Siegel. The reporter in her was itching to ask him some questions. Find out some of his secrets. The idea was the only thing keeping her sane. It was a little over a month until his death, and a picture with the gangster would be a cool trophy. Maybe an interview, not that she could ever publish it except as an op-ed.",
        "\"What are you doing?\" Bobby asked, pushing her along, ignoring the whistles from the construction workers. \"This isn't the best place to stop. Besides, we need to find a computer and the Z4 doesn't exist here.\"",
        "\"What's that?\" Ming asked. She strained her neck. Even the air smelled a little better, with less car exhaust. A part of her just couldn't accept that any of this was real and kept looking for the cameras.",
        "Bobby grimaced. \"It's one of the first electronic computers in the world with the computing capability to get us home, but it's only in Europe. As it is, finding one here, if it is here, will be difficult. We need another kind of computer help.\"",
        "\"What do you mean? Where are we going?\" Ming asked.",
        "She pointed east. \"That way. While I was getting rid of Steven, I overheard some people talking about an underground Blues bar. To get there, though, is difficult for two white-bread women.\"",
        "Ming ignored what he said about Steven. She didn't want to think about Bobby killing someone. Steven had killed the bodies they were in -that was still disturbing- but killing him seemed excessive. She had fought with Bobby over what to do and won. Bobby took him out into the desert and said she let him go. Ming chose to believe that Bobby didn't kill him there, but it was going to be difficult for Steven to survive.",
        "She raised an eyebrow. \"Blues? Why do we need the Blues? I thought you needed a computer,\" Ming smiled and grabbed her pen and notebook from her bag.",
        "Bobby rolled her eyes. In the two days they had been in 1947, Ming had gotten used to thinking of the punk rocker window washer as a she. The body Bobby wore was still young and beautiful, even if she had been Jessica's mother.",
        "\"Yes, I need a computer to do the calculations, but without a copy of the code to work with, I'd be writing it from scratch, which would take years. What I have can be checked by the computers of the era, women. However, the heart of the code is the music. It's the power that drives the magic in my code. Others who live closer to the music can access the magic without the extras. For me, without Motley Crue to connect my soul to nature, the code is just numbers on a screen. Blues will hopefully work; it underpins all of their work.\"",
        "Ming stopped walking. A few people pushed past her, grumbling at the young woman standing in the middle of the street.",
        "Bobby guided her over to the side of the street, away from the press of people. \"What are you doing?\" she hissed.",
        "\"Magic? You're kidding, right? Magic isn't real,\" Ming said in a panic. Science was the guiding force of life. With the right application of logic, anything was possible. \"Time travel is science fiction. There is no such thing as magic,\" She mouthed, closing her eyes.",
        "\"I'm not kidding,\" Bobby said, bringing her face closer to Ming's. \"How do you think we got here? With just a computer code? Don't be silly,\" he scoffed. \"Even if I paid the cost with my life, there's only so much even it can do. Magic is everywhere. I just hacked it. For the real practitioner, they know how to draw it out of the air, or the water, or the blood, for the right sacrifice. I found my secret way by accident years ago, and it ruined me.\" He paused. \"You remember Ivan's humming?\"",
        "Ming nodded.",
        "\"That's how he can access his power. He discovered it by accident years ago. By humming, he can use his connection to nature to enhance his power. He had a great time using it to hoist Vlad and me around when we were children. It was like having our own Superman and Big Brother all in one. Gregory found him when Ivan was about thirteen and trained him to be his bodyguard.\" Bobby frowned. \"I still remember when they took him away. Ivan promised he'd be fine. When he returned six years later, I didn't recognize him, and Ivan had cut out his own tongue. Before he left, it was the last time I saw him smile.\" He shook his head and continued. \"Science and magic get along very well. They're both a love letter to nature, if you know how to weld them together,\" Bobby whispered.",
        "Ming looked around. Nobody was listening to them, but Bobby wasn't taking any chances.",
        "\"I guess so,\" Ming mused. She took a deep breath, let it out and jotted a few notes down on her notepad. She'd found it in Jessica's room after the first night. She looked up at her mother, Catherine. Steven had been very forthcoming when Bobby had started breaking fingers. Ming stared at the whiteness of her hand. \"Are you sure they'll be all right when we leave?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"I don't know,\" Bobby said. \"As I told you before, you healed quickly, while I took too long. Your body's soul is probably still nearby and should hang around for a few more days. Mine's most likely gone.\" Bobby started Ming forward again. \"We'll deal with that when the time comes.\"",
        "\"What's this about women being computers?\" asked Ming, but Bobby ignored the question, mumbling something about reading some history books. Ming grunted and followed.",
        "They continued east. Bobby stopped a few construction workers and asked them for directions to the speakeasy. A few waved her off. One threatened to call the police. Ming had forgotten how bad women had it in the past. Just asking for directions to the local black music bar was dangerous, especially for two white women. Most of the people couldn't believe they wanted to go there. Back in the present, she'd experienced some trouble because her parents were Chinese, and Dean had his own troubles based on his family, but not the open hostilities she was experiencing here.",
        "She became a reporter to expose the secrets of the world. To expose what she couldn't explain. She didn't believe in the power of intuition, like Dean, although she could respect it. But magic was something beyond her.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "February 17^th^, 1947",
        "Bobby stood outside a small building on a side street. Music blasted out from the closed door. He couldn't make out the words, but the beat called to him. It wasn't punk, but it pushed the butterflies down. Despite the situation and Ming's insistence on using that pronoun, he refused to think of himself as' she'. It was getting harder, though, and Ming didn't help. Every time he stared in the mirror, the older, beautiful woman with the blond hair who stared back took a piece of him, making it harder to come back. He said her soul was gone, but maybe a part of it remained. Every time Bobby looked at Ming in Jessica's body, what he could only describe as a motherly instinct coursed through him. It was unnerving.",
        "The sun had set, taking the heat from the day, and settling the dust. It had invaded his nose and rubbed his throat raw. After taking Steven out to the desert, it had gotten worse. The reporter thought he'd killed the boy, but random murder wasn't something he was comfortable doing anymore, even with the block removed.",
        "That didn't mean he left him whole.",
        "\"Is this the place?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"Yes.\" Bobby swallowed. \"Two white women, in sundresses, going into an Underground Blues bar won't end well.\" He turned to Ming. \"You can go back to the house and wait this out if you want.\"",
        "\"No! I came this far. I'm going to see it through.\"",
        "Bobby nodded and led her down the stairs. They pounded on the door, a slot opened, and the eyes behind it narrowed. \"What's some Honky bitches doing down here?\" The man said as he spat to the side, scorn radiating from him.",
        "\"We came here for the music,\" Bobby said, swaying to the beat. It was calling to him; invading his bones.",
        "\"Some mayonnaise monkeys are here? Are they looking for an Oreo?\" Another voice had replaced the first, opened the door and scoffed.",
        "This man was taller than Ivan, but not as wide. Skinny, but with muscles straining his shirt.",
        "\"This isn't a safe place for your kind, woman.\" He pointed his finger up the stairs. \"Leave.\"",
        "Ming placed her hand on his arm. Bobby covered her hand with his and faced off against the man. \"Is that Kansas Joe McCoy I hear in there?\" he said, pulling some money out of his purse. \"I have the cover charge, now let us in before he finishes the song. I've come a long way to hear him.\" He put his hands on his hips and stared. The stronger you were with men like these, the quicker they respected you.",
        "The doorman stared at the two women and smiled. \"I like 'em feisty. It makes the lovin' that much\" -- he licked his lips -- \"better.\" He took the money and stepped out of the way.",
        "\"Thank you,\" Bobby said and pushed Ming into the bar.",
        "\"What the hell was that?\" Ming whispered. \"Are you trying to get us killed?\"",
        "\"Speak up! It's louder than a chainsaw through a skull in here. I had to show him we meant business. Besides, it was fun. I like letting loose once in a while.\"",
        "Ming tried not to gag.",
        "They stepped into a dark room covered with a thin haze of smoke. The corners were shrouded in darkness, and most of the tables were filled with people nursing drinks while smoke drifted to the rafters. They all swayed to the beat while listening to a black man sitting on the stage playing the guitar. The lighting in the room hid most of the people in the audience. Perfect if there was a raid.",
        "Bobby noticed the soft beat of the song and compared it to the Led Zeppelin remake from the 70s. Plant's lyrics and Bonham's drumming breathed new life into the music, but listening to the original without the scratches was breathtaking. Everything else faded away, and he couldn't take his eyes off the man.",
        "\"Is that really Kansas Joe McCoy?\" Bobby asked the man by the door.",
        "\"Yep!\" he said, moving along to the music. \"He snuck down for a couple of days and wanted to get some sessions in.\" He turned to Bobby, and his eyes went wide. \"What are a couple of Honkys doing in here?\"",
        "\"The same thing as the other ones, I'd bet,\" Bobby said, pointing to the white couples sitting at a few tables. \"Enjoying the music.\"",
        "He led Ming to an empty table near the back of the crowded bar and sat. A waiter brought him two beers. He took a sip and closed his eyes. The guitar beat flowed into him, washing away the stress from the last few days. The flight from his home and the fucked-up virus in the window, all faded. He recognized the lyrics and finger work of a master. This wasn't a chance. He needed to get a message to the man. Respect nature, and it will nudge open a door.",
        "\"What are you doing?\" Ming asked, breaking the spell. Good music was its own magic, even if there was nothing behind it. Bobby peeked at her and opened his eyes, sighing. The reporter was a tough woman, but this was something outside her range of experiences. Judging from her reaction to his mention of magic earlier, she was a nonbeliever.",
        "\"As I said, a computer alone won't get us out of here,\" he said, taking another sip. \"We need someone to play the right kind of music that'll power my code. I could do It but I need to input the right numbers at the right time while holding the correct beat. I can play, but I'm not that good. Back home, the computer battery can be a substitute if you have the right code plugged in; here, we'll need someone to help us. Someone who knows what it means to make magic. Just be glad this isn't Russia. Finding the right music there in the sixties was a nightmare.\"",
        "Kansas Joe finished his set and went to the bar to get a drink. Bobby took a swig of his beer and stood up. He went over to the bar and sat down beside the man. Kansas Joe looked Bobby up and down and scrunched his nose. \"What's a white woman doing here, all alone?\"",
        "This was the dangerous part. The last time he'd met a magic practitioner, in 1960's Berlin, the man had tried to kill him, sticking a baba-yaga on him. Musicians were easier to talk to, though. Something about the music connected their souls to the natural force powering the world.",
        "\"I need your help, Mr. McCoy,\" Bobby said, placing his hand near the singers. \"I'm in a spot of trouble.\"",
        "He smiled and shook his head. \"Sorry, lady, I'm not the right person to help you.\" He picked up his drink and left the barstool. \"Find some other stud for that.\"",
        "\"Not that kind of trouble,\" he said, following after McCoy. Bobby reached into his purse and pulled out a folded sheet of paper. \"Please look at this and tell me if you can help.\" He gave it to Kansas Joe. The man took the paper but didn't look at it and put it in his pocket. He smiled and continued back to the stage.",
        "\"What was that paper?\" Ming asked, sliding up next to Bobby.",
        "\"Before coming here, I wrote some computations and musical scores down. He should recognize the significance.\" Bobby drank the last of his beer. \"Come on. It's time to go.\"",
        "\"Don't we need him?\"",
        "\"Our numbers' on the paper. He'll contact us if he wants to help. You can't force it.\" Bobby glanced around the bar. The other patrons were not looking at them, but in an, *I saw everything you were doing, kind of way*. There was no hiding who they were here, and no way a man like Kansas Joe would help them so publicly.",
        "\"Hello, ladies,\" said a white man in a dark suit and a hat. \"Can I buy you a drink?\"",
        "\"No thanks,\" Bobby said. \"We're just leaving.",
        "\"But you just got here. Please, I insist.\"",
        "Ming tugged at Bobby's arm and whispered into his ear. \"That's Bugsy Siegel. I recognize him from the pictures.\"",
        "\"You know me? Excellent. Saves time.\" He smiled and leaned into the bar. He was wearing a pinstriped suit and set his hat on the counter. Kansas Joe started playing, \"Why Don't You Do Right,\" and Bugsy nodded along with the music. \"I was listening to some good music and wondered what these two beautiful women were doing here. They seemed so out of place.\"",
        "Bobby swayed along with the music and smiled up at Bugsy. \"I came for the music as well, but it's past my daughter's bedtime.\" He gestured to Ming. \"We have a busy day tomorrow and can't stay.\" He moved away from the bar and nodded to Bugsy. \"Thank you for the offer, Mr. Siegel, but we'll have to decline. Come on, Jessica.\"",
        "\"Slazney said you'd be stubborn,\" Bugsy said. \"And that I shouldn't take no for an answer.\" He sipped his drink.",
        "Bobby and Ming stopped and turned back to the gangster. He gave them a knowing smile and gestured to his table, where three other men and a woman were sitting.",
        "Bobby started swearing in Russian."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 18,
      "title": "Chapter 18",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "11:30 AM",
        "Pulling into the broken parking lot of Squeegees R' Us, Dean turned to Barbie. \"Ming said the manager here is a young man, so it's possible he would ignore the blood on your face.\" He handed her a cloth and pointed to the rearview mirror. \"But we don't want to tip our hand. We don't know how he's connected to Slazney, yet.\"",
        "\"Thank you,\" she said, pulling down the visor and wiping her nose. The blood had dripped onto her blouse. \"I did wipe it off. My nanites have turned off. Usually, they just repair the initial damage to the body, then go dormant to conserve energy. I've been using them too much, and it's been over fifteen hours since the Maker reset them. I could absorb some of the ambient heat to restart them, but that would require me to go into a coma while they work. I still have my training, but I can't repair myself the same way. Besides, I was expecting him to stare at my chest.\" She adjusted the tight outfit she was wearing to hike up her breasts. \"Isn't that what men in this time usually do?\"",
        "\"What do they do in your time?\" Dean sighed, regretting the questions. He was beginning to like the woman. She was beautiful, but her casual attitude towards violence and sex grated on him. After what happened with his ex-wife, he didn't trust the direct approach. It was always hiding something.",
        "\"Not something so vulgar. You went up to someone you liked and told them you liked them. Social problems became unimportant after Alaska was sold back to Russia and the Second Civil War poisoned the Great Lakes.\" She paused and frowned, slapping her head. \"I don't remember that happening. Reality waves are happening, changing things. We have to hurry.\"",
        "Dean smiled and nodded. He didn't know what to believe with her. She sounded sane one moment, even if she could do things he couldn't explain. Then something like that came out of her mouth, and he wished she would disappear.",
        "\"Let me ask the questions. Please.\" He got out of the car and opened the door to the building. A freezing wind blasted him in the face. The air-conditioner was going full blast. There was a big kick about energy efficiency in Vegas these days, but that wasn't the case here. It was a small, cramped office with one secretary, connected to a washing bay. A truck sat there through the glass doors. Stepping up to the counter, he rested his elbow on the desk, holding his badge out to show the man sitting there.",
        "\"Can I help you?\" he said.",
        "\"Yes. I'm Detective Lifante. I'd like to speak to the manager, Chip, please. We spoke on the phone yesterday.\"",
        "\"Ah, yes.\" The secretary gazed at Dean. \"Your voice matches your face perfectly. I like it.\" He winked at Dean.",
        "Dean smiled and nodded his head. Barbie came up and stood beside him, copying the same pose. Dean narrowed his eyes but ignored her. This wasn't the time to get into why copying someone wasn't polite.",
        "\"One moment. He's in a meeting with an employee,\" the secretary said, turning back to his computer. He pulled up a YouTube animated video and started lip-singing along with it.",
        "\"This isn't right!\" A door crashed open, and a woman walked out. A strong spicy scent of cologne burst out with her. She wore jeans and a T-shirt, but her hair was short, and she wasn't wearing any makeup. \"I told you not to call me by my dead name. It's Kat, and I go by They and Them!\"",
        "\"You are Catherine in the system, and that's how you'll stay in mine until you change it,\" said the male voice from the room. \"You want to be called 'Kat', fine. But get the paperwork done and submit it to me.\"",
        "She... No, not she, Dean corrected himself. They stormed out of the office, past the two standing at reception. Kat was furious. Their scowl sucking in all the energy from the room, lowering the temperature a good five degrees. They locked eyes with Dean and Barbie and paused. Their scowl turned to slight confusion as they moved to the wash bay connected by the other door. Dean watched Kat turn back and look at them through the glass.",
        "\"Sorry, you had to hear that. HR problems,\" Chip said, stepping up to Dean and shaking his hand. \"You must be Detective Lifante. Who's your friend?\" He stood in front of Barbie and smiled. \"Chester Punk. Nice to meet you.\" He stuck out his hand. The spicy smell was digging into Dean's eyes. He rubbed his hand, the smell sticking to it. He couldn't feel anything else about the young man, though. His instincts were silent. He narrowed his eyes. They were never silent.",
        "\"This is my partner, Barbie,\" Dean said, running his hand down the side of his pants to get the smell off.",
        "Barbie smiled and showed Chip her teeth, with a missing front tooth in her lower jaw. He drew back, losing his smile, but quickly came forward and put his arm around her shoulder.",
        "\"Please step into my office.\"",
        "\"This is bordering on sexual harassment,\" Barbie said. \"Will you please remove your arm before I have to break it? And what's that smell? My nose is burning.\"",
        "Chip's face turned white, and he stepped back, raising both of his hands in the air. \"Sorry about that. I spilled my aftershave on myself today.\" Adjusting his collar, he turned to Dean. \"What can I do for you, Detective?\"",
        "Dean needed to change the mood. It was difficult to get a read on Chip. He went from playboy wannabe to serious in the space of a heartbeat. \"I believe you spoke to a colleague of mine yesterday, Ming Na Liu. She mentioned how helpful you were to our investigation.\"",
        "\"Yes, Ming Na. How is she? She promised to write a feature on me.\" Chip sat down at his desk and put his feet on the corner. \"Help yourself to a caramel. I just replenished my stash.\" He pointed to an open jar on the desk. After getting shut down by Barbie, he was trying to show he was still in charge. Dean couldn't stand people like him. You had to stroke their ego and make them think they were important to move the investigation forward.",
        "Dean and Barbie sat down in the chairs in front of the desk. \"She's hard at work on that and hopes I could speak with your father directly about his business partner.\"",
        "Chip put his feet down on the floor and opened a book on his desk. \"Anything for her and Bobby. He's my best washer. He never complains, unlike some people.\" Chip tisked. \"As for my father, he isn't feeling very well and doesn't like talking to strangers.\" Chip shrugged his shoulders. \"I asked him who our partner was, and he sent me this number.\" He passed a piece of paper to Dean. \"Dad said he'd only met him once when he was setting up the business.\" Chip stood up. \"Sorry, I can't be of more help.\" He reached over and grabbed Dean's hand, giving it another shake.",
        "\"No, this is great. Thank you, Mr. Punk. It's been a big help.\" Dean stood up and placed his hand over Chip's. \"This is a huge break in our investigation.\" Picking up the number, he tucked it into his shirt pocket and left the room. The smell was causing his eyes to water.",
        "Barbie followed behind, bumping into Dean as they exited the office and stepped back into the blazing sun. After the frigid hell of the office, the heat felt good, but he couldn't get rid of the smell of Chip's cologne.",
        "\"Why was it so cold in there?\" asked Barbie. \"My nipples were standing up. Also, what was with that spicy smell? It plugged up my nose. I've of a mind to claim smell harassment!\"",
        "Dean closed his eyes, shut out her voice and took a deep breath to remove the last vestiges of spice from his nose. He also had to leave the air-conditioning on in his place, just like this. If he didn't, the smell from the bodies would have overwhelmed the neighbours in hours. Ming would have come back to a bloated meat sack. His electricity bill next month was going to be insane.",
        "\"That's not important,\" he mumbled to himself.",
        "\"You talk to yourself a lot,\" Barbie said. \"You could talk to me. I'm a certified counsellor in Greater Vegas.\"",
        "\"Really?\" Dean raised an eyebrow. \"What kind of counsellor?\"",
        "Barbie smiled. \"I'm a certified seventh-dan Akido-therapist. I will beat the pain out of you.\"",
        "Dean took a deep breath and pulled out the number. \"Maybe later. We have this to deal with first.\"",
        "\"I can't wait. Maybe we can find a connection to the Maker,\" Barbie said, bouncing on her heels.",
        "\"Just wait. If I do this, we need to set up a trace first. I'm not going to call the number and have them skip out on me.\" He paused. \"But maybe there's something I can do.\" He scanned the street and located an old pay phone. Opening the door, he went inside and pulled out the number. It had a local area code, so it wouldn't be difficult. Putting coins in the slot, he dialled. The person on the other end answered after three rings.",
        "\"S-Class Consultants. When the A class isn't good enough, how may I help you?\" a young female voice said. Dean could tell she was reading from a script.",
        "\"Hi, I'm calling to talk about your insurance provider,\" Dean said, affecting a bad Indian accent.",
        "\"Sorry. We're not interested. Bye.\" The woman hung up.",
        "\"Excellent.\" Dean hung up the receiver and stepped out of the booth.",
        "\"What was that all about?\" Barbie asked, hands on her hips.",
        "Dean wrote the name S-Class Consultants on the back of the paper Chip gave him and put the number away in his wallet. \"There are many Indian call centers buying stacks of numbers. They call people trying to sell insurance. Most people hang up and forget them. They won't remember us, and now we have their name. I can track them down with that.\"",
        "\"The past is so strange. You hide your feelings and lie all the time. Nanites make everything so much better. In the future, after taking the Canadian healthcare system over, everybody was much happier.\"",
        "\"The Canadian healthcare system?\" Dean asked.",
        "\"Yes. They didn't need it after the civil war there. Nobody was left except the maple syrup traders.\" Barbie shook her head and stepped back. They returned to Dean's car, but the person arguing with Chip stepped out of the wash bay and waved them over.",
        "\"Yes. What can I do for you?\" Dean asked. \"Kat, right?\"",
        "They nodded. \"You're Dean Lifante, aren't you? Ming Na Liu's friends?\"",
        "\"Yes. How do you know her?\" Dean asked.",
        "\"I helped her wash the windows at the Shujing the other day.\" They looked around, checking the door to the office. They licked their lips and turned back to Dean. \"I thought she mentioned you, but part of me never believed her.\"",
        "Dean smiled and stepped back. His gut was telling him not to run away, but his head was screaming, warning.",
        "\"For years, my grandmother had been going on about this letter her mother left her. It had advice about what to do and what to avoid. It made our family a lot of money. She passed a few years ago and left my mother all her things. She didn't care much about it. She was too busy raising six kids, but enjoyed the money. In Grandma Jessica's things, there was a sealed letter addressed to a Dean Lifante.\" They handed Dean a letter. \"When I saw your name on the news with Bobby, I started carrying it with me, just in case. This is for you.\"",
        "\"Why? How did you know I would be here today?\"",
        "Kat shrugged their shoulders. \"I didn't. In the letter my grandmother had, it only mentions your name. I had a big fight with my family and left it there. I'm the youngest and only girl. When I decided to transition, my mother couldn't accept it. She is over sixty and pretty set in her ways. Grampa kept it and sent it to me when I got the job here. He knew something was going to happen. He was always a bit cagy.\" Kat smiled. \"I didn't need the money, which is good. This place pays crap. I was just curious who would get the letter.\"",
        "Dean looked at the letter. It was in Ming's handwriting. He'd recognize her writing anywhere by the way she curled her 'Ds'. He ran his finger along the back and flicked the open flap. \"It's not sealed anymore. Did you read it?\"",
        "\"Of course. I don't want to believe everything in it, but it was fun, if it's true. It also explains a few things about Bobby and how my family got its money.\" They looked around and whispered, \"Don't read it here, though. You don't know who's watching.\"",
        "\"Thank you.\" Dean put it in his pocket. \"I'll read it later. What are you going to do now?\"",
        "Kat smiled. \"I've done what I set out to do. Now I'm going to quit this joke of a job and head back to my real passion, following Baby Metal. I've even been learning Japanese to understand their songs better.\" They waved and yanked open the door to the office.",
        "\"I like her,\" Barbie said. \"She's cool. She would fit in back home.\"",
        "Dean didn't correct Barbie. He barely understood the whole pronoun thing himself. After the sensitivity training at work, he tried to follow what people wanted, but it usually left him shaking his head.",
        "Getting in the car, Dean opened the letter. From the first word, his hands started trembling.",
        "\"What is it?\" Barbie asked. \"Who's the letter from?\"",
        "He handed it to her,",
        "*Dear Lifante,*",
        "*If you're reading this, then I survived. This is Ming Na Liu. Bobby and I landed in a mother-daughter pair in 1947 Vegas. I have no idea what's going to happen to me here. I'm writing to tell you that you have to open Bobby's computer and bring up the program 'Death Metal'. The computer password is 'I will see Mickey 9'. Before the twenty-four-hour mark, you need to type in 'Return' in the final prompt line and hit enter. From there, we should be able to come back. However, if you fail, then I will either live out my life or fade from this body. According to Bobby, we can't stay longer than a week in this time before it's impossible to return. While I'm here, I plan on leaving some information for these people. They've had a tough life. I hope this letter will make it to you, but even if it doesn't, I just wanted to let you know I don't think your instincts are always wrong. I can't explain how I got here, but I've seen things now that are making me question everything I've ever known. Forgive me. I'm rambling now.*",
        "Barbie turned to Dean and slapped the letter. \"I knew she liked you. When you see her again, say how you feel, sheesh!\" She continued reading.",
        "*Bobby has a plan to get us back. If it works, we'll see each other soon. If it fails, I don't want to go without saying this: I care for you.*",
        "*Please don't forget to use the computer, or I'll have to kick your ass. I can do it too, even if I have to come back as a ghost from '47.*",
        "*Love Ming.*",
        "\"We know where they are now. That's great.\" Barbie was smiling as she put the letter back in the envelope. \"Now all we need to do is get the computer.\" She slapped Dean on the shoulder.",
        "He just stared ahead, gripping the steering wheel. \"Let's head back to the station.\"",
        "They needed the computer, but they only had less than thirteen hours to find it and no idea where it was. Chip was a dead end, but maybe his father would be more useful. They also had to track down S-Class Consulting and find any connection to Slazney. Either it or Yichen were their best bet.",
        "*Zacoski couldn't be involved, could he*?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 19,
      "title": "Chapter 19",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "February 17^th^, 1947",
        "Bobby smiled at Bugsy and remembered he was a woman and beautiful. He didn't know how old this body was, but he'd spent some time admiring it in the mirror when he got dressed. Unlike Ming, he wasn't concerned with modesty. Besides, this wasn't the first time he'd been stuck as a woman. This one was too skinny for his taste but attractive with a well-toned body. He preferred women with more meat, though. Whenever he read books about men switching bodies with women, he always scoffed at the awkwardness of a man looking at the female body and dealing with toilet issues. After spending two days as a burnt corpse, anything was better.",
        "According to the history books, Bugsy Siegel was a playboy and loved to chat up any beautiful thing. Bobby smiled at the gangster and placed his hand on Bugsy. \"So how do you know this Slazney?\"",
        "\"I met him a few years ago. We got off to a rocky start, but he gave some great advice. Told me to invest in the Flamingo,\" Bugsy said, wrinkling his nose. \"Wish I'd listened to him when he said I should go slower, but live and learn, I always say.\"",
        "\"Did he say anything about me?\" Bobby asked the gangster and glanced at the Reporter. She was fingering her pen and looking at Bugsy as if he were a piece of cheesecake.",
        "\"Only some strange people who didn't fit the atmosphere might be coming around one day. When that happened, I should drop his name and see their reaction.\"",
        "*Shit!*",
        "Bobby continued to smile and looked around at Bugsy. Several other men had already surrounded them, preventing them from running away. The other patrons had moved away from the fight, leaving a void. He needed to get out of here. He glanced at the stage. Kansas Joe was tuning his guitar, ignoring them.",
        "\"Well, now, Mr. Siegel. I don't know this Slazney. I'm sure he was a good person, but I'm just a housewife with a deep interest in the Blues,\" Bobby said, \"I came here because I heard Kansas Joe was playing, and it would have been a shame to miss him. I have nothing to hide.\" He needed to tell Ming this was a trap if she didn't already know.",
        "\"And I'm a priest,\" he scoffed at his joke and put his hand on the small of Bobby's back. He led him to his table. Bobby and Ming sat across from Bugsy, and he had his men set some drinks on the table. \"Now, please tell me the truth?\"",
        "The music started, and McCoy started to croon. \"*You Know You Done Me Wrong.*\" Like before, the music infused the room with its sound. Bugsy's men turned to the singer and swayed along with the music, ignoring the women.",
        "The beat washed over him with its message. He'd heard recordings, but hearing it live was like listening to Crue for the first time; exquisite. Bugsy must have thought the same thing since the man stared at McCoy. His mouth had gone slack, and he was no longer watching the two of them. This song was different. Magic was in the air.",
        "\"Great. Jessica, it's time to go,\" Bobby said, turning to the reporter and frowning. \"What are you doing?\"",
        "Ming was swaying to the music like Bugsy's men, oblivious to the world.",
        "\"Fuck!\"",
        "Bobby ran his fingers through his hair and stared at the stage. McCoy continued to ply, gesturing to a few people in the audience. They came over and picked Ming up under her armpits, walking her over to a private door. Bobby followed them, tracking Kansas. He heard him repeating the refrain in a soulful voice, infusing Bobby with joy and sorrow at the pain of loss. \"Baby, you know you've done me wrong.\"",
        "\"Sasha,\" he mumbled, following Ming through the door.",
        "In the back room, the music was muffled. Ming shook her head, blinking her eyes and came out of the trance. \"What happened? I remember meeting Bugsy Siegel, then nothing,\" she said. \"It's as if I were transported to another world.\"",
        "\"You were,\" Bobby replied, sitting down and closing his eyes. \"Kansas Joe McCoy's music has that kind of power. Get some rest. We may be here for a while.\"",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "Ming paced the small room, her fingers twitching. Bobby was sprawled out and snoring in the chair, but she couldn't sit. Bugsy Siegel was out there, and he had them surrounded by his goons. Ming wanted to ask him some questions about his involvement in the Vegas mob scene, how he knew Slazney and what he was planning to do. Bugsy was going to die in less than a month, and this was perfect.",
        "Ming stopped moving and put her hand on the wall of the small dressing room. She was hyperventilating again. This wasn't a dream. She had travelled through time to 1947 and met Bugsy Siegel. \"How the hell was this possible?\"",
        "Bobby said this was magic. Ming looked at the sleeping woman and shook her head. Magic wasn't real. Everything had an explanation and a cause. She was one of the best reporters in the city and on her way to winning the Pulitzer.",
        "Yet she was in 1947, in a sixteen-year-old white girl's body, and she'd been talking to Bugsy Siegel. Ming grabbed her head and sank to the floor. \"This is a dream, isn't it?\"",
        "The door to the dressing room banged open, and the singer from the stage walked in. Ming looked up at the black man and scuffled closer to Bobby.",
        "\"What are you doing?\" Ming asked the singer and stood in front of Bobby. She was the only one Ming could trust at this time. Her insides clenched up. She hated feeling helpless. It was the same after her father's accident. Those hours were the worst.",
        "The black man shrugged and sat down in the chair opposite Bobby, putting his guitar down. A muffled beat came through the doors.",
        "\"Who's playing the music?\" she asked.",
        "The black man was silent.",
        "Bobby snorted, blinked his eyes and sat up. \"Mr. McCoy, thank you for taking the time to meet with us,\" she said. Bobby was polite and respectful to the man, completely unlike the bouncers.",
        "\"So, care to tell me how you got those bodies?\" Kansas Joe said.",
        "Ming's eyes widened, and she pushed herself deeper into the corner. This wasn't happening. She could ignore everything, file it away as a story, as a dream. But it was real. She stared at the black man, but he was serious. Ming turned to Bobby, hoping for something, anything that would explain this.",
        "\"You could tell?\" Bobby said.",
        "\"You aren't the first travellers I've met,\" Joe replied, \"The last ones cost me five years.\"",
        "Ming stopped moving and took a deep breath. Part of her wanted to yell and scream; this wasn't real, but it was time to let go. Running away wouldn't solve anything. She was here and had to deal with it. Dean would call it listening to his gut. She'd always dismissed his feelings and relied on the facts, but she couldn't let her doubt drive her to make more stupid decisions. If this were magic, she needed to deal with it the best way she could. Taking a deep breath, she pulled out some paper and a pencil.",
        "\"Then you know we need to get home. This was an unintended trip to the past,\" Bobby said.",
        "Kansas Joe took a towel and wiped his head. He wasn't happy with the situation. He was tapping his finger on the edge of the chair, a nervous twitch if Ming was any judge of body language. \"You're lucky I don't like Siegel and his men. They are a necessary part of the Vegas scene, but I wish they'd never come here.\"",
        "Bobby smiled. On her real face, it wasn't so friendly. This one showed genuine warmth. \"If it makes you feel better, he's going to check out soon.\"",
        "\"It doesn't.\" Joe scowled. \"There are too many like him.\" He narrowed his eyes. \"Where you from? Can't quite place the accent?\"",
        "\"Russia. The USSR fell in 89. I'm from later than that.\"",
        "Joe's scowl grew deeper. \"I don't want to know anymore. The less, the better.\"",
        "Ming's pencil flew across the page. She'd never heard of Kansas Joe McCoy before, but she couldn't deny the power of his words on Bobby. As she wrote, Ming could push out the strangeness of the world. It was still there, but the darkness no longer threatened to overwhelm her. The pencil was her shield.",
        "\"What about her?\" Joe pointed to Ming. \"She's a strange one. I can't get a read on her.\"",
        "Bobby frowned. \"She's a pleb and got caught up in this mess. From what I can tell, she's never had anything conscious to do with magic before. I'm afraid she's in over her head.\"",
        "The pencil broke, and a snap filled the room.",
        "Ming stood up and leaned over Bobby. \"Mr. Miladev.\" Her voice went ice-cold. \"I appreciate everything you've done for me since we arrived in this era, but don't presume to judge me. I may have been overwhelmed, but that doesn't give you the right to relegate me to second class.\" Ming shoved her face closer to Bobby's, forcing her to draw back and hit her head against the wall. \"If you still had your balls on you, I'd make sure to show you how useless they were.\" The one thing she liked about being in Jessica's body was the size. As herself, she needed to convey the image of being bigger than she was. Now she stood taller than Bobby and Joe.",
        "Kansas Joe chuckled, pounding his knee while holding his chest. \"Please, don't surprise me like that, Miss. I have a bad heart,\" he said, wiping the side of his eyes. He took a deep breath and pulled out the paper Bobby gave him. \"It looks like you have the math right, but I can get Millie to check tomorrow. What about the power?\"",
        "\"Power?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"All magic is powered by something. The code is just there to direct it, sort of like the programming that runs your smartphone.\" Bobby said, rubbing her arms. \"I can get some records that will give me the beat, but my base is heavy metal, which hasn't been invented yet. There's no guitar I can play properly.\"",
        "\"Siegel will be after you the moment you leave this room,\" Joe said. \"I could only keep him contained for a short time.\" He looked at his watch. \"We got just a few minutes left. My current student is keeping the music going, but he's not as skilled, and I won't let him pay the cost for some fools who took a wrong turn.\" He grabbed a piece of paper and wrote something on it. \"Come to this address tomorrow. I'll let Jim know to expect you. He's my best apprentice.\" He handed the paper to Bobby.",
        "\"Thank you, Mr. McCoy. I will never forget this,\" Bobby said, standing up. She put the paper in her purse and shook his hand.",
        "\"Don't. I can't get you out of here. That's up to you,\" he said and opened the door. \"Get back to your seats and good luck.\"",
        "\"Is it okay if we break some of the bar?\" Bobby asked Kansas Joe as he was leaving the room.",
        "Joe smiled. \"As I said, I don't want to know, but if you can, do it outside. They still have a business to run.\" He paused. \"But, if you break Siegel as well, I'm good with it.\"",
        "Ming put her broken pencil away and poked her head around the corner. Bugsy and his men were still swaying to the music. \"What are we going to do?\"",
        "Bobby asked, \"Can you fight?\"",
        "\"Yes. I have a black belt in karate, and I was on the high school wrestling team,\" Ming said, cracking her knuckles. \"How about you? From what I saw when you fought Ivan, you were good at running away.\" She smiled.",
        "Bobby sneered. \"Come on,\" she said, leading her back to the seat. \"The music's going to stop. When it does, stand up and follow my lead.\"",
        "\"Why don't we just leave?\" Ming pointed to the door.",
        "\"That'll leave too many questions, and Kansas wouldn't like that,\" Bobby said. \"He's helping us here, Reporter. Let's not betray that.\"",
        "Bobby sat down in the same position as before, and Ming sat across from him. She was directly behind one of Bugsy's men.",
        "The music continued playing, there were a few more chords, and the song wound down. Bugsy and his men shook their heads and smiled.",
        "\"That was a good song,\" Bugsy said, blinking. He turned to Bobby. \"Last chance, doll. Why are you here?\"",
        "\"Let's go outside, and I'll tell you. I'm feeling a bit stuffy in here,\" Bobby said, standing up. She grabbed her purse and pushed past the men surrounding them.",
        "Ming stood up and followed her. She counted seven guys, including Siegel, probably with guns. Bobby went straight for the door and brushed past the bouncer. Two of Siegel's men were on her heels. Coming out of the underground club, Ming shivered in the nighttime air. Because Vegas wasn't the premier tourist destination yet, it always dropped close to freezing after the sun went down. In this time without the pressure of people and buildings, the heat just vanished.",
        "Bugsy emerged from the hole and strolled right in front of Bobby. \"So, what did you want to tell us, doll? Or do we have to take a ride? I hear the desert is beautiful at this time of night.\"",
        "Bobby smiled, put her purse down on the ground, stood up and shoved her palm directly into Bugsy's nose. He jerked back, and Bobby just missed driving his nose into his brain. Bobby followed his palm strike with a roundhouse kick to the temple, driving Bugsy Siegel to his knees.",
        "\"Get her!\" one of Siegel's men shouted.",
        "Two men rushed Bobby. She punched one in the face, but the other grabbed her from behind.",
        "Ming yanked the jacket of the man standing next to her and pulled it over his head, blinding him. She followed it up with a punch to the kidneys and then kneed him between the legs. The man standing next to him fumbled for his gun and tripped over the first man. Ming jumped, brought her foot back and kicked him in the head. His eyes went dark, and he joined the man writhing on the ground, clutching his groin. It was hard to judge her strength in this strange body.",
        "She turned back to Bobby. One man was on the ground, but two men were circling her. Bobby had taken a belt from one of the men and was holding it out like a whip. Ming counted six men. \"Where was the seventh?\"",
        "A pair of arms grabbed her from behind and hoisted her up in the air. \"Gottcha bitch. Yous gonna pay for what you did to Sammy.\"",
        "Ming squirmed in his arms, but they held her tight. Forcing her legs back, she wrapped them around the bigger man and twisted. He grunted but didn't let go. She reached back, took hold of his ears, yanked them and was rewarded with a scream. He threw her to the ground, driving the breath from her body.",
        "She was gasping when he jumped on top of her. \"I'm gonna have me some fun before I kills, ya,\" he said, ripping her blouse. Ming reached down, shoved her hands into his pants and squeezed his balls. He let out a high-pitched scream, fainting on top of her. She pushed him off of her and knelt in the dirt, panting. Raising her head, she looked at Bobby.",
        "The other two men were on the ground. Bobby's face sported a black eye and several cuts, her dress was torn in three places, and her bra strap was hanging out, but she was still standing. She had the belt around Siegel's neck, her foot on his back, and she was pulling it tight.",
        "\"If you think about coming after my daughter or me again, Mr. Fuckface, I won't stop at a slight choke.\" She leaned in and placed her mouth directly next to Bugsy's ear. \"The pigs love to feed off fat-asses, and once they've tasted flesh, well, they get hungry for more.\" She grabbed her purse and smacked him in the side of the head. Bugsy went down and didn't move.",
        "\"Come on, let's get out of here before they come to,\" Bobby said, grabbing Ming's hand and pulling her away from the carnage. Several of the men were moaning, but two were getting up and reaching for their guns. Ming and Bobby turned the corner when they heard a gunshot ring out, chips of plaster scattering over them.",
        "\"They won't chase us through here,\" Bobby said, as they wove through the streets, back onto the main one. \"Even so, we have to get home. I'm not going to meet Kansas Joe's man tomorrow looking like this.\"",
        "Ming held her blouse together and followed Bobby through the streets. She was shivering, but not from the cold. This was the second time she had been almost violated since she'd been here. The present wasn't perfect, but at least it was safer. A few of the people they passed turned to stare at them, but nobody stopped to help. Two women getting attacked wasn't an important event in Vegas. That wasn't right."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 20,
      "title": "Chapter 20",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "12:30 PM",
        "Barbie dashed out of the car and ran inside the precinct the moment they arrived, ignoring Dean. He was a little worried about what happened at Stanley's pharmacy. Lieutenant Zacoski would be pissed that he left the scene. He was a stickler for the rules. Dean needed to leave the precinct before Zacoski found out.",
        "Getting out of his car, he glanced at his watch. It was twelve-thirty in the afternoon. Two days since the Shujing murders. Seven hours since he found Ming's body. He had under thirteen hours left, and time was running out. Since the beginning of the case, nothing had made sense. Hell, he was driving around with the murdered victim. Just thinking all this made his head hurt. His Lieutenant was going to hate him. He sighed, popped in another candy and went into the station.",
        "When he got to the front desk, Ivan was signing a form.",
        "Dean pointed to the big man. \"What's he doing out of lock-up?\" Dean asked the sergeant at the desk. \"I still have questions I need to ask him.\" Barbie was nowhere to be found. She'd entered before him and disappeared. The clerk just shrugged his shoulders and went back to the paperwork. \"Hey! Answer me.\" Dean slapped his hands on the desk in front of the clerk.",
        "Ivan just stared at him.",
        "\"We don't know what he was charged with, detective,\" said Lieutenant Zacoski. He poked his head out of his office and pointed his finger at Dean. \"Come here, Lifante. Now.\" He ducked back inside.",
        "\"Keep him here until I get back,\" Dean said to the front desk clerk and pointed to the chair next to the desk. The clerk rolled his eyes, and Ivan sat down. Dean swore the big man's lips moved.",
        "Dean went into the office and closed the door. Lieutenant Zacoski came from behind the desk and placed his hand on Dean's shoulder. \"Starfield filed a report with HR, saying you called her a cow. They called me, but I was able to shoot it down. I heard what you said to her yesterday and told them exactly what happened. You have to be more careful with your mouth. It's gotten you in too much trouble.\"",
        "\"Thanks, Lieutenant,\" Dean said. They had been friends for ten years, and Zacoski had been his first partner on the force. He went on to a higher position but never forgot Dean. Zacoski was the only reason he was able to get him this position here. Dean kept him on a short list of people he trusted. Ming held the only other spot. Everyone else had their own agenda and could lie to achieve it. Dean stared at Zacoski and ground his teeth. He couldn't be a mole for Slazney. He should ask him here about the man.",
        "\"Is this about your wife?\" Zacoski asked. \"You have to move on from her. Not all women are out to get you. Here's one who'll melt your heart.\" He picked up a framed picture of his daughter and showed it to Dean. He started making kissy faces at it.",
        "Dean went stone-faced. He hated it when that bastard turned on the beautiful daughter switch. The kid was only three years old but had Zacoski by the nose hairs. \"Why are you letting the big Russian go? He attacked me,\" Dean said, changing the subject.",
        "Zacoski put the picture back and sat down. \"And where's the paperwork? The evidence? All we had was a shattered office and a strange man in the holding cell. You didn't file any report, didn't call it in. There's no video, nothing. It took hours to clean up.\" He slapped the file on his desk. \"That's not like you. Besides, the man is connected to some Russian bigshot businessman. His lawyer came and forced the release.\" Zacoski looked at Dean and frowned. \"This is sloppy police work, Dean. I expected better from you.\"",
        "\"Sorry, Lieutenant. It won't happen again,\" Dean said. Balling his fists, he hit his leg. How could he be so stupid?",
        "\"See that it doesn't. You're already walking on thin ice as it is, and I can't always be there to help you. Speaking of which. What's happening with the missing body at the Shujing?\" Zacoski asked. He stared at Dean over his desk.",
        "\"I'm following up on a few leads, and I should know some more today,\" Dean said, arching an eyebrow.",
        "\"Good. Keep me posted,\" he said, turning back to his paperwork and grabbing a pen.",
        "Feeling dismissed, Dean got up and went back to his desk. Ivan was still sitting at the front counter, but Dean ignored him. There was nothing he could do except draw his release out. It didn't matter anyway. He had some recordings to go through.",
        "He couldn't get a clear read on Zacoski. It was like his gut was failing him. His instincts said that Yichen was the key, but he was too well-protected. He could wait till later. He had nothing on Zacoski and didn't want to look unless he had to. He was the same daughter geek he'd always been. Zacoski did the same thing when he was talking about his wife when they were dating. You couldn't fake that level of geekiness.",
        "\"I should have checked this earlier,\" Dean mumbled to himself. \"Damm battery.\" He plugged his recorder into the computer. While it was charging enough to turn on, he pulled up the records from the archives on the murders twenty years ago at the Shujing and the number Chip gave them. One of them should provide a hint as to who stole the computer that wasn't Zacoski. He had to start somewhere.",
        "The red light flicked off, indicating his recorder had enough power. Opening the files, he scrolled down to the time index and started mumbling. \"It was after twelve, hmm.\" He put in some earphones and pressed play, fast-forwarding through the static.",
        "His eyes widened, and he turned to Ivan sitting at the reception.",
        "Ivan stared back and blinked.",
        "\"What are you listening to?\" Barbie asked, sitting down beside him.",
        "Dean didn't turn from Ivan and gave Barbie the headphones. She put them in and pressed play.",
        "\"This is Russian.\" She listened some more. \"When was this? He's saying that the Maker was a fool, but why did he call him Petor?\" She took the headphones out.",
        "\"Where were you?\" Dean asked.",
        "\"I had to use the girls' room. I needed to do a number two.\"",
        "He shook his head and went back to the front desk.",
        "\"Detective,\" the front desk clerk said, \"I must finish processing the Russian. His release papers are clear.\"",
        "\"I understand. Just give me a minute.\" He turned to Ivan, crossed his arms and stood in front of the giant. Even sitting down, Ivan was almost as tall as Dean. \"Ivan, I want to speak to your boss, Gregory. Today.\"",
        "Ivan raised an eyebrow, nodded and pointed to his watch.",
        "\"How long will it take to finish processing him?\" He asked the front desk clerk.",
        "\"About twenty minutes.\"",
        "Dean turned back to Ivan. \"When you're finished, can you take me to see your boss?\"",
        "Ivan nodded, stood up and went back to the receptionist.",
        "Barbie came up behind Dean and poked him in the ribs. \"What are you doing? You can't take him on. He's too powerful, and you're a wimp.\"",
        "\"I'm going to see Gregory. You heard the voice on the tape. I recognized it, I know I did, but the Russian made it difficult to place.\" Dean pulled up the address for S-Class Consulting. He needed more information on them, but if he started digging now, it would alert Zacoski, and he didn't want to tip him off just yet. Dean was running out of time. Ming had a little over half a day left.",
        "He needed to trust someone with this.",
        "Dean stared at Zacoski's door and heard his phone ring. He could ask him, but the Lieutenant was also a stickler for the rules. He'd want to know why Dean was going to meet the Russian. He didn't trust Starfield to do a proper job in this case, and Ortiz was too new.",
        "That left Barbie, but she wasn't related to the force in any way. Dean bit his lip and listened to his gut. It was growling, but then he hadn't eaten in twelve hours. Otherwise, it was silent. \"We're running out of time. Can I leave S-Class Consulting with you?\" he asked Barbie. \"It may have deep ties with Slazney, and I don't have time to go to both places.\"",
        "Barbie smiled and took the address from Dean's hand. \"It's about time you unclenched. I can help. Trust me.\" She pounded her chest and ran out the door. \"I'm taking your car, and I'm not stopping at the store for some candy like you,\" she said,",
        "\"Can you even drive?\" Dean asked.",
        "\"Of course. I've been certified on all ancient vehicles. Retro cars are really popular back home. I'm the best driver in my car group. I've only smashed two of them.\"",
        "\"Damn! Meet me at Darah's Diner when you're done.\" Dean gave her the address.",
        "She waved the keys behind her and skipped out of the station.",
        "Dean stomped back to the front and stopped in front of Ivan. \"Let's go! Did you drive here?\"",
        "Ivan nodded.",
        "\"We're taking your car.\"",
        "1:30 PM",
        "Ivan pulled up in front of the Bellagio and got out. Dean stared at the waterfall in front of the ritzy place and sighed. One night here would have depleted his savings completely. \"This isn't the time for this,\" he grimaced. *Coming here took too long*. He stepped out of the car and followed Ivan into the hotel as the valet took the car away.",
        "They went to the elevators and took a private one to the penthouse. \"This is the second penthouse I've been to in two days,\" he said, trying to make small talk. Still nothing from the giant. He wasn't expecting an answer. Bobby said he didn't have a tongue, but a grunt would have been nice. Dean just stared at the doors and put his hand on his gun. Outside the elevator, there were two more bodyguards. They weren't as big as Ivan, but just as silent. It seemed this Gregory had a type.",
        "\"Why is it everywhere I go, all I see is your typical goon?\" he asked. The smallest of the three was the same size as Dean. He gestured Dean over and patted him down, taking his gun.",
        "\"I want that back,\" Dean said. The guard handed him a receipt for the gun and placed the piece into a box on the table beside him. He closed it up and stood back. The second guard opened the door and ushered Dean inside.",
        "\"I'm getting Deja Vu here,\" he mumbled. This was the same set-up Yichen had. The room was more lavish with gold-trimmed mirrors, expensive paintings and couches that looked like they cost as much as a car. Yichen's looked more lived in, though. There was a lack of presence here, implying the guests were only temporary visitors. Nobody stayed here for long. Dean looked down at his K-Mart jacket and pulled it tight. Like Zacoski said when he started, \"It didn't matter what you wore. Fake the confidence you feel well enough, and anything becomes a tuxedo.\"",
        "He looked at the older man sitting on an L-shaped couch. There was some grey in his dark hair and some lines on his face. The left side had a large scar that ran down to his jaw. It shouted he was dangerous. With the plastic surgery available today, he could have removed it. Dean's gut feeling told him he could ignore the two women and one man typing on tablets showing some sort of bar graph. They were like the furniture, functional, but nothing else. Unlike Wu, the secretary at Yichen's place. He needed to be careful of her.",
        "Ming once asked him to explain his 'gut', but it was impossible. It was like describing the colour blue to a deaf-mute. Without a frame of reference, there was no way to put it into words. Even now, facing the man on the couch, Dean had to stop his stomach from jumping into his spleen. It was telling him to run and not look back.",
        "\"Gregory? Nice to meet you. I'm Detective Dean Lifante.\" Dean held out a card with his number on it. Gregory ignored it, and the male secretary took it. \"Thank you for taking the time to meet me.\"",
        "\"Ivan tells me you were the one to lock him up,\" Gregory said. \"But who was the one who took him down? It wasn't Petor or you, I know that lazy fool couldn't lay a hand on him.\"",
        "Dean remained standing. He was already losing the initiative in this meeting. \"That would be Bobby's friend, Barbie,\" Dean replied. \"She's quite strong.\"",
        "\"I'd love to meet her. I'm always on the lookout for new talent. Why didn't you invite her along with you?\" Gregory said, gesturing for a drink. One of the secretaries stood up and poured him some scotch.",
        "\"Maybe next time.\" Dean played out this man's voice in his head and compared it to the recording. There was no way to tell for certain, but this wasn't the voice on the tape. Either he didn't have Bobby's computer, or he had sent someone else into the precinct.",
        "\"Why are you here, detective?\" Gregory asked.",
        "\"I'm looking for something and was wondering if you'd seen it?\"",
        "\"What are you looking for?\" Gregory was signalling to his men to move in behind Dean.",
        "Taking a deep breath, Dean strode forward and stood directly over Gregory. He could feel the situation start to control him. This was too similar to what had happened at the Shujing to be a coincidence. According to Bobby, the program he'd developed could control what happened to time and space. The world was an unpredictable mess, and any attempt would leave scars that wouldn't go unnoticed. It couldn't account for everything. Everything was too contrived. Someone was trying to manipulate the situation. His gut was screaming the same feeling as the courtroom when his ex-wife introduced her 'evidence' of his abuse.",
        "\"You already know what I'm looking for, or you wouldn't have let me come here.\" Dean held out his recording device. \"Like I said, I need some help. This is connected to my account and is uploading what I say, right now. If you allow me, I'll play something for you.\" He needed to take back the initiative from whoever was trying to direct him.",
        "\"I could just take it,\" Gregory said, not looking up.",
        "\"You could, but that would mean Slazney would win. I don't think you want that.\"",
        "Gregory paused for a moment when Dean said the name. If he had looked away, he would have missed seeing the action. It was too quick. Gregory gestured to the female secretary, and Dean backed off. She brought a laptop over, and Dean plugged in his recording device. He'd already copied everything to his account and had set up a protected server. Gregory could still hack him, but it was unlikely in the few minutes he'd be connected.",
        "Dean opened the file he was looking for and played the audio. \"Give it a minute. I was unconscious for some of this.\" He forwarded through the silence and stopped on the voice.",
        "**\"Petor, Petor, Petor. Yesli by ty prisoyedinilsya ko mne, mne ne prishlos' by etogo delat'. Nadeyus', ty menya prostish'.\"**",
        "*(Petor, Petor, Petor. If only you would join me, I wouldn't have to do this. I hope you forgive me.)*",
        "Gregory gave nothing away. His face was a mask. Dean was hoping that he'd do something, but the man just sipped his drink.",
        "\"Thank you, Detective. I appreciate your candour. May I ask, why are you trusting this to me?\" he said.",
        "Dean's gut was settling. It wasn't playing hopscotch on his spleen any longer. That meant he'd probably survive this. \"Ask the men behind me to stand back, and I'll tell you,\" Dean said, not turning around. He was rewarded with a raised eyebrow and a wave.",
        "\"Thank you. I need to find the man who said this, and I had to know if you or one of your men was him. As for trust, that's not even a consideration. I figured the best way to keep you from interfering with my investigation is to keep you involved.\"",
        "Gregory nodded and pointed to Ivan. \"He will shadow you, Detective. That way I'll know when you've achieved your objective.\"",
        "Frowning, Dean ran his fingers through his hair. \"How do I know he'll listen to me? He's already destroyed my precinct trying to get to Bobby.\"",
        "\"Petor,\" Gregory said.",
        "\"Petor,\" Dean acknowledged. \"If I allow him to accompany me, will he listen to me?\" Dean asked again.",
        "\"He will do exactly as you ask him to do, as long as it doesn't interfere with my interests. Until you find Petor, he will be your muscle,\" Gregory said.",
        "Dean kept his eyes from widening. He frowned and turned to Ivan. Gregory didn't know where Bobby was, nor that his computer was missing. Ivan hadn't told him exactly what happened at the precinct. Why? What did the giant want?",
        "\"I can accept that,\" Dean said, nodding. Gregory dismissed them with a wave, and one of Gregory's men directed him back to the door. The meeting was over. Dean nodded and backed out of the room, getting his gun at the door. Strapping his piece back on, Dean let out a nervous breath and looked at his watch. He was running out of suspects he could question. It was all up to Barbie now.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ivan",
        "1:30 PM",
        "Ivan pushed the button for the first floor and glanced at the detective. The man stood up to Gregory and hadn't flinched. Petor had found himself a good friend. Maybe it would rub off on him. If anything, maybe he could help Petor stay away from Gregory a little longer.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Barbie",
        "1:30 PM",
        "\"Welcome to S-Class Consultants. How may I help you?\" the secretary said in a bubbly voice as Barbie walked in the door. The woman smiled and bowed like the characters in the old-style cartoon Barbie watched. She was curious to see how people in this time handled visitors. Back home, she'd have to go through a retina scan to verify her identity and a cavity check to make sure she wasn't carrying any insects hidden in her body.",
        "\"I'd like to speak to Slazney, please,\" she said. Dean had told her to be polite, so she was trying.",
        "The secretary frowned. \"I'm sorry, but we don't have anybody here by that name.\"",
        "\"I see. Then, I'll speak to whoever is in charge,\" Barbie replied.",
        "\"Very well,\" she said, picking up the phone. \"Please have a seat.\"",
        "Barbie sat down and examined the sterile room. The white panelling matched the white sofa-like chairs. In the center was a triangle-shaped glass table, balanced on two more inverted triangles. The only colour in the room was the magazines sitting on top. \"I don't like this place,\" Barbie said. \"It has no soul.\"",
        "\"I'm sorry you feel that way,\" said a voice from the door. \"We hoped it would convey a sense of relaxation.\" A man stepped out and stopped in front of Barbie. \"Welcome to S-Class Consultants. I'm Richard. How may I help you?\"",
        "The man was tall. Not as tall as the Detective, and skinnier too. Barbie grabbed his hand and pumped it up and down. \"Hi. I'm Barbie. I'm looking for your connection to Slazney.\"",
        "\"I see. Please come into my office,\" Richard said, gesturing through the open door.",
        "In the office, Barbie sat down in an inverted dome-shaped chair. \"This is comfortable and awkward at the same time. Why do you use it?\" she asked.",
        "\"We want to give the impression we're looking towards the future.\" He drew back. \"Did I say something funny?\"",
        "Barbie was rolling on the ground holding her sides.",
        "\"Yes! The future doesn't need these kinds of chairs. It has much better things,\" she said, getting back into the chair and wiping her eyes. She put her hand on her chest to calm herself. \"Thank you for the joke. I needed a good laugh. It's been a rough day.\"",
        "\"No problem,\" he said, frowning.",
        "\"I'm here looking for Slazney. A boy at the Squeegee R'Us place said you were the ones who helped him set up the business. That true?\" Barbie asked. She sat back in the chair and crossed her legs in front of her. She'd noticed that the men in this time seemed fascinated by them.",
        "Richard's smile returned. \"Ah, yes, Mr. Slazney. He's our founder and guiding light. However, we don't advertise his presence. He likes to operate as a silent partner.\"",
        "\"I don't care if he's silent. I need to speak to him,\" Barbie said, standing up and leaning over Richard's desk.",
        "He leaned back and pushed a button on his desk. \"Mr. Slazney warned us someone would be coming by, looking for him.\" The door opened behind Barbie. \"When that happens, we should escort them to our special office.\" He gestured and pointed to Barbie.",
        "Someone touched Barbie's shoulder. Elbowing him in the throat, she grabbed his head and smashed it down on the desk. \"Oops. I hope I didn't kill him,\" she said without a giggle. Two more men rushed her. She grabbed the jacket of the first one and thrust him into the second, sending both flying into the wall. They slid down in a heap.",
        "\"You're crazy!\" Richard said, edging towards the door.",
        "\"No, just using my training. Mr. Richard, could you please tell me how to find Slazney?\" Barbie jumped between him and the door. \"Aikido doesn't preach violence, but I will use it if I have to.\"",
        "Richard slid down and sat on the floor. \"Mr. Slazney never told me how to find him. He was just the money guy, providing start-up funds for businesses. We decided how they were used.\"",
        "Barbie picked up Richard by the collar and perp-walked him back to the desk. \"Sounds good. Can I get a list of all the businesses you started with Slazney's money?\" She smiled at him. \"Please?\" Dean would be happy with her. She was polite."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 21,
      "title": "Chapter 21",
      "paragraphs": [
        "February 18, 1947",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "Ming stared at the blank page. Last night, the rush of the fight had driven all the thoughts from her head. Sitting in the morning sunlight, they flooded back. Writing was her shield. It usually helped her understand the world, putting everything into perspective. If only she could start with the first word.",
        "Escaping from Bugsy Siegel, tossing Steven into the desert, and almost getting raped twice. Ming tapped the broken pencil on the page, and her thoughts drifted back to the source of it all.",
        "Magic.",
        "There was no way magic existed. There was a logical reason for everything. Even her first story about the doctor thrown from his car. He survived because that dune cushioned his impact. There was no magic involved, she was sure.",
        "After they came home, Bobby grabbed a bottle of scotch from the cabinet and went to bed. Ming tried to sleep but moved to the table and sat. If Bobby's plans worked, they would be home. Jessica might survive, but Catherine was dead. She was only walking around because of Bobby's soul. When they left this time, Jessica would be alone.",
        "Maybe this was magic, but it was also time travel. Ming could do something to make Jessica's life better than it was. Every movie she'd watched on the subject said to be careful of a paradox, but they'd already beaten Bugsy Siegel and brought these two back to life. Paradox had sailed.",
        "\"What are you doing?\" Bobby groaned as she stumbled through the door. Her hair was a mess, and she smelled a little sour. Ming had already heard her throwing up in the bathroom.",
        "\"Trying to decide what to leave, Jessica,\" Ming said, tapping the pencil on the pad of paper. She wanted to give her some information about the future, but didn't want to change the future too much.",
        "\"Nothing would be a good choice. The less we interfere, the better.\" Bobby sat at the table, stretched her legs under it and closed her eyes.",
        "\"I can't do that,\" Ming said, slapping the pencil on the table. \"What happens if this fails? If we can't get home?\"",
        "Bobby was silent for a moment and replied, \"Then we stay here, live out our lives and die in this time.\" She stood up. \"Or, we do what Slazney is doing and leap from body to body, causing more trouble.\" Putting on the kettle, Bobby started making some coffee. \"It's too tempting to use this kind of power, but you heard Kansas Joe. He's met others like us, but have you ever heard of him?\"",
        "Ming shook her head.",
        "\"He was pretty famous when he was alive, but most regular people have forgotten about him. That's because he didn't use his gifts to overwrite nature. Everything has a purpose, even if we don't know what it is. Whatever reality is, it doesn't like being trifled with and will bite back.\" Bobby poured herself some coffee and sat down. \"The code is dangerous, unpredictable and impossible to control, addictive, drawing you in to use it. It's like catching chaos in a bottle. It never lasts.\"",
        "Ming got her own coffee and returned to the notebook.",
        "\"I know how difficult this must be. Things will work out.\" Bobby put her hand on Ming's shoulder and squeezed. She took a sip of the coffee and smiled. \"Let's get ready. We have to meet with the person Kansas Joe recommended in a couple of hours.\"",
        "\"Slazney. Do you know who he is?\"",
        "\"Not really.\" Bobby shrugged. \"I've never heard of the name before going to the pharmacist, but if I had to guess, based on what's happened, it's probably my fuck-up twin brother. I'm guessing he screwed up somewhere.\"",
        "Ming gulped her coffee, some of it spilling down her chin. \"Why do you think that?\"",
        "\"There are very few people who know how to use the code. My brother was one of them. He couldn't do much with it, but he could copy it. I wouldn't be surprised if he was carrying a buggy version with him, and his death was an act. If he was the Slazney I met, then he wasn't firing on all cylinders. The American who got me out of Russia said my brother was gone. I never expected he meant literally, but it makes sense. I never trusted that guy. Anyone who'd wear a Metallica T-shirt is a two-faced liar.\"",
        "\"Is he really Slazney?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"Like I said, I don't know. Just going on my gut.\" Bobby stood up, took a swig of the coffee and left Ming at the table, staring at the page.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "\"Are you feeling better?\" Ming was still sitting at the table when Bobby came back from the shower. Ming had written a few things but scrunched them up and tossed them aside. Most of the page was still blank. Bobby smiled and said, \"I still remember my first time travelling...\"",
        "The front door shook. Both Bobby and Ming jerked at the sound of someone pounding.",
        "\"Open up, Catherine! I know you're in there. I forgot my key,\" the voice continued to pound on the door. \"I heard what happened at the club, Catherine. You won't be getting away from this one.\"",
        "Bobby moved the curtain covering the window. A police officer was standing there. He was blond, taller than Jessica and pounding on the door.",
        "\"Who is he?\" Ming asked, sliding up next to her.",
        "Shrugging her shoulders, Bobby opened the door. \"Who the fuck are you?\" The man shoved past her and stomped into the kitchen. He had broad shoulders and a short two-day stubble on his square chin.",
        "\"What kind of game are you trying to pull here, Catherine? Even if we're divorced, you know who I am.\" He stepped over to Ming. \"When I heard the news, I hurried back.\" He held out his arms. \"No hug for your father?\"",
        "\"Daddy?\" Ming said, jumping into his arms. \"Where've you been?\" Her eyes were bugging out. Where had he been the last two nights? He mentioned a divorce.",
        "\"I had extra duty taking that convict to Arizona, remember?\" He kissed her on the cheek. \"When I get back here, I find a report by Bugsy Siegel describing two women he wants found. He's keeping it quiet, but three of his men are in the hospital. One had his balls almost crushed.\"",
        "\"What's that got to do with us?\" Bobby said, crossing her arms. She sounded nervous, her voice shaking. Ming held on tight to her father. This man could spoil everything. And being a policeman made it that much more difficult to get away from him.",
        "He grimaced and moved away from Ming. \"I recognized the dress and the description of the two of you first. Bugsy has enough men on his payroll in the force to track you down.\" He poured himself a coffee and opened a flask. Ming smelt the whisky as he poured some in. \"Now, what did you do?\" He pointed the coffee cup at Bobby, spilling some on the floor.",
        "\"Fuck!\"",
        "The father slammed the cup on the table and loomed in front of Bobby. \"You've never used that kind of language in front of me when we were married. I ignored the first one, but I can't this time. What happened to you?\" He grabbed Bobby by the shoulders and pushed her back. \"What are you doing with Jessica?\"",
        "Bobby glared up at the man and shoved her finger into his chest, forcing him to step back. \"We're divorced! What gives you the right to barge in here like this?\"",
        "He raised his hands. \"I---\"",
        "Bobby continued to push him backward with her finger. \"Furthermore, the fact you know what Bugsy is after tells me you're on his payroll as well, right?\"",
        "\"Yes, but I---\"",
        "Joining her, Ming picked up his coffee cup and dropped it into the sink. It shattered. \"I expected better of you, Daddy,\" she said, remembering how her own father would ignore her after the accident. Fathers usually had a soft spot for their children. \"Why'd you take money from that bastard?\"",
        "\"Jessica! How dare you use that kind of language when speaking to your father?\" he said, stepping forward.",
        "Shoving him into the chair, Bobby leaned directly in his face. \"You will tell us exactly what Bugsy knows about us before I get angry.\" She cracked her knuckles.",
        "\"Yes, Daddy,\" Ming added. \"Please!\" Her fingers were twitching.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "\"Are you sure he's your husband?\" Ming asked Bobby. \"What's his name?\"",
        "\"Jack. I didn't recognize him at first, but yeah. I found some pictures in a box in her closet when I was looking into Catherine,\" Bobby said, closing the door to the bathroom. \"They were divorced two years ago. He's a deadbeat, but she never wrote anything bad about him. Just that he drank too much.\"",
        "Ming put her hand on the bathroom door. \"Will he be okay in there?\"",
        "\"He should be fine. If he's anything like Steven, he'll get out soon. I wish they had zip-ties in this time. They make it so much easier.\" Bobby shrugged. \"Anyway, by the time he gets free, we should be gone.\" Bobby turned, \"If Jack was telling the truth, they'll be looking for us. He didn't want to give us up, so we have a small head start, but get ready. We'll leave in twenty minutes,\" Bobby said, tossing Jack's keys in the air and walking away. \"We can use his car.\"",
        "Ming stared at the bathroom door for a few moments and turned away. She needed to finish the letter to Jessica and maybe leave one for Dean, too. Just in case.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "\"We're here,\" Bobby said, turning off the car.",
        "Ming put her pencil away and folded the paper. She put it in an envelope and placed it in her bag.",
        "\"Are you sure about that thing?\" Bobby pointed to the letter.",
        "\"Yes. I have to do something. This is her life, and she let me use it. I can't just abandon her. Besides, don't you need somebody to activate the computer?\" she asked.",
        "Bobby scoffed. \"I don't expect that'll happen. If Barbie could have done it, we'd already be out of here by now. It's been three days. We have about three or four more before we're stuck here. After twenty-four hours there, it's permanent.\"",
        "\"You said that before. What do you mean?\"",
        "Bobby shrugged, \"Every four hours there is about a day here.\"",
        "Ming got out of the car and looked at the motel to stop her hands from shaking. \"The Sunnyside. I've been here before.\" She pointed to the second floor. \"That was where Dean's wife was holed up after she accused him of rape,\" she said. She looked around the parking lot. It was old and dusty, but there wasn't the drug-like feel it had in the future. It was still new, with a fresh coat of paint. \"It's almost comfortable here.\"",
        "\"Don't get used to it.\" Bobby pointed to room 204. \"That's where we have to go.\"",
        "\"You're kidding with me, right?\" Ming said, her eyebrows shooting up. \"It's the same room.\"",
        "\"Coincidence?\" Bobby said, leading the way up the stairs. At room 204, she pounded on the door. It opened just a crack. Music blared out.",
        "\"What do you want?\" a voice said over the jazz. It was similar to the music she'd heard last night but with a faster beat. Ming couldn't make out his face, but he sounded young.",
        "\"Kansas Joe McCoy sent us here. He said you could help us.\"",
        "The sun was rising high into the sky. The heat pounded down on them, giving Ming a headache. Even so, she was shivering. When the door opened fully, a blast of ice went down to her bones. She wrapped her arms around herself and tried to keep warm.",
        "\"Sorry,\" the voice stepped back. \"Come in.\"",
        "A young black teenager wearing a winter jacket and a knit hat held the door open. His breath formed a cloud in the air. \"The air conditioner is set too low,\" she said, stomping her feet to get some circulation going. Bobby was holding her hands in front of her face, blowing into them.",
        "\"Who's the newb?\" the boy asked.",
        "\"She's not used to what can be done with power,\" Bobby said, pointing to Ming. She turned to Ming. \"He's an apprentice.\" He turned back to the teen. \"Kansas Joe's?\"",
        "The teen nodded.",
        "\"This is his studio,\" Bobby continued, waving his arm around the room.",
        "Ming looked around the room and tried to remember what it looked like in sixty years. The basic design was the same. Two beds, a table between them and a lamp with a dresser and TV on one side and a table with two chairs on the other. Just the colour and the furnishings had changed. She narrowed her eyes at Bobby. \"I get it. He's Mickey Mouse. Can we move on?\"",
        "\"Hey! You watch it there, bitch. I ain't no Mickey!\" He crossed his arms in front of his chest and glared at Ming.",
        "\"S-s-s-s-orry. C-c-c-c-could you please turn up the heat?\" Her teeth were chattering, and her fingers were turning blue.",
        "\"Yeah, sorry.\" The boy went over to the stereo and turned off the music. \"I'm trying something new and needed to keep it localized.\" He started removing his clothes and laid them on the bed. With the music gone, the room soon heated up.",
        "The air conditioner conked and sputtered. The boy hit it with his fist and kicked the side. It sputtered twice more and started humming.",
        "\"Thank you,\" Ming said, jumping up and down. \"How old are you? What's your name?\"",
        "\"I'm seventeen. Thank you very much.\" The teen just sneered at her and didn't give his name. \"You, Bobby?\" he asked.",
        "\"That's me,\" Bobby said. \"This is Jessica, but you can call her Ming. Kansas Joe said you could help us.\"",
        "The teen put his finger to his lips and started tapping. \"Depends. I got a source for the power you need, but do you have the circle?\"",
        "\"Circle?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"The code,\" Bobby said, \"Yes, that's no problem.\" Bobby pulled a wad of papers from her purse and gave it to the teen. He started checking them over on the chair in the corner.",
        "There were a bunch of other papers on the table with similar markings. The code. Magic. She was beginning to understand how strange the world was. Turning and looking out the window, she wrapped her arms around herself. Closing her eyes, she remembered what Dean told her about his gut feeling.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "*\"It's hard to explain. You know how when you put a sentence down on paper, and there is something about it that doesn't feel natural?\" Dean asked.*",
        "*\"Yes, usually when I haven't had enough coffee to wake me up,\" Ming replied, sipping her coffee in the diner.*",
        "*\"That's my gut,\" Dean said, lighting a cigarette. \"I don't know why it's doing what it's doing, but I can usually follow what it's telling me I need to do.\"*",
        "*Ming narrowed her eyes and tapped her pen on the paper. \"I see. So, when you saw the doctor helping your wife...\" she trailed off.*",
        "*\"I knew he was her lover, and that they had set me up for rape,\" Dean said, hitting the table. He cringed when the server glared at him, but didn't apologize.*",
        "*Ming wrote all this down. \"You know a gut feeling isn't admissible in court.\" She stared at Dean's face. It had gotten older since the last time they'd seen each other, but she could still see the boy who'd helped her out. She wanted to believe in his gut, but instinct couldn't trump facts.*",
        "*Dean scoffed. \"I know. They threw my last case out because I testified with that. The D.A. was pissed.\"He smiled.*",
        "*\"Do you have any evidence of their affair or the set-up?\" she asked. \"That's what will win you the case.\" She'd already found a paper trail and a lead to a motel, but needed to know what he'd found.*",
        "*He smiled and pulled out a thumb drive. \"Found this in my house after I was released on bail. Thought I'd lost it, or the wife took it, but it has everything you need.\" He put it on the table.*",
        "*\"What's on it?\" Ming asked.*",
        "*\"Pictures. My gut told me to set up a camera in the house when things started going missing, and that's what I did. Thought I'd catch some kids rifling through my stuff. I wasn't prepared for what it really was. Good audio too.\" He winced and took a sip of some coffee. \"When I heard what they said, I'm afraid I went off the deep end a bit. It's what got me arrested. The wife found the recording and destroyed the original. Glad I made a backup and stored it in my smokes.\" He inhaled and let out a cloud of smoke. \"She hated the things.\"*",
        "*\"She's not the only one,\" Ming said, waving her hand to drive away the smell. \"Why are you telling me all of this? I'm a reporter, and you broke the nose of the last one you were talking to.\"*",
        "*Dean took another sip of his coffee and stared at her. \"There's something about you, something I remember from when I was young. I can't quite put my finger on it, but I trust you. You won't do me wrong.\"*",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "Ming opened her eyes and started chuckling.",
        "\"What's so funny?\" Bobby said.",
        "\"Just remembering something.\" She stared out the window, and three cars pulled into the parking lot. Several tough-looking men got out and pointed to the second floor. \"Bobby, we have trouble,\" Ming said, pointing out the window.",
        "\"What?\" Bobby came and moved the curtains. \"Fuck! That's Bugsy! How the fuck did he find us?\" Bobby turned away from the window just as a shot filled the lot and the window shattered, throwing her across the bed.",
        "Ming spun back to the window. Bugsy, with a bandage across his nose, lowered a gun."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 22,
      "title": "Chapter 22",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "2:00 PM",
        "\"What's he doing here?\" Barbie said, pointing to Ivan. \"Didn't I kick his ass already?\" She stood in front of Dhara's Diner with her hands on her hips. She had a file folder tucked under her arm with an 'S' stamped on the front and a rip in her blouse.",
        "\"Yes, you did. You okay?\" Dean pointed to her blouse.",
        "\"This?\" Barbie grabbed the fabric. \"No problem. The S-Class Consultants were a little rude, but I stayed polite.\" She smiled.",
        "\"Great to hear,\" Dean said, pushing his way inside. He'd asked her to meet him here so they could avoid the station. Besides, he was starving. Other than candy, he hadn't eaten anything since lunch the day before. He needed to find that computer, but he would be no good to Ming if he dropped from hunger.",
        "They sat at the booth in the back, and Dean ordered the hashbrowns and coffee. Barbie got a peach pie. Ivan ordered nothing. \"Gregory 'loaned' him to us to help find Bobby and his computer,\" Dean said.",
        "\"What do you mean?\" Barbie asked. \"Bobby's---, Ow! Why'd you kick me?\" She rubbed her leg.",
        "\"Sorry. My foot slipped. What did you find at the Consultants?\" Dean took a bite of his lunch. He hoped Barbie would get the hint and stop talking.",
        "Barbie glared at him, scrunching her nose. \"Not much. I did get a list of all the businesses Slazney is involved in.\" She handed the list to Dean and dug into her pie. Smacking her lips in pleasure, she pointed to Ivan with her fork. \"Again, why is he helping us find Bobby? We know--- Ow! You kicked me again.\"",
        "\"Sorry. I'm clumsy today,\" Dean said. He leaned forward and put his hand on his face, covering his mouth and whispering, \"Don't say anything about where Bobby is, please. At least until we find his computer.\"",
        "\"Fine! Ba, if you kick me again, I'm punching you in da face,\" Barbie said through a mouthful of pie.",
        "Ivan just raised an eyebrow and frowned.",
        "Dean flipped through the list of names Barbie had brought. \"A few of these were crossed out in Stanley's files. The squeegee place owner is still the only person we haven't checked out,\" he said, swallowing his hashbrowns. \"These three businesses are out of state.\"",
        "\"Is there anything useful there?\"",
        "He flipped a few more pages, stopped, and slammed the folder shut. \"This was a waste of time.\"",
        "\"Rake it easy, Detective,\" Barbie said, spitting food. \"Ri'm sure there's womthing.\"",
        "\"Close your mouth when you eat,\" Dean said. He finally realized how Ming felt. His phone buzzed on the table.",
        "\"Dammit! It's Zacoski.\" Dean flipped the phone over and took a sip of his coffee. \"I have to talk to him.\" He looked at Ivan. \"Can you take her to Chester Punk Sr.'s place and talk to the father?\"",
        "Ivan nodded.",
        "Dean turned back to Barbie. \"Give me my keys back. Go. Question the father and make sure he confirms what the son told us. If he doesn't, ---please don't kill him---, come find me.\"",
        "\"Crazy! I love it.\" Barbie finished shoving the pie in her mouth and picked up the check. \"Rets go big guy.\"",
        "Dean wolfed down the rest of his hashbrowns and waved to Ivan to follow Barbie.",
        "3:00 PM",
        "\"Close the door, Dean,\" Lieutenant Zacoski said, sitting at his desk. He stared at Dean. There was a closed file on his desk, with Stanley's name on the tab.",
        "Dean looked at his friend and narrowed his eyes. His gut was silent. Despite the file he'd found in Stanley's office, nothing told him Zacoski was out to get him, but he'd been wrong before. Sometimes he wanted something to be the truth so badly, he shoved his gut instinct out the door.",
        "\"Why didn't you call in the body the moment you found it, Dean?\" he asked, quietly. The muffled sounds of the precinct, even through the door, made it difficult to hear him.",
        "\"What did you say?\" Dean asked in a louder voice.",
        "Zacoski sneered. \"Turn off the recorder and lay it on the desk.\"",
        "Dean raised his eyebrows. He reached into his jacket pocket and placed the small recorder on the desk. He clicked it off.",
        "Zacoski was silent.",
        "\"You know something about the body, don't you, Lieutenant?\" Dean asked. Ever since the incident with his wife, he'd taken to recording all his conversations if he could. Zacoski knew that. Usually, he'd turn it off when talking to the man as a sign of trust, but now, he wasn't so sure trusting him had ever been a good idea. Dean glared at his Lieutenant and waited for the man to continue.",
        "\"I'm not here to talk about that. Why'd you ignore procedure? And when the first responders looked at the security camera, they said you were with someone, a woman. Who was in it? Where did you go?\"",
        "\"Some customer from the strip mall, I guess?\" Dean said. \"I think her name was Jillian. She said she'd smelt something, so I checked it out. I couldn't get into the office, so I called in my suspicions.\"",
        "Zacoski raised an eyebrow and scoffed. \"They checked the inside cameras, Dean. I was expecting a better lie than this.\"",
        "Dean was silent. This was his best friend. *What would Ming do? She'd go for the jugular.*",
        "\"Why was your name in the doctor's records, Bart? Did you know him?\"",
        "Zacoski stood up and paced behind his desk. There was a window, hidden by blinds, behind him. Zacoski paused and opened the slats, brightening the room.",
        "\"You're stalling, Bart. Why?\"",
        "\"I don't have to tell you anything, Dean. Why I went to see Dr. Stanley is my business,\" Zacoski said. He sat, interlocking his fingers in front of him. \"We're here for your fuck-up.\"",
        "Dean stared at his friend. Zacoski was sweating. Small beads rolled down his forehead and disappeared under his collar. His eyes darted around the room, but the rest of him was stiff. Dean stared at Bart's hands. They were clenched, trembling. Something was wrong. Dean glanced up at the window. A small sliver of sunlight peeked through the blinds and hit a picture of his wife and daughter. Zacoski glanced at the picture and back to Dean's face. It was there, deep in his heart; someone was targeting Zacoski. His gut wasn't wrong.",
        "\"Yes. I fucked up. I'm sorry, Lieutenant. I was looking for evidence to tie the Shujing murders in a bow. I'd received a tip that the window washer had been seen at the doctor's office, and went to check it out. When I got there, it was locked, but I noticed a suspicious smell and someone coming out of the back door. He escaped before I could pursue him, and I needed to check on the scene. The body was long dead, so I didn't think the person who'd left had anything to do with it, but I needed to track him down before he got too far.\"",
        "Zacoski relaxed and unclenched his hands. He tilted to the side and picked up a picture of his family. \"That's not for you to say. You should have chased the perp.\"",
        "\"My gut told me to check out the office first,\" Dean replied.",
        "\"Ah, yes. Your famous gut.\" Zacoski shook his head and put the picture down on his desk. In it, Zacoski's wife and daughter were smiling while he stood, looking serious, behind them. \"You're like an uncle to my daughter, Dean. She misses seeing you. When are you coming around?\"",
        "\"After I finish this case. I have a good lead, Lieutenant.\"",
        "\"What's your gut saying now, Dean?\" he asked.",
        "Dean stared at his friend. He was connected to Slazney, the evidence said as much. But it wasn't a body-hopping type of deal. After Stanley, Dean had Barbie point out the smell. Dean had taken a good sniff when he entered the office, and that distinctive scent wasn't here. He was convinced the mystery man had something on the Lieutenant. Glancing at the family picture, Dean was certain what it was. Bart would do anything for his daughter. What he didn't know was why.",
        "\"That I should trust you and continue with my investigation.\"",
        "Zacoski nodded. \"Don't forget to call in anything you find, detective. No matter how small.\"",
        "Dean nodded. He picked up his recorder and left the office.",
        "Heading back to his desk, Dean ignored the banter around him. The rookie was talking with Starfield. The older woman was pointing at him, punctuating her speech with her finger. Ortiz's eyes widened as she turned and avoided staring in his direction. Another person who probably believed the rumours. He sighed and focused on his seat. There was no reason for Zacoski to take such an interest in the Stanley case and no reason for Dean to tell him everything he'd found so quickly. Except for the computer, Dean knew where everything was.",
        "He sat up in his chair. The computer. Slazney didn't have the computer. That's why he needed Zacoski now, but not why he got in touch in the first place. That was a mystery for another day. Dean pulled up the recording he'd taken of the Russian voice on his computer and listened to it again.",
        "**\"Petor, Petor, Petor. Yesli by ty prisoyedinilsya ko mne, mne ne prishlos' by etogo delat'. Nadeyus', ty menya prostish'.\"**",
        "After running it through a program to remove the voice and isolate the sounds, Dean realized that whoever had said the phrase didn't do anything else. Nothing was taken from the room, and there was no noise beyond his snoring.",
        "\"Someone else took the computer,\" he mumbled. There were two hours of recordings to go through. He didn't have that kind of time.",
        "\"What was that, Detective?\" the rookie said.",
        "\"Ortiz, right?\" Dean asked and was rewarded with a nod. \"Nothing important. What can I do for you?\"",
        "\"There are two Asians at reception asking for you,\" she said.",
        "\"Thank you.\" Dean got up and brushed past her. She must have heard the stories about him by now, but she was still willing to talk to him. It was refreshing. Dean wondered if there was an ulterior motive.",
        "\"No! I can't live my life like this. I have to trust what I'm feeling is right,\" he mumbled. He would trust her on spec until something happened to prove otherwise.",
        "\"I'm Detective Lifante,\" he said, stepping up to the front counter and facing the couple. \"How can I help you?\" They were short, not much higher than his chin. They looked to be in their early sixties but without grey hair. The man looked familiar. He'd seen him before, but couldn't quite place the face. \"Have we met before?\" he asked as he sniffed the air. He couldn't smell anything but a standard perfume. However, something was off.",
        "The woman scowled. She placed her hands on her hips and thrust her face up into his. \"Where's our daughter, Lifante? I know you've seen her.\"",
        "Dean stared, and something clicked. The woman had a sharp face, while the man was rounder. \"Ming's parents! Nice to meet you.\" He smiled and stuck out his hand to cover his nervousness. \"She looks like you. What can I do for you? Your daughter. I haven't seen her since yesterday.\"",
        "\"Don't screw with me, Lifante,\" she said, poking his chest with her finger. \"I know she was here last night. Her work called, and she hasn't been answering her phone. It was turned off.\"",
        "She stepped forward, forcing Dean to take a step back. \"What did you do to her, Loser?\"",
        "He grabbed her hand and removed it from his chest. \"I know we used to live in the same building, Mrs. Liu, but that doesn't give you the right to insult me. I've never met you before in my life.\"",
        "She scoffed and threw her hands in the air. \"See, I told you he'd deny it. He's nothing but a useless liar.\" She turned to her husband. \"You should have had the owner kick his family out when he stood up to Hong. He broke his jaw. Because he did that, Ming missed her chance to get married before twenty-five.\"",
        "Her husband just nodded and said nothing.",
        "\"I remember that incident,\" Dean said, slapping his head. \"I was going home, and a stuck-up prick was hurting a girl in the stairwell.\" He was silent for a moment, his mouth dropping. \"That was Ming?!\"",
        "\"Yes, that was Ming, you animal.\" Mrs. Liu slapped him in the face. \"You stay away from our daughter. I won't have you ruining her like you did your own life.\" She huffed and stormed out.",
        "Dean rubbed his face and listened to the silence around him. If they hated him before, this would give them more than enough fodder to extend the gossip a hundredfold.",
        "\"I'm very sorry about my wife. She gets overworked and tends to lose her filter,\" Mr. Liu said. \"She's usually a very kind person.\"",
        "\"I'll believe that when I see it,\" Dean said, betraying nothing on his face. His eye twitched, and he forced it to settle. He nodded to the man and watched him leave.",
        "\"What was that all about?\" Zacoski said, stepping out of his office. \"Who were they?\"",
        "\"My next lead,\" Dean said, rushing to his desk and popping some antacids. His gut had been screaming at him from the moment those two walked in, but went into freefall when Mr. Liu started talking to him. Slipping on his coat, he ran after the couple before they could get too far.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Barbie",
        "3:00",
        "\"Why'd I have to be stuck with a mute? Can't you say anything?\" Barbie asked Ivan. She was sitting in the passenger seat of his car. She had a map to the Vegas strip open on her lap, and she was following the path to Chester Punk Sr.'s house with her finger.",
        "\"This place will really change in the future.\" She pointed to the right. \"That's where the Heavy Metal Hall of Fame will be built. Over there is the New White House. After the President sold Washington along with Alaska to Russia, the government had to move. I like the new place. It has an amusement park.\"",
        "A hint of a smile appeared on Ivan's face. He nodded and continued driving.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Yichen",
        "3:00",
        "\"What are they doing?\" Yichen yelled into the phone. \"No, keep following them. I have to get ahead of Slazney before they do.\" He slammed the phone on the desk and winced at the crack.",
        "\"It's hard to replace the older-style phones, sir. Please stop breaking them,\" Wu said. She was still following a live video with her tablet.",
        "\"Are you watching the Liu's?\" he asked, pouring himself a drink.",
        "\"Yes. They've just left the police station, and the Detective is following them,\" she said.",
        "\"Good. Let me know when they arrive home,\" Yichen said. He was pacing back and forth in front of his desk.",
        "Wu raised an eyebrow and switched to the feed following the girl. \"The girl and the Russian will soon arrive at Chester Punk's place.\"",
        "Yichen threw his drink at the wall. \"God Dammit! What is Slazney doing?\" He went to his desk and flopped into his chair. Yanking on a desk drawer, he pulled out a picture of a family with a young girl around three years old in it. He ran his finger over the woman's face and stopped on the child.",
        "\"She's grown up well, hasn't she?\" he asked Wu.",
        "\"As well as can be expected.\"",
        "\"To think she's become interested in a police detective?\" he said, smiling. \"I thought she'd have better taste.\" He raised his head. \"Do you think she knows what Slazney did to her father?\"",
        "The secretary shook her head. \"She doesn't trust magic and relies too much on what she sees.\"",
        "\"Have you found her yet?\"",
        "\"No. When Shazad removed the computer, they were all passed out. He heard someone coming and had to leave before he could check on them. Given that Mr. Lifante and the pink girl are moving around without her, we can assume something bad happened to Ming.\" She continued to scroll through the feeds on her tablet. \"Harley is checking out the Detective's place now, but there are too many people in the neighbourhood watching it. He's having trouble getting access.\"",
        "\"Tell him to hurry. We need to find her.\" Yichen grimaced and put the picture atop a black computer with a Motley Crue logo. He shut the drawer and moved away from his desk. \"The moment you find anything that connects me to Slazney or where Ming is, let me know. We can't let another mistake like Stanley get away from us.\"",
        "\"Yes, sir,\" she said, not moving from the tablet."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 23,
      "title": "Chapter 23",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "February 18, 1947",
        "Bobby held his shoulder, trying to stop the bleeding, and forced himself up from the floor. \"Fuck! Do you got a back way out of here?\" he yelled at the apprentice.",
        "\"This is a motel room on the second floor! Of course, there's no back door, jackass,\" the teen yelled back. \"We gotta get to the first floor.\"",
        "\"Do we fight them like we did last night?\" Ming asked, hiding behind the wall.",
        "\"We got lucky. I'm in no shape, and Bugsy's too angry,\" Bobby said, wincing as another bullet went through the window. He stared at the floor. \"Do you think you can open a hole here?\" he asked the apprentice.",
        "He was silent for a moment. \"Give me five minutes. You can't rush the math, and I don't have music.\"",
        "Bobby went to the window and peeked out through the broken glass. Bugsy's men were standing at the corner, just outside the shards. \"I've got a gun here, Bugsy. Tell them to step forward if you want to lose your men.\"",
        "\"Hold!\" Bugsy said. The men stopped moving. \"You dames have caused me a lot of trouble. I'm worried about you, Catherine. If I hadn't found your ex-husband tied up in your bathtub, why, you might have hurt someone else.\"",
        "Ming gasped. \"Jessica's father. Dammit. He must have heard us talking.\"",
        "Nodding, Bobby glanced at the apprentice. He was sitting in the middle of the floor, tapping his knee to get the right beat. He raised three fingers.",
        "\"What do you want, Bugsy?\" Bobby yelled down to the gangster.",
        "\"I want to talk.\" He put his gun away and opened his hands to show he was unarmed. \"It occurs to me that, like Slazney, you could have knowledge that would benefit us. I want you to share what you know with me.\"",
        "\"You're going to die next month, Bugsy,\" Ming yelled. \"Gunned down in your home.\"",
        "\"Don't tell him that,\" Bobby waved his good hand in an X at Ming. \"You could screw up everything.\"",
        "She glared at him and glanced at his shoulder. Gasping, she ran to the bathroom and grabbed a towel. She wrapped it around his shoulder and tied it tight. \"What about the nanobots?\" Ming asked. \"I thought they would heal you.\"",
        "\"Long since past the twenty-four-hour limit.\" Bobby winced. \"They don't last forever.\"",
        "Ming stepped back. \"You've lost too much blood. We need to get you to a doctor.\"",
        "\"No time.\" Bobby gripped the towel. \"Thank you.\" He turned back to the window. Bugsy's men were inching closer. \"**Perestan' shevelit'sya, zasranets**. I'll fire!\"",
        "Bugsy smiled. \"What the hell were you speaking? That don't sound like English. Are you some sortta spy? I'm sure the government would love to get a hold of ya.\" Bugsy raised his head and pointed to room 204. \"Boys, move in.\"",
        "\"Apprentice! You finished?\" Bobby yelled at the teen.",
        "\"Yeah. Stand back,\" he said, and stomped down with his right foot. The floor gave a loud crack as the room shook. The floor buckled, then caved in, dropping the three to the first floor.",
        "\"What the fu---\" Ming was cut off.",
        "Dust spilled into the air, coating everything. Bobby closed his eyes as he bounced off the bed onto the floor. Ming landed on top of him with a grunt and rolled off. He didn't see where the apprentice went.",
        "Bobby groaned as he got to his feet, hacking from the dust. The apprentice stood at the back of the room, feeling the wall. The reporter had already gone to the window.",
        "\"It won't take them long to find us here,\" Bobby said, spitting out more dust. \"Do you have a way out of this room?\"",
        "The apprentice smiled and tapped a brick on the wall. \"We always have a way out,\" he said. The wall opened, leading to a passageway between the buildings behind the motel.",
        "\"Ming! Let's go!\" Bobby grabbed his shoulder and winced. The towel was gone, and blood dripped down his arm, leaving a pool on the floor. The room spun, making everything appear doubled.",
        "\"Stop!\"",
        "Bobby looked up. Two men stared down at them from the hole in the floor. He flipped them the bird and ran out the new door.",
        "\"Where are we going?\" the reporter asked.",
        "\"To a safe house, I suspect. Right?\" he asked the apprentice. \"Same place as last night?\"",
        "The teen was silent but nodded and directed them to follow him. He was panting, sweat beading on his brow. He bit his lip. They could still hear Bugsy's men following them into the alley. The reporter was also breathing heavily, panting with each step. He kept his hand on his shoulder. It didn't hurt as much as it should.",
        "\"Fuck! I'm going into shock. Apprentice,\" he said to the teen, \"If I pass out, leave me for Bugsy and take Ming. She needs to get away.\"",
        "\"Why should I help her?\" he said, peering out at the street. It was clear of cars and no signs of Bugsy's men.",
        "\"She's an innocent caught up in all this. Besides, you had to use your inner energy for that stunt with the floor.\"",
        "The apprentice grumbled.",
        "\"You're almost out of power, so is she.\" Bobby paused. \"Her story's not yet written, or did Kansas not teach you about destiny yet?\"",
        "The teen scrunched down. Bobby couldn't see his face but imagined it wasn't happy.",
        "A series of gunshots pinged off the side of the alley wall, sending chips of plaster raining over their heads. \"Split up!\" Bobby shouted. \"Go with him, Ming!\"",
        "He ignored her pleading hand and ran in the opposite direction down the street. He heard her shout, but he was too far to stop. Still clutching his shoulder, he plowed ahead through the sea of people. Most of them stared at the woman in the sundress holding a bloody hand on her shoulder, but nobody stopped to help, and Bobby didn't give them the chance. He turned around to check if anybody was following him, but it was quiet. The only people looking at him were the other pedestrians on the street. Two were coming forward.",
        "\"Fuck!\"",
        "\"Are you okay, ma'am?\" Somebody asked. Bobby turned, and a worker pointed to his shoulder.",
        "\"Yes. Just cut myself shaving,\" Bobby said, ignoring the stares. He stumbled and fell to his knees. His head was spinning. He had to get back there. Ming was in trouble, and it was all his fault. Raving about destiny and then leaving her there. This was all his fault. Bobby tried to force himself up but collapsed onto his side.",
        "\"Call an ambulance!\" somebody said.",
        "\"Losing too much blood now,\" he mumbled. \"Fuckin' hell.\" He couldn't lose anybody else.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "Ming bit her lip and wondered if the apprentice was okay. Bugsy's men had pistol-whipped him and left him in the alley when they picked her up. She hoped he was breathing, but was more worried about Bobby.",
        "She sat in Bugsy's car and stared at the gangster. She wished she had her notebook. She was still uncertain about time travel, but Einstein was convinced it could happen, and she was now living proof. Einstein was still alive. What she wouldn't give to pick his brain before it gets stolen.",
        "\"Where's the mother?\" Bugsy said to one of his men. They were still in the motel parking lot, but sirens were coming. The hole the teen had made in the floor and the gunshots had been too noisy.",
        "\"We can't find her, but Sammy reported a woman being picked up by an ambulance on Third and taken to de Lima. According to the reports, she had a gunshot wound,\" one man said.",
        "\"That must be her.\" Bugsy waved to his men. \"Call our man there. We'll get her later. Let's go!\" He tapped on the driver's shoulder and pointed to the road.",
        "She bit her lip and breathed a sigh of relief. Bobby was in trouble, but she was going to the hospital. The towel wasn't going to stop the bleeding.",
        "Ming looked at Bugsy, her fingers twitching for a pencil. She had to take this chance. If she didn't, she'd regret it. Bobby was okay and would probably understand. What if it were Motley Crue?",
        "\"Mr. Siegel, can I ask you a few questions?\" Ming asked, locking the guilt away.",
        "He raised an eyebrow. \"Sure, doll. Ask away.\" He leaned back in the seat and closed his eyes. The bandages across his nose and black eyes made him look like a skull.",
        "\"When you took over the ownership of the Flamingo, how did you deal with the pushback from the previous owner?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"Huh? I threatened to shoot him in the face. What kinda question is that?\" he asked.",
        "\"The probing kind,\" Ming replied. \"In addition, how did you stifle resistance within your organization to your building plans? I know some weren't happy about moving here.\"",
        "Bugsy just turned away from Ming and stared out the window. She heard him mumbling about stupid questions.",
        "She clicked her teeth together. She'd had difficult interviews before, but usually, they gave her something. \"How did you meet Slazney and what did he do for you?\" she asked. She wanted to know so many things about who he was and why he did the things he did, but if he could answer this one, the others could wait.",
        "\"He came to me one day with a plan to buy the Flamingo. Said it would put my name in everybody's mouth. I believed him. He was very---,\" Bugsy paused on the word, drawing it out. \"--- convincing. I wasn't that interested before. Vegas was a nothing town, but once I got here and took a look at the potential, I was all in.\"",
        "He was distracted. Now was the perfect time for the punch.",
        "\"Aren't you worried that the accusations you and Ms. Hill were skimming the construction funds will come back to haunt you?\" Ming asked.",
        "\"What? Gina would never do that!\" He glared at her and raised a hand. \"I don't like what you're getting at. No more questions till we get to the Flamingo.\"",
        "Ming raised her hands, palm out in a non-threatening gesture, nodded and sat back in the seat. \"Sorry. I just don't get to talk to important men like you very often.\"",
        "\"Apology accepted. Now be quiet.\" Bugsy stared out the window.",
        "When they arrived, some of Bugsy's men dragged her to a room bigger than Jessica's house. She could get lost in this place, and nobody would ever find her. They shoved her in and shut the door. The carpet was a deep red, and the canopy bed looked inviting. Ming was tired, but this was no time to sleep. She still ached from the fight the night before and the chase through the streets. She hated violence. There was never a purpose for it. Ignoring the bed, she stepped up to the window and stifled a yawn with her fist. She moved the lace curtains aside and stared out over Las Vegas. \"I hope Bobby's okay.\" She sighed. \"Everything seems so small and quiet.\"",
        "\"Really? I thought it was pretty noisy,\" Bugsy said from the door.",
        "Ming closed her eyes and took a deep breath. \"Why would I expect you to knock? Here I thought you were a gentleman.\"",
        "\"Being a gentleman was tossed out the window when your mother broke my nose.\" Bugsy went to a fancy red velvet chair and sat. \"Now, let's continue the conversation we started in the car. Why are you here, and what's your connection to Slazney?\"",
        "Ming moved to the desk and opened the drawer. \"What, no paper? You should keep note paper and pens in the room, in case someone has to write something down.\"",
        "\"I'll keep it in mind. Now stop stalling. Talk!\" Bugsy was no longer playing the playboy.",
        "She went to the chair opposite Bugsy and sat. Leaning forward, she kept her shoulders back. He had all the power in this room, and she needed to let him think she was intimidated, but not too much. Besides, his reputation as a hound was quite famous, and Jessica was beautiful. If only she were wearing a low-cut blouse.",
        "Ming closed her eyes and said a little prayer. \"No, I can't use her like that. Sorry for even thinking about it.\" She couldn't shake the disgusting feeling.",
        "\"Why are you sorry?\"",
        "\"I wasn't talking to you.\" She opened her eyes and stared at Bugsy. \"Slazney is responsible for us being here. He sent us to tell you what you're doing in Vegas is wrong, and if you continue on this path, you will die within the month.\" Ming bit her lip. It was the truth, but if he believed her, it could change history.",
        "He stared at her. His mouth was a thin line, a smile slowly tugged its way up, and he started chuckling. \"I see.\" He shook his head and sighed. \"One last chance. Why are you here?\" The smile disappeared. \"This time, I want to believe you.\"",
        "Ming shook her head. \"The truth too unbelievable for a liar? Fine. I'm here by accident. I have no connection to this Slazney and no idea where he is. In fact, if you can tell me anything about him, I'd really appreciate it. I've been looking for him for years.\" She crossed her arms and glared at the gangster.",
        "\"Why is that?\" Bugsy asked. He pulled out a cigar and lit it. Taking a deep drag on it, he released the smoke directly at Ming.",
        "Ming coughed. The stench invaded her throat. She turned her head and took a breath of clean air. \"I'm convinced he's the secret mover behind most of the Vegas mob scene, and an expose on him would propel me into the top level of journalism.\" He didn't need to know the second reason.",
        "Bugsy started chuckling. It turned into a gut-aching belly laugh. \"You're lying. I can tell.\"",
        "Ming betrayed nothing on her face.",
        "\"I see.\" He stood up. \"No matter. I don't need you. Your mother, I'm undecided about. I was worried when Slazney said to be careful of strangers asking questions, but I think I can relax.\" He went to the door and knocked; two men walked in. \"I need you two to take her to the desert and lose her.\"",
        "\"You can't do this,\" Ming said. She glared at Bugsy. She stood up, thrust her hands to her side and moved into a fighting stance. There was no way she was going to let anybody touch her.",
        "\"I can. Though rest assured, I'm not going to kill you. That's not gentlemanly, and a man should always strive to be polite to a beautiful dame, such as yourself.\" He smiled. \"That doesn't mean you'll survive.\" He bowed to her. \"It was a pleasure to meet you.\" Straightening his tie, he left the room.",
        "Ming watched the two men close in on her, leering. The one on the left glanced at the bed and loosened his tie. She may not have Dean's sense for people, but why do men go there?",
        "Ming stepped away from the front of the chair and moved behind it, bringing up what her Aikido teacher said about defending herself, forcing them to separate. It would give her a few extra seconds if they needed to go around the furniture. The first man reached for her shoulders. Ming grabbed his elbow with her left hand and thrust her palm up into the man's chin, staggering him. He fell backwards and tripped over the chair, slamming his head on the ground.",
        "The second man was stunned, probably surprised that a girl could fight back. Ming used his hesitation to spin towards him, drop between his legs and punch his crotch. He screamed and dropped, holding his hands between his legs.",
        "She stood up, looked at the two men and said a silent thanks to her teacher Richard. His advice to go for the crotch always paid off. Ignoring the two men twitching on the floor, Ming ran to the door. The fight you avoid is the fight you always win, or so he'd like to say. It was unlocked. She took a deep breath, grabbed the knob, slowly twisted it to the open position in case someone was standing outside and yanked it open.",
        "The hallway was empty. She gripped the door frame to keep from falling, but she wasn't finished yet.",
        "Running back to the unconscious man, she patted his pockets and found a set of car keys in them. He was starting to groan and rub his head. Raising her leg, she stomped on his face and heard his nose crunch.",
        "\"Come back here,\" the second man groaned. He had pulled himself up and was hanging off the chair. His face was white, and he was reaching into his jacket.",
        "She dashed over to him and smashed her palm against his nose. He dropped back to the ground, unconscious.",
        "Spinning, Ming raced back to the door and went for the stairs. She jumped down the three flights, skipping the steps and pausing on the platforms to catch her breath. At the bottom, she burst into the empty casino. The grand reopening was coming soon, but for now, it was quiet.",
        "Ming took the keys in her pocket and threw them into the corner. Let them think she tried to steal a car. She knew how to get to de Lima, but first, she needed some help."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 24,
      "title": "Chapter 24",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "3:30 PM",
        "Dean followed the Lius' white car. Traffic was heavy, and he was afraid of losing it. There were already three other white Ford Endeavours around him. He stuck two car lengths back to stay out of their way. His stomach wouldn't stop jumping, dread gnawing at him. Usually, his instinct was just a feeling that something was wrong. Ever since he'd met Ming's parents, he realized a new level of pain. There were some slight butterflies when he shook the mother's hand, but the father was different. The last time this reaction happened, he was hit with a summons from his ex-wife and arrested for rape and the murder of her lover. Ming had been the only one to help him clear his name.",
        "He gripped the steering wheel tighter. The rubber squeaked in protest. Ming couldn't be involved in this, could she? Her parents weren't on Stanley's list, just Yichen. Why did he feel like he couldn't trust her? This was going to kill him.",
        "\"Where are they going?\" he muttered.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Barbie",
        "3:30 PM",
        "\"What do you mean he's dead?\" Barbie yelled at the door. She waved her arms in the air and stomped her foot. \"His son said he talked to him today and that Chip Sr. was fine.\"",
        "\"I'm very sorry my husband's death has inconvenienced you,\" Mrs. Punk said, huffing. \"He died in a car accident a few years ago.\" She shut the outer door. \"Now, please leave.\"",
        "Barbie stood outside the Punks' door and puffed her cheeks out. \"Pbthhh.\" She spun around and stomped back to the car. Yanking the door open, she slid in. \"Give me your phone. I gotta call Dean.\"",
        "Ivan reached into his pocket with his right hand and handed his phone to Barbie. He pulled out a second phone with his left hand, kept it low and started typing.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "4:00 PM",
        "The Lius turned down the road leading to his neighbourhood. After Dean had divorced his wife, he had moved into this run-down part of the city. The houses still had their paint, but it wasn't fresh with exposed panelling. The yards needed work with the fences and grass showing the same kind of neglect.",
        "He sped up, overtaking their white Ford and pulled into the spot in front of his house. Parking at an angle, he jumped out and raced to the porch. He could still hear the hum of the air conditioner through the door. Testing the door to see if it was still locked, he spun around and faced the Lius as they were coming up the sidewalk.",
        "\"Why were you following us?\" Mrs. Liu asked. Her hands were on her hips, and she was glaring at him. Mr. Liu was behind her.",
        "\"This is my house. Can I ask what you're doing here?\" Dean placed his hand on his gun, wary of what his wife might do. However, he kept his instinct trained on the older man. He had no idea what Mr. Liu was capable of.",
        "\"We're looking for our daughter.\" Mrs. Liu poked Dean in the chest with her finger again. \"We traced her phone here and know you've done something to her.\"",
        "\"Her phone?\" Dean smiled at the woman. *How could I have been so stupid? Of course, she'd be carrying a tracking app on her phone.*",
        "\"She must have forgotten it last night,\" Dean said, praying that Ming would forgive him. \"We were brainstorming the latest case. She's working with me.\" Dean cringed. Why was everything he said digging him deeper into the hole? He knew enough about Chinese culture that you never mention their daughter spent the night at your place.",
        "\"Who are you looking for?\" Mr. Liu said, stepping closer to the door.",
        "Dean tuned out Mrs. Liu's voice and stared at Ming's father. Why was this feeling racing through his body? It was a cross between falling and wanting to throw up. When Ming first tried to help him, he did a background check on her and her family. He'd uncovered her connection to Yichen and the Shujing. That had concerned him, but she was able to explain it. He was her grandmother's brother.",
        "Ming's mother was a typical housewife, angry and controlling. Nothing was interesting about her father's life. He was a salesman and often travelled for work. The only interesting fact Dean had uncovered about the man was that when Ming was seven, he'd been in a car accident and almost died. She said he was cold afterwards. Like something had changed.",
        "\"No,\" he whispered. The realization hit Dean like a bullet to the head. He took a step back, his eyes widening. This was the same setup as with Doctor Stanley. He stared at Mr. Liu, and the pit in his stomach stopped falling. That only happened when he made the right decision.",
        "\"Stop ignoring me and tell me where my daughter is!\" Mrs. Liu yelled. She got into Dean's face, the veins in her neck ready to pop.",
        "Placing his hands on her shoulders, he pushed her to the side. \"When did he die?\" he asked Mr. Liu. \"Was it the accident or in the hospital?\"",
        "\"What are you talking about?\" Mrs. Liu screamed. \"When did who die? My husband isn't dead, you sicko.\"",
        "Mr. Liu was silent. He gave a small smile. \"The hospital bed,\" he mouthed.",
        "Dean staggered back and fell against the door. Sprawled on the front porch, he narrowed his eyes at Ming's father. \"Does Ming know?\"",
        "\"She suspects,\" Mr. Liu said.",
        "\"Does Ming know what?\" Mrs. Liu stomped her foot. \"I've had enough of this farce.\" She went to the door and started pounding on it. \"Ming! I know you're in there. Open up.\"",
        "\"What's with the old lady?\"",
        "Dean turned and watched Barbie get out of Ivan's car. She was pointing at Mrs. Liu. The big man stood on the other side, staring at the house. He raised a phone and took a picture.",
        "\"Who's she?\" Mrs. Liu screamed, pointing a finger at Barbie. \"Another floozy? Are you bringing my daughter down to match the depravity of your life?\"",
        "His neighbour's curtains twitched. He wouldn't be surprised to find this incident posted on the tabloid sites soon.",
        "\"Why'd you come here?\" Dean asked Barbie, rubbing the bridge of his nose.",
        "\"I couldn't get you on the phone.\" She shrugged. \"When I called the station, a Zacoski said you'd taken off. I figured you were checking on the Maker.\"",
        "Dean closed his eyes and looked around Barbie at the car. \"Maybe Ivan didn't hear that. Again. Why are you here?\"",
        "\"Chester Punk Sr. is dead. He was in a car accident a few years ago and didn't survive,\" Barbie said.",
        "\"There are a lot of accidents around you, aren't there, Slazney? Isn't that a bit too cliché?\" Dean said to Mr. Liu. He just smiled and continued to stand where he was. Barbie's eyes widened as she looked at the older Asian man. Dean nodded, and she smiled. She got behind him. Ivan completed the circle around the old man, leaving him pinned in on three sides.",
        "\"Do something, you fool!\" Mrs. Liu yelled at her husband. If this were a cartoon, Dean would have expected her teeth to fly out and chomp him on the nose. The absurdity of the situation fits that response.",
        "\"Yes, Dear,\" Mr. Liu said and relaxed his stance.",
        "\"Take it easy, sir. We have some questions for you.\" Dean stepped forward, reaching for the older man.",
        "Mr. Liu slapped Dean's hand away and took a step back. \"You don't want to be doing this. Not here,\" he said.",
        "\"The questions won't take long.\" Dean directed Ivan to hold onto the man. He remembered how difficult it was to take him down in the police station. There would be no escaping from the Russians' grip.",
        "\"That's too bad,\" Mr. Liu said. \"This body had been very useful, but I was almost finished with it anyway.\"",
        "\"Dear?\" Dean heard the confusion in Mrs. Liu's voice. It was less shrill and more worried. Her eyes narrowed, and she was frowning. \"What are you saying? I don't understand.\"",
        "Her husband ignored her and hit a switch on his belt. A stream of black gas hissed out and wrapped itself around Mr. Liu, covering the whole front of Dean's house in seconds, forcing Barbie and Ivan back.",
        "\"Dear!\" Mrs. Liu shouted, stepping forward, hands outstretched. Her face was a mask of concern.",
        "\"Fuck!\" Dean shot forward and stepped into the smoke. \"Don't let him get away!\" Waving his arms around, he felt nothing. \"Where are you, Mr. Liu?\"",
        "No answer.",
        "\"What are you doing?\" Mrs. Liu said from outside the cloud. \"Where did this smoke come from? Find my husband!\" She started coughing.",
        "Dean stepped forward and tripped over something in the darkness. Sprawled on the ground, he turned around and sprawled in something sticky. Crawling over to it, he pulled out his phone, moved in close and turned on the flashlight app.",
        "Mr. Liu's dead face stared back at him. The eyes had already sunk into the back of the head, and he was starting to putrefy. The smell hit Dean like a truck. He tripped, staggered out of the smoke and started coughing.",
        "\"What happened?\" Mrs. Liu said, grabbing onto his sleeve. \"Where's my husband? What did you see?\"",
        "Barbie and Ivan stared at the smoke. Both of them stood with their arms crossed.",
        "Dean grumbled and pulled out his phone. \"I'm sorry, Mrs. Liu. Your husband is dead.\" He hated himself for being so cold. The only way he knew how to deal with the sight was to shut it out while dialling the precinct. He wasn't going to be able to hide this.",
        "\"No! You're lying!\" Mrs. Liu turned to the black smoke and watched as the wind picked up and blew it away, revealing a pile of bones, clothes and a watch. Some of the bones had already turned to dust, leaving the teeth and his clothing. Mrs. Liu clenched her face with her hands and fell to her knees. She started screaming, rocking back and forth.",
        "\"What the fuck?\" Dean said. His mask shattered. Nausea worked its way up.",
        "Barbie came up next to him. \"Slazney was using the body for too long, and the soul is long gone. When he abandoned it, it reverted to the state it should have been in,\" she said. \"The Chinese often cremate the dead, so when Slazney left, he became mostly dust.\"",
        "Mrs. Liu continued to cry and rock back and forth on the ground. Her wailing pierced Dean's heart. Wiping his eyes, he placed a call to the precinct.",
        "6:00 PM",
        "Dean ground his teeth as he watched Ortiz load Mrs. Liu into a car to take her home. Fischer was kneeling over the pile of bone dust, poking at it with a pen. Everything was taking too long.",
        "\"Are you sure it was her husband?\" he asked Dean. He started scooping it into one of the plastic baggies.",
        "\"Yes. The neighbour got it all on video,\" Dean said, winging. \"I've already sent a copy to Zacoski.\"",
        "\"Humm!\" Fischer said.",
        "\"What is it?\"",
        "The head CSI was silent and finished cleaning up the remains. \"I've only ever seen this kind of thing once before.\" He put the plastic bag into a larger canvas one. \"You say there was a black smoke, and when it cleared, the body was gone, and the bones were turning to dust.\"",
        "\"Yes. I've already told you three times,\" Dean grumbled. \"Where are you going with this?\"",
        "\"The last time I saw this was a few years ago, when the body of a perfectly healthy businessman suddenly keeled over and dissolved during a business meeting. None of the other people in the room was affected.\"",
        "\"I never heard of that,\" Dean said, drawing back. \"When was this?\"",
        "\"I'm not surprised. Zacoski and the FBI hushed it up. Told me never to say anything.\" He turned to Dean. \"I'm sure they'll be here soon.\" He packed up his bag and walked away.",
        "Dean had always hated Fischer. It wasn't on purpose, but the CSI found the evidence that Dean had killed his wife's lover. His wife had planted it in his kitchen, and Fischer, doing his job, uncovered everything and never apologized when the charges were proven bogus. Dean had never forgiven the man, and Fischer knew it. He always acted like a prick, insulting Dean every chance he got, so it made it easy. Now, it was hard to keep it up.",
        "He went over to Ortiz. \"How's Mrs. Liu?\"",
        "\"In denial. It's not every day someone you love dissolves in front of you,\" she said. \"She could only deal with it by blocking it out. She said she's planning on cooking dinner for her husband when he gets home from his latest trip. Hell, if I hadn't seen the video, I wouldn't believe it. I'm going to take her home.\"",
        "\"Thank you, Ortiz. I really appreciate it.\" Dean nodded and turned away.",
        "\"Detective Lifante?\" she said.",
        "\"Yes, Ortiz?\"",
        "\"I ran up on the name of the person who leaked Mr. Miladev's name to the press,\" she said.",
        "\"What did you find out?\"",
        "She glanced to the side, almost as if she was worried someone was listening in on her. Taking a step forward, she lowered her voice. \"According to the man I spoke to at the news office, it was from an official statement given to them by Lieutenant Zacoski.\"",
        "Dean grunted. \"I'll talk to him about it when I get the chance.\"",
        "\"Yes, sir. Umm. I don't believe everything they say about you at the precinct. You aren't the person they say you are,\" she said. She was looking down and twiddling her thumbs.",
        "Dean raised an eyebrow. Ten years ago, if a young woman had said something complementary to him, he'd be drawing a short breath and blushing. Now, he narrowed his eyes. He hated how far he'd fallen since those days. \"What makes you say that?\"",
        "\"I don't know.\" She ran her hand through her brown hair. \"Just a gut feeling.\" She stared up at his face.",
        "Dean chuckled. \"Keep that feeling strong. It'll take you places.\" Dean turned around and waved his hand in the air. Maybe people weren't all bad. He walked away and tripped over a loose stone, stumbling forward and landing on his porch.",
        "\"You've got a red face,\" Barbie said. \"I thought you liked the reporter. Why are you trying to get into the young woman's pants?\" she asked.",
        "\"Shut up!\" Dean growled. \"Why are you outside the house?\" he whispered. \"I told you to make sure nobody saw those two. That's why I sent Ivan away as well. Two uniforms are already chasing his car.\"",
        "Barbie scrunched her face. \"The Maker is fine. He could use a bath, but the woman is gone.\"",
        "Dean pushed past Barbie and ran to the bedroom. Bobby's corpse was on the bed, turning stiff. There was no sign of Ming, though, just her phone."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 25,
      "title": "Chapter 25",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "February 18^th^, 1947",
        "Ming raced through the Vegas streets, ignoring the stares. A woman running in a dress was a rare sight in this place, but there was no time. The heat pounded the streets, and sweat rolled off her.",
        "When she passed the construction site from the previous day, she paused and took a deep, gulping breath. \"I know this place. I can find it,\" she mumbled, rambling. She started looking for the same path Bobby took to get to the bar. At an intersection, she paused and put her hand against the wall. Slumping against the solid structure, she took deeper breaths, gasping for water and fanning herself. It felt like pins and needles were running down her legs. By now, Bugsy should know she was gone. She needed to get to the hospital, but it would take about four hours on foot. He could get there in thirty minutes.",
        "\"Why'd I dump the keys?\" she admonished. \"I could have used the car.\" *And gotten caught by Bugsy before I drove out of the hotel.*",
        "Straightening, Ming turned into the alley where the bar was located. She coughed out the dust and found the same door set in the basement. She pounded on it and waited.",
        "\"I know it's late afternoon, but c'mon,\" she yelled. \"Where's the rude shit from yesterday?\" Pounding again, the tears blurred her vision. \"Open up! Please, help me. I need to get Bobby. I don't want to stay here.\" She was blubbering, but she couldn't spend the rest of her life here and never see her parents again. Ming missed her mother, even with the woman's incessant desire to marry Ming off to a rich man. She would even be willing to try and thaw her father's cold attitude. Most of all, she missed Dean. She had avoided thinking of Dean the whole time she was here. Even her letter to him said she would get home. She needed to stop playing around with him and take their relationship to the next step.",
        "\"I need my family.\" She started crying harder. \"I don't want to be alone.\"",
        "\"Whatcha doing here? Haven't you done enough?\"",
        "The voice came from above. She wiped her tears on her sleeve and turned to see Apprentice standing at the top of the stairs. He had a bandage around his temple, black eyes and a split lip with a small stitch to keep it closed. He stared at her like she was a plague and the tax man rolled into one.",
        "\"You're okay!\" She laughed as she stumbled up the stairs and gave him a bone-squeezing hug. \"I was so worried about you.\" He stiffened, then relaxed and put his arms around her.",
        "\"It takes more than a beating to bring me down.\" He pushed her back. \"Again, whatcha doing here?\"",
        "\"I need some help, Apprentice. Kansas Joe was here yesterday. Bobby's in the de Lima hospital, and it's only a matter of time before Bugsy'll get to her.\" It all rushed out. Ming told him about getting kidnapped, what Bugsy said, and beating the two men. He looked at her with narrowed eyes, but they soon softened, and he was nodding at the end.",
        "\"Jim. Call me Jim,\" he said, looking away. \"Apprentice sounds stupid.\"",
        "\"Jim.\" Ming smiled. \"Thank you. It's a nice name. I'm Ming, although she's Jessica.\" Ming pointed to herself. \"I'm rambling, I know. I feel like my chest is clenching up and threatening to go all explodey like in the movie, which won't exist for another thirty or so years.\" Jim's face was so absurd it kicked her brain back on track, and she remembered where she was.",
        "\"Sorry, I wasn't speaking straight. You know where we come from, right?\" She narrowed her eyes and stared back at him.",
        "\"Somewhat. Joe let me know before he and Millie went back home. They couldn't stay. His heart is getting real bad.\" Jim frowned. He shook his head. \"Anyway, let's get you to the hospital. I've got a car.\" He took her hand and led her away from the jazz bar.",
        "The ride was silent. Jim was concentrating on the road, and Ming needed to organize her feelings. She had to admit that magic was real. All the evidence was pointing towards it being the truth. It was disguised as science and computer code, but how else could she explain it? \"The evidence is only leading me one way.\" And she trusted the evidence.",
        "\"What'd ya say?\"",
        "\"Nothing.\"",
        "She pulled out the letter she'd written to Jessica. \"Can I ask you a favour?\" Ming asked Jim, staring at the envelope.",
        "\"Depends on the favour,\" Jim said, not looking at her.",
        "\"If we get out of here or disappear, can you make sure Jessica gets this letter?\" Ming held it out. \"I left some things in here about what happened to her and how she can help us in the future.\"",
        "Jim grunted. \"That's a pretty big favour. What's in it for me?\"",
        "Ming opened her mouth and closed it again. \"Nothing. I can't give you anything, but my thanks.\" She put the letter back in her purse.",
        "\"I'll do what I can,\" Jim said. \"There is something you can give me, though.\"",
        "\"What?\"",
        "\"A promise is very powerful among us. One day, if not me, possibly my descendant, depending on when you're from, you'll have to pay this favour back, no questions.\" He turned to her. \"Is that acceptable?\"",
        "\"Yes, of course.\" Ming was ready to pay anything for this. The one thing she realized about magic was that almost anything was possible if one was willing to pay the price.",
        "Jim held out his hand, and Ming shook it.",
        "\"Ow! I was shocked. Static electricity?\" She rubbed her palm.",
        "Jim smiled. \"No. That was the soul binding. The promise is now a part of who you are and will follow you everywhere. When the time comes, you'll know what it means.\"",
        "Ming continued to knead her fingers into her palm and stared out the window. She smiled. At least Jessica would be all right. The pins and needles feeling started travelling up her arm.",
        "Reaching the hospital, Ming pointed to the entrance and ducked down in the seat.",
        "\"What is it?\" Jim asked.",
        "\"The men over by the front. They're Bugsy's. He's here.\" Ming pushed herself into the brown leather, hiding behind the door. \"Find a parking space away from the front.\"",
        "\"No problem. They don't let blacks in there anyway.\"",
        "Ming heard the contempt in his voice as he drove away from the front. She peeked over the seat, but they weren't following. Twisting back around, the butterflies in her stomach grow. The tingling feeling from the binding had spread through her chest and settled into her head. It was contrasting with her stomach.",
        "\"I feel funny,\" she said, rubbing her stomach.",
        "\"How so?\" Jim asked. He was parking the car on a side street, away from the main doors. He put his arm over the headrest.",
        "\"Like I'm going to fly away and fall at the same time. I feel all tingly from the binding and flighty. It's weird.\"",
        "\"That shouldn't be happening,\" Jim said, putting his hand on Ming's forehead and closing his eyes. She heard him mumble something, but couldn't make out the words.",
        "\"What is it?\"",
        "\"Shush!\" He opened his eyes and grabbed her face, turning it to look at him. His eyes were crimson, but they were shifting to lavender.",
        "The butterflies changed into birds. Ming grabbed her stomach but couldn't look away from Jim. \"What's going on? Am I going to die?\"",
        "\"I couldn't say. When I saw your lifeline, it still had some space to grow. But it looks like your time here is up, miss. Your body is rejecting the extra soul, and it's being forced back to where it came from.\"",
        "Ming nodded. She reached into her purse and pulled out the letter. She placed it in Jim's hands. \"How about Bobby?\"",
        "\"I don't know. I'll check on her, hell him, whatever she is.\"",
        "\"Thank you.\" Ming winced and doubled over. The pins and needles were poking every part of her body now and stretching it out into space. \"Dammit! I wanted to interview that bastard just once.\" A knock on the car door distracted her, but before she could turn, the feeling engulfed her toes, driving everything out. She gave a small squeak-like shout, and everything turned black.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "February 18^th^, 1947",
        "Bobby blinked slowly. Lead weights were holding his eyes down. He raised his hand to rub them, and something pulled at it. Looking up, there was an IV drip in his arm. Wincing, he turned and looked at his shoulder. It was bandaged, but he could still feel the bullet in it.",
        "\"Where am I?\" he groaned. \"Nurse?\" he tried to shout, but it came out as a croak. Struggling to sit up, he reached for a buzzer. \"Nothing.\" Looking around, he found a string with a loop at the bottom. Yanking it, he heard bells ring somewhere. The room was spinning, and he squeezed his eyes shut.",
        "\"Are you awake?\" A young doctor came into the room. He was tall and handsome with perfect teeth. Bobby wouldn't be surprised to see him on the cover of a magazine.",
        "\"Yes. Where am I?\" he asked, squinting. The man's teeth were starting to give him a headache. \"Have you seen my daughter?\"",
        "\"In de Lima hospital.\" He picked up Bobby's hand and checked his pulse. \"Someone shot you. Do you know who?\" He looked at Bobby with worried eyes.",
        "\"No. Didn't see a thing, Doctor Teeth.\" It didn't matter how cute he thought he was; there was no way he was getting any information out of him. Bobby's eyes widened. *Why am I thinking a guy is cute? Fuck! I've been in this body too long.*",
        "\"I see,\" the doctor said, marking a few ticks on Bobby's chart. \"There is someone here to see you.\" He replaced the chart and smiled.",
        "Bobby didn't like his smile. \"Who?\"",
        "\"He says he's a friend.\" The doctor leaned out the door. \"You can come in now.\"",
        "\"Thanks, doc.\" Bugsy placed a hand on the doctor's shoulder as he and three of his men walked in. \"I owe you one.\"",
        "\"It's my pleasure, Mr. Siegel. After all, you've done so much for me.\" The doctor nodded and stood in the corner.",
        "\"Never trust the pretty ones,\" Bobby grumbled. \"They'll always fuck you in the back while smiling to your face.\"",
        "\"That's no way for a dame to talk,\" Bugsy said, feigning indignation.",
        "\"Wow! If you were any sexier, I'd be looking for the vibrator to finish myself off.\"",
        "Bugsy frowned and pulled out a pack of cigarettes. \"Mind if I smoke?\" He lit one and took a puff.",
        "\"Why the fuck did you even ask, you cock-sucking son of a bitch?\" Bobby sneered, then smiled when the cigarette dropped from Bugsy's open mouth. \"Oh, going for a new look as a flycatcher, or would you like me to shove the catheter in there? Just replace that bandage across your nose with some flypaper, and you're set.\" He laughed and held his stomach. The bandage on his shoulder pulled at him.",
        "\"That felt good. I've had a lot of stress these last few days,\" Bobby said, pursing his lips. \"So, Mr. Siegel, what would you like to know?\"",
        "Bugsy took out another cigarette and lit it. \"First, you won't use that kind of language again. Understand?\" He wrinkled his nose at Bobby.",
        "\"Yes sir, sir!\" Bobby saluted. \"Did they give me some drugs? I'm feeling really good here. Can I get some more?\" He smiled and let out a sigh as he snuggled into the bed.",
        "\"Doc?\"",
        "\"Well, we gave her some opiates for the pain. It should keep her lucid and might explain her mouth,\" the handsome doc said, running his hand through his hair. He gave a nervous laugh.",
        "\"You want to know about Slazney, right?\" Bobby said, pushing himself up. \"What is my connection to him, right?\"",
        "\"Yes.\" Bugsy turned to one of his men and pointed at Bobby. The man scrunched his eyebrows.",
        "\"He wants you to get on the other side of me, Brainiac. In case I make a break for it, tied to the bed like I am, I could still break his other nose.\" Bobby rolled his eyes. \"I don't have all day.\" He turned back to Bugsy. \"As for Slazney, well, he fucked up my life, made me remember a bunch of useless shit I had blocked out for my safety and sent me here. Probably tried to hack my code.\" Bobby spat on Bugsy's shoes. \"The useless prick could never do anything right.\"",
        "\"You speak as if you know him?\" Bugsy asked. He was frowning.",
        "\"I should. He's got to be my fuck-wit brother. I'm ninety percent sure.\" Bobby clicked his tongue. \"I thought he was dead. When I see him again, I'm going to feed him to the pigs.\" Bobby flopped backwards onto the pillow, wiggling deeper into the covers.",
        "Bugsy squirmed and gave a lopsided smile. \"Used to being in control, ain't ya? Oh no,\" Bobby said, poking his pointer fingers to his dimples and twisting them. \"What are you going to do, Mister Mobster Man?\"",
        "\"If you ever want to see your daughter again, you'll stop acting like a blasted clown and pay attention!\" Bugsy bit down on his cigarette, snapping off the filter.",
        "Bobby stopped twisting in the bed. \"**Yesli ty prichinish' yey vred, ya skormlyu tebya svin'yam**.\" (If you hurt her, I'll feed you to the pigs.)",
        "\"What language was that, boys?\" Bugsy turned to his men. \"She ain't speaking American.\" They started laughing.",
        "\"It's Russian, you son of a whore.\"",
        "Bugsy slapped Bobby across the face. \"You will never insult my mother!\" He stuck his fist in front of Bobby's face. \"Next time you'll get a closed one.\"",
        "Bobby spat out some blood. \"Then I expect the same consideration for my daughter, you donkey.\"",
        "\"Very well.\" He smiled. \"Speaking of her, would you like to meet her? One of the men saw a coloured driving a car. They followed them and found a present in the front seat.\" He waved to the door. \"She was worried about you.\"",
        "The pit of his stomach dropped and kicked him in the crotch. The door opened, and Ming walked in. She was trembling, swinging her head between the two men. When she shifted her head to Bobby, she let out a gasp.",
        "\"Mother, what happened to you? Were you shot?\" She twisted her shoulders out of the men's hands and ran to Bobby's side. Grabbing his hands, she asked, \"Who did this?\"",
        "\"I'm okay, Ming. Don't worry.\"",
        "Ming twisted her head to the side, and a puzzled look flashed across her face. \"Did you hit your head, Mom? It's Jessica.\"",
        "\"Fuck,\" Bobby groaned, covering his face with his hands. His stomach dropped further, but now a pit of acid replaced it, tearing up his insides."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 26,
      "title": "Chapter 26",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "6:30 PM",
        "\"How?\" Dean asked, falling to his knees. Tears of frustration welled up behind his eyes and he forced them back. \"Where did she go?\"",
        "\"I have no idea, but if we don't find the Maker's computer soon, it won't matter. Neither of them will come back.\" Barbie bit her lip and started pacing back and forth.",
        "They had a little over six hours left to find the computer. Dean put his hands on the floor in front of him and gripped the carpet, pulling out small tuffs of the fabric. They'd found Slazney, but Ming's father was dead. The sight of him dissolving was going to stay with Dean for a long time. He shuddered and shoved that image into a box. There was no time for that.",
        "Chester Punk Sr. was a dead end. He must have been a candidate, but Slazney abandoned him when Bobby got the job. His gut still told him to trust Zacoski. Slazney was holding something over him, probably his family. That man was a maniac about his daughter, always showing him pictures of her. Going on about how smart she was. She was three-years-old. It was annoying, but you couldn't fake that level of insanity. It would explain the release.",
        "Dean went to his computer to check on the cameras. They were expensive, but he'd had them set up around his yard. The server was supposed to be protected and unhackable.",
        "\"Dammit!\"",
        "\"What?\" Barbie asked, twirling around.",
        "\"The video's been erased.\" Dean hit his desk. \"I'm going to head back to the video store and persuade the manager to give me a complete refund, even if I have to pull out his teeth one by one.\"",
        "\"Play with your friends later,\" Barbie said. \"What are we going to do?\"",
        "\"We're going back to the Shujing,\" Dean said, standing. \"Stanley had a file on Yichen. It must have been about Ming's father, but maybe there's more to it.\"",
        "\"Why? We were there earlier and couldn't find anything.\"",
        "\"We were tied up at the time. Anyway, it's a feeling I'm having. Something important will happen there. Besides, he's the only one left.\"",
        "\"Sounds good.\" Barbie pointed to Bobby. \"What about the Maker?\"",
        "Dean looked at Bobby. \"Pick him up. We'll Bernie him around,\" he gave a nervous chuckle. This day was becoming more absurd.",
        "Barbie twisted her head to the side. \"I don't get the reference. I thought I was going to carry him.\"",
        "Dean blinked and rubbed his eyes. \"Sorry. Old movie. I used to watch it when I was a kid. Didn't think it would happen to me,\" he sighed. \"Pick him up and take him to the car. I'll be along in a moment.\" He watched Barbie swing Bobby over her shoulder. She grunted and staggered. Bobby was getting stiff and was no longer bending. Rigor mortis had set in. Picking up Ming's phone, he turned it off to stop anybody else from tracking it down. \"I'm going to find you,\" he promised her, caressing the phone and putting it in his pocket.",
        "A loud crash came from the living room.",
        "\"What's going on here?\" Dean yelled, running into the room. Ivan was on the ground where his coffee table used to be. Barbie was holding Ivan's arm behind him and kneeling on his back. Pieces of wood and glass were spread out under him. Bobby had been tossed into the corner like used laundry.",
        "\"This monkey thought he could take the Maker with him. I had to show him why it was a bad idea,\" growled Barbie. Steam rose from her back.",
        "Ivan tried to force himself up, but she tightened her grip and forced him back down. \"You're not going anywhere.\" She turned to Dean, her voice turning harder. \"Get the Maker out of here. Now!\"",
        "Dean rushed to Bobby, picked up his body under the armpits and started dragging him to the door. He needed to be careful. His neighbour was probably still watching. She was always watching. At the door, he got under Bobby's arm and hoisted it up, over his shoulders.",
        "Barbie crashed through his new TV and bounced off the wall.",
        "\"You Cheese Head!\" she yelled, jumping onto Ivan, pummelling his head with a piece of the TV.",
        "\"Dammit!\" Dean yanked open the door and walked Bobby to his car at the curb. He got three steps when Barbie flew through the window and ricocheted off his car, pushing it into the street. She landed in front of it and started groaning.",
        "\"What the hell?\" Dean stumbled and dropped Bobby to the ground with a thud. He heard something break in the rocker. Scrambling to his feet, he turned around to see Ivan step out of the broken window. He slapped the razor-sharp glass from the frame to give him more space and pushed through. Coming forward, he brushed off the small pieces and loomed over the detective.",
        "Before Ivan had a resigned attitude toward everything, like his life was a lie, and he hated it all. Now, staring into his eyes, Dean was reminded of the second before a gun fired. You knew it was dangerous and someone was going to die if you took the wrong step. Ivan reached down for Bobby.",
        "Dean whipped out his gun and shoved it into Ivan's face. He heard the big man start to hum, now that he was close. There was something Bobby said about Ivan's humming. Bobby was scared of it.",
        "\"Sorry, big guy. I can't let you take him. I promised Ming I'd help him, and I'm not breaking that. Take a step back before you do anything.\"",
        "Ivan raised an eyebrow.",
        "\"Yes, I promised Gregory, too, but not to hand Bobby over to him. We have to get his soul back in his body, or he won't be of any use to anybody.\" He grimaced.",
        "Ivan shrugged, and his arm shot out like lightning. He grabbed Dean's gun; his humming grew louder. When he took his hand away, the barrel was bent and useless.",
        "\"What the hell?\" Dean stared at the barrel and tossed the gun to the side. \"How did you do that?\"",
        "Ivan picked Bobby up with one hand. A slight light appeared around Ivan's arms as well. His gun was useless; Ivan was too strong. Barbie moved in, just behind his car. She could take Ivan down if the big man didn't see her. Dean punched Ivan in the face, and the big man didn't even flinch. He just sighed, gave Dean a backhand and sent him flying into the flowerbeds.",
        "Spitting out dirt, he looked up. Ivan moved towards his car, dragging Bobby on the ground. A noise distracted him, and Ivan turned.",
        "Barbie jumped off the top of Dean's car, denting the roof and kicked Ivan square in the face, sending the Russian backwards and dropping Bobby. She picked Bobby up and swung his body over her shoulder.",
        "\"Get the car, fool!\" she shouted to Dean, her voice dripping blood.",
        "Shocking Dean out of his stupor, he picked himself up and yanked his keys out of his pocket. Dropping them, he kicked them forward and scooped them up.",
        "\"Don't play with them!\" Her voice dropped another two degrees lower. The blond stereotype was gone, replaced by whatever she was.",
        "\"Sorry.\" Dean unlocked the door and popped the other one open. Barbie chucked Bobby into the back seat and dove on top of him.",
        "\"Drive!\"",
        "Dean shifted the gear and slammed the pedal to the ground. He reversed and heard a thunk.",
        "\"What was that?\"",
        "Barbie leaned back and stared out the window. \"Good work. You hit the meathead. Now, faster!\"",
        "Dean shifted the gear into drive and took off down the street. Looking in the rearview mirror, he saw Ivan getting to his feet. He was pulling out a phone when Dean turned the corner, and the Russian was no longer visible.",
        "\"Is he coming?\" Dean asked.",
        "\"I don't know. The Maker said he was strong, but I wasn't expecting that much power.\" Barbie opened and closed her fist. Steam poured off her, heating up the car and fogging the windows. Dean rolled down the window to cool it off. \"My hand is hurting, and I can feel the nanobots breaking down. I had to forcefully excel over half to keep up with him. I only have about thirty percent remaining.\" She turned back to where they had left Ivan. \"If we meet him again, I don't think I can help.\"",
        "Dean stared ahead. It was getting closer to seven o'clock. They were running out of time. They needed to find where Ming was, and the Shujing was their last choice.",
        "7:00 PM",
        "Usually, the Shujing parking lot was full of buses and cars from travellers looking to start betting on the Strip. Now, despite the morning rush, half the spots were empty. The murder and broken window might keep a few away, but not everyone. Something else was up. Where were all the guards?",
        "\"Stay in the car.\" He handed Ming's phone to Barbie, turning it back on. \"If I find the computer or Ming, I'll call you, and you bring Bobby up. We can't hide a dead body here. There are too many cameras.\"",
        "\"The Maker thanks you for all your help,\" she said. She was back to her innocent self. Dean wasn't quite sure which one was the real Barbie.",
        "Dean nodded and gave her a small smile. Getting out of the car, he adjusted his coat and pulled out another candy. He wanted a smoke badly. The candy was starting to get expensive, and he was sure he was developing a cavity. His jaw hurt, and not from a punch. He'd had enough of those to know the difference.",
        "\"What are you waiting for?\" Barbie asked. \"Sam Spade to pat your shoulder? Sheesh. The Maker's dying here.\"",
        "\"Sorry.\" Dean stood up straight and fixed his coat. He checked his backup piece. With Ivan destroying his usual gun, he needed the smaller one.",
        "Inside the lobby, there were still a few people playing the slots. Even if there was an earthquake, the same few people would stick around for the final jackpot. He rang the bell at the front desk, but the rude guy from last time wasn't there. Going through the side entrance, Dean headed for the service elevator.",
        "\"Can I help you?\" a woman's voice said.",
        "Dean turned around and jerked back. Yichen's secretary, Wu, was standing at the door of the security office. She still had the tablet, tucked under her arm.",
        "\"I was looking for Yichen. I need to ask him some questions about a kidnapping. Mine,\" Dean said, coming up to her.",
        "\"I'm sorry, but the owner is busy at the moment. Please make an appointment and come back when it's more convenient.\" She pushed her small half-moon glasses up and stared at Dean over them.",
        "He took a step back and blinked. There was something different about the woman. Barbie mentioned a scent last time, but now it was overpowering. It wasn't perfume. It was more of a presence forcing itself on him, making it hard to think. His rational brain shut down, and his animal part took control. He held his hand under his nose and started coughing. \"Thank you very much, but this can't wait. I need to see him today.\" He pushed the up button and got in the elevator.",
        "She got in with him.",
        "Dean took a deep breath and didn't let it out. He couldn't stop staring at her dress and the curves. Her clothes hugged her body, accentuating everything. Before, she was always in the background or busy typing away at her tablet. Now, she dominated the small space like a power librarian. Now, his animal brain broke through his rational one and pounded it into hamburger.",
        "However, his gut wouldn't stop reaching up and choking his animal brain.",
        "There was a war inside his stomach, telling him to stay away. Dean popped a bottle of antacids and dumped a handful into his mouth. Crunching the hard tablets drove away the smell for a moment. He watched the elevator light move up the floors. The Shujing was only six floors, but he was being slowly roasted in a kinky, study hall hell.",
        "She stared at him over her glasses again, arms crossed, sending the sexy librarian image to the next level. Sweat dripped down Dean's collar. He closed his eyes and started listening to his gut. It had stopped talking and started kicking at him to get out of the elevator and take the stairs. Opening his eyes, he pushed the button for four and slipped through the opening doors. He dashed for the stairs and let out a gasp when he opened the door. Hanging over the railing, he sucked in the stale air of the stairwell.",
        "It tasted delicious.",
        "\"What the hell was that?\" When Barbie mentioned the secretary smelled good nothing said this would happen. Dean took out his phone and texted Barbie. He told her to bring in Bobby and use the stairs. There were too many coincidences to wait any longer. He looked up the stairs and climbed the next two floors. When he opened the door, the secretary was standing there. Her smell hit him like a hangover after a three-day bender.",
        "\"What are you doing to me?\" Dean asked, plugging his nose. He could still taste it on his tongue.",
        "\"The owner asked me to keep you away. He didn't want me to hurt you, so I figured if you lost yourself to lust, it would be easier, and I could store you away somewhere.\" She changed her stance and crouched down. \"I'm afraid I have no choice now but to do it the hard way.\"",
        "Her scent changed. It was no longer sensual. It smelt feral, metallic. Something told Dean to move. Her arm shot out, grazing his shoulder, cutting through his jacket and drawing blood. He rolled to the side, coming out behind her and held the wound. \"What the fuck?\"",
        "\"I can still make this easy. The owner doesn't want you dead. He likes you and approves of your relationship with Ming,\" she said, taking her glasses off and setting them on a table in front of one of the rooms.",
        "Dean backed up, bumping a table with his elbow. A vase, holding a yellow flower, tipped over. Dean grabbed it before it could fall. Yichen's room was at the end of the VIP hallway. He could run, but she'd be on him before he got three steps. Pulling out his backup piece with his right hand, he fired two shots into the floor to drive her back. He tossed the vase at her. She kicked it out of the air, shattering the ceramic and spilling water all over the floor. Wu made a disgusted face and paused. Dean ran before she could recover. He didn't like it, but he couldn't shoot her here. He was the one breaking in.",
        "Tripping on the carpet, he fell flat to the ground. The pressure of the wind passed where his head had just been. Twisting, he fired another wide shot at the secretary, forcing her to flow backwards. Dean got up and held the gun in front of him. She was standing in front of Yichen's door.",
        "\"You only have two shots left, detective and you won't hit me with them.\" She relaxed her stance and stood straight. Dean noticed her hair was unruffled and her suit still looked pressed. Her back foot dripped water.",
        "\"I'm going in there.\" He pointed to the door. \"You'll have to kill me to stop me.\"",
        "She shrugged and went back into her first stance.",
        "Dean was confident he could overpower her if he could get his arms around her. He spent an hour every day lifting weights and working on his body. He didn't want to kill her and put his gun back into his pocket.",
        "He lunged for her, trying to get her in a bear hug. She slapped her palm across his face and sent him crashing into the wall, shattering the glass that framed the painting hanging there. He slumped to the floor, wincing as the glass cut into his hand.",
        "\"How? Are you like Barbie?\" Dean asked, tugging the glass out of his hand. The blood stained the carpet.",
        "\"No, I'm not as strong as your blond friend, but anybody could block a simple attack like that,\" she said. \"If you want to get past me, please do better than a limp panda.\"",
        "He forced himself to stand and tossed pieces of glass and blood from his cut fingers at her. She flinched and dodged the drops, allowing Dean to land a kick to her gut. She let out a grunt and fell back, holding her stomach.",
        "\"You're not perfect,\" Dean said, smiling. \"I know your weakness. You telegraphed it when you hit the vase.\"",
        "\"What's that?\" she asked. Dean heard a hint of concern in her voice and noticed a twitch in her eye.",
        "\"You don't like dirt.\" He pointed to her jacket and the large boot print on it. She grunted, and Dean was rewarded with a small fire in her eyes. Her scent went a bit spicy. An angry fighter was stronger, but sloppy. He couldn't overpower her. If he could keep this up, though, maybe he could get by her.",
        "Dean crouched forward and rushed the secretary like a linebacker. Charging the smaller woman, he thrust his shoulder at her chest and tried to grab her with his bloody hands. She sidestepped him and punched him in the kidney. Grunting, Dean swung his bloody hand at her, forcing her to duck. Her hand shot up, catching his elbow and bending it in a way bones shouldn't.",
        "The crack filled the hallway, followed by a scream of pain. Dean cradled his left arm in his right and sank to his knees. Pain blinded him. Shock numbed his arm. She stood over him, jacket off and hands behind her back. He wasn't going to win this playing nice.",
        "\"Again, the owner didn't wish you hurt. He permitted me to stop you however I wished, short of death. If you continue to persist in moving forward, I'll have to take your legs as well.\"",
        "Dean rocked back and forth on the ground, tears flowing down his face. The shock had faded, but the pain rose to a dull roar as his brain worked to shut out the damage. First Ivan, now her. Was there anything he could do? Was he always going to be a slave to those with more power than him? He needed his rational brain back. He glanced at the door. There was a beam of white light appearing through the cracks. He remembered seeing that light at the police station. It was the same thing he'd seen when Ming and Bobby had disappeared*.*",
        "*Please let it be her.*",
        "He needed to get in there. Reaching into his pocket, he pulled out his backup piece. There was no time for decency. Ming needed him. Spinning around, he shot the secretary in the right foot. She fell, gasping and clutching it.",
        "Dean jumped up and smashed into the door with his good shoulder, thrusting it open. The white light was blinding. He brought his arm up to block it and moved into the room. \"Ming? Where are you?\"",
        "A foot smashed into his side and sent him flying into the wall. Slumping down, the same shoes as in the hallway stood over him. There was some blood on the side, but he'd missed the center of her foot. The white light was clearing up, and a woman was lying in the middle of the floor, stirring. As Dean blinked the spots from his eyes, he could make out Ming's features. She was alive and moving.",
        "\"Thank god!\" He closed his eyes and smiled."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 27,
      "title": "Chapter 27",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "February 18^th^, 1947",
        "The real Jessica grabbed Bobby's hand and started crying. She looked different than Ming. Less confident. Less cynical. Nothing big, just a softening around her eyes. If Bobby hadn't spent the last few days with the reporter, he'd never have noticed the difference.",
        "\"Mom. What happened to you?\" Jessica said, wiping her face.",
        "He patted her on the head, ignoring Bugsy and his men. She was an innocent in all this and didn't need this. He needed time to think. It wasn't time for them to fade yet. They still had another two or three days left here before they would disappear. \"How much do you remember of the last few days?\" he asked.",
        "Jessica stopped sobbing and blew her nose. \"I remember Steven coming over. He wanted to talk.\" She narrowed her eyes. \"After that, it's a blank. What happened?\"",
        "Bobby smiled and put his hand on her cheek. It wasn't the reporter. She'd never let him do this in front of others, and she'd never call him 'Mom'. \"He tried to kill us both,\" he lied. Bugsy didn't need to know the truth. \"I was able to take care of him and left him in the desert, but he hurt us, and we had to check into the hospital.\"",
        "Jessica drew back, her hand going to her mouth. \"No,\" she whispered.",
        "Bugsy whistled. \"I knew you was a tough dame.\" He took off his hat and mock bowed to Bobby. \"I can see why Slazney wanted me to keep an eye out for you.\" He reached over and grabbed Jessica's shoulders, drawing her back.",
        "\"Don't touch her!\" Bobby shouted.",
        "\"Take it easy,\" Bugsy said, moving Jessica to the background and giving her to his men. \"Nobody will do a thing to her as long as you answer my questions.\" He directed the man to take her out of the room.",
        "\"Mother?\" Jessica said, sniffing.",
        "\"Don't worry. I'll be fine. If he touches you, grab his nut sack and twist,\" Bobby said, not taking his eyes off Bugsy.",
        "\"I warned ya.\" Bugsy raised his hand.",
        "Bobby ignored the hand and glared at the mobster. \"Why did Slazney come to see you in the first place?\" Bobby asked, trying to stifle a giggle. Bugsy looked like a raccoon.",
        "Bugsy lowered his hand. \"He had a bunch of money he wanted to invest in the Flamingo. He gave some good advice about placement and design, but he wanted me to move it to a different spot and include a different kinda window. Too much pink.\" Bugsy shrugged and cringed. \"I refused. He threatened me and killed a few of my men before I was able to get rid of him.\"",
        "\"You killed him?\" Bobby asked.",
        "Bugsy spat into the corner. \"He told me I'd regret it, like some kinda pulp baddie.\" Bugsy shook his head. \"I figured he was a moron who had been hit in the head one too many times. I appreciated the advice, but he wore out his welcome. Then it got annoying and weird. I thought I had him rubbed out, but each time he kept coming back through a different proxy. Usually, as the oddest people. I could never figure out why so many people were wasting their lives for him.\" He turned to one of his men. \"Remember the priest?\"",
        "The tall man slapped his head. \"Yeah! That guy was freaky.\" He shivered. \"When he pulled his gun out of that bible in the church, I was expecting lightning to strike him.\"",
        "\"It's been quiet for the last few years, but I've never forgotten the bastard. Like some sorta bad fungus.\"",
        "Bobby narrowed his eyes. \"You knew Slazney was different people?\"",
        "\"Yeah. I eventually figured it was some sorta cult of killers. I could never figure out why each of them called themselves by the same name.\" He scratched his nose. \"Whatever they were, they caused me a lot of trouble.\"",
        "\"That's why I'm here,\" Bobby mumbled.",
        "\"Speak up, woman!\" Bugsy strode forward and grabbed Bobby's shoulders. \"You said he's your brother, before. Elaborate!\"",
        "\"Yes.\" Bobby nodded, wincing at the pain. \"I think so. I haven't seen him in years, and I thought he was dead.\" He lay back down in the bed. \"I'm not here to kill you, Mr. Siegel. I don't care what happens to you.\" Bobby smiled. \"If I see Slazney, I'd probably try and kick his ass myself.\" He shook his head. \"But I know why he was here. Maybe.\"",
        "Bugsy tapped his foot. \"Are you going to tell us?\"",
        "\"This is just a guess, but he probably wanted to set up something to impart a computer virus into people. Whatever he used to jump, he just couldn't figure out how to make it work properly,\" Bobby said, frowning. \"He'd probably then use the virus to control their decisions and take control of the gambling industry. Vegas will be a very rich place one day, with billions going through here annually. He wanted a part of that payday.\"",
        "*It couldn't be that simple, could it? But then Vlad never really thought things through.*",
        "\"Billions?\" Bugsy smiled. \"That's a number I could never get used to.\" He frowned. \"What the heck's a computer virus?\"",
        "Bobby turned to the gangster, ignoring the question. It would require more time than he cared to spend to explain the code.",
        "\"You stifled his plans. Set him back decades. He tried to force the situation here, but the conditions weren't right, and he's a piss-poor programmer. I must have been drawn in because of the anomaly.\"",
        "\"Programmer? What's with these strange words? Whatever.\" Bugsy lit another cigarette. \"They don't sound important. I was going to stick around here for a few more months, but I think I'll head to California. Virginia's been after me to spend some time in her new place.\" He waved to his men to leave the room.",
        "At the door, he paused and snapped his fingers. \"I almost forgot.\" He turned back to Bobby. \"We got some unfinished business, you and me.\" He smiled. \"I'm afraid you and your daughter have to go on a little ride.\"",
        "\"Dammit!\" Bobby groaned. \"If this is you, Vlad, I'm not going to stop at the pigs.\"",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "\"Mr. Siegel is sorry for the trouble, but you'll have to find your way home from here,\" the mobster said, getting into the car and driving away.",
        "The heat from the day pushed down on Bobby. Siegel's men drove Bobby and Jessica a hundred miles into the desert. Watching the city go by, Bobbie tried to think of ways to get out of the car, but there was nothing he could do without leaving Jessica alone. He couldn't abandon her.",
        "The afternoon sun was setting, and the coolness of the desert seeped into his bones. He sneezed as the sand settled into his nose. Catherine's body was thin and couldn't handle the cold as well as his male one could. He needed to get home. Bobby glanced at Jessica. She was shivering and rubbing her hands along her arms.",
        "\"Sorry about this girl. I didn't mean to get you mixed up in this,\" he said.",
        "\"What's going on, Mother?\" She'd spent the first part of the ride crying. Now her eyes were red and puffy.",
        "\"I beat the shit out of Bugsy Siegel the other day, and your father sold us out to him,\" Bobby said.",
        "Jessica was silent as her eyes went wide, trying to form words, only her brain probably wasn't working.",
        "\"In addition, Steven killed me. Sorry. I'm actually not your mother, I'm just using her body. My name is Bobby, and I'm from Russia.\" He stuck out his hand. \"Nice to meet you.\"",
        "Jessica's eyes rolled up into her head, and she collapsed to the ground, unconscious.",
        "\"I thought so,\" Bobby sighed. \"Ripping off the band-aid never works as well as they think it does.\" He shook his head. There was no way to make this hurt any less. \"Nothing better than a shared trauma to start a relationship,\" he mumbled. He just wished he believed it.",
        "***SCENE_BREAK***",
        "After moving Jessica out of the sunshine, Bobby found some small pieces of wood and a tumbleweed. The night was cold, but the fire burned in a small pit Bobby had dug off to the side of the road. Nobody travelled to these parts this late at night, so finding shelter was the most important thing. The first thing he learned when moving to Vegas was how to survive in the desert. He figured the skills would come in handy if Gregory ever tracked him down. Too bad he didn't have any plastic. It would make it easier to catch the condensation early in the morning. Bobby and Jessica sat around the fire, warming their hands. True night had fallen, leaving the world in darkness. The only pinpoints of light were the fire and the stars in the sky. It would have been beautiful if it weren't so sad.",
        "Jessica stared into the flickering light. After waking, she spent an hour crying and then another hour fighting Bobby. Only after shouting at her in Russian did she calm down.",
        "\"Let me get this straight,\" Jessica said. \"You were forced to remember a code that would cause untold destruction, and it sent you here to nineteen forty-seven, instead.\"",
        "Bobby nodded.",
        "\"You had developed it years ago, but erased it from your mind because it was too dangerous. However, the only way to get it back out of your head was to remove the blocks, finish writing it and use it.\"",
        "\"That's the basis of it. I didn't realize it was this flawed at the time. The guy who shoved it in my head was a terrible programmer. I thought it was buggy, but often you don't realize the extent until after you run it the first time and it doesn't work.\"",
        "\"What do you mean?\"",
        "\"Well, when you learn how to code a program, you start by breaking up each job into manageable parts. You don't really create a code as a whole from the beginning, so you ignore a lot of detail until you need it.\" Bobby moved closer to the fire. He was shivering. \"I just wanted it gone from my head. I didn't realize what it was doing.\"",
        "\"My mother?\" Jessica asked. The firelight reflected off her face. The flickering flame cast shadows and made her seem like an alien one moment and a scared child the next.",
        "\"She's dead.\" Bobby didn't sugarcoat it. \"Steven killed her, and then he strangled you. When Ming jumped into your body, there was still time for the nanobots to heal you and her concern for you tethered your soul to hers. When I jumped in, your mother's soul was gone, and I wasn't in any shape to bring it back.\"",
        "Jessica turned away from the fire. Her shoulders shook as she started crying again. He wanted to grab her and hold her. If this had happened to his child, he'd feel the same way.",
        "\"What is this code anyway?\" Jessica asked between sobs.",
        "\"Something very dangerous and difficult to control. I wish I'd never found it,\" Bobby said. \"It was fun for a while, but no one should have the power over time and space. All it does is warp people.\"",
        "\"Some people want it?\"",
        "He nodded. \"They spend their youth trying to learn magic and then spend the rest of their lives dealing with the problems it causes. My code makes a shortcut. I don't want that headache.\"",
        "Bobby fed some more sticks to the fire. It was too dark to walk back yet, but they'd have to move before the sun came up. The heat of the day would kill them before the lack of water would. When they drove them out here, Bobby counted the miles but stopped after a hundred. If they were that far from the nearest city, they would have to walk for days to get anywhere.",
        "\"You should have never forgotten the code,\" Jessica grumbled.",
        "\"Maybe, but that was my choice at the time, and I'd make the same one again.\"",
        "He watched her curl up by the fire. It would be easier to curl up together and share the warmth, but Bobby let her have her space. As much as her pain hurt him, he wasn't her mother, and there was no reason for him to act like it. He still remembered what it was like to be a kid. Hell, he still lived like one.",
        "\"I hope your disappearing doesn't mean what I think it means, Ming,\" he mumbled.",
        "*The fact that I'm still here is a little more worrying. Barbie would have brought me back with you.*",
        "He lay down in front of the fire and closed his eyes. At least now there were no visions of zombies and blown-up buildings when he opened them. A good night's sleep was the only positive thing about finishing the code."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 28,
      "title": "Chapter 28",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "The Present",
        "7:30 PM",
        "Ming opened her eyes and winced. \"Where am I?\" She groaned. The floor was hard and cold. It smelled like cleaner and dust. After the heat and leather scent of Jim's car seats, it was like wanting vanilla ice cream but getting wasabi. You weren't quite sure how to react. Pushing herself to a sitting position, she groaned and started rubbing her eyes. The light was dimmer, less natural. She was inside. How?",
        "\"Jim? Where are you?\" she asked, her voice sounding like a ten-pack-a-day smoker.",
        "*Why do I feel like every nerve ending is firing at the same time?*",
        "\"You're back! Thank God it worked,\" a male voice said",
        "She knew that voice. Inching her head to the sound, every movement sent waves of pain through her. Yichen sat at a desk. Relief softened his face from his usual hard mask. In front of him was Bobby's computer. She remembered it from the police station. There weren't many grown men with Motley Crue stickers on their laptops.",
        "\"Uncle? What are you doing here?\" She looked down. \"What the? I'm back in my body. How?\" She ran her hands all over herself. \"Why am I so tingly?\"",
        "\"You've been almost dead for almost nineteen hours. Rigour mortis had set in, so it's going to take some time for you to readjust to your body,\" Yichen said. \"If Bobby's notes are correct, the nanites should be repairing your tissue. That's probably the tingling.\"",
        "Ming heard a noise to her right. Dean groaned off to the side of the room. Wu was standing over him, her jacket open and finally dirty. She was always so clean. Wu adjusted it and stood at attention.",
        "\"Dean!\" Tears welled up, stinging her eyes. She hadn't seen him in forever. \"What happened to you?\"",
        "\"I had a little trouble,\" Dean groaned. His arm looked broken, but Ming couldn't be sure.",
        "She turned her head back to Yichen and toppled over, like someone was probing her body with a saw. \"What the hell is going on here, Uncle?\"",
        "\"Your detective friend has been searching for you.\" He shrugged. \"I didn't want him to interfere with the transfer.\" He stamped his cane on the ground. \"I asked him to wait, but he refused, causing more trouble than he was worth, so Wu had to get creative.\" He turned to Wu, frowning. \"You may have gone too far. I didn't want him hospitalized.\"",
        "Wu nodded. \"I will accept my punishment. He was more resourceful than I expected.\"",
        "Yichen raised an eyebrow but said nothing.",
        "Ming stared at Yichen. \"You're lying!\" she shouted. She tried to stand up, but her legs wouldn't move. Slapping them was no use either. They tingled and popped as they healed. The same thing happened when she jumped into Jessica's body, but this time it was much slower.",
        "\"Rest. Recover. He won't get past Wu. She's trained too long and hard to lose to a simple detective,\" Yichen said, smiling. He pulled up a chair and sat in front of her. \"Where were you? I couldn't find any evidence in the code to tell me.\"",
        "\"Nineteen forty-seven. I met Bugsy Siegel and he...\" Ming trailed off and stuck her hand to her mouth. \"Where's Bobby?\" She looked around and didn't see him.",
        "\"I didn't need him, so I left him at the detective's place.\" Yichen turned his head towards Dean. \"You brought him here, didn't you?\"",
        "\"Yes,\" Dean croaked out. \"Barbie's bringing him up now. We need his computer to revive him.\"",
        "\"I thought so.\" Yichen gestured to the machine. \"It's almost out of power. And the save function has been disabled, probably by Bobby.\" He smiled. \"Once that happens, the code will probably disappear. Or I could just destroy it now?\"",
        "\"No! Please don't, Uncle.\" Ming struggled to her feet. There was no way she was going to face her uncle on her knees. \"You knew what Bobby was capable of the whole time, didn't you?\"",
        "\"I suspected it after Slazney had me hire him. It took him far too long to find the code.\"",
        "\"You knew it was in the windows?\" Ming staggered to the side and bumped against the desk. Her legs still weren't moving correctly. It was as if she'd forgotten how to walk and had to relearn.",
        "He scoffed. \"Of course. The first week I was the owner, I took Slazney's suggestion and looked at some of the windows in the right sunlight, much like you did. Although I stayed in the room.\" His face drew back in disgust. \"Too many of the windows have that cursed code embedded in them. Anyway, after I woke up, most of the code was gone, thank god. The bits and pieces I remembered were enough to know that Slazney was dangerous. I didn't know what he wanted, but there was no way I would let him tell me what I could and couldn't do. I had enough of that in the Triad.\"",
        "\"Why was that?\" Dean asked Yichen. He had pushed himself to a sitting position. \"What happened? I found your name in Stanley's files. I already know who Slazney was using. What's his connection to all of this?\"",
        "Ming watched Yichen when Dean was talking. Yichen's face went from anger to concern and back to indifference in a heartbeat. There was something Dean wasn't saying.",
        "\"Wait?\" She turned to Dean. \"You found Slazney? He was also in nineteen forty-seven, but had left before we got there. Where is he?\"",
        "Dean stopped talking.",
        "\"Where is he, Detective?\" Yichen said. \"Wu has been very generous, but she will start breaking your fingers if you don't tell me what happened.\" The tension in his voice was rising.",
        "Dean winced and glanced at the secretary. \"No need.\" He took a deep breath. \"After I confronted Slazney, he decided the body he was inhabiting was no longer necessary. He activated a smoke device and jumped out. The body turned to dust, but I don't know where he is.\"",
        "Yichen started swearing in Cantonese and reached for the phone. Ming recognized some of the words but usually spoke in a different dialect. Her father's name stood out.",
        "\"What about my father?\" she said, moving closer to Yichen.",
        "Her uncle stopped talking, put the phone down and looked at Wu. Worry filled his face. He was scared.",
        "\"It's time, sir,\" said Wu, standing away from Dean and picking up a tablet on the table. \"After everything that happened, she may finally believe it. She needs to hear the truth.\"",
        "Yichen nodded, stood up and started pacing. \"When you were a child, do you remember your father being in a car accident?\"",
        "\"Yes. He spent several days in the hospital,\" Ming said.",
        "\"He was killed in that accident.\"",
        "Ming scoffed. \"My father wasn't killed when I was seven. He changed, sure. Before, he loved playing with me. Afterwards, he grew distant and cold. Something happened in that accident, and it scared him, but he is still my father.\" Tears started as doubt crept in. \"How dare you say that?\" She couldn't believe the man who took her to amusement parks and told her bedtime stories every night had died. She clenched her fists and glared at her uncle.",
        "Yichen looked at Ming. His eyes glistened with tears. \"When I bought the Shujing, I was planning to rip out all the pink windows. It was useless in a respectable hotel, and I wanted a better image,\" Yichen said, sitting. He was holding a picture in his lap. \"I was tired of the Triad following everything I was doing and had already taken steps to distance myself from them.\"",
        "Ming sank to the ground. This was everything she'd wanted, but hearing it was a shock. She patted her pants for a pen and paper, even her phone, but she had nothing on her.",
        "\"I had hired the contractors and the renovations were set to begin in a few days when I got a call from the hospital.\" He looked up. \"My daughter and her husband were in a car accident, and he had been thrown through the windshield. I raced down there, but it was too late. He died in surgery.\"",
        "\"I know all that. I remember you there. What's it got to do with my father?\" Ming yelled. She struggled to her feet, grabbed Yichen by the collar, and hauled him up. Adrenaline gave her the strength to push past the pins and needles running through her body. Her eyes went wide. \"What do you mean by daughter?\"",
        "\"I didn't want your mother tainted by my dealings with the Triad, so my sister raised her and said she was her daughter. I never let her know.\" Yichen smiled. \"I'm your grandfather.\"",
        "Ming dropped him back into the chair and staggered away. She grabbed onto the column in the center of the room to keep from falling.",
        "\"Imagine my surprise when your father started breathing again. We were overjoyed. Your mother was still unconscious, but she would recover. Your father was moved to recovery. That's where I met him.\" Yichen growled. His voice was harder than Ming remembered.",
        "\"Him?\" Ming said. Tears flowed.",
        "\"Slazney. He has a type and jumps to multiple bodies. Accidents are recorded in papers. When a person miraculously survives, nobody thinks twice. The first thing your father said to me when I saw him was to stop the renovations at once, or your daughter will become a widow and lose her child on the same day.\"",
        "Ming stared at the old man. \"No,\" she whispered.",
        "Yichen gave her a sad smile. \"A part of you knew your father was different after the accident.\"",
        "\"He stopped reading to me and took longer business trips, but ...,\" she trailed off. \"It can't be.\" After her trip to the past and experience with Jessica, she knew what a person using magic could do. \"A person can only stay a week or so in a body!\" she shouted, fists clenched, straining forward, tears staining her face.",
        "\"That's Bobby's magic. He created his through computer code and built in his limitations, they all do.\" He pointed to Wu. \"She can't do magic, but she trained her body to the pinnacle of perfection. She had to shut down her emotions to do so. In addition, dirt disgusts her. It's not magic, but even a basic manipulation of nature comes at a cost. I don't know what Slazney's is. He seems to be working without a net.\"",
        "Wu stepped forward and swiped at her tablet. \"Please hurry, sir. The other woman is coming, and you sent the security away so they wouldn't be a part of this.\"",
        "Yichen nodded.",
        "Dean groaned in the corner and stood up. \"I'm sorry, Ming. It's true. Your father was Slazney. He told me so himself. Your mother is in the hospital now, recovering from the shock. She was there when he dissolved.\"",
        "Ming collapsed in front of the column. \"No.\" All this time she spent searching for the man, and he was in her house.",
        "\"I tried to fight him, but every time I thought I was winning, he pulled out the threat on your life,\" Yichen said, pounding the arm of the chair. \"When he asked me to hire Bobby, I was curious why he wanted the man, but I did it.\" He stared at Ming. \"When you started investigating Slazney, I was worried you would find something. I know how good you are, but I didn't expect you to get this far--,\"",
        "The doors to the penthouse burst open, and Barbie stepped through. She was carrying Bobby over her shoulder and dropped him onto the floor with a thud. \"Oops. Sorry, Maker.\" She turned to Dean. \"What took you so long, detective? I was growing old just waiting for you.\"",
        "\"Barbie!\" Ming shouted.",
        "\"Reporter? You're back. That's great.\" Barbie turned to Yichen and scowled. \"You're the scab that stole the Maker's computer. Give it back.\"",
        "\"It's over there on the desk.\" Yichen pointed to the laptop. \"But it's almost out of power.\"",
        "\"No problem.\" Barbie pulled a cord from Bobby's pants. \"I got the power cord with me.\" She skipped over to Bobby's computer with a smile and plugged it in. \"Where's your outlet?\"",
        "\"Look out!\" Ming shouted.",
        "Wu had silently moved up behind Barbie and kicked her in the side. Barbie went flying across the floor and landed beside Dean. Flipping to her feet, Barbie's arm was dangling loose. She was cradling it and crying. \"What the sugar did you do that for, you meanie?\"",
        "\"*Meanie?\"* Dean and Ming said, echoing each other. Wu stood in front of the computer, ready to defend it.",
        "\"My mother doesn't like me swearing,\" Barbie said, popping the shoulder back in place.",
        "\"Bobby is too dangerous to bring back,\" Yichen said. \"I don't know why Slazney wants him, but after looking at the code, it can't be good.\"",
        "\"That's not for you to decide!\" Barbie stomped back to the computer. Wu threw a punch, but Barbie blocked it and pushed her back. \"You still smell good. Are you using a lust scent?\" she asked the other woman.",
        "\"Yes. I don't like it much.\" Wu paused. \"What do you think?\"",
        "\"I like it. When I finish with the computer, we can explore it further. Now, please move,\" Barbie said. She squared her body and plowed into Wu. The smaller woman spun around Barbie's back, grabbed her hair and yanked it back, halting her momentum.",
        "\"Ouch!\" Barbie swung her good arm behind her, catching Wu in the side. Grunting, she let go of Barbie's hair and staggered back, clutching the injured area.",
        "Crawling around the fight, Ming moved closer to Dean. When she took over Jessica's body, the healing went quickly. This was taking too long.",
        "Yichen had already moved into the corner and covered his mouth with a cloth. Pieces of furniture and dust filled the room as the two women destroyed the penthouse.",
        "\"Are you okay?\" Ming asked Dean, checking out his face. She'd missed him. He was covered in bruises, and his arm was broken, but he was still the same. He smelt the same.",
        "\"Nothing a good shower won't cure.\" He paused, and guilt flashed across his face. \"I'm sorry about your father. If--\"",
        "\"No. This isn't the time.\" Ming dismissed him with a wave. The pain there was too raw. \"I'll worry about grieving later. If I start now, I won't get up.\"",
        "She couldn't think about her father. She'd been trying to gain his approval for years. To win him back. Deep in her mind, she'd hoped that if she found out more about his accident and the connection to Slazney, it would explain what had happened to him. To find out he was Slazney was too much. She couldn't collapse here.",
        "Ignoring Dean's concerns, she plowed ahead. \"We need to get that computer to bring Bobby back. She's stuck back in nineteen forty-seven, and Bugsy Siegel was getting too close to her. He's going to kill her.\"",
        "\"She? What do you mean? I can't follow.\" Dean narrowed his eyes.",
        "Ming winced. She still thought of Bobby as a woman. \"Not now, later. I promise.\"",
        "\"Okay. What can we do?\" asked Dean.",
        "\"I still can't walk.\" She pointed to the corner where Barbie dropped the power cord. \"Can you get it?\"",
        "\"I think--\"",
        "They watched Barbie crash into Yichen's desk and send the computer flying.",
        "\"No!\" They both shouted at the same time as they watched it fall to the ground--",
        "-- and bounce to a stop near them. The main screen came up showing a five percent symbol.",
        "\"What the hell?\" Dean said.",
        "\"Grab it, Detective. The Maker put a protective spell around it, but it's draining the battery,\" Barbie shouted. She had Wu in a headlock and was pounding her with her palm.",
        "Wu punched Barbie in the kidneys and wriggled out of the headlock. She dove for the computer, but Barbie grabbed her by the back of her jacket and hauled her to the ground, sliding her back to the remains of the desk.",
        "\"Go!\" Ming pointed. \"I'll get the charge cord.\"",
        "Dean stumbled to his feet, cradling his left arm and picked up the computer. He ran, hunched over and hid under the piano near Bobby's corpse. Ming tossed him the socket end and plugged it in. The countdown timer disappeared as power surged through the machine.",
        "\"Pull up the code!\" she shouted.",
        "Dean enlarged the minimized screen, scrolled down to the bottom and stared at it. \"What the fuck do I do now?\"",
        "Ming crawled over and erased her name on the final line. She retyped Bobby's and hit return.",
        "Nothing happened.",
        "\"You stupid, fucking piece of shit!\" Ming went back to the final line, erased the space and tried Petor. \"Why isn't it working?\"",
        "\"It probably means he's dead and can't come back,\" Yichen shouted from the corner. \"It's over.\"",
        "The computer turned black and fizzled out with a spurt."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 29,
      "title": "Chapter 29",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "February 19^th^ 1947",
        "\"You're lucky I placed a tracking spell on the girl,\" Jim said as the sun began to rise, driving away the freezing desert. \"Well, I put it on the other girl, but I guess she got a part of it too.\" He gave Jessica a quick look. She smiled and looked away.",
        "Bobby stared at the two from the back seat, holding his nose. \"When was the last time you cleaned up back here?\" he asked Jim. \"There's food sticking to the seats.\"",
        "\"I could've left you back in the scorching sand, or you could reach through to the trunk and shut up,\" Jim shot back.",
        "Grumbling, Bobby opened the seat and stuck his hand into the trunk. His eyes went wide as he pulled out a guitar. \"Is this Kansas'?\"",
        "\"Yep. He said you could use it to make the music you need to get yourself back. I can't help you with that one.\" Jim coughed. \"My skills are about drawing out what's in nature and enhancing it, and I'm nowhere near as powerful. For me, the natural rhythm of the music is more about enhancing than creating. I can't do what you do, travelling through time. According to Millie, though, you got the math right, so you're halfway there.\" Jim was silent as he swerved around a dead coyote in the road. \"Who taught you anyway?\"",
        "\"Self-taught. Just lucked into it.\"",
        "Jim scoffed. \"Hedge witches. God, I hate them. Full of talent, but always one mistake away from blowing their own blasted head off.\"",
        "\"Why do you think I made myself forget it? If I hadn't been forced to remember, I'd still be living in bliss.\" Bobby tuned the guitar, hefting it up and down. It felt right and had the energy from a real musician infused into it. He ran his fingers over the strings, bringing out a slight noise. Placing it in his lap, he started playing a riff from Crue.",
        "The car swerved and almost went off the road. \"What the hell was that squawking? Did you break Kansas's guitar?\" Jim shouted.",
        "Jessica took her hands off her ears and rolled down the window to let in some fresh air. The heat remained and grew stronger.",
        "Jim turned around and shouted at Bobby. \"You're supposed to caress the natural vibrations. Not murder them.\"",
        "\"Eye's front, boy,\" Bobby said. \"It's a Motley Crue song, Save Our Souls. The lyrics and theme are perfect for what I need. The music has to match the situation and connect you to nature. I can see your point, though. Even if it was their worst song, I liked it.\" He tuned the guitar a little more, wincing as his shoulder pulled at him. They had left the bullet in and just taped everything up. A forced walk through the desert hadn't helped. He wished the nanites hadn't cut out after twenty-four hours.",
        "Jim continued to drive. \"It's getting too hot here, and the sun's getting too high. I passed a rest stop on my way here, so we'll break there. This hunk'a crap won't last the heat.\"",
        "Bobby nodded and stared out the window, watching the heat radiate off the desert floor. The wind rolling through the windows provided some relief, but not enough. Fever racked Catherine's body. His body. He didn't want to die here.",
        "Jim drove in silence for a few miles. The sun beat down on the car, making the leather seats painful to touch. \"Can you play it again? Without the screeching parts?\" he asked.",
        "Bobby lifted his head. \"Save Our Souls? Sure.\" He started on the opening rift. \"It's slower than a lot of their stuff and works better if there's percussion,\" he said. He got to the chorus and started rocking his head back and forth, especially when he repeated the same lines over and over. There was something about the words that just infused him. The poetry filled him with promise.",
        "\"Stop there,\" Jim said.",
        "Bobby put the guitar down. \"What? Did you catch something?\"",
        "Jim was silent as he navigated the road. Jessica stole glances at the young black teen. She was fingering the package Ming had left for her. She hadn't opened it yet, but Bobby could tell it was thick. Ming had been thorough. She'd spent the whole night writing the thing, discarding draft after draft.",
        "\"Have you tried slowing down the beat and adding the rhythm from Weed Smoker's Dream?\" Jim said. \"If you can combine the two, it might create something that could harmonize with the world. You need the correct beat to open the path, right? After that, the math can guide you to where you need to go.\"",
        "Bobby's eyes shot open, and he smiled. \"You might be right. I'm just opening a path back to my body. That's the easy part, and reality will help me out there. The hard part was already done coming here.\" He turned back to the guitar and practiced his fingering. There was no way the two songs could be combined easily. They shared a similar tempo, but the theme and topic were completely different. However, Jim was on to something. Bobby sighed. There was something else he needed to take care of.",
        "\"I have about a day left here before I die. Jessica, what are you going to do after I'm gone?\"",
        "\"Bobby! Why would you say that?\" Jessica turned in her seat and glared at Bobby. \"You're going to be fine.\"",
        "\"No, I'm not.\" Bobby pulled down the shirt to show her the bandage. Black lines were radiating out from underneath. \"They left the bullet in there, and the rot has already set in. I'll be dead before the end of this day, tomorrow at the latest.\"",
        "Jessica started crying and turned around to huddle in the seat.",
        "\"Why'd you have to lay bad news on her like that? Don't you have a heart, mother-fucker,\" he yelled, pounding the wheel. He glanced away from the road and laid a hand on Jessica's back, rubbing it in small circles.",
        "Bobby shrugged. \"I'm a realist. It's important to lay all the cards on the table and then make your decision.\" He noticed Jim becoming a bit more protective of Jessica. If he put a tracking spell on Ming, it probably bonded the two of them together. Jessica as well. He gave a sad smile. *At least someone will look after you, Jessica.*",
        "He fingered the guitar again and added the sound from Weed Smoker's Dream, but said the lyrics from Save Our Souls. The mismatch was odd, but had potential. If he had several days to work on it, maybe he could find a way to get himself back. It would have been so much easier with his computer. The programs there could do all the hard work. Whoever had it must have just wanted Ming.",
        "\"Probably the Detective,\" Bobby grumbled.",
        "They drove through the desert until eleven. The afternoon sun was getting too hot, and Jim pulled off the side into a shaded area. He got out and gave Jessica some water. Bobby watched them walk off into the desert, hand in hand. Jim said there was a small oasis around the back. \"You had to step just right to get in, but the place was beautiful.\"",
        "Bobby may be a hedge witch, but when two people were into each other, the signs were clear. They would have enough trouble without him getting in the way.",
        "He fingered the bandage and winced again. The pain was getting worse. That quack in the hospital had killed him this time. He snorted. Dying almost fifty years before he was born. Vlad was always overstepping himself. He needed to learn his limits and not mess with things he had no right to.",
        "\"I wish I knew what you wanted, ya dirty Metallica shill,\" he grumbled.",
        "Bobby ignored the guilty pang in his stomach and played the guitar. It was just as much his fault that he was here as his brother's. He's the one who used the code in the first place. When he showed it to Vlad, he had no idea what his brother would do with it. That the twat would copy it, ending up with Bobby stuck here, swelting in fifty-degree heat. He never got the whole Fahrenheit thing.",
        "He shook his head, getting rid of the distractions. He was getting somewhere with combining the two songs, but it wasn't quite there yet; the heat was too oppressive.",
        "\"Why don't you just give it up, Petor?\"",
        "Bobby spun around at the voice and saw Vlad walking through the desert. Heat waves rising from the floor distorted his features, making him appear like a ghost, but it was him. He looked the same as the last time he'd seen him.",
        "\"Why are you still wearing that fucking ugly shirt? Tie-dye went out years ago.\"",
        "Vlad plucked the front of his shirt and shrugged. \"This is your hallucination. You tell me. Besides, it's a classic. They never go out of style.\"",
        "\"I've missed you, Vlad, even if you fucked up the code you tried to shove into my brain. There are much easier ways to hack a human body than using pink windows. The code is a thing of beauty, not something you shoehorn in,\" Bobby chuckled.",
        "\"I've missed you, too, you butt-ugly troll.\"",
        "\"Haw! I'm in the body of a beautiful woman now. You can't call me ugly.\" Bobby smiled. Nobody insulted him as well as his brother.",
        "\"Are you still wasting your potential?\" Vlad said, staring down at Bobby.",
        "The heat of the desert flowed through him and blasted Bobby. He wiped the sweat off his forehead and plucked a few strings.",
        "\"What do you mean?\"",
        "\"You could have had anything with that code. Freed us from Gregory and saved Ivan. Why'd you throw it away?\"",
        "Bobby was quiet. The music filled the small shaded area where he sat. \"I was lucky to find the code and CD in that computer,\" he started. \"It was great to get everything I wanted at first, but after that final assignment in Korea and what happened to Sasha, I wanted nothing to do with it. The consequences of messing around with it were too high. The code was too seductive to use.\" Bobby looked up at his brother. \"Power like that should be earned, not found. I had no right to it, and I wasn't worthy of it. Hell, I was scared of it.\"",
        "\"You could have learned to control it,\" Vlad said. \"Harnessed it for good instead of throwing it away.\"",
        "\"Yes, I could have. But I wasn't ready. I may be one day.\" He thought of the name Barbie called him. If she was telling the truth and if she was who he thought she was, then one day, maybe he would be. Until then, it was best to keep the code under lock and key.",
        "Vlad shook his head. \"How are you going to get home, you piece of rechewed fish shit?\"",
        "\"It's been a while since I've heard that one.\" Bobby sighed. \"I don't know, but it's time for you to go now, Slazney.\"",
        "Vlad paled and stepped forward. Bobby played a riff on the guitar, sending the shade blowing away into the wind. It was too early for hallucinations even with the heat, and Vlad always did tend to overplay his hand. He never really understood how to use the code. The computer was there to act as the catalyst and correct any of the problems that crop up. It was also the failsafe, preventing a meltdown. You have to work with the natural world, not force your will on it. The modern world wants results too quickly.",
        "Probably why he had to use the windows. *You always used a hammer to open a package when a small knife would do the trick, Vlad.*",
        "Sending a vision through time was child's play. However, with all he was doing, the casualty payback was going to be a bitch. It probably explained the Mad Max-like world back when the code first invaded his mind.",
        "Bobby turned his head to where Jessica and Jim had disappeared and heard some sounds coming from behind the rocks. She was going to be trouble, but Jim seemed like he could handle it. They were about the same age, and he knew how to respect nature. Hopefully, they would be all right.",
        "The sky was blue and clear. Bobby took one last look around and stood up. He set the guitar down and picked up a stick. Starting at the top corner of the sand nearest the shade, he scratched the math into the dirt. Two hours later, Jessica and Jim were silent, but the stark beauty of the code stared back at him. Sweat poured down his body. He'd taken his shirt off, and the sun had turned his skin a beet-red. He was finished. The path was clear to his eyes. With it, he could do anything.",
        "\"I have to try.\" Bobby stood up and stretched. The wound had stopped hurting.",
        "He was ready to die, but first, he had to play. Dropping the stick and picking up the guitar, he started belting out a riff, mixing the two songs. The music filled his soul. As it lifted and pushed away his doubts, he could feel the effects of the code swirl up from the desert sand and settle around him. He winced. His skin tingled as the math converted itself into the power he needed and dug itself deep into his bones. \"Nature is so hard to read.\" He shook his head. \"One minute it beats you down, the next it embraces you.\"",
        "He couldn't use a computer's battery for this and needed life energy to complete the code. This body was almost gone, but the blood would still give it that extra oomph he needed to break the barrier and send him home.",
        "\"Mother?\"",
        "Bobby looked up from the music. Jessica was peeking over the ridge where she and Jim had disappeared. He averted his eyes.",
        "\"I'm sorry, Jessica, but you can't call me that anymore. I'm sorry for the pain I'm going to cause you, but I have to leave early. I know your mother loved you. I can feel it in my own soul. It's probably what drew us to you and her in the first place.\"",
        "Jessica nodded and turned away. Jim put his arms around her and held her close. Her shoulders shook as sobs filled the spaces the music missed.",
        "\"God damn you, Vlad,\" Bobby said. \"I'm going to make sure you pay for this.\" He played to the end of the piece and used his foot to fill in the last line of the code. With the final beat of the song filling the air, he stomped his foot down, and a bolt of lightning crashed through the sky, shaking the desert sand, sending up a cloud into the air. Blackness engulfed him and took him away."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 30,
      "title": "Chapter 30",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "Present",
        "8:30 PM",
        "Bobby breathed, coughed, and twisted to his side. \"Fucking hell. Were you using me as a doorstop?\" Every nerve-ending fired as he flexed his fingers and toes to work the blood back into them. \"My body wasn't this beat up the last time I travelled through time.\" He'd finally found the right pattern to power the spell. Like Kansas had said, all it needed was the proper beat to get him back.",
        "He was going to miss nineteen forty-seven and Jessica. That time had grown on him. Hopefully, she'd be okay.",
        "\"Maker! You're back,\" Barbie squealed. \"Sorry, I had to throw you around.\"",
        "He turned to the voice and saw a blond-pink blob wrestling with a shorter black blob, maybe a woman.",
        "\"Who the fuck is that?\" he said, squinting at the brightness. Each movement sent waves of agony shooting through his body. Wincing, he focused his eyes and whistled as the scene came into focus.",
        "\"Dammit, girl, you're powerful.\" He recognized her now. She was Yichen's secretary. \"How are you stopping her, Barbie?\"",
        "\"I don't know.\" Barbie elbowed the secretary in the ribs. Steam rising from her shoulders. \"She's a slippery one,\" she said, panting, \"and I'm losing my strength. Even at half excel, I can't keep up.\"",
        "The secretary staggered back, clutching her chest. Barbie followed it with a roundhouse kick to the side, sending her bouncing off a pillar. Barbie grabbed a piece of a broken chair and pounced on the woman.",
        "\"These pillars are the only thing---.\" She swung the chair leg at Wu's head, but was cut off as the other woman wrestled Barbie to the ground.",
        "Ming was crawling to his left. \"Bobby! I thought you were stuck in forty-seven.\" He heard the relief in Ming's voice. The Detective stood to his right, cradling one arm and mashing the computer keys.",
        "\"Put my computer down, Detective. You don't want to break it.\" Bobby turned to Ming. \"Where are we? And who broke all my bones?\" Bobby groaned as he sat up. His bones started knitting together, like tiny pinpricks administered by a jackhammer. Steam rising from his body. \"It looks familiar, but no way is it your place.\" The piano and collection of guitars were beyond anything a policeman could afford.",
        "\"We're at the Shujing,\" Ming said. \"This is my Uncle's penthouse. What happened? Is Jessica okay?\"",
        "Bobby nodded, ducking his head as another piece of chair flew past him. \"She and Jim were starting something when I left. I don't know if it'll last, but she seemed to like him. He gave her your package.\"",
        "Ming smiled and lowered her head. Bobby could have sworn she was crying. He turned away. It wasn't polite to watch when people were vulnerable.",
        "He ducked his head as another piece of furniture came flying at him. He couldn't see Barbie anymore. The fight must have moved into the kitchen based on the jingle of dishes breaking.",
        "\"Why'd you have to come back, Washer?\" said Yichen.",
        "\"Lee Chang? That you?\" Bobby squinted. Everything was still blurry. He scratched his head, wincing. After the cold pain of Catherine's wound, feeling the fire of his bones knitting together was unpleasant. \"What are you doing here? Did you help Ming get back?\"",
        "Yichen rushed forward. The sheath of his cane dropped to the floor with a clack.",
        "\"What are you doing?\" Bobby yelled, twisting to the right, flopping against a piano leg and stopping. The blade slashed the floor, missing his head. Yichen brought it around, slicing Bobby across his back.",
        "\"Dammit! What are you doing? That hurt!\" He grabbed his back, and his fingers came back sticky. \"I'm still healing from whatever fucked up games you were playing with my body, and that just gives the nanites more work to do. I can't get any more. You're going to burn them out before they finish.\"",
        "The detective lumbered towards the old man, his arm hanging at an odd angle. Yichen must have been on some powerful drugs, the way he ducked under the Detective's grip and used the handle of his cane to send the Detective stumbling back into one of the pillars in the room, knocking pictures of a family to the floor.",
        "\"Dean!\" Ming shouted. \"Uncle, what are you doing?\"",
        "\"Slazney wants you, Bobby, more than anything else. I can't let him have you. I was happy to see you dead and your computer out of power. If I could have, I would have destroyed it myself. I wish you hadn't come back.\" He was gasping for breath, clutching his chest. His face was grimacing in pain.",
        "\"My heart,\" he groaned.",
        "Bobby could still feel the bones in his legs knitting together. He was able to bend his knees, but there was no way he could stand now. Yichen was coming too close.",
        "\"I don't want anything to do with Slazney. He screwed me over as well, and he's trying to change too much. He failed in forty-seven, but I'm ready for him.\" Bobby grimaced. He wasn't healing fast enough.",
        "\"That doesn't matter. He controlled you once, he'll do it again.\" Yichen stepped forward.",
        "\"Maker!\" Barbie rushed the old man and tackled him. His cane went flying and clattered on the ground. \"Stay down!\" She stood over him, panting. Bobby couldn't see the secretary.",
        "He was groaning on the ground and clutching his chest. He raised his head and said, \"Wu. It's up to you.\" His arm fell, and he stopped moving. He was breathing, but it looked shallow.",
        "\"Uncle!\" Ming yelled, crawling to him. She was still healing, too. \"Get away from him!\" she shouted at Barbie.",
        "Her face was angrier than when his mother caught him and Vlad stealing cookies from the neighbour. Ming cradled Yichen's head, rocking it. After the concern she showed for Jessica, Bobby wasn't surprised. She cared about people more than a story, no matter what she said.",
        "\"Sorry! I didn't mean to hurt him, even if he touched my tushy.\" Barbie panted. She was running out of breath. \"Maker! Look out!\"",
        "Bobby rolled to the side, missing the foot that would have gone through his back. He stopped moving when he hit the pillar closest to the remains of a desk. Wu's foot shattered through the floor, and she toppled over.",
        "\"How did you see me coming?\" she asked Bobby. She was getting back to her feet and stalking over to him.",
        "\"I didn't,\" Bobby grunted. \"Anybody could smell you coming. When was the last time you took a bath?\"",
        "Wu's face turned hard.",
        "Barbie rushed in front of her and stood over Bobby. \"If you want the Maker, you'll have to go through me, you meanie.\"",
        "\"You have strength but no skill. You haven't been able to stop me yet, girl.\" Wu circled to the left of Barbie, and her palm shot out, catching Barbie in the nose. Barbie staggered back, kicking Bobby, and landed in a flower pot by the desk, toppling it over.",
        "\"Ow!\" Bobby winced.",
        "\"Sorry, Maker.\" Barbie shot forward and grabbed Wu in a bear hug, pushing her back against the wall.",
        "\"Give me my computer!\" Bobby shouted to Dean. \"Slide it over here, then go help out Barbie!\"",
        "\"It's out of power!\" Dean yanked the cord from the wall and wrapped it around the laptop. He slid it across the floor toward Bobby and glanced at where Barbie and Wu were fighting. Clutching his broken arm with his right one, he ran across the room.",
        "\"No problem.\" Bobby stopped the computer with his foot and gritted his teeth as a tsunami of pain travelled up his body. \"There's a trick you have to follow.\" He stuck the charger in the slot in the back and connected it to the outlet under where Yichen's desk used to be.",
        "Flipping the computer, he ripped off the battery cover and flicked a switch. The machine powered up. Without the limiter, the machine would charge up twice as fast. It would also burn out twice as quickly. He didn't care. He needed this finished.",
        "Dean tried to tackle Wu and give Barbie a hand. Wu grabbed the Detective by his broken arm and spun him into another pillar, clipping Barbie in the process. He went down with a grunt of pain. Barbie staggered, and Wu grabbed her by her shirt. She smacked Barbie back and forth across the face, dropping her to her knees. Holding her head, Wu brought her knee to Barbie's chin, smashing it back and forcing her to the ground. Barbie stopped moving.",
        "She was breathing, but the spark was gone from her eyes.",
        "\"It's over, Window Washer.\" Wu limped past Ming and stood over Bobby.",
        "Her foot was dripping blood, and there was a hole in it. The front doors opened, and a massive shadow made its way into the room.",
        "\"Baba -- Yaga,\" Bobby whispered, his eyes going wide.",
        "Dean struggled to stand, but couldn't get his legs under him.",
        "\"Wu, leave him alone!\" Ming yelled. She was massaging Yichen's chest, trying to keep his heart from stopping.",
        "\"Fucking hell!\" said Bobby, backing up. \"I didn't make it out of the desert to die here. I still got a Crue concert I want to see.\"",
        "The pillar behind Bobby shattered into dust, and two large, meaty hands wrapped themselves around Wu's head and pulled it forward. She bounced off the broken wood and slumped to the side. A piece of the pillar jutted from her left eye, and blood gushed down her face. The other one was open but stared at nothing. Her chest was moving. He didn't know whether to be relieved or not.",
        "Turning around, shocked, Ivan stepped around the pillar and looked down at him.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Dean Lifante",
        "8:40 PM",
        "Dean watched the big Russian dust the rubble from his suit from where he huddled on the ground, cradling his arm. Where the hell had he come from? There's no way he could know where to find them. He tried to get up, but the secretary had hurt him badly. His arm was broken, and he could barely feel his legs. They felt like someone had torn them off, dripped them in molasses and shoved them back on, upside down. That last toss had been the worst. His arm snapped in a different place. It was getting difficult to breathe. Shock was setting in.",
        "\"Ivan!\" Bobby crab walked backwards away from the big man. He bumped into the wall in the back and couldn't go any further. \"What the fuck are you doing here?\" he giggled. Bobby was scared. Dean couldn't remember him not shouting a curse word.",
        "Ivan ignored the damage in the room and strode towards Bobby. He reached down and picked him up by his shirt.",
        "\"Careful. This is a limited edition signed Crue shirt,\" he babbled, hitting Ivan's arm. \"I have enough blood on it.\"",
        "Dean looked over at Barbie. She was still holding her head. Looking ... human for a change. Whatever had given her the strength to take Ivan down the first time was gone. The beating Wu had given her had been too much. He watched as she tried to get up but collapsed to the floor.",
        "Ming was still holding Yichen and cradling his head. The old man was still breathing, but he was in trouble. Blood bubbles were popping from his mouth.",
        "It was up to him.",
        "Ivan turned around and started for the computer, dragging Bobby behind him.",
        "\"Dammit!\" Dean forced himself to stand. He looked for a weapon, anything to take him down. He'd already lost to the big man twice. He still had his backup piece, but with how shaky he was feeling, hitting the floor with it would be a challenge.",
        "\"Hey, Mountain Man!\" He took one step, then another and another and plowed into the big Russian's legs. No matter how big something is, they have to have a weak spot. The sudden jolt caused him to drop Bobby.",
        "\"Get outta here, you fucken roadie,\" Dean yelled, trying to trip the big Russian. Nothing had worked before, but he was out of options.",
        "Ivan reached down and picked up Dean by the belt.",
        "\"What the hell?\" shouted Dean, punching Ivan's hand with his good one. Ivan raised Dean to eye level and sighed. The stub of a tongue was clear in his mouth.",
        "\"Let me down, you freak!\" Dean yelled, heart racing.",
        "Ivan shrugged, raised his arm back, and tossed Dean into the wall, ass-first, driving the breath from his lungs. He smashed through the treated wood and hung with his back hanging out the other side, breath coming out in gasps. Spots and stars fought with each other across his eyes, and Ming shouted his name through a fog. It sounded good coming from her.",
        "Looking up, he watched as Ivan lumbered forward, grabbed the two structural supports and brought them down on top of Dean. Dust and plaster filled his lungs. He gasped for air as his life flashed before his eyes.",
        "*\"Welcome, Rookie. I hope you can live up to your name.\"* Zacoski said as the lumber covered his head. He still wondered what Zacoski was hiding.",
        "*\"I'm Ming Na Liu. Nice to meet you. I want to help you uncover the truth, and I will make you trust me.\"*",
        "She certainly did. The darkness filled his eyes, and something pierced his side. He let out a grunt. More dust invaded his mouth, choking him.",
        "*\"Not guilty!\"*",
        "Ming hugged him, and Zacoski patted his shoulder when the judge dismissed the case against him and sentenced his ex-wife to three years for perjury. The open hatred on her face was the only stain.",
        "The light faded as darkness swallowed him.",
        "*Why didn't I tell Ming how I felt about her?*",
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "8:45 PM",
        "\"Dean!\" Ming shouted, putting Yichen's head on the ground. She rushed over to the broken wall and tried to dig him out. His broken arm poked through the rubble, but the rest was buried. \"What the hell do you think you're doing?\" she yelled at Ivan, tears spilling down her face. Pulling at the boards on the top, some of them shifted and collapsed further on Dean.",
        "\"No!\" Ming shouted.",
        "Ivan turned away from her and started back to Bobby.",
        "\"Fuck!\" Bobby said, backing away from the big man. \"Stay away from me!\"",
        "\"Maker! Please run!\" Barbie said, standing. Her nose was broken, and blood covered her chin. She looked like she had one foot in the grave.",
        "Ivan stopped and started swaying, startling everyone. He put his hands to his head and rocked back in a silent scream.",
        "\"What's happening?\" Ming asked Bobby.",
        "\"The fuck if I know. He could be having a meltdown,\" Bobby shrugged, crawling",
        "toward his computer. \"This is more emotion than I've seen him show in years.\"",
        "Grunting, Ivan dropped his arms to the side, then winced and turned to the left. He walked over to Yichen and picked him up by his shoulders. The old man's head was weak and flopped forward.",
        "\"What are you doing, Russian?\" Yichen said. His voice was weak and tired.",
        "\"Put him down!\" Ming stood up and clenched her fists, tears dried on her face. Blood dripped from her fingers; her palms were cut from shifting the wood. The nanites had stopped healing her body. Bobby said twenty-four hours. Was there another limit? Whatever damage she had from her time travel trip had been reversed. \"He's not a danger to you.\"",
        "\"Yes, but he has interfered too many times,\" a new voice said from the doorway. A young man in a simple blue button-down shirt with a squeegee over the pocket stepped through. He was holding a tablet computer and swiped up. \"Finish it, Ivan.\"",
        "\"Chip?\" Ming's jaw dropped. \"Squeegee's R' Us, Chip!\" This is impossible.",
        "\"What the fuck are you doing here, Chip?\" Bobby yelled from the other side of the room. He slouched on the wall on the far side of the room. His damage had been more extensive.",
        "\"Setting an example,\" Chip said. He wasn't smiling, raised a finger high in the air and tapped something on the tablet.",
        "Ivan winced and shook, tears flowing down his face.",
        "\"Stop it!\" Ming yelled, stalking toward Chip. She smashed against an invisible wall, just outside arm's length. \"What the hell?\"",
        "\"I'm not making the same mistake as I did with your father, dear,\" Chip said, leering.",
        "\"Slazney!\" Ming put her hand to her mouth and stepped back.",
        "\"Yes.\" He turned back to Ivan. \"You know what I want, Ivan. Do it, and you can go back to Gregory, but without Petor!\" He pushed the button again.",
        "Ivan stopped trembling and grabbed Yichen's head. Mouthing something, he twisted. The crack filled the room, bringing silence with it.",
        "\"Grandfather!\" Ming collapsed. She couldn't think, couldn't breathe. This was too much. She couldn't take her eyes off the big man.",
        "Yichen fell to the floor. Dead. Ming couldn't see any light in his eyes. Ivan staggered and moved towards the back. Chip slapped the tablet a few more times and sighed. He dropped his arm, and Ivan left through the emergency door across from where he had smashed Dean into the wall.",
        "\"Thank you, Ivan. I'll see you again.\" Chip sighed as the door closed.",
        "With Ivan gone, Ming turned her head and stared at Yichen, her uncle/grandfather. She had hated the man. He was overbearing and opinionated, but also always there to help her family when they needed him. Giving advice and helping out. His dancing was atrocious, but now he would never have the chance to get better.",
        "She turned to the pile of debris. Dean was still there, and Ming had no idea if he was alive or dead. She bent forward and pounded her fist against the floor."
      ]
