    {
      "number": 31,
      "title": "Chapter 31",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "9:00 PM",
        "\"Who are you?\" Bobby shouted at Chip. \"Is that you, Vlad? In Chip's body?\" Two faces were superimposed on each other. A side effect of Barbie's code? One was his manager, the other his brother. Bobby shuddered.",
        "\"You guessed it, Petor. I'm impressed,\" Chip smiled, tapping his finger on the tablet.",
        "\"How are you any better than Gregory? You forced Ivan to kill him, didn't you?\" Bobby said, pointing at Yichen's body. He was leaning against the pillar, exhausted. The nanites had stopped fixing the biggest damage and had gone dormant, but he needed to sleep.",
        "Bobby knew Chip. He hated the boy. Chip was always trying to be better than he was. Claiming he could do things that he really couldn't, and freaky weird as hell. In some ways, just like Vlad.",
        "Bobby slapped his head. \"When did you take over Chip?\"",
        "\"I don't remember. The first time I travelled after Ivan smashed my head against the sink, my mind split. Do you know how hard it was to control so many bodies at the same time? There are still so many out there. After I got into Stanley, I was able to bring some sense to it, direct it all for this day, but it wasn't easy.\" Chip shrugged. \"Gregory gets off on control. I'm more practical.\"",
        "\"Practical? You had Ivan kill a man.\" Bobby took a step forward. He was having a hard time separating the two. He hated them both. \"Why? Because you wanted to do it!\"",
        "Chip shook his head and smiled. \"No, I never wanted to do anything like that. All I've ever wanted was to be free.\" He raised his arms to the ceiling. \"Free from Gregory. Free from killing. Free to do what I want. Back in my own body!\"",
        "\"You're crazy,\" said Bobby.",
        "\"Gregory had us under his thumb. The only thing that saved us was that he didn't know the extent of your coding abilities.\" Chip pointed a finger at Bobby. His face locked in hate and looked more like Vlad every second. \"You could have had freedom, Petor. Saved everyone. With the code, you could have done anything.\"",
        "\"No, it was too dangerous,\" Bobby said, inching toward his computer. \"It destroyed my world.\" A few more steps and he'd be able to stop any of Chip's counters.",
        "\"Dangerous?\" Chip said, laughing. \"How in the world did you think it was dangerous?\" He slid his finger and tapped a few times on the pad. One of the pillars next to Barbie exploded, sending a shower of wood chips into her face. She screamed and covered her head as the wood pierced her body. \"It's so useful.\"",
        "\"Stop it! Don't hurt her! Why are you using the code to hurt people?\" Bobby was almost at his computer.",
        "Chip snorted. \"Hurt people? I'm helping them. Without my guidance, they would be lost.\"",
        "Bobby stared at his boss. It was hard to disconnect the boy he knew from his brother. However, even Vlad wasn't as unhinged as this. He must have completely fractured the first time.",
        "\"I never used the code to do anything stupid like body hopping through time! What the fuck were you thinking?\" Bobby yelled.",
        "\"You used the code to steal records! You frittered it on useless crap like free take-out and didn't even notice the world changing!\" Chip yelled at Bobby. With each exclamation mark, he tapped down on the tablet, and a small explosion erupted among the pillars standing next to Bobby, filling the room with dust and ice chips. The nanobots had stopped their healing and turned off. He was on his own.",
        "He dove for his computer, slipping on the ice Chip used to explode the pillars.",
        "Coughing, his eyes watering, Bobby brought up the program. \"Damn, only two percent power!\" he yelled. Turning off the limiter had failed.",
        "\"Fuck!\" He brought up the program hard copy and scrolled to the final line. Typing in a shield program, he stopped the rest of the pillars from exploding by drying them out. Now, Chip couldn't force the water inside to freeze and expand. He looked up. The ceiling sagged, ready to dump the roof on them. He extended the shield to hold it up, but it was only a matter of time.",
        "\"You have to stop, Vlad! You're going to bring the Shujing down.\" Bobby yelled. He forced the code through. \"You're messing with reality. Things are going to rebound in fucked-up ways. Just look at Steven Segal.\"",
        "\"I don't care about this hotel anymore. It's done what I needed it to do. It got the code back into your head. And this time you can't erase it.\" Chip smiled. \"I need you. The code I stole is breaking down, and I can't update it. Everything I try makes it worse, and I fragment further.\" He waved his hands at the room. \"Do you know how difficult it was to achieve this? I had to do multiple jumps backwards and forwards through time just to ensure you'd be here. Even then, that dead bitch almost fucked everything up!\"",
        "Bobby's face dropped. He watched Barbie shake herself off from the dust of the pillars and turn to Chip. Blood ran down her face and body from dozens of small cuts. Biting her lip, she ran at Chip only to bounce off a shield protecting him, flying backwards and landing in front of Bobby. She groaned and held her back.",
        "\"Why'd you do that?\" Barbie said, getting up. She was moving more slowly than before.",
        "\"What do you want, Vlad? I was in forty-seven. Why did you go back there? Money?\" Bobby asked. He needed more time to let his computer charge. Pulling up a Motley Crue file, he started playing 'Kickstart My Heart' from the Dr. Feelgood album. He loved the beat, and the tempo would provide the boost he needed to shut down Vlad.",
        "\"What are you talking about, Petor? I was never in forty-seven. I had enough trouble setting this up in the eighties.\" Chip wrinkled his nose and shuddered. \"Are you still playing that shit music? Why don't you grow up? With the code, we can do anything.\" Chip spat on the ground. \"I hate it. Why'd you have to tie your code to that drizzle?\"",
        "Bobby eyed the ceiling and grimaced. The cracks were growing. \"I don't understand, Vlad. Tell me! You have the code. What do you need me to update it for?\"",
        "Chip was silent as he tapped some more on the tablet. \"Gregory was right, Petor. You're special. I've tried to code and copy what you've done. But I haven't had the same success you had. Every time I jump, I leave a broken copy behind. I've seen how I failed, and I don't know what I'm doing wrong. I need you to complete it. Make me whole again!\"",
        "\"If I gave you access to the code, do what you want, what would you do with it?\" Bobby looked down. His computer was still sitting at three percent. It was plugged in, but the shield and the music were draining the battery too quickly. Barbie tiptoed towards Chip. Bobby needed to distract him if she had any chance of taking him down.",
        "\"I would use it to get rid of Gregory,\" Chip shouted, fists at his side, anger turning his features closer to Vlad's. The image of the two fading, combining into one. \"To give us everything we ever dreamed of! Bring Sasha home. To get my body back. I miss my body. We were his slaves! He'd already destroyed Ivan. I didn't want the same thing to happen to you.\"",
        "Another explosion blew Barbie back. She shouted in pain as she crashed into the piano, shattering the black wood. A rebounding twang filled the chaos.",
        "\"Stay over there, you bitch. I don't know where you came from, but you've made a mess of everything!\" Vlad screamed. \"Things would have worked. Bobby would have fixed the disaster I'd made!\"",
        "\"Nothing can fix the fuck-up you made of reality, Vlad,\" Bobby said. \"Barbie better be all right!\"",
        "She had gotten to within three feet of Vlad, but whatever he was using to protect himself was state-of-the-art and fully powered. Bobby watched as a guitar formed above the tablet and solidified. A computer could only do so much without the cords powering it. Bobby's code was based on Crue's music, and playing it was the best way to manipulate it, but Vlad hated music. Frowning, Vlad played a riff on his guitar, and Barbie was blocked as a sheet of pink glass shot up from the ground in front of her.",
        "*When did I stop thinking of him as Chip?*",
        "\"Rot in there, bitch. You ruined everything!\" Vlad yelled.",
        "Using the distraction, Bobby entered a program into the computer, ran to the side of the room and grabbed one of Yichen's guitars. It had been signed by Axel Rose, but he wouldn't let Yichen's bad taste stop him. He needed the real thing for this part.",
        "\"Dammit, Vlad. What do you think I was doing with the code? I was happy.\" Bobby hit execute on his computer and opened up with a counter riff on the guitar. Jim had taught him the perfect way to use 'Save Our Souls'. The new beat used Neil's butchering and made it a thing of beauty, tying it to nature directly. The theme was perfect, melding function with style. The pink glass melted into dust and blew itself back at Vlad, encasing his feet and the side of his body in stone.",
        "\"You can't keep creating things out of nothing. The cost is too high! Causality will come back and bite you in the balls!\" Bobby yelled. \"And stop trying to kill my family!\"",
        "\"Fuck you, Petor!\" Vlad yelled, flinching. \"You're not going to win this.\" He pounded furiously on his tablet, dropping the guitar. He could never do much with it anyway. Vlad needed to input the counter before the stone became permanent.",
        "\"Fuck!\" Bobby pounded his fist against his leg. He dove back to his computer and started typing. It had enough power left for two or three more functions, and Vlad would get out of the stone cage quickly.",
        "\"Maker, what are you going to do?\" Barbie asked. She'd crawled close to Bobby, leaving a small trail of blood slicking the floor behind her.",
        "\"Oh, my God. Barbie! Your foot!\" Bobby said, reaching for her. Vlad's last attack had sheared off her right foot. Bobby grit his teeth. \"Fuckin bastard. How dare he do that to you!\"",
        "\"Thank you for worrying, Maker,\" Barbie said. \"But it's gone, and I don't have the power to get it back. The last of my nanobots burned out closing the wound. We can't stop him. He's had too much time to plan his position.\" She pouted.",
        "\"Stop that. You're over twenty, and what would your mother say?\"",
        "Barbie's mouth opened in shock. \"Do you remember everything?\" she asked. Hope filled her voice.",
        "\"Yes, but now's not the time...\" he trailed off. Bobby's eyes grew wide, and he shifted to his computer. \"Time. That's it.\" He pulled up the code and started typing. \"I can't have the music on and use the code at the same time. It's draining the battery too much. Can you play?\" He thrust the guitar at her.",
        "\"Of course,\" Barbie huffed. \"Every citizen of the Greater Vegas area learns the guitar. My Handler taught me personally.\" Barbie turned red and raised her hands. \"But, she said, I can't use the code. I cause too much destruction without a limiter.\"",
        "\"I don't care what she said,\" Bobby cut Barbie off with a wave of his hand. \"He hurt my baby girl, and I can't have that.\"",
        "Barbie teared up. \"I'll do it. Just don't tell my Handler.\"",
        "\"Great. Keep him off me! I need to mess with reality a bit.\" Barbie took the guitar. And caressed the strings. Using the code, he brought up the lyrics to Save Our Souls and combined it with the music he'd altered from Weed Smokers Dream. He had the code display the music in the air next to Barbie. \"Play this! I'll set the computer to translate it into an attack and a shield,\" said Bobby.",
        "\"I know this one. It's beautiful, Maker,\" Barbie said, her eyes misting as she ran her finger along the cords. \"This is your signature piece. I'm honoured to play it.\" She turned over and set the guitar on her lap.",
        "\"What do you think you can do against me, Petor!\" Vlad shouted. His renewed attack shattered the shield around Bobby's computer and rained pieces of broken force down on the two. The pillars continued to explode, sending more showers of concrete, ice and wood. Dust filled the air. Bobby sneezed, covered his head with one hand, wiped off his computer screen and continued typing with the other. Barbie tapped a rhythm on the guitar and set off a reverb, shattering Vlad's attack, turning it into flowers.",
        "\"How are you going to stop his attack, Maker?\"",
        "\"I'm going to have to send you back in time to when the you in the Shujing were killed, Barbie,\" Bobby said. \"You're the only one who can do it. I need you to kill your past self before Vlad infects me and then hide in the folds of reality until I can send you back. You'll also have to reprogram your past self using the worm I'm going to give you, so that it counters Vlad's virus.\"",
        "Barbie gave Bobby a side look of worry and continued playing, rebuilding the shield piece by piece. Vlad's attack was digging in, slowing it down, but not stopping the wall from growing.",
        "\"Are you sure it'll work, Maker? Time travel is like picking up hot broken glass,\" said Barbie. She played another chord. The air around Vlad turned to steamy cola, covering him in foam.",
        "\"Yes, it will, because it's already happened.\" Bobby continued to type. \"I know what your mission really was, Barbara Millicent. I know what you were supposed to do. I realized it in forty-seven when I remembered the last time you came here.\" Bobby stuck his tongue out. \"I didn't want to die then, and I don't want to do it now.\"",
        "Barbie's mouth opened and closed like a fish. Her eyes went wide, and she stopped playing the guitar.",
        "\"Don't stop!\" Bobby shouted.",
        "Vlad used that empty second to dig further into the shield, knocking it back down and causing the ceiling above Bobby to explode. Sparks and plaster rained down on the two of them, burning his arm. The stink of burnt flesh filled the air.",
        "\"Give it up, Petor,\" Vlad shouted over the din. \"I don't want to kill you, but I can't have you interfering with my plans. If I have to bring you back, it won't be the same.\"",
        "\"I've already travelled once this trip. A twofer would break nature,\" Barbie belted out another chord, reinforcing the shield. Her face went hollow.",
        "Bobby grimaced. She was using her life force to power the spell. \"It's a lot to ask, but you're the only one who can survive as a ghost, and this time, I'll make sure you can last,\" Bobby said to Barbie, wiping his brow and smearing blood over it. He entered a command, and a knife formed over the computer. \"When you get there, use the knife. It'll transmit the counter code and stop Vlad's virus from overwriting my personality. When you use the blood in your other self to set up a reverse algorithm, it'll create a feedback loop.\"",
        "\"I get it,\" Barbie said, raising the guitar and sending a reverberating cord back at Vlad. It shattered his guitar and knocked him into the instruments. She took the knife and tucked it into her belt. \"While I'm there, I can use the nanites to recover. She can regain her body when you complete the first part of the code.\" Barbie drew back. \"What about me? Won't I cease to exist? A ghost form can bend the laws of reality for only a little while. There can't be two of me in the era at the same time. The power needed to send me back will leave you defenceless, and could warp reality.\"",
        "\"Fuck!\" Bobby winced and hit enter. A small blue ball of energy formed above his computer. Steaks of light coalesced around it into a solid mass, the stink of burning metal and electricity filling the air and drowning out the smell of flesh. He pulled his shirt off and wrapped it around his hand, wincing as he touched it. The tingling travelled down his arms. \"I know. Don't stay. After you finish what you need to do, use the power that's set off when the glass explodes to kickstart the spell and send yourself back home. Blood magic is powerful and shouldn't fuck-up reality any more than it already has.\" He guided the energy ball over to Barbie. \"This is the anti-code. It'll counter Vlad's attack. It'll also get you home.\"",
        "\"With you? Mother's waiting for you,\" Barbie said, wobbling. She'd lost too much blood. Another trip with the code should remedy that.",
        "Bobby gulped. \"Not yet. I can't go just yet. Tell Sasha that I'm sorry.\" He put both hands behind it and shoved the ball into Barbie's chest. She screamed as the blue energy infused her body, causing her to spasm. She flung the guitar off her lap and shook.",
        "\"No! You can't!\" Vlad shouted, sending another wave of explosions at Bobby and Barbie. The floor pitched, breaking Bobby's concentration.",
        "\"Dammit!\" Bobby turned back to his computer, but one hand wasn't fast enough to keep up with the shifting code. He needed to get the energy into Barbie if she was going to survive.",
        "\"No. Please, Maker. Come with me. We need you, Father,\" Barbie pleaded, still shaking from the energy coursing through her."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 32,
      "title": "Chapter 32",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Ming Na Liu",
        "9:00 PM",
        "Blood soaked the wood, dripping on Ming as she wiggled her way out from under the debris. Dean was still trapped above her, and she couldn't hear if he was breathing. Worry etched lines on her face as she stepped toward him. The destruction Chip was causing had jarred some of the debris from him, exposing him and tossing her away from the fight. A large piece of wood pierced his side.",
        "\"Oh my God, Dean!\" Ming raised her hand to her face. Reaching out with a shaky palm, she checked his pulse. \"Thank God!\" Closing her eyes, she let out the breath she hadn't realized she was holding. \"I'll get you out of there. Just wait.\"",
        "She couldn't look at where Yichen's body was, averting her gaze. His death at Ivan's hand was still too raw. She couldn't believe he was gone. The last twenty minutes from when Chip appeared, nothing but a momentous joke that would end, and everything would be normal again. Then Chip blew up the pillars holding the ceiling and attacked Bobby. Her hands twitched.",
        "*This is not the right time.*",
        "The ceiling was cracking. Ming watched the spectacle unfold, mouth wide in disbelief. She had to make sure it was actually Chip, from Squeegees R' Us, destroying the Shujing's penthouse while wailing on a guitar. Everything was too bizarre. He had set his tablet on the table, and its speaker was amplifying the heavy metal rhythm blasting from the machine. His face had turned from pimply-faced boy Chip to one embroiled in fury. Ming couldn't recognize him as the same person who'd stared at her chest and popped a caramel. That Chip had ceased to exist. Bobby had called him Vlad. It seemed fitting. She needed to help Bobby, but she'd already seen Barbie bounce off something and shatter the piano. Ming wouldn't survive that. She didn't think Barbie could again either.",
        "Scanning the room, she saw the emergency doors near Dean, and an idea hit her. When Ivan went through the door earlier, there was a fire hose hanging on the wall that might work as a distraction. She could use it, but Dean still needed her.",
        "She looked at the fight. Vlad was back pounding on his tablet. He'd dropped the guitar. Bobby was on the other side of the room, pushing a blue ball of crackling energy into Barbie. Ming wrinkled her nose at the smell of ozone and dust carpeting the space around them.",
        "\"No. Please, Maker. Come with me! We need you, Father!\" Barbie said.",
        "Ming's fingers twitched. *Father? I really need a pencil*. She turned back to Dean, clenched her teeth and said, \"I'm sorry, Dean. Bobby can't wait. If he fails, we die.\" She gave a confused smile. \"I feel it in my gut.\"",
        "*You tell anyone I said that, I'll make you wish you'd died here.*",
        "Sliding along the darkness towards the door, she slinked towards the emergency exit just outside the penthouse and the fire hose behind it. Vlad wasn't looking at her, but that could change in a heartbeat. She had no idea what that energy ball could do, but after spending time with Bobby in nineteen-forty-seven, Ming trusted his judgment on this magic stuff.",
        "*I'll find out what Barbie meant later when I have a notebook.*",
        "Easing the door open, Ming checked on the hose. It was still connected, and the pressure should knock Vlad back. She was lucky. He was too intent on Bobby and the crackling energy ball, whatever it was. There was no way she was going to let Vlad get away with his stupid plans.",
        "\"I wanted you to work with me, Petor,\" Vlad said. \"I needed you to fix the code, make me whole! Liu! Stanley! Chip! Jillian! Sanford! My mind is fractured beyond count. It's becoming something I can't control any longer. Without Stanley, I have no way to track them all!\"",
        "\"You should have thought of that before playing with nature, Vlad!\" Bobby shouted, but didn't turn away from the energy ball.",
        "\"If you won't help me now, maybe I'll go back to the bakery in Canada!\" Vlad shouted. \"It failed the first time, but I was so close. I'll make sure it works this go around!\"",
        "\"That was you! Ryan almost bit my head off for that!\" Bobby snarled.",
        "\"I'd rather not have you disrupt my plans anymore. I'm sorry, brother!\" Vlad said, pulling back his hands and looking up.",
        "Ming had only seconds. The ceiling was already buckling, and it would bury them all. If Vlad attacked now, Bobby was dead. She raised the fire hose and spun the wheel, releasing the pressure. It jumped in her hands, but she held on. The water hit Vlad in the face, sending him tumbling toward the window, knocking his tablet out of his hands and pushing him against the glass.",
        "\"Yes! Keep it up, Ming!\" Bobby yelled.",
        "Ming stepped forward, clenched her teeth and opened the hose to its widest setting, dulling the pressure. She didn't want to kill him, but she needed him to suffer. The glass behind the man spiderwebbed. \"How dare you kill my grandfather, you slimy piece of filth!\" she snarled. He was going to pay for this. Ming held the hose on Vlad as he squirmed against the glass, the force drowning out her screams.",
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "9:15 PM",
        "\"I love you, Ming,\" Bobby shouted and turned back to Barbie. Guilt filled his face, but he didn't stop. \"Forgive me, Barbie. Please tell Sasha I love her, but I can't come with you, just yet.\" Bobby finished pushing the blue energy into Barbie with a grunt, dropped his shirt and shook his hand to get rid of the tingling. The ozone smell hung in the air with an undercurrent of burnt flesh.",
        "\"Maker,\" Barbie gasped. \"Father, please.\" She reached for him, tears flowing down her face.",
        "Bobby sobbed as he typed the final lines of code and hit enter. Barbie was engulfed in a beam of light and faded from the room. This was the second time he'd lost a daughter today.",
        "\"NO!\" Vlad shouted from the window, his voice muffled by the water. \"What did you do?\" He pushed himself to his feet and stared at Bobby. Ming's attack was still pushing him against the glass. Cracks appeared in the reinforced material.",
        "\"I sent her back. Her body was created here from some blood she picked up at the crime scene and was unstable. She's in a loop now and is going to stop you, Vlad.\" Bobby typed another function on his computer, and the glass behind Vlad shattered, sending Chip's body into the air.",
        "\"Damn you, Petor!\" shouted Vlad. He fell six floors, ending with a thud.",
        "Bobby looked away. \"It's over,\" he said, slumping to the ground. Barbie was gone, and Yichen was dead. Vlad probably wasn't gone; body hoppers always had a backup plan. But Bobby didn't care, not anymore. Whatever Vlad had tried to do had failed. That was enough for the moment.",
        "\"Damn you to the pigs, Vlad. There's no way anybody should come into power over time and space. It's too dangerous.\" Bobby closed his eyes and said a prayer over his brother. Opening his eyes, the world shifted with a jolt.",
        "\"What the hell?\" Outside the window was devastation and destruction. The hotel across the street had fallen into itself, and dust clouds filled the air. Emergency sirens blared through the night, mixed with the screams.",
        "\"Bastard! You destroyed that hotel as well!\" He rubbed his eyes and stared again, but nothing had changed. \"You're a fucking virus, Vlad,\" Bobby said, gritting his teeth.",
        "He let out a sigh and turned to his computer. There was no way to reverse this. He didn't even have enough power left in it to purge his memory of the code again. It was powering up now, but was running on one percent. Sending Barbie back took everything it had. If he tried now, his counter virus could take some of Vlad's garbage out, but he couldn't rewrite what was there and make himself forget. He needed to get the bad stuff out first and destroy whatever was on Vlad's tablet as well. He walked over to the abandoned tech and picked it up.",
        "\"Password locked.\" He scrunched his nose. \"Fingerprint too. Probably Chip's. Bastard.\" He took the tablet and smashed it across his knee, splitting it in two.",
        "\"What did you do that for?\" Ming asked. She had crawled back to Dean and was pulling the rubble off him. Bobby headed over to help.",
        "\"I can't access it, and it's too dangerous. Two hotels are enough. If anybody should get into it, the destruction won't stop there,\" Bobby said, wavering. He was tired.",
        "\"You used it well enough,\" replied Ming.",
        "\"I was too stupid. If I'd spent the time to learn how to use it properly instead of just hacking it, then maybe.\" He pointed to the piece of wood in Dean's gut. \"You shouldn't touch anything else. If you're not careful, he'll bleed out.\"",
        "\"I know. We have to pack it, though. Stop the bleeding.\" Ming paused. \"Why don't you learn how to use it?\" she asked.",
        "Bobby ignored the question. It cut to the very heart of him, and he didn't want to think about it. \"Just fumbling through the code had caused this much trouble. I don't want to imagine what it would be like if I studied it for real.\"",
        "\"Maybe you could change the world?\" Ming said.",
        "He chuckled and went back to his computer. It still wasn't ready yet. Just five percent. He had to wait a bit longer to get this virus out of his brain, save the Detective, and erase their memories. It would take away all the thoughts of his daughter as well, but there was no choice.",
        "He hated waiting, but he could prepare the way for it. He started typing in his program, adding a few lines of code to tweak the result, maybe mitigate some of the cost. It would prolong the drought, but Vegans had already adapted. What was thirty more years? Ming's words rattled around in his head with each keystroke.",
        "The fire trucks were already here, and the ambulances weren't far behind. They could take the Detective. He'd have to try his handler, Ryan, again, so they could move him to a new safe place. Gregory would find him in a heartbeat, now.",
        "He narrowed his eyes. Something was wrong. His computer power was climbing, but it was going too fast. The power gauge went up past six, then jumped to ten. \"Now, turning off the limiter's working,\" he scoffed and looked up. A shadow moved by the door.",
        "Bobby's eyes went wild. \"Get back! Now!\"",
        "Ivan pushed his way back into the room. Gregory followed behind him. Ming jerked and reached for the hose again. It was still lying near Dean, but was blocked.",
        "Ivan shot forward and swatted her with the back of his hand, sending her flying across the table into the wall.",
        "\"We don't want any disturbance, now do we, Petor?\" Gregory said, smiling. He stepped up to the edge of the table and picked up the pieces of the broken tablet. He glared at Bobby from across the room. \"After all the trouble I went through to find you.\"",
        "\"Gregory. What do you want!\" Bobby stared at Vlad's tablet. It was in pieces, but that wouldn't stop Gregory. He could find value in the smallest things. Bobby had to get it out of Gregory's hands before the bastard could repair it.",
        "\"What I've always wanted, Petor. For you to continue working for me.\" He paused and put his finger to his chin, thinking. \"Pity I didn't realize what you could do before with this code. We'll have to remedy that. Your talents are, shall we say, unique, and I love collecting the unique.\" He waved his hand at Ivan. The big man started moving towards Bobby, picking his way over the rubble of Vlad's last attack.",
        "Bobby typed a command into his computer, and Vlad's tablet melted into a pile of slag. Gregory dropped it, shaking his fingers at the heat. \"Sorry, Gregory,\" he giggled. \"I couldn't leave it there for someone to stumble across.\" He shrugged his shoulders and glanced at his laptop. Melting the tablet had sent the power gauge back to eight. Bobby wrinkled his nose. He needed at least fifteen percent to erase the memory of everybody in the room. Thirty if he wanted to survive.",
        "\"That wasn't very nice, Petor,\" Gregory said, blowing on his fingers. His scar was flashing red in the dark light. He pointed to Ming. Ivan changed directions, moving to her. \"Luckily, I have a second option. I heard she was able to see the code. She may have forgotten it, but with some persuasion, maybe it'll come back.\" Ivan dropped Ming to the floor in front of Gregory and stood behind him. She was still breathing, but in pain, clutching her chest.",
        "\"I can be very persuasive.\"",
        "\"How do you know she's seen the code?\" Bobby asked his old boss.",
        "Gregory snorted. \"You know I have my ways, Petor. It's a pity Vlad had to go out the window. I passed the pile of dust that was him on my way up here. It would make it so much easier to have a Leaper on my team.\" He shook his head. \"I have been too hands-off. That must change.\"",
        "\"What hold does Gregory have on you, Ivan?\" Bobby asked. The big man just shrugged.",
        "\"What's it going to be, Petor? Do I take you willingly, or do I take her and you by force?\" Gregory pointed to the Reporter.",
        "Bobby snuck a look at his computer. It read ten percent. \"Fuck!\" He grabbed the keyboard and started typing.",
        "\"I see.\" Gregory sighed. \"Ivan, try not to kill him, please, and save his computer. We'll check it out later,\" Gregory said, pointing to Bobby."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 33,
      "title": "Chapter 33",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Ivan",
        "9:20 PM",
        "Ivan started humming and moved forward. He raised his fist and closed his eyes. There was no going against Gregory. That scarred bastard's fist was around his heart even now. A glow surrounded Ivan's right hand, releasing a musk scent as he built up his energy. He needed to control the output, put Petor to sleep, or Gregory would get angry.",
        "Maybe he should just end Petor here?",
        "*No, that would leave the woman in Gregory's hands.*",
        "He glanced at the detective and gave a mental sigh. The man was still breathing. After all the effort Ivan had gone through to make sure the impact wouldn't kill him, he was going to die. Nothing he ever did worked out. Even sacrificing himself for Petor and Vlad failed. Vlad went crazy. Petor was unable to save him. Gregory was too powerful.",
        "As Ivan's humming grew stronger, the stringent order infused the room. A bit more would destroy the computer. *I will be punished, but Gregory doesn't need any more power.*",
        "Cackling energy filled the room along with the smell of burnt flesh, overpowering the musk.",
        "\"Ivan, you know he's wrong!\" Bobby yelled over his typing. \"Don't do this!\"",
        "\"He can't answer you, Petor. You know what he is. What he gave up for you. Why are you even trying?\" asked Gregory, shaking his head. He picked up Ming and took her to the side of the room. She was struggling and holding her chest. Ivan's slap probably broke some ribs.",
        "\"Fuck! Fuck! Fuck! He was my friend once. I can't let you do this to him!\" Bobby wasn't going to finish in time.",
        "*It's too late, Petor.*",
        "Ivan reached Bobby and bent down for his computer.",
        "BLAM!",
        "The gunshot echoed in the penthouse. There was a pinprick in his neck, just above his right side. Ivan turned back to the pile of rubble. Dean was sitting up and holding a gun. His face was a rictus of pain. \"Guess I had one bullet left. Old habit. Was saving it for the ex.\" He grinned and slumped down."
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 34,
      "title": "Chapter 34",
      "paragraphs": [
        "***POV_HEADER***Bobby",
        "9:25 PM",
        "\"Dean!\" Ming screamed. She struggled to escape Gregory's grip, yanking her arm up and down, fury giving her extra strength. She turned back to the big man and kneed him in the crotch.",
        "\"Dammit!\" Gregory bent over, releasing Ming's arm and holding his package. The shadows from the failing light fell on his face, hiding his eyes and making his scar stand out. Ming scrambled over the broken furniture, climbing towards Dean.",
        "Ivan stood over Bobby, teetered and rocked backwards. There was a small light peeking out from his fist. Bobby looked at Ivan's face. There was a smile. The first one on Ivan's stone face he'd seen in twenty years.",
        "\"Did you want this?\" Bobby whispered, his eyes wide.",
        "Ivan mouthed 'Free,' and he fell backwards, crashing into the middle of the penthouse. His pent-up energy exploded into the wood in a shower of fire and splinters.",
        "\"No!\" Gregory snarled through the pain and dove for the main door. He made it out as the floor under Ivan buckled, dropping him into the room below. The floor rebounded, sounding like a dozen jackhammers all pounding at once and shaking the rest of the penthouse.",
        "\"Ivan's going to explode,\" Bobby shouted to Ming over the noise. \"He built up all his energy but didn't release it. We have to get out of here.\" The ceiling sagged further downward. Vlad had destroyed the pillars, and with Ivan destroying the floor, there was nothing to support the penthouse anymore.",
        "\"Not without Dean!\" Ming climbed over the rubble, holding her chest.",
        "\"Fool! What can you do with broken ribs!\" Bobby mumbled to himself. His computer was at twelve percent power. There was enough to get Dean out and maybe seal up the wound. \"Reality is going to kick me in the head for this,\" Bobby grunted. Entering the commands, he hit run and watched the light burst from the screen. It was smaller than the light for time travel, but still blinding. \"Ten percent. Maybe Fate won't crush my balls today.\" He closed his computer and ripped the power cord from the outlet, sparks shooting up the side of the wall.",
        "The heaving floor caused the rubble to fall away from Dean, and he slumped to the ground. The piece of wood still pierced his side, but the bleeding had stopped. Ivan's power continued to course through the structure, sending wave after wave through the building. Ming screamed as she tried to get the Detective over her shoulders.",
        "\"What's going on?\" Ming tried to shout over the humming noise. She started hacking as the dust rained down on them.",
        "\"Carry this,\" Bobby thrust his computer at her and hoisted the detective in a fireman's carry. \"You can't carry this Hunk'a Donuts with that rib,\" Bobby grunted, shifting the big man over his back. He stumbled to the side. His foot had finished healing, but he was still weak. The fight with Vlad didn't help. \"Don't lose it. Come on. We don't have enough time.\" He stumbled to the door. \"Ivan's going to blow.\"",
        "\"How bad will it be?\" Ming asked, fumbling with his computer.",
        "\"You remember my trailer?\" Bobby said.",
        "Ming nodded.",
        "\"Think three times that and maybe add a mushroom cloud,\" said Bobby. \"His humming ties him directly to nature, and he can access all the energy stored in it.\"",
        "\"Shit!\" Ming glanced back at the hole. She put her hand on her mouth. \"Grandfather! We can't leave his body.\" She turned back to where Yichen's body was, but rubble blocked the way. \"Where is it?\"",
        "\"There's no time, and I can't carry two,\" Bobby shouted.",
        "Ming reached out. Guilt flooded her face. She nodded and lowered her hand. Tears flowed down her face. They pushed through the heaving waves. Bobby stumbled once, but Ming was able to keep him from dropping Dean.",
        "At the emergency door, they met Wu. She was covered in blood, and one eye was a puffy mess with a large splinter jutting out. She was carrying Yichen's body in her arms and said nothing.",
        "Bobby stared at her and nodded.",
        "She nodded back.",
        "Ming rushed forward and hugged Wu. \"Thank you,\" she said.",
        "\"I owe him this much,\" she said, unsmiling. A mix of fire and regret filled her remaining eye.",
